{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIM: Paternal use of analgesics during the time of conception and adverse birth outcomes are poorly studied. We investigated the association between paternal exposure to non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs and opioids within 3 months before the date of conception and the risk of adverse birth outcomes (preterm birth, small for gestational age, low Apgar score, and major congenital malformations). METHODS: We used nationwide data from the Danish health registers. We included information on all singleton live births, and their fathers and mothers from 1997 to 2018. We created two exposed cohorts, children with preconception paternal exposure to (1) non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs and (2) opioids. The unexposed cohort was children without preconception paternal exposure to non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs or opioids, and we performed a sub-analysis against paternal use of acetaminophen (paracetamol). We used logistic regression models to estimate the odds ratios of adverse birth outcomes including 95% confidence intervals. RESULTS: We identified 1,260,934 children, 45,667 children with paternal exposure to non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs, 10,086 children with paternal exposure to opioids, and 1,205,181 unexposed children. The adjusted odds ratio for preterm birth was 1.08 (95% confidence interval, 1.03-1.13) after paternal exposure to non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs and 1.21 (95% confidence interval, 1.08-1.35) after paternal exposure to opioids. The adjusted odds ratio for small for gestational age was 1.09 (95% confidence interval, 1.03-1.17) after paternal exposure to non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs, and 1.03 (95% confidence interval, 0.88-1.21) after paternal exposure to opioids. We found null-associations for a low Apgar score and major congenital malformations. Estimates were attenuated when compared against paternal paracetamol exposure. CONCLUSIONS: Overall, we found null-associations across the comparisons made. Weak associations were found for paternal exposure to non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs or opioids and preterm birth and small for gestational age, but not with low Apgar score or major congenital malformation. All associations were attenuated when compared against an active comparator of paternal paracetamol exposure. The effect sizes were small and less likely to be of clinical relevance.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lund, Ken","Garvik, Olav Sivertsen","Aagaard, Signe Marie","Jølving, Line Riis","Larsen, Michael Due","Damkier, Per","Nørgård, Bente Mertz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-791833"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Lund, Ken"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Adult","Adverse birth outcomes","Analgesics Opioid adverse effects","Anti Inflammatory Agents Non Steroidal adverse effects","Cohort Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Infant Newborn","Infant Small for Gestational Age","Male","NSAIDs","Opioids","Paternal","Paternal Exposure adverse effects","Preconception","Pregnancy","Premature Birth epidemiology","Registries"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"paternal preconception exposure to non steroid anti inflammatory drugs or opioids and adverse birth outcomes a nationwide registry based cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/263877587/andr.13551.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-791833","identifier":[{"id":"37941509","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85176281554","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-5b051386-fa47-4fba-9160-f2d55f2b76c6"],"keyword":["Adult","Analgesics, Opioid/adverse effects","Anti-Inflammatory Agents, Non-Steroidal/adverse effects","Cohort Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Infant, Newborn","Infant, Small for Gestational Age","Male","NSAIDs","Paternal Exposure/adverse effects","Pregnancy","Premature Birth/epidemiology","Registries","adverse birth outcomes","opioids","paternal","preconception"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D062B529D1A70B0A927DCEAD834EE7D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/263877587/andr.13551.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Epidemiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ken","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"3e515437-3278-4ff2-8fa9-a76034835003","name":"Lund, Ken","orcid":"0000-0002-3959-2926","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olav Sivertsen","key":"garvikpau","last":"Garvik","locid":"9d246a61-f14d-4821-a571-3bb9c27c1cb0","name":"Garvik, Olav Sivertsen","orcid":"0000-0002-6062-1488","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Marie","key":"aagaardpau","last":"Aagaard","locid":"dafa62a9-632f-4e7f-ab89-0ca838df19ca","name":"Aagaard, Signe Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Riis","key":"jølvingpau","last":"Jølving","locid":"524924f0-2e37-4535-9dd3-59630ea8c815","name":"Jølving, Line Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-7433-7656","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Due","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3de91a40-2cd5-40f2-b680-9ef23b0778cf","name":"Larsen, Michael Due","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-2481","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"damkierpau","last":"Damkier","locid":"e254325b-c1ab-405c-a1cc-00b299596c9a","name":"Damkier, Per","orcid":"0000-0003-0591-7187","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Mertz","key":"nørgårdpau","last":"Nørgård","locid":"3d41d6fb-8f1c-4899-9ebd-b72f88e3935d","name":"Nørgård, Bente Mertz","orcid":"0000-0002-9514-3033","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37941509"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/andr.13551","issn":["20472919","20472927"],"issn_org":["20472919"],"issue":"1","journal":"Andrology","pages":"72-81","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Andrology","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85176281554"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-5b051386-fa47-4fba-9160-f2d55f2b76c6"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Paternal preconception exposure to non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs or opioids and adverse birth outcomes : A nationwide registry-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-791833","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The genus Aspergillus is diverse, including species of industrial importance, human pathogens, plant pests, and model organisms. Aspergilus includes species from sections Usti and Cavernicolus, which until recently were joined in section Usti, but have now been proposed to be non-monophyletic and were split by section Nidulantes, Aenei and Raperi. To learn more about these sections, we have sequenced the genomes of 13 Aspergilus species from section Cavernicolus (A. cavernicola, A. californicus, and A. egyptiacus), section Usti (A. carlsbadensis, A. germanicus, A. granulosus, A. heterothallicus, A. insuetus, A. keveii, A. lucknowensis, A. pseudodeflectus and A. pseudoustus), and section Nidulantes (A. quadrilineatus, previously A. tetrazonus). We compared these genomes with 16 additional species from Aspergilus to explore their genetic diversity, based on their genome content, repeat-induced point mutations (RIPs), transposable elements, carbohydrate-active enzyme (CAZyme) profile, growth on plant polysaccharides, and secondary metabolite gene clusters (SMGCs). All analyses support the split of section Usti and provide additional insights: Analyses of genes found only in single species show that these constitute genes which appear to be involved in adaptation to new carbon sources, regulation to fit new niches, and bioactive compounds for competitive advantages, suggesting that these support species differentiation in Aspergillus species. Sections Usti and Cavernicolus have mainly unique SMGCs. Section Usti contains very large and information-rich genomes, an expansion partially driven by CAZymes, as section Usti contains the most CAZyme-rich species seen in genus Aspergillus. Section Usti is clearly an underutilized source of plant biomass degraders and shows great potential as industrial enzyme producers.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Nybo, J. L.","Vesth, Tammi Camilla","Theobald, Sebastian","Frisvad, Jens Christian","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","Kjærbølling, Inge","Rothschild-Mancinelli, Kyle","Lyhne, Ellen Kirstine","Barry, K.","Clum, A.","Yoshinaga, Y.","Ledsgaard, Line","Daum, C.","Lipzen, A.","Kuo, A.","Riley, R.","Mondo, S.","Labutti, K.","Haridas, S.","Pangalinan, J.","Salamov, A. A.","Simmons, B. A.","Magnuson, J. K.","Chen, J.","Drula, E.","Henrissat, Bernard","Wiebenga, A.","Lubbers, R. J. M.","Müller, A.","Gomes, A. C. dos Santos","Mäkelä, M. R.","Stajich, J. E.","Grigoriev, I.","Mortensen, Uffe Hasbro","de Vries, R. P.","Baker, S. E.","Andersen, Mikael Rørdam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808291"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Mikael Rørdam","Baker, S. E.","de Vries, R. P."],"country":["Finland","France","Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["Aalto University","Aix-Marseille Université","All Global Affiliations","Joint Bioenergy Institute","Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory","University of California at Riverside","Westerdijk Fungal Biodiversity Institute"],"keyword":["Aspergillus","CAZymes","Comparative genomics","Secondary metabolites"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"section level genome sequencing and comparative genomics of i aspergillus i sections i cavernicolus i and i usti i","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3114/sim.2025.111.03","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808291","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12070157","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"001445607000002","type":"wos"},{"id":"40371420","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-22eb533c-74f1-497a-b312-c1de6677a82b"],"keyword":["Aspergillus","CAZymes","Comparative genomics","Seco