9","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The potential of intraoral 3D photo scans in forensic odontology identification remains largely unexplored, even though the high degree of detail could allow automated comparison of ante mortem and post mortem dentitions. Differences in soft tissue conditions between ante- and post mortem intraoral 3D photo scans may cause ambiguous variation, burdening the potential automation of the matching process and underlining the need for limiting inclusion of soft tissue in dental comparison. The soft tissue removal must be able to handle dental arches with missing teeth, and intraoral 3D photo scans not originating from plaster models. To address these challenges, we have developed the grid-cutting method. The method is customisable, allowing fine-grained analysis using a small grid size and adaptation of how much of the soft tissues are excluded from the cropped dental scan. When tested on 66 dental scans, the grid-cutting method was able to limit the amount of soft tissue without removing any teeth in 63/66 dental scans. The remaining 3 dental scans had partly erupted third molars (wisdom teeth) which were removed by the grid-cutting method. Overall, the grid-cutting method represents an important step towards automating the matching process in forensic odontology identification using intraoral 3D photo scans.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kofod Petersen, Anika","Forgie, Andrew Hugh","Bindslev, Dorthe Arenholt","Villesen, Palle","Staun Larsen, Line"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-744566"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kofod Petersen, Anika"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Glasgow"],"keyword":["3D scans","Data science","Forensic odontology","Identification"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"automatic removal of soft tissue from 000000000003d dental photo scans an important step in automating future forensic odontology identification","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-63198-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-744566","identifier":[{"id":"85195004195","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11139984","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38816447","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-729bd59d-157f-4e00-991d-176dac179ae4"],"keyword":["3D scans","Automated comparison","Data science","Forensic odontology","IOS (intraoral scanner)","Identification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6E9896A1956B8C451FA3079D64517AB4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-63198-2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Forensic Medicine","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Forensic Medicine, Department of Forensic Medicine - Department of Forensic Medicine - Forensic Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of glasgow","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Glasgow","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anika","key":"kofodpetersenpau","last":"Kofod Petersen","locid":"66df1431-908c-44b2-a391-2215ee5b7377","name":"Kofod Petersen, Anika","orcid":"0000-0001-5913-8723","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew Hugh","key":"forgiepau","last":"Forgie","name":"Forgie, Andrew Hugh","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorthe Arenholt","key":"bindslevpau","last":"Bindslev","locid":"a95ac976-ed75-421f-a895-8fc5ec9c62c0","name":"Bindslev, Dorthe Arenholt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Palle","key":"villesenpau","last":"Villesen","locid":"c1c4bd28-befd-4150-bbbb-10138e528d53","name":"Villesen, Palle","orcid":"0000-0001-7589-8781","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"staunlarsenpau","last":"Staun Larsen","locid":"35e2ae60-25db-4a15-893f-dc8906e2bccf","name":"Staun Larsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-5884","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38816447"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-024-63198-2","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"12421","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195004195"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-729bd59d-157f-4e00-991d-176dac179ae4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Automatic removal of soft tissue from 3D dental photo scans; an important step in automating future forensic odontology identification","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-744566","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"DEBAT: Sundhedsprofessionelle skal genoverveje deres roller i mødet med borgerne, hvis hensigterne om at reducere ulighed i sundhed for borgere med type 2-diabetes i sårbare positioner skal lykkes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mærsk, Jesper Larsen","Hansen, Tania Erika Aniol","Qasimi, Edris","Nielsen, Marie Konge","Bindslev, Peter","Lindahl-Jacobsen, Line Elisabeth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765765"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Socialt arbejde og sociale forhold","Sundhed ernæring og livskvalitet"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sundhedsprofessionelle skal have mere opsøgende rolle i mødet med borgere med type 000000000002 diabetes i sårbare positioner","src":["pha"],"src-code":["DI-UC-AB"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-765765","ids":["pha-3631c5fc-577b-4d17-9d43-c3ef37720cab"],"keyword":["Socialt arbejde og sociale forhold","Sundhed, ernæring og livskvalitet"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DEE179EC43FB6AECDBA2842F400578E1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Sundhed, Social og Engineeringområdet, Absalon - Hverdagsliv og Sundhed","Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Sundhed, Social og Engineeringområdet, Ergoterapeutuddannelsen - Næstved"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Center Sjælland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Larsen","key":"mærskpau","last":"Mærsk","locid":"498dd3b8-2091-4d8a-8316-14799fe80c52","name":"Mærsk, Jesper Larsen","orcid":"0000-0002-5290-7937","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tania Erika Aniol","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"153050ca-b338-49d1-adf3-0d3cbdc05657","name":"Hansen, Tania Erika Aniol","orcid":"0000-0002-3952-3189","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Edris","key":"qasimipau","last":"Qasimi","locid":"f5a64e43-e8b2-4307-9a06-8f71fb19f2d1","name":"Qasimi, Edris","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Konge","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6d14ac10-b9e1-4196-aef4-392a862e55f4","name":"Nielsen, Marie Konge","orcid":"0000-0002-3683-8361","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"bindslevpau","last":"Bindslev","name":"Bindslev, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Elisabeth","key":"lindahljacobsenpau","last":"Lindahl-Jacobsen","locid":"cb2c3d9c-2ec4-43e2-b6ec-7cf77ac4f758","name":"Lindahl-Jacobsen, Line Elisabeth","orcid":"0000-0002-8538-217X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-3631c5fc-577b-4d17-9d43-c3ef37720cab"],"src":["AB University College Absalon"],"title":"Sundhedsprofessionelle skal have mere opsøgende rolle i mødet med borgere med type 2-diabetes i sårbare positioner","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-765765","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Gain-of-function variants in GFAP leads to protein aggregation and is the cause of the severe neurodegenerative disorder Alexander Disease (AxD), while loss of GFAP function has been considered benign. Here, we investigated a six-generation family, where multiple individuals presented with gliosis of the optic nerve head and visual impairment. Whole genome sequencing (WGS) revealed a frameshift variant in GFAP (c.928dup, p.(Met310Asnfs*113)) segregating with disease. Analysis of human embryonic tissues revealed strong expression of GFAP in retinal neural progenitors. A zebrafish model verified that c.928dup does not result in extensive GFAP protein aggregation and zebrafish gfap loss-of-function mutants showed vision impairment and retinal dysplasia, characterized by a significant loss of Müller glia cells and photoreceptor cells. Our findings show how different mutational mechanisms can cause diverging phenotypes and reveal a novel function of GFAP in vertebrate eye development.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Sarusie, Menachem V. K.","Rönnbäck, Cecilia","Jespersgaard, Cathrine","Baungaard, Sif","Ali, Yeasmeen","Kessel, Line","Christensen, Søren Tvorup","Brøndum-Nielsen, Karen","Møllgård, Kjeld","Rosenberg, Thomas","Larsen, Lars Allan","Grønskov, Karen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777690"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel i gfap i frameshift variant identified in a family with optico retinal dysplasia and vision impairment","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-777690","identifier":[{"id":"39471354","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85212457548","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["