a4e1cdfdf5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Feasibility and acceptability of school-based intervention components to promote healthy weight and well-being among 6–11-year-olds in Denmark : mixed methods findings from the Generation Healthy Kids feasibility study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.96-785431","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Grey seals from both the Atlantic and Baltic Sea subspecies are recovering from dramatic declines and recolonising former ranges, potentially leading to overlapping distributions and an emerging subspecies transition zone in Kattegat between Denmark and Sweden. The two subspecies have asynchronous moulting and pupping seasons. We present aerial survey data from 2011 to 2023 in Danish Kattegat during the Atlantic subspecies’ moulting (March–April) and pupping (December–January) seasons, as well as the Baltic subspecies’ moulting season (May–June). During the Atlantic subspecies’ peak moulting season, 82% of the grey seals were recorded north of the island of Læsø (N57°18′, E11°00′). In contrast, during the Baltic moulting season in those years, only 9% of the grey seals were recorded here. This indicates a predominance of Atlantic grey seals in the north and Baltic grey seals in central and southern Kattegat. In 2022 and 2023, three pups were recorded around Læsø during early January, which coincides with the pupping season of northern Wadden Sea grey seals. Previously, pups have been recorded in the same locations during the Baltic pupping season, which demonstrates overlapping breeding ranges. Grey seals are known to have plasticity in the timing of pupping indicated by a west to east cline of progressively later pupping in the eastern North Atlantic. Historical sources document that the Baltic pupping season in Kattegat was earlier than it has been in recent years. Thus, the expanding ranges may be associated with convergence of Atlantic and Baltic subspecies’ pupping seasons and potential hybridisation in this emerging transition zone.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Galatius, Anders","Olsen, Morten Tange","Allentoft-Larsen, Marc Christian","Balle, Jeppe Dalgaard","Kyhn, Line Anker","Sveegaard, Signe","Teilmann, Jonas"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-724490"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Galatius, Anders"],"keyword":["Abundance","Grey seal","Hybridisation","Kattegat","Monitoring","Phenology","Pinnipeds","RANGE","Subspecies","recolonisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evidence of distribution overlap between atlantic and baltic grey seals","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S0025315424000213","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-724490","identifier":[{"id":"85187973949","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1818a13c-971a-4091-aa27-f906476d46e1","ku-a95d524b-9fc1-4640-8295-95436f857445"],"keyword":["Kattegat","abundance","grey seal","hybridisation","monitoring","phenology","pinnipeds","range","recolonisation","subspecies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9276D68CF1B00C4879998CB1E2E33958"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S0025315424000213","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/388547871/evidence_of_distribution_overlap_between_atlantic_and_baltic_grey_seals.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/419825554/evidence-of-distribution-overlap-between-atlantic-and-baltic-grey-seals.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Mammal Research 1"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"galatiuspau","last":"Galatius","locid":"34804171-9f60-4314-a4f4-70df2c4fe2bf","name":"Galatius, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Tange","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"8efdc85b-49df-4bf0-89ec-d985ce76226d","name":"Olsen, Morten Tange","orcid":"0000-0001-6716-6345","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marc","key":"allentoftlarsenpau","last":"Allentoft-Larsen","locid":"e36a0e8f-b04e-4133-b46e-75e629309b4e","name":"Allentoft-Larsen, Marc Christian","name_org":"Allentoft-Larsen, Marc","orcid":"0000-0001-7978-1783","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe Dalgaard","key":"ballepau","last":"Balle","locid":"2346769b-d269-409a-9afa-e5bd87b4ac05","name":"Balle, Jeppe Dalgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Anker","key":"kyhnpau","last":"Kyhn","locid":"aa05c724-f1c2-4ace-959a-9a81158fe5bb","name":"Kyhn, Line Anker","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Signe","key":"sveegaardpau","last":"Sveegaard","locid":"ea1c364f-09ba-4d20-a1cc-9c0d6f568664","name":"Sveegaard, Signe","orcid":"0000-0002-8893-9842","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"teilmannpau","last":"Teilmann","locid":"733c70b6-2727-4145-b8d2-c8778c6bfce2","name":"Teilmann, Jonas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0025315424000213","issn":["00253154","14697769"],"issn_org":["00253154"],"journal":"Journal of the Marine Biological Association of the United Kingdom","paperid":"e30","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of the Marine Biological Association of the United Kingdom","volume":"104"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85187973949"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1818a13c-971a-4091-aa27-f906476d46e1","ku-a95d524b-9fc1-4640-8295-95436f857445"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evidence of distribution overlap between Atlantic and Baltic grey seals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-724490","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The oxytocin system has been thought to contribute to obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD). Few studies, only involving adults, have investigated this hypothesis and have found inconsistent results regarding oxytocin system activity and OCD. We investigated whether salivary oxytocin concentrations differed between children and adolescents with and without OCD and qualified our comparative analysis by investigating the possible covariates age, pubertal stage, and sex. Participants included 113 children and adolescents (8–17 years) with OCD and 88 children and adolescents without any previous or current psychiatric disorder and their parents (254 parents included). Salivary oxytocin concentrations were measured in children and parents with enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA). Statistical analyses were performed using frequentist and Bayesian approaches. We found no evidence of a difference in mean salivary oxytocin concentrations between children and adolescents with and without OCD. Bayesian analysis indicated anecdotal to moderate support for the null hypothesis. We found an association between oxytocin and age and between oxytocin and pubertal stage, which by visual inspection of plots and post-hoc tests indicated nonlinear relationships. We found no association between oxytocin concentration and sex. Our findings do not suggest elevated oxytocin concentrations in pediatric OCD. Nonlinear changes in oxytocin across development show the importance of accounting for hormonal and behavioral changes during puberty.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Mora-Jensen, Anna Rosa Cecilie","Clemmensen, Line Katrine Harder","Grønberg, Manja Gersholm","Lebowitz, Eli R.","Quintana, Daniel S.","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Larsen, Charlotte Sewerin","Bak, Lasse Kristoffer","Christensen, Gitte Lund","Pretzmann, Linea","Uhre, Valdemar","Christensen, Sofie Heidenheim","Uhre, Camilla","Korsbjerg, Nicoline Løcke Jepsen","Thoustrup, Christine Lykke","Hagstrøm, Julie","Ritter, Melanie","Plessen, Kerstin Jessica","Pagsberg, Anne Katrine","Lønfeldt, Nicole Nadine"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-768413"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Mora-Jensen, Anna Rosa Cecilie"],"country":["Norway","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lausanne","University of Oslo","Yale University"],"keyword":["Adolescents","Age","Children","Obsessive compulsive disorder","Oxytocin","Pubertal stage"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the association between salivary oxytocin age and puberty in children with and without ocd","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-80194-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-768413","identifier":[{"id":"39562644","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85209777003","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11576962","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-b4f4a75c-5fa6-450d-b708-37b1e5753007","ku-07194c14-2080-433e-abe6-2e1aaa34076d"],"keyword":["Adolescents","Age","Children","Obsessive-compulsive disorder","Oxytocin","Pubertal stage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DD16C0323C8ACD5BD8DA21CD90C22E24"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-80194-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/413625054/s41598_024_80194_8_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","ty