{"abstract":"It is well known that inflammatory markers play an important role in the development and maintenance of healthy pregnancies. However, the literature regarding inflammation in relation to lifestyle and adverse pregnancy outcomes in twin pregnancies is remarkably uncovered. Therefore, this study aimed at evaluating the concentration of inflammatory markers in dried capillary blood spot samples from 523 women with twin pregnancies, included at a median gestational age of 21+1 weeks. The relationship between inflammatory markers and maternal lifestyle (current smoking status and pre-pregnancy body mass index) in addition to adverse pregnancy outcomes (preeclampsia, gestational diabetes mellitus, and small for gestational age) was analyzed. The study showed that active smoking at inclusion was associated with an elevated concentration of interleukin-8. Furthermore, maternal obesity was associated with an elevated concentration of C-reactive protein and monocyte chemoattractant protein-1. Analysis of the data showed no statistically significant variations in the concentration of the assessed inflammatory markers for neither preeclampsia, gestational diabetes mellitus, nor small for gestational age. The current study promotes future research on the pathophysiology of twin pregnancies in relation to adverse pregnancy outcomes, as the literature within the area remains scarce.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Christiansen, Cecilie Holm","Kirk, Mille","Worda, Katharina","Hegaard, Hanne Kristine","Rode, Line","Larsen, Helle","Holmskov, Anni","Andreasen, Kirsten Riis","Uldbjerg, Niels","Ramb, Jan","Sperling, Lene","Hinterberger, Stefan","Krebs, Lone","Zingenberg, Helle","Weiss, Eva Christine","Strobl, Isolde","Laursen, Lone","Christensen, Jeanette Tranberg","Skogstrand, Kristin","Vogel, Ida","Krampl-Bettelheim, Elisabeth","Tabor, Ann"],"cuid":["S04-093.15-751602"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["Collaborators – The PREDICT-group","The PREDICT-Group"],"corresponding_author":["Rode, Line"],"country":["Austria","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helgelands Hospital, Norge","Innsbruck Medical University","Landeskrankenhaus Klagenfurt","Medical University of Graz","Medical University of Vienna","Vienna"],"keyword":["Adult","Biomarkers blood","Body Mass Index","C Reactive Protein analysis","Chemokine CCL2 blood","Female","Gestational diabetes","Humans","Inflammation","Inflammation Mediators blood","Inflammation immunology","Life Style","Preeclampsia","Pregnancy","Pregnancy Complications immunology","Pregnancy Outcome","Small for gestational age","Smoking adverse effects","Twin pregnancy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inflammatory markers in relation to maternal lifestyle and adverse pregnancy outcomes in twin pregnancies","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85197211697","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding for the Prevention of Preterm Delivery in Twin Gestations (PREDICT) study was provided by The Danish Medical Research Council, The Fetal Medicine Foundation, The Copenhagen University Hospital's Research Fund, The Aase and Ejnar Danielsens Fund, The Augustinus Fund, The Ivan Nielsen Fund, The Doctor Sofus Carl Emil Friis an