l Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Non-Profit Organisations","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Region Zealand","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-efa594e3-d2c9-499a-85ba-9e29a267da73","dtu-a1e7b8d0-650f-4263-9526-d70f0d42665f","kp-41a4a22a-9c8f-4d2a-a423-66275d643b2b","ku-638e3da2-cc0a-418b-adf5-3cba4d334827"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Executive Control and Associated Brain Activity in Children With Familial High-Risk of Schizophrenia or Bipolar Disorder : A Danish Register-based Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-096.57-735349","year":"2024","yearsub":2024}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Food bolus obstruction (FBO) leading to hospital treatment is often associated with eosinophilic oesophagitis (EoE), stenosis, or oesophageal cancer (1). Danish national guidelines recommend that patients with FBO undergo a diagnostic upper endoscopy within two weeks of presentation to exclude possible malignancy, and histological evaluation of eight biopsies (2, 3). AIMS: The aims of this study were to (1) report the incidence and describe the causes and treatment of FBO in the North Denmark Region (NDR), (2) determine the proportion of patients who underwent upper endoscopy and biopsy according to regional and national guidelines, and (3) identify International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision (ICD-10) diagnosis and procedure codes applied to the hospital visits due to FBO in the NDR. METHODS: Among all acute hospital visits in the NDR in 2021, all visits with ICD-10 codes possibly reflecting FBO, as well as a random sample of 14,400 visits with unspecific ICD-10 codes (R and Z codes), were screened manually for possible FBO. Diagnosis, follow-up, and treatment of all patients with FBO were recorded. RESULTS: The median patient age was 66.0 (Q1-Q3: 49.8-81.0) years, and half of the patients had experienced FBO before. Two thirds of patients (66.0%) were never diagnosed with a cause of FBO, followed by 17.3% with EoE. 30% of patients did not undergo upper endoscopy within two weeks of the hospital visit, and 50.7% were never biopsied in the oesophagus. Of 1886 hospital visits with registry ICD-10 codes that possibly reflected FBO, 8.4% were due to FBO, while FBO was present in 0.028% of the random sample of unspecific ICD-10 codes. CONCLUSIONS: Most hospitalized FBO patients in the NDR in 2021 were never diagnosed with a cause. In these patients there is a high risk of overlooked EoE or upper gastrointestinal cancers. The area needs immediate focus and changed routines to improve treatment and prevent new FBO.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Terkelsen, Jacob Holmen","Hollænder, Martin","Bredal, Kasper","Nielsen, Sara Munk","Thomsen, Kristoffer Koed Vittrup","Baggerman, Amanda","Ofverlind, Emilia Colding","Koc, Alptug Mertcan","Pakes, Hannah","Mahdi, Marco Bassam","Larsen, Sanne Ørnfeldt","Gonzalez, Vanessa Parra","Riis, Johannes","Frandsen, Line Tegtmeier","Melgaard, Dorte","Krarup, Anne Lund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-716883"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Krarup, Anne Lund"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Denmark epidemiology","Eosinophilic Esophagitis complications","Eosinophilic oesophagitis","Food Bolus obstruction","Humans","Middle Aged","Oesophageal cancer","Oesophagus","Retrospective Studies","Upper endoscopy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a retrospective cohort study on oesophageal food bolus obstruction in the north denmark region in 000000002021 two thirds were never diagnosed with a cause","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12876-023-03077-8","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was funded by Marie Pedersen and Jensine Heiberg’s Foundation, Center for Clinical Research, North Regional Hospital Hjørring, Denmark. The funding was used for language revision and publication fee."],"id":"S01-000.00-716883","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10759704","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85181240671","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38166672","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-98830de9-d447-45d6-91f0-af6ee3784251"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Denmark/epidemiology","Eosinophilic Esophagitis/complications","Eosinophilic oesophagitis","Esophageal Stenosis/diagnosis","Food Bolus Impaction","Food Bolus obstruction","Humans","Middle Aged","Oesophageal cancer","Oesophagus","Retrospective Studies","Upper Endoscopy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AA872E275C442FA09CC8CB18D8A1A1AB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12876-023-03077-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/645684964/Terkelsen_et_al._2024_._A_retrospective_cohort_study_on_oesophageal_food_bolus_obstruction_in_the_North_Denmark_region_in_2021-two_thirds_were_never_diagnosed_with_a_cause.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Holmen","key":"terkelsenpau","last":"Terkelsen","locid":"3d04ee86-d553-4fc2-888d-804738e5f5b9","name":"Terkelsen, Jacob Holmen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"hollænderpau","last":"Hollænder","locid":"04781380-1daf-45df-89aa-2c0f2c100f62","name":"Hollænder, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"bredalpau","last":"Bredal","locid":"4cbd89aa-c7ca-4939-adc0-dfc61351d719","name":"Bredal, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Munk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3cc01e82-b942-4ddb-aa47-8958aaff4930","name":"Nielsen, Sara Munk","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristoffer Vittrup Koed","key":"thomsenpau","last":"