{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Palle","Larsen, Stina Meyer","Carlsen, Anne-Marie Fiala","Gerbild, Helle Nygaard","Andreasen, Line Stripp","Sørensen, Line","Kristensen, Berit Hytteballe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-784024"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Sundhed ernæring og livskvalitet"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evidens og vidensproduktion nr 000000000006","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.ucl.dk/ws/files/110457471/Evidens_og_videnproduktion_nr_6_Okt.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-784024","ids":["ucl-102b3cf9-4a68-4dbb-9878-1d1b8f46e3ae"],"keyword":["Sundhed, ernæring og livskvalitet"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-23203CA747E0C328530C97CBEC702919"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.ucl.dk/ws/files/110457471/Evidens_og_videnproduktion_nr_6_Okt.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Anvendt Sundhedsforskning"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Palle","key":"larsenpalleped","last":"Larsen","locid":"66794e08-8226-47e4-a21f-f329638ef5e8","name":"Larsen, Palle","orcid":"0000-0002-6112-8935","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Meyer","key":"larsenstinameyerped","last":"Larsen","locid":"8f543caf-2ac2-46be-a40d-28a4477afc3a","name":"Larsen, Stina Meyer","orcid":"0000-0001-5836-370X","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne-Marie Fiala","key":"carlsenannemariefialaped","last":"Carlsen","locid":"0d21f291-c4fb-4bae-832b-01bd5f174aed","name":"Carlsen, Anne-Marie Fiala","orcid":"0000-0001-6912-1546","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle Nygaard","key":"gerbildhellenygaardpau","last":"Gerbild","locid":"f9c4cee1-f09b-408d-9316-86b363d18ad5","name":"Gerbild, Helle Nygaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0699-4264","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Lundell","key":"andreasenlinestripppau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"9d6a41c6-7bf7-4f81-a947-842972a6c344","name":"Andreasen, Line Stripp","name_org":"Andreasen, Line Lundell","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"sørensenlinepau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"e8b28e33-d425-463d-be67-be53d1383145","name":"Sørensen, Line","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Berit Hytteballe","key":"kristensenberithytteballepau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"1adc0f78-6bbe-400d-b03b-d1ef6598bd56","name":"Kristensen, Berit Hytteballe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"75","place":"Odense M","publisher":"UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-102b3cf9-4a68-4dbb-9878-1d1b8f46e3ae"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Evidens og Vidensproduktion : Nr. 6","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-784024","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Facilitatory and inhibitory conditioned pain modulation (CPM) responses are observed in healthy volunteers and chronic pain patients, but the clinical implications for phenotyping are unknown. This study aimed to subgroup and compare chronic knee pain patients according to their CPM responses. Methods: This explorative, cross-sectional study included 127 patients with chronic knee pain (osteoarthritis or following total knee arthroplasty). Individual CPM responses were categorized as facilitatory (test stimuli pain intensity increased when conditioning stimuli were applied), as inhibitory (test stimuli pain intensity decreased) or as no change (defined as less than 5.3% change in pain intensity). Outcomes were clinical pain intensities, temporal summation, widespread pain, self-reported physical function, PainDETECT questionnaire and Pain Quality Assessment Scale. Data were analysed as comparisons between the inhibitory and the facilitatory groups and using multivariate linear regression models. Results: Fifty-four patients had facilitatory CPM responses, 49 had inhibitory CPM responses, and 24 showed no change in CPM response. A between-group difference was observed for self-reported physical function, with the facilitatory CPM group reporting better function (54.4 vs. 46.0, p = 0.028) and the facilitatory CPM group reported more deep pain sensations (3.2 vs. 2.0, p = 0.021). The remaining outcomes showed no between-group differences. Higher clinical pain intensity and facilitated temporal summation were associated in the facilitated CPM group but not in the inhibitory CPM group. Conclusion: These explorative findings indicated that quantitative clinical and experimental differences exist between facilitatory or inhibitory CPM responses in a chronic knee pain patient population. Differences in patients’ CPM responses should be further investigated to unravel possible clinical importance. Significance: Our findings confirm that conditioned pain modulation consist of inhibitory and facilitatory responders among a patient population with chronic knee pain. This explorative study indicates that patients with either facilitatory or inhibitory conditioned pain modulation could exhibit differences in pain outcomes. Subgrouping of chronic pain patients depending on individual conditioned pain modulation responses could be considered in phenotyping patients prior to inclusion in clinical trials or used for personalizing the management regime.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Jesper Bie","Madeleine, Pascal","Sørensen, Line Bay","Sachau, J.","Otto, J. C.","Baron, R.","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-692901"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["AMEOS Gruppe","All Global Affiliations","University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"subgrouping of facilitatory or inhibitory conditioned pain modulation responses in patients with chronic knee pain explorative analysis from a multicentre trial","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejp.2185","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Ralf Baron reports grants and research support from EU Projects: ‘Europain’ (115,007). DOLORisk (633491). IMI Paincare (777500). German Federal Ministry of Education and Research (BMBF): Verbundprojekt: Frühdetektion von Schmerzchronifizierung (NoChro) (13GW0338C). German Research Network on Neuropathic Pain (01EM0903). Pfizer Pharma GmbH, Genzyme GmbH, Grünenthal GmbH, Mundipharma Research GmbH und Co. KG., Novartis Pharma GmbH, Alnylam Pharmaceuticals Inc., Zambon GmbH, Sanofi‐Aventis Deutschland GmbH. RB received speaking fees from Pfizer Pharma GmbH, Genzyme GmbH, Grünenthal GmbH, Mundipharma, Sanofi Pasteur, Medtronic Inc. Neuromodulation, Eisai Co.Ltd., Lilly GmbH, Boehringer Ingelheim Pharma GmbH & Co. KG, Astellas Pharma GmbH, Desitin Arzneimittel GmbH, Teva GmbH, Bayer‐Schering, MSD GmbH, Seqirus Australia Pty. Ltd, Novartis Pharma GmbH, TAD Pharma GmbH, Grünenthal SA Portugal, Sanofi‐Aventis Deutschland GmbH, Agentur Brigitte Süss, Grünenthal Pharma AG Schweiz, Grünenthal B.V. Niederlande, Evapharma, Takeda Pharmaceuticals Internation AG Schweiz, Ology Medical Education Netherlands. RB reports consultancy fees from Pfizer Pharma GmbH, Genzyme GmbH, Grünenthal GmbH, Mundipharma Research GmbH und Co. KG, Allergan, Sanofi Pasteur, Medtronic, Eisai, Lilly GmbH, Boehringer Ingelheim Pharma GmbH&Co.KG, Astellas Pharma GmbH, Novartis Pharma GmbH, Bristol‐Myers Squibb, Biogenidec, AstraZeneca GmbH, Merck, Abbvie, Daiichi Sankyo, Glenmark Pharmaceuticals S.A., Seqirus Australia Pty. Ltd, Teva Pharmaceuticals Europe Niederlande, Teva GmbH, Genentech, Mundipharma International Ltd. UK, Astellas Pharma Ltd. UK, Galapagos NV, Kyowa Kirin GmbH, Vertex Pharmaceuticals Inc., Biotest AG, Celgene GmbH, Desitin Arzneimittel GmbH, Regeneron Pharmaceuticals Inc. USA, Theranexus DSV CEA Frankreich, Abbott Products Operations AG Schweiz, Bayer AG, Grünenthal Pharma AG Schweiz, Mundipharma Research Ltd. UK, Akcea Therapeutics Germany GmbH, Asahi Kasei Pharma Corporation, AbbVie Deutschland GmbH & Co. KG, Air Liquide Sante International Frankreich, Alnylam Germany GmbH, Lateral Pharma Pty Ltd, Hexal AG, Angelini, Janssen, SIMR Biotech Pty Ltd Australien, Confo Therapeutics N. V. Belgium. This research was financially supported by Grünenthal GmbH and the Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain (CNAP), which is supported by the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF121). Research funding was acknowledged from the Shionogi Science Center, Daiichi Sankyo TaNeDS Europe Grant, Pfizer The Global Medical Grant and Innovation Fund Denmark (grant No. 40‐2014‐3). The sponsors were not involved in the execution of the study, the interpretation of data or the publishing of the results. Center for Clinical and Basic Research, and C4Pain, Aalborg, Denmark and the Physiotherapy Department, Aalborg University Hospital, Denmark are acknowledged for administrative and logistic support. Dr Ole Simonsen is acknowledged for his assistance with recruitment and logistic support. Juliane Sachau reports consultancy fees from Pfizer Pharma GmbH, speaking fees from Grünenthal GmbH and Alnylam Germany GmbH and travel support from Pfizer and Alnylam Pharmaceuticals Inc."],"id":"S01-000.00-692901","identifier":[{"id":"85173093146","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a5cf760b-4fb8-4a2e-b111-48315ff2d310"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8DF011D8E456960518B9B48E2BE04D84"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/628214247/European_Journal_of_Pain_-_2023_-_Larsen_-_Subgrouping_of_facilitatory_or_inhibitory_conditioned_pain_modulation_responses.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejp.2185","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Musculoskeletal Health and Implementation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university medical cen