{"abstract":"Expression level of the gene Wheat Breadmaking (TaWBM) has been shown to be correlated with bread quality, and influences the rising of the bread loaf. We found that a family of the wbm homologous genes are present not only in wheat, but also in oat, rye and barley. However, a WBM protein has never been demonstrated experimentally. We have identified the existence of a family of WBM-like Seed Proteins (WSPN) from the prolamin fraction of barley flour, encoded by three closely linked genes on the long arm of chromosome 7H, analysing the gene expression by qPCR and relative protein levels by mass spectroscopy. All three genes are expressed specifically in seeds with no detectable expression in the leaves. The barley WSPNs share a common gene structure with a single exon containing an open reading frame in the size 253–313 bp, with the first 80 bp predicted by TargetP 2.0 to encode a sorting peptide. Furthermore, they all contain the conserved motif C–P-X-G-X4-C-X(4–8)-C-X-C. Structure prediction with Alphafold 2.0 suggest that this motif is a structurally conserved microdomain consisting of two antiparallel strands where the cysteines align.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Andrzejczak, Olga Agata","Olesen, Esben","Nielsen, S. D.H.","Tóth, Lili","Madsen, Claus Krogh","Pedersen, Line","Poulsen, Nina Aagaard","Kidmose, Ulla","Larsen, Lotte Bach","Hebelstrup, Kim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745070"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hebelstrup, Kim"],"keyword":["Baking","Barley","Prolamins"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"wheat bread making wbm like seed proteins wspn a new family of small prolamins in barley","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcs.2024.103961","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745070","identifier":[{"id":"85196556675","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-abd300e6-d8dd-40cd-b96a-c5471209860b"],"keyword":["Baking","Barley","Cysteine network","Prolamins","Wheat wbm"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-80B015DF2DD97AB472B669B91F90EDBE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcs.2024.103961","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/420290528/1-s2.0-S073352102400119X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Genetics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"O. A.","key":"andrzejczakpau","last":"Andrzejczak","locid":"591d74a1-7fcc-477e-a5e1-5edefd34ade0","name":"Andrzejczak, Olga Agata","name_org":"Andrzejczak, O. A.","orcid":"0000-0002-5178-5229","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"E.","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"3098d2b4-bd0a-491d-8cbe-7e4e3b9c668b","name":"Olesen, Esben","name_org":"Olesen, E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"S. D.H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, S. D.H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L.","key":"tóthpau","last":"Tóth","locid":"19cbcc29-c13d-473b-a938-19d9d2019bbc","name":"Tóth, Lili","name_org":"Tóth, L.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"C. K.","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"483c5221-13c3-4c94-a6f5-164754c12557","name":"Madsen, Claus Krogh","name_org":"Madsen, C. K.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0192a00d-61bd-4ead-8712-f2f5b2fea184","name":"Pedersen, Line","name_org":"Pedersen, L.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"N. A.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"c6f00bcb-f900-41bb-98ee-c685ea6f8894","name":"Poulsen, Nina Aagaard","name_org":"Poulsen, N. A.","orcid":"0000-0001-9983-9663","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"U.","key":"kidmosepau","last":"Kidmose","locid":"7a1c5721-dba1-4cbe-9786-132f693dde79","name":"Kidmose, Ulla","name_org":"Kidmose, U.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L. B.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"204d7240-6828-4ee0-8ef5-77a4a2ac92d4","name":"Larsen, Lotte Bach","name_org":"Larsen, L. B.","orcid":"0000-0001-9674-0107","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K. H.","key":"hebelstruppau","last":"Hebelstrup","locid":"e20721de-154d-42bf-b85a-114d8097fbbf","name":"Hebelstrup, Kim","name_org":"Hebelstrup, K. H.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcs.2024.103961","issn":["07335210","10959963"],"issn_org":["07335210"],"journal":"Journal of Cereal Science","paperid":"103961","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cereal Science","volume":"118"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196556675"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-abd300e6-d8dd-40cd-b96a-c5471209860b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Wheat bread making (WBM)-like seed proteins (WSPN) : A new family of small prolamins in barley","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-745070","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Metabolic syndrome encompasses amongst other conditions like obesity and type-2 diabetes and is associated with gut microbiome (GM) dysbiosis. Fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) has been explored to treat metabolic syndrome by restoring the GM; however, concerns on accidentally transferring pathogenic microbes remain. As a safer alternative, fecal virome transplantation (FVT, sterile-filtrated feces) has the advantage over FMT in that mainly bacteriophages are transferred. FVT from lean male donors have shown promise in alleviating the metabolic effects of high-fat diet in a preclinical mouse study. However, FVT still carries the risk of eukaryotic viral infections. To address this, recently developed methods are applied for removing or inactivating eukaryotic viruses in the viral component of FVT. Modified FVTs are compared with unmodified FVT and saline in a diet-induced obesity model on male C57BL/6 N mice. Contrasted with obese control, mice administered a modified FVT (nearly depleted for eukaryotic viruses) exhibits enhanced blood glucose clearance but not weight loss. The unmodified FVT improves liver pathology and reduces the proportions of immune cells in the adipose tissue with a non-uniform response. GM analysis suggests that bacteriophage-mediated GM modulation influences outcomes. Optimizing these approaches could lead to the development of safe bacteriophage-based therapies targeting metabolic syndrome through GM restoration.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Mao, Xiaotian","Larsen, Sabina Birgitte","Zachariassen, Line F.","Brunse, Anders","Adamberg, Signe","Castro-Mejía, Josué L.","Larsen, Frej","Adamberg, Kaarel","Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","Hansen, Axel Kornerup","Hansen, Camilla Hartmann Friis","Rasmussen, Torben Sølbeck"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747582"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Estonia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tallinn University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transfer of modified gut viromes improves symptoms associated with metabolic syndrome in obese male mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-49152-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747582","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11148109","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85195006914","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38830845","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1c23bd00-19ed-4d14-9af9-e0fa49f300e0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F013197CF325F5766CB43CE73B6BEB7B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-49152-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/394532699/Transfer_of_modified_gut_viromes_improves.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Microbiology, Gut Health, and Fermentation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ee","key":"tallinn university of technology","loc":["Estonia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Tallinn University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaotian","key":"maoxiaotianpau","last":"Mao","locid":"b95866c7-bb3f-4bc8-be38-fc921bb75a01","name":"Mao, Xiaotian","orcid":"0000-0001-9425-683X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"