{"abstract":"Purpose: The aim of the study was to describe the temporal changes in causes and prevalence of childhood visual impairment in Denmark based on the National Danish Registry of Children with Visual Impairment (NDRCVI). Methods: Annual reports on the NDRCVI since its establishment in 1979 were reviewed and data on the number of registered children and the causes for registration with a visual impairment were evaluated. Results: The average annual incidence of childhood visual impairment in Denmark is 2.8 per 1000 live-born children and the prevalence of childhood visual impairment is 1.6 per 1000 children <18 years. Today, fewer children are severely visually impaired (visual acuity ≤6/60) at the time of registration (31.6% since 2010 vs. 51.1% in the 1980s). Cerebral visual impairment and optic nerve atrophy have remained common causes of childhood visual impairment whereas sequelae to retinopathy of prematurity have been almost eliminated as a cause. Systemic comorbidities are more common now in children with visual impairment (seen in 63.9% in the last decades vs. 44.6%in the 1980-ties). Conclusion: Whereas the prevalence of visual impairment has remained relatively stable over the years, the severity of visual impairment has improved, suggesting that more children will be able to live an active life supported by aids compensating vision loss. However, more children have systemic comorbidities in combination with their visual impairment suggesting that children with visual impairment face a life not only limited by the obstacles of poor vision. This calls for multidisciplinary management and support of affected children and families.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kessel, Line","Jensen, Hanne","Larsen, Ann-Cathrine","Rosenberg, Thomas","Nissen, Kamilla Rothe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777417"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blindness","Childhood","Pediatric ophthalmology","Vision impairment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"temporal changes in incidence prevalence and causes of childhood visual impairment learnings from 000000000045 years with the national danish registry of children with visual impairment","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.16700","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-777417","identifier":[{"id":"85191228742","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38662528","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-37d3e5ea-d055-4d6c-bf9e-f5727c0fefff"],"keyword":["blindness","childhood","pediatric ophthalmology","vision impairment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FA137417A6F42F0FCC41C5B05C1C01B1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.16700","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/411838860/Acta_Ophthalmologica_2024_Kessel_Temporal_changes_in_incidence_prevalence_and_causes_of_childhood_visual_impairment_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Hanne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ann-Cathrine","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Ann-Cathrine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"rosenbergpau","last":"Rosenberg","name":"Rosenberg, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kamilla Rothe","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","name":"Nissen, Kamilla Rothe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38662528"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.16700","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"7","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"790-796","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"102"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85191228742"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-37d3e5ea-d055-4d6c-bf9e-f5727c0fefff"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Temporal changes in incidence, prevalence and causes of childhood visual impairment – Learnings from 45 years with the National Danish Registry of Children with Visual Impairment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777417","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"I rapporten til en ny museumsreform fremstår forskningsbegrebet meget svagt i forhold til, hvordan den fremtidige forskning på museerne skal vægtes og måles. I Dansk Center for Museumsforskning (DCM) er vi enige i, at forskning skal være et uomgængeligt krav til statsanerkendte museer. Det er forskningen, som ligger til grund for alle andre aktiviteter. Derfor bør den ikke som nu på forhånd devalueres eller sløres ved et mere favnende begreb om vidensudvikling.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Christensen, Hans Dam","Handberg, Kristian","Jensen, Jens F.","Knudsen, Line Vestergaard","Larsen, Ane Hejlskov","Mortensen, Christian Hviid","Sørensen, Anne Scott","Vestergaard, Vitus","Yates, Mia Falch"],"cuid":["S03-084.09-724476"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["Danish Centre for Museum Research","Dansk Center for Museumsforskning"],"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Hans Dam"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"center for dansk museumsforskning forskningsbegrebet står alt for svagt i museumsreformrapporten","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://kulturmonitor.dk/debat/art9711337/Forskningsbegrebet-st%C3%A5r-alt-for-svagt-i-reformrapport","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-084.09-724476","ids":["au-1355b96c-5dbf-4451-89bf-35f1658128ed","au-17202fc4-fbca-4626-b2ad-d50022030dae","sdu-5c7ee73b-b7a4-4938-96b5-b3551a35dc01"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-3-8ED6CC6A32E64E6F56E48B0A8260304D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://kult