"issue":"2","journal":"AIDS","pages":"311-321","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"AIDS","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144590168"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ecbde8c0-7e2d-4ba1-a230-fdad44569b71"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Outcomes following SARS-CoV-2 infection among individuals living with and without HIV; a Danish nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-264450","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Data Centers (DCs) consume a significant amount of energy, making overall energy consumption a major concern. The scale of a DC affects its energy efficiency, with larger centers having more resources for energy-saving measures but at the same time different challenges than those faced by DCs of smaller scale. This work analyses and compares energy efficiency of small, medium, and large DCs, analysing factors such as resource and server utilization and design. Finally, the energy minimisation techniques are evaluated for their potential impact on DC energy consumption, as well as their contribution to DCs of different sizes","author_count":3,"contributors":["Friis, Simon","Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Ruepp, Sarah Renée"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-669513"],"event":{"end":"2023-04-27","place":"Venice, it","start":"2023-04-24","title":"Twenty-Second International Conference on Networks","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cloud","Data center","Energy efficiency","Green","Low Power","Scalability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"strategies for minimization of energy consumption in data centers","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/321149064/Datacenter_EE_5_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-669513","ids":["dtu-eb421234-e3e1-42f7-8ae8-2de270e01c9a"],"keyword":["Cloud","Data center","Energy efficiency","Green","Low Power","Scalability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F0E83013532C0869242542C273E00D32"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/321149064/Datacenter_EE_5_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","name":"Friis, Simon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Maria Pyndt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sarah Renée","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781685580360"],"pages":"17-22","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of Twenty-Second International Conference on Networks"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-eb421234-e3e1-42f7-8ae8-2de270e01c9a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Strategies for Minimization of Energy Consumption in Data Centers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-669513","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Neural differentiation, synaptic transmission, and action potential propagation depend on membrane sphingolipids, whose metabolism is tightly regulated. Mutations in the ceramide transporter CERT (CERT1), which is involved in sphingolipid biosynthesis, are associated with intellectual disability, but the pathogenic mechanism remains obscure. Here, we characterize 31 individuals with de novo missense variants in CERT1. Several variants fall into a previously uncharacterized dimeric helical domain that enables CERT homeostatic inactivation, without which sphingolipid production goes unchecked. The clinical severity reflects the degree to which CERT autoregulation is disrupted, and inhibiting CERT pharmacologically corrects morphological and motor abnormalities in a Drosophila model of the disease, which we call ceramide transporter (CerTra) syndrome. These findings uncover a central role for CERT autoregulation in the control of sphingolipid biosynthetic flux, provide unexpected insight into the structural organization of CERT, and suggest a possible therapeutic approach for patients with CerTra syndrome.","author_count":85,"contributors":["Gehin, Charlotte","Lone, Museer A","Lee, Winston","Capolupo, Laura","Ho, Sylvia","Adeyemi, Adekemi M","Gerkes, Erica H","Stegmann, Alexander Pa","López-Martín, Estrella","Bermejo-Sánchez, Eva","Martínez-Delgado, Beatriz","Zweier, Christiane","Kraus, Cornelia","Popp, Bernt","Strehlow, Vincent","Gräfe, Daniel","Knerr, Ina","Jones, Eppie R","Zamuner, Stefano","Abriata, Luciano A","Kunnathully, Vidya","Moeller, Brandon E","Vocat, Anthony","Rommelaere, Samuel","Bocquete, Jean-Philippe","Ruchti, Evelyne","Limoni, Greta","Van Campenhoudt, Marine","Bourgeat, Samuel","Henklein, Petra","Gilissen, Christian","van Bon, Bregje W","Pfundt, Rolph","Willemsen, Marjolein H","Schieving, Jolanda H","Leonardi, Emanuela","Soli, Fiorenza","Murgia, Alessandra","Guo, Hui","Zhang, Qiumeng","Xia, Kun","Fagerberg, Christina","Beier, Christoph Pa