McCabe, Brian D","rank":81,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"delosriospau","last":"De Los Rios","name":"De Los Rios, Paolo","rank":82,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"35","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorsten","key":"hornemannpau","last":"Hornemann","name":"Hornemann, Thorsten","rank":83,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giovanni","key":"dangelopau","last":"D'Angelo","name":"D'Angelo, Giovanni","rank":84,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vincenzo A","key":"gennarinopau","last":"Gennarino","name":"Gennarino, Vincenzo A","rank":85,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36976648"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1172/jci165019","issn":["00219738","15588238"],"issn_org":["00219738"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Clinical Investigation","paperid":"e165019","publisher":"American Society for Clinical Investigation","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Investigation","title_org":"The Journal of Clinical Investigation","volume":"133"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159733545"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-48346282-4246-4625-976e-36b3724e611d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"CERT1 mutations perturb human development by disrupting sphingolipid homeostasis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671604","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Low-carbon scenarios for enabling heat demand flexibility in district heating networks include smart home technology (SHT), which can automate control of heating by responding to utility signals while considering household preferences. This study empirically explores how control of space heating using SHT is performed in heating practices by occupants. The study is based on in-depth interviews and home tours with occupants living in smart homes in Denmark. The results suggest that (1) practical knowledge, (2) notions of being in control, and (3) temporal aspects of everyday life are of specific importance for how occupants perform control of space heating using SHT. Furthermore, results show how occupants act when feeling out of control. The data illustrate that control of space heating using SHT is performed in a variety of different ways, displaying the dynamic relationships between the materiality of the home, the importance of practical knowledge that occupants draw upon, and the meaning they ascribe to ‘homely’ practices. As SHT limits people’s active engagement in controlling space heating by relying on automated features, the findings presented in this paper highlight how control of space heating is more than the ability to control but concerns the dynamics of social practices performed within and outside of the home. Based on the results, the paper recommends four specific design and policy implications for future SHT solutions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Simon Peter Aslak Kondrup","Gram-Hanssen, Kirsten","Madsen, Line Valdorff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-674057"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Control","Demand side management","Energy demand","Energy flexibility","Everyday life","Smart home technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in control or being controlled investigating the control of space heating in smart homes","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/su15129489","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-674057","identifier":[{"id":"85164000974","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b9136d7b-ee14-40bc-84c9-f2569c5ab3e3"],"keyword":["control","demand-side management","energy demand","energy flexibility","everyday life","smart home technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FEAE20147C6A435AE3BE33F9991966B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/su15129489","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/538892385/sustainability-15-09489.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Peter Aslak Kondrup","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"84e32191-0b2f-499d-bd83-8947b95f917a","name":"Larsen, Simon Peter Aslak Kondrup","orcid":"0000-0002-9367-4500","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kirsten","key":"gramhanssenpau","last":"Gram-Hanssen","locid":"e08c8bc7-62c8-4905-99f4-5a5a9c9f4e4d","name":"Gram-Hanssen, Kirsten","orcid":"0000-0002-8543-2501","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Valdorff","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"4384fb97-d4b8-4c24-a82a-66fadb2d872a","name":"Madsen, Line Valdorff","orcid":"0000-0003-0861-0041","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/su15129489","issn":["20711050"],"issue":"12","journal":"Sustainability","paperid":"9489","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute","status":"p","title":"Sustainability","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164000974"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b9136d7b-ee14-40bc-84c9-f2569c5ab3e3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"In Control or Being Controlled? Investigating the Control of Space Heating in Smart Homes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-674057","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"CONTEXT: Nonpharmacological strategies are increasingly used in pediatric procedures, but in pediatric MRI, sedation and general anesthesia are still commonly required. OBJECTIVES: To evaluate the effectiveness of nonpharmacological interventions in reducing use of sedation and general anesthesia in pediatric patients undergoing MRI, and to investigate effects on scan time, image quality, and anxiety. DATA SOURCES: We searched Ovid Medline, CINAHL, Embase, and CENTRAL from inception through October 10, 2022. STUDY SELECTION: We included randomized controlled trials and quasi-experimental designs comparing the effect of a nonpharmacological intervention with standard care on use of sedation or general anesthesia, scan time, image quality, or child and parental anxiety among infants (<2 years), children, and adolescents (2-18 years) undergoing MRI. DATA EXTRACTION: Standardized instruments were used to extract data and assess study quality. RESULTS: Forty-six studies were eligible for the systematic review. Limited to studies on children and adolescents, the meta-analysis included 20 studies with 33 873 patients. Intervention versus comparator analysis showed that nonpharmacological interventions were associated with reduced need for sedation and general anesthesia in the randomized control trials (risk ratio, 0.68; 95% confidence interval, 0.48-0.95; l2 = 35%) and nonrandomized studies (risk ratio, 0.58; 95% confidence interval, 0.51-0.66; l2 = 91%). The effect was largest among children aged 3 to 10 years when compared with older children and adolescents aged 11 to 18 years. LIMITATIONS: There was substantial heterogeneity among nonrandomized studies. CONCLUSIONS: Nonpharmacological interventions must be considered as standard procedure in infants, children, and adolescents undergoing MRI.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Thestrup, Jakob","Hybschmann, Jane","Madsen, Thurid W","Bork, Nanna E","Sørensen, Jette Led","Afshari, Arash","Borgwardt, Lise","Berntsen, Marianne","Born, Alfred Peter","Aunsholt, Lise","Larsen, Vibeke A","Gjærde, Line K"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-702325"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Juliane Marie Centre and Mary Elizabeth's Hospital"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nonpharmacological interventions to reduce sedation and general anesthesia in pediatric mri a meta analysis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1542/hpeds.2023-007289","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-702325","identifier":[{"id":"37727937","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85173842701","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cc493d4e-6419-4797-b19a-a5480b8669fb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F250A2BB1E571404AF20650C134D0C23"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1542/hpeds.2023-007289","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/374567022/hpeds.2023_007289.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Juliane Marie Centre and Mary Elizabeth's Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Department of Pediatrics and Adolescent Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob","key":"thestruppau","last":"Thestrup","name":"Thestrup, Jakob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jane","key":"hybschmannpau","last":"Hybschmann","name":"Hybschmann, Jane","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thurid W","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Thurid W","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nanna E","key":"borkpau","last":"Bork","name":"Bork, Nanna E","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jette L","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"84ce4092-8277-45c1-89d5-afedea9c65f0","name":"Sørensen, Jette Led","name_org":"Sørensen, Jette L","orcid":"0000-0002-7320-2784","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Arash","key":"afsharipau","last":"Afshari","locid":"9c54dedc-02ce-45c0-81f9-9927febcd9d3","name":"Afshari, Arash","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lise","key":"borgwardtpau","last":"Borgwardt","name":"Borgwardt, Lise","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne","key":"berntsenpau","last":"Berntsen","name":"Berntsen, Marianne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Alfred Peter","key":"bornpau","last":"Born","name":"Born, Alfred Peter","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lise","key":"aunsholtpau","last":"Aunsholt","locid":"1c8a5c3e-3b93-4a1e-9e9b-ce6b150bd56a","name":"Aunsholt, Lise","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Vibeke A","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Vibeke A","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Line K","key":"gjærdepau","last":"Gjærde","name":"Gjærde, Line K","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37727937"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1542/hpeds.2023-007289","issn":["21541663"],"issn_org":["21541671"],"issue":"10","journal":"Hospital pediatrics","status":"p","title":"Hospital pediatrics","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173842701"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","department of pediatrics and adolescent medicine"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cc493d4e-6419-4797-b19a-a5480b8669fb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nonpharmacological Interventions to Reduce Sedation and General Anesthesia in Pediatric MRI : A Meta-analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-702325","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Time domain induced polarization (TDIP) method suffers from a plethora of undesired responses which prominently includes powerline harmonics, electric spikes, self-potentials of the earth and random noise. These undesired responses restrict access to the spectral content which is vital in characterizing rocks, soil and minerals present in the subsurface. Hence, mitigating the impact of these noisy responses measured along with the IP potentials is among the core processing challenges faced by TDIP method today. To this end, we propose the use of variational mode decomposition (VMD) that can decompose time series data into its intrinsic frequency modes (IMFs) which are essentially time series containing a narrowband signal component. Such a decomposition is vital in TDIP signal processing because IP decay is known to have a dominantly low frequency spectrum while noise has considerably higher spectral range. Hence, we employ successive use of VMD on the raw TDIP signal to gradually extract and accumulate the low frequency components of the IP decay in initial IMFs (while noise is distributed among latter modes). We validate the performance of the proposed VMD based approach through synthetic as well as field examples.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Naveed, Khuram","Meldgaard Madsen, Line","Grombacher, Denys","Larsen, Jakob Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-706816"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-07","place":"Edinburgh , gb","start":"2023-09-03","title":"NSG2023 29th European Meeting of Environmental and Engineering Geophysics","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"variational mode decomposition based processing of time domain induced polarization data","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-706816","identifier":[{"id":"85182928508","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-14c8b142-5981-46b0-a5e6-60cb2993a5c5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DADA14F2DF5B445A63DB9BE2281255C2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Signal Processing and Machine learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Khuram","key":"naveedpau","last":"Naveed","locid":"4f58e982-d7d5-4523-b0f6-a5c4850686b8","name":"Naveed, Khuram","orcid":"0000-0001-8286-6139","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"meldgaardmadsenpau","last":"Meldgaard Madsen","locid":"9e5e14d1-c032-4469-bde5-e1fba2710bf2","name":"Meldgaard Madsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0001-5435-9914","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Denys","key":"grombacherpau","last":"Grombacher","locid":"4abc41e2-38a9-4496-8861-7c076cc891f1","name":"Grombacher, Denys","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Juul","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3606236a-56cc-44ea-9024-093ba943b481","name":"Larsen, Jakob Juul","orcid":"0000-0002-4509-4480","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-14c8b142-5981-46b0-a5e6-60cb2993a5c5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Variational Mode Decomposition-Based Processing of Time-Domain Induced Polarization Data","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-706816","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Data centers are to become a vital part of mobilenetworks when exploring new architectures such as cloud radioaccess network, which is seen as a more energy efficient alternative to today’s mobile network installations. However, the scaleof a data center affects its energy efficiency, with larger datacenters having more resources for energy-saving measures butat the same time different challenges than those faced by datacenters of smaller scale. Hence, this work analyzes and comparesenergy efficiency of small, medium, and large data centers, andexplores the energy minimization opportunities for cloud radioaccess network data centers. When moving processing from theradio access network to a data center to save energy in the radioaccess network, the mobile network operator does not want tomove the energy consumption from the radio access network tothe data center. Hence, energy consumption must be reduced inall segments of the network, and not moved to another segment.In the case study provided, cloud radio access network datacenters are categorized as mid-scale and small-scale dependingon the size of area they cover due to strict latency requirementsof mobile network traffic flow. Thus, even though larger DCsprove to be more energy efficient, other factors, which in thecase of mobile networks will be latency, will impact the size ofthe data center. Hence, this is a major driver to consider howenergy consumption can be minimized in small data centers.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Friis, Simon","Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","Ruepp, Sarah Renée"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-711734"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt"],"keyword":["C RAN","Cloud","Data center","Energy efficiency","Green RAN"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy consumption minimization in data centers for cloud ran","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/347512293/EXTENDED_Datacenter_CR.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-711734","ids":["dtu-988c751f-10d7-49cd-827e-484d8ccde419"],"keyword":["C-RAN","Cloud","Data center","Energy efficiency","Green RAN"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-20C90A0A88689348373E460E14B63B38"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/347512293/EXTENDED_Datacenter_CR.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["TDC NET A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Maria Pyndt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","name":"Friis, Simon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Lehrmann","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sarah Renée","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19422644"],"issue":"3 & 4","journal":"International Journal On Advances in Networks and Services","pages":"75-89","publisher":"IARIA","status":"p","title":"International Journal On Advances in Networks and Services","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","tdc net a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-988c751f-10d7-49cd-827e-484d8ccde419"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Energy Consumption Minimization in Data Centers for Cloud-RAN","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-711734","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Aske Gye","Sadolin, Line Ø.","Thomsen, Trine Rolighed","Oliveira, Anderson Souza"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-726003"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a preliminary analysis on the feasibility of detecting gait events using machine learning and motion sensors embedded in smartphones","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-726003","ids":["aau-8f999006-e37a-40e3-8803-9114d36bd206"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-107390D38F4E42EF9396A808CC8F6369"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aske Gye","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"46714b8a-5f5a-43f8-b9a9-a59f8255c179","name":"Larsen, Aske Gye","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Ø.","key":"sadolinpau","last":"Sadolin","locid":"613d453c-10e0-451e-8317-66aeec7bd8ff","name":"Sadolin, Line Ø.","orcid":"0009-0006-2187-2125","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine Rolighed","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"2a598ca5-d398-4f6f-a07a-e27982669ee8","name":"Thomsen, Trine Rolighed","orcid":"0000-0002-7393-9372","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anderson Souza","key":"oliveirapau","last":"Oliveira","locid":"52dfbf20-ae09-400b-aabf-b90a8b84f69c","name":"Oliveira, Anderson Souza","orcid":"0000-0003-2186-8100","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"29","status":"p","title":"Program &amp; Abstracts: 15th Annual Meeting of the Danish Society of Biomechanics."},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8f999006-e37a-40e3-8803-9114d36bd206"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A preliminary analysis on the feasibility of detecting gait events using machine learning and motion sensors embedded in smartphones","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-726003","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To examine the potential of different head-mounted displays in the rehabilitation of individuals with visual impairment. Methods: This prospective explorative study conducted between September 2019 and August 2020 included participants with Stargardt disease with moderate to severe visual impairment and a relatively preserved peripheral visual field. AceSight, eSight 3, IrisVision Live, and Jordy were tested. After instruction and training, participants chose two head-mounted displays for home use for two weeks per device. The Canadian Occupational Performance Measure was used for evaluation. Results: Twelve participants (aged 16–53 years) tested all head-mounted displays in the clinic. Distance visual acuity and reading distance improved with all head-mounted displays and eSight and Irisvision improved near visual acuity. Six participants decided not to test the head-mounted display at home due to lack of time or energy, dizziness and discomfort, double vision and peripheral visual field limitation, or aesthetics. After home use, the participants reported improved visual function at a distance with IrisVision, AceSight, and e-Sight, whereas only AceSight improved vision during near tasks. IrisVision and eSight improved reading ability, and none of the devices improved vision during tasks involving computers. Five participants used the devices sparingly, and five avoided public use owing to aesthetics. Conclusion: We found an improvement in distance visual acuity and increased reading distance for all tested head-mounted displays. Additionally, IrisVision and eSight improved visual function at near and eSight also improved contrast vision at distance. Despite the possibility of improving vision, social stigma and device aesthetics kept the participants from using head-mounted displays in public and limited their use at home.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Schmidt, Diana Chabané","Kjølholm, Christine Dahlgren Bohnsack","Jordana, Joaquim Torner","Spange, Vibeke","Højstrup, Pernille Duelund","Larsen, Bo Schack","Kessel, Line"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-731068"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Head mounted display","Stargardt Disease","Visual impairment","visual aid"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Institute for the Blind and Visually Impaired"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"at home trial of four different head mounted displays in visual rehabilitation of people with stargardt disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/OPTO.S434404","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-731068","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10693250","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38046087","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85178365448","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4c89cbdc-88bd-4b42-ac5d-3552067c5ed1"],"keyword":["Stargardt disease","electronic glasses","head-mounted display","visual aid","visual impairment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AD4D506B79E48CE77500060DF52B375E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/OPTO.S434404","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/386573601/OPTO_434404_at_home_trial_of_four_different_head_mounted_displays_in_vis.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Institute for the Blind and Visually Impaired"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Diana Chabané","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Diana Chabané","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christine Dahlgren Bohnsack","key":"kjølholmpau","last":"Kjølholm","name":"Kjølholm, Christine Dahlgren Bohnsack","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joaquim Torner","key":"jordanapau","last":"Jordana","name":"Jordana, Joaquim Torner","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke","key":"spangepau","last":"Spange","name":"Spange, Vibeke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Pernille Duelund","key":"højstruppau","last":"Højstrup","name":"Højstrup, Pernille Duelund","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bo Schack","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Bo Schack","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38046087"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2147/opto.s434404","issn":["11792752"],"journal":"Clinical Optometry","pages":"271-281","status":"p","title":"Clinical Optometry","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178365448"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4c89cbdc-88bd-4b42-ac5d-3552067c5ed1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"At-Home Trial of Four Different Head-Mounted Displays in Visual Rehabilitation of People with Stargardt Disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-731068","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Recurrence of cancer is not routinely registered in Danish national health registers. This study aimed to develop and validate a register-based algorithm to identify patients diagnosed with recurrent lung cancer and to estimate the accuracy of the identified diagnosis date. Material and Methods: Patients with early-stage lung cancer treated with surgery were included in the study. Recurrence indicators were diagnosis and procedure codes recorded in the Danish National Patient Register and pathology results recorded in the Danish National Pathology Register. Information from CT scans and medical records served as the gold standard to assess the accuracy of the algorithm. Results: The final population consisted of 217 patients; 72 (33%) had recurrence according to the gold standard. The median follow-up time since primary lung cancer diagnosis was 29 months (interquartile interval: 18–46). The algorithm for identifying a recurrence reached a sensitivity of 83.3% (95% CI: 72.7–91.1), a specificity of 93.8% (95% CI: 88.5–97.1), and a positive predictive value of 87.0% (95% CI: 76.7–93.9). The algorithm identified 70% of the recurrences within 60 days of the recurrence date registered by the gold standard method. The positive predictive value of the algorithm decreased to 70% when the algorithm was simulated in a population with a recurrence rate of 15%. Conclusion: The proposed algorithm demonstrated good performance in a population with 33% recurrences over a median of 29 months. It can be used to identify patients diagnosed with recurrent lung cancer, and it may be a valuable tool for future research in this field. However, a lower positive predictive value is seen when applying the algorithm in populations with low recurrence rates.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Linda Aagaard","Christensen, Niels Lyhne","Winther-Larsen, Anne","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","Virgilsen, Line Flytkjær","Jensen, Henry","Vedsted, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-099.94-685971"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Linda Aagaard"],"keyword":["Algorithms","Denmark","Lung Neoplasms","Recurrence","Registries","Validation study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a validated register based algorithm to identify patients diagnosed with recurrence of surgically treated stage i lung cancer in denmark","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S396738","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.94-685971","identifier":[{"id":"36890800","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9986467","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85149645758","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7a570e89-4ed2-484e-8226-6d0cc3f92450","ku-7966fda5-ab83-49de-b10c-ccdf93a63227"],"keyword":["Denmark","algorithms","lung neoplasms","recurrence","registries","validation study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-808327632A5D37F54B628B3A118E3A04"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/363063575/CLEP_396738_a_validated_register_based_algorithm_to_identify_patients_di.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S396738","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark"