{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Staun Larsen, Line","Neuhaus, Klaus W","Gjørup, Hans","Jacobsen, Pernille Endrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-709607"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bern"],"level":"pop","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"osteogenesis imperfecta","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-709607","ids":["au-e6cd25ea-d0d1-42b4-841a-5dfb05ca7e28"],"lang":"German","level":"Popular","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-48615D13F806A42218009749F9FE5E59"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"university of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bern","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"staunlarsenlinepau","last":"Staun Larsen","locid":"35e2ae60-25db-4a15-893f-dc8906e2bccf","name":"Staun Larsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-5884","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus W","key":"neuhausklauswpau","last":"Neuhaus","name":"Neuhaus, Klaus W","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"gjøruphanspau","last":"Gjørup","name":"Gjørup, Hans","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Endrup","key":"jacobsenpernilleendruppau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"4346e517-a182-4f10-bfd2-ed3958521afc","name":"Jacobsen, Pernille Endrup","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas","key":"filippiandreaspedh","last":"Filippi","name":"Filippi, Andreas","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cornelia","key":"filippicorneliapedh","last":"Filippi","name":"Filippi, Cornelia","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"wneuhausklauspedh","last":"W Neuhaus","name":"W Neuhaus, Klaus","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783868676266"],"pages":"308-312","place":"Berlin","publisher":"Quintessence Publishing","status":"p","title":"Die zahnmedizinische Behandlung von Menschen mit Special Needs"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e6cd25ea-d0d1-42b4-841a-5dfb05ca7e28"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Osteogenesis imperfecta","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-709607","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To compare the risk of a positive severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) test and coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) outcomes in people with HIV (PWH) with the general population, and estimate the association with vaccination status. DESIGN: A nationwide, population based, matched cohort study. METHODS: We included all Danish PWH ≥18 years ( n  = 5276) and an age and sex-matched general population cohort ( n  = 42 308). We used Cox regression analyses to calculate (adjusted) incidence rate ratios [(a)IRR] and further stratified and restricted the analyses. RESULTS: We observed no major difference in risk of first positive SARS-CoV-2 test [aIRR: 0.8 (95% confidence interval (CI): 0.8-0.9)], but a higher risk of first hospital contact with COVID-19 and hospitalization with severe COVID-19 for PWH vs. controls [IRR: 2.0; (1.6-2.5), 1.8 (1.4-2.3)]. Risk of first hospitalization decreased substantially in PWH with calendar time [first half of year 2022 vs. 2020 IRR: 0.3; (0.2-0.6)], whereas the risk compared to population controls remained almost twofold increased. We did not observe increased risk of death after SARS-CoV-2 infection [aIRR: 0.7 (95% CI: 0.3-2.0)]. Compared to PWH who had received two vaccines PWH who receiving a third vaccine had reduced risk of first positive SARS-CoV-2 test, death (individuals ≥60years) and hospitalization [aIRR: 0.9 (0.7-1.0); 0.2 (0.1-0.7); 0.6 (0.2-1.2)]. CONCLUSION: PWH have almost the same risk of a positive SARS-CoV-2 test as the general population. Although risk of hospital contacts and severe outcomes following SARS-CoV-2 infection is increased, the risk of death does not seem to be substantially increased. Importantly, a third vaccine is associated with reduced risk of infection, and death.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Line D.","Cowan, Susan","Gerstoft, Jan","Kronborg, Gitte","Johansen, Isik S.","Larsen, Carsten S.","Weise, Lothar","Dalager-Pedersen, Michael","Leth, Steffen","Nielsen, Lars N.","Lunding, Suzanne","Omland, Lars H.","Obel, Niels"],"cuid":["S03-093.56-691863"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Obel, Niels"],"keyword":["COVID 19 epidemiology","Cohort Studies","Coronavirus disease 2019","Denmark epidemiology","HIV CD4 cell count","HIV Infections complications","Humans","SARS CoV 2","Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2","severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 vaccines"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outcomes following severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 000000000002 infection among individuals with and without hiv in denmark","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/QAD.0000000000003393","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank the staff in test sites and in the hospital Departments of Clinical Microbiology. We further wish to thank staff at the Department of Virus & Microbiological Special Diagnostics, Test Center Denmark, and the staff of the Data Integration and Analysis Secretariat (DIAS), all at Statens Serum Institut."],"id":"S03-093.56-691863","identifier":[{"id":"85144590168","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36129108","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-dfdbc031-cce0-4308-b94f-b4bb25036a5e","ku-b7e77622-d6bd-4ab9-a9f9-a96c1a6a6d38","sdu-37e8daf6-44bb-4918-a6ca-c9ea73093e71"],"keyword":