"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"teilmannjonaspau","last":"Teilmann","locid":"733c70b6-2727-4145-b8d2-c8778c6bfce2","name":"Teilmann, Jonas","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"tougaardjakobpau","last":"Tougaard","locid":"edd6deab-ccc4-4f22-b130-f9ec24fd6a48","name":"Tougaard, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-4422-7800","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771567458"],"issn":["22449981"],"issue":"529","pages":"220","publisher":"Aarhus Universitet","repno":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi, No. 529","series":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dc83f1bd-501c-4acf-9506-3bcf07772e67"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Marine områder 2021 : NOVANA","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-668789","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Smart heating systems are increasingly entering the domestic sphere. Such smart home technology (SHT) intends to provide comfort, control, and convenience in the home as well as energy efficiency and energy flexibility. However, the success of these promises depends on users’ ability to implement the SHT in everyday practices. In previous research, the importance of embodied competences acquired through previous experiences has gotten little attention. In this paper, we argue that broad scale implementation of SHT requires more knowledge on the interaction between previous experience in the formation of new competences and domestic heating practices. In this paper, we explore how users integrate new smart technologies into their everyday heating practices in different ways by focusing on embodied competences. Based on 24 qualitative household interviews with SHT users, conducted through two Danish case studies, we identified three ways of approaching and integrating SHT in heating practices. First, the reluctant appears hesitant when adopting SHT and loses interest quickly. Second, the compliant follows orders and does what is expected by the new setup. Third, the committed encompasses a playful approach and shows strong interest in SHT design. From this background, we find that embodied competences and previous experience are essential for how users adopt and integrate SHT in everyday life. For example, some users’ previous experience, here younger and technically interested individuals, may match well with the logics of SHT, and for some users, here older and less tech-interested individuals, previous experience may not match well with SHT.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madsen, Line Valdorff","Hansen, Anders Rhiger","Larsen, Simon Peter Aslak Kondrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-674208"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Madsen, Line Valdorff"],"keyword":["Competences","Everyday life","Households","Practice theory","Residential heating","Smart heating","Smart home technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"embodied competencies and smart home technology in energy use three ways users integrate smart heating systems in everyday practices","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12053-023-10138-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-674208","identifier":[{"id":"85163765202","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ddbd49f3-44c9-4b61-8f67-7949835949fe"],"keyword":["Competences","Everyday life","Households","Practice theory","Residential heating","Smart heating","Smart home technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7DE615B9FE5CF0C8A5191146ACC667D9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/538891528/s12053-023-10138-0.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12053-023-10138-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Town, Housing and Property","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Sustainable Cities and Everyday Practice Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Green Societies","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Center for Design, Innovation and Sustainable Transitions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Valdorff","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"4384fb97-d4b8-4c24-a82a-66fadb2d872a","name":"Madsen, Line Valdorff","orcid":"0000-0003-0861-0041","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Rhiger","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ce8ac34d-41b4-4871-8e74-09ca48990792","name":"Hansen, Anders Rhiger","orcid":"0000-0003-2771-062X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Peter Aslak Kondrup","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"84e32191-0b2f-499d-bd83-8947b95f917a","name":"Larsen, Simon Peter Aslak Kondrup","orcid":"0000-0002-9367-4500","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12053-023-10138-0","issn":["1570646X","15706478"],"issn_org":["1570646X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Energy Efficiency","paperid":"55","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Energy Efficiency","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163765202"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ddbd49f3-44c9-4b61-8f67-7949835949fe"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Embodied competencies and smart home technology in energy use: three ways users integrate smart heating systems in everyday practices","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-674208","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
