":["1755375X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"9-21","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135093427"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3d42dcc0-d76e-4dcd-8b59-815bf23d2d81","sdu-7eaacde8-fcc3-4d11-8994-1350240b629e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prevalence of allergic sensitization with vernal keratoconjunctivitis : A systematic review with meta-analyses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.23-041689","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To examine the prevalence and risk factors for hypothalamus–pituitary–adrenal axis suppression (HPA axis suppression) in infants receiving glucocorticoid (GC) eye drops after ocular surgery. Methods: This was a clinical observational cohort study. Children under the age of two receiving GC eye drops after cataract or glaucoma surgery between 1 January 2017 and 31 December 2021 were included at one centre. Medical history and results of the adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) stimulation tests were obtained through patient charts. Results: Forty-nine infants were included in the study. Ten out of 22 patients (45.5%) tested during treatment and two out of 27 patients (7.4%) tested after treatment cessation were diagnosed with HPA axis suppression. The duration of HPA axis suppression extended beyond 3 months in 8 out of 12 patients. Logistic regression showed that infants with HPA axis suppression had received a higher GC dose/body weight/day before the first ACTH test (p < 0.001). There was a 79% (95% CI:1.28;2.50) increase in the odds of having HPA axis suppression for a 0.01 mg GC increase/kg/day corresponding to an additional daily eye drop for an infant weighing 5 kg. There was an association between HPA axis suppression and number of days from surgery to test (p = 0.003), age at surgery (p = 0.035) and cumulated GC dose (p = 0.005). Three infants with HPA axis suppression had affected growth and one had Cushing-like features, but there were no cases of Addisonian crisis. Conclusion: Infants are at risk of having hypothalamus–pituitary–adrenal axis suppression if they receive a high daily glucocorticoid dose per weight by topical ocular administration. Infants receiving glucocorticoids after ocular surgery should be monitored clinically or by ACTH testing.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Schmidt, Diana C.","Kessel, Line","Bach-Holm, Daniella","Main, Katharina M.","Larsen, Dorte Ancher","Bangsgaard, Regitze"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-024513"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Schmidt, Diana C."],"keyword":["Adrenal insufficiency","Cataract","Children","Eye drops","Glaucoma","Glucocorticoid"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence and risk factors for hypothalamus pituitary adrenal axis suppression in infants receiving glucocorticoid eye drops after ocular surgery","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.15253","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-024513","identifier":[{"id":"36165330","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85138700056","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a1cf8841-4122-4238-bdc5-54fc9991e15e","ku-02279d31-3298-478d-ac2d-d88e4952977c"],"keyword":["adrenal insufficiency","cataract","children","eye drops","glaucoma","glucocorticoid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4CA0018D3D3CBE7C9EC3B5E833970EBD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/338063705/Acta_Ophthalmologica_2022_Schmidt_Prevalence_and_risk_factors_for_hypothalamus_pituitary_adrenal_axis_suppression_in.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.15253","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/404087273/Acta_Ophthalmologica_-_2022_-_Schmidt_-_Prevalence_and_risk_factors_for_hypothalamus_pituitary_adrenal_axis_suppression_in.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Diana C.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Diana C.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Daniella","key":"bachholmpau","last":"Bach-Holm","locid":"8b33b618-7a43-481a-a590-79dc9de2bc11","name":"Bach-Holm, Daniella","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Katharina M.","key":"mainpau","last":"Main","locid":"1770eebd-1659-4088-b44c-c9de22a4bb0b","name":"Main, Katharina M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte A.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5e903371-0f65-473a-ad66-1a909c98a776","name":"Larsen, Dorte Ancher","name_org":"Larsen, Dorte A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Regitze","key":"bangsgaardpau","last":"Bangsgaard","name":"Bangsgaard, Regitze","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36165330"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.15253","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"229-235","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138700056"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a1cf8841-4122-4238-bdc5-54fc9991e15e","ku-02279d31-3298-478d-ac2d-d88e4952977c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prevalence and risk factors for hypothalamus–pituitary–adrenal axis suppression in infants receiving glucocorticoid eye drops after ocular surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-024513","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Tilbage i 2005 gennemførte Trafikforskningsgruppen sammen med Odense Kommune et projekt, hvor vi testede den sikkerhedsmæssige effekt af kørelys på cykel. Vi testede den sikkerhedsmæssige effekt på en, på det tidspunkt, nyudviklet magnetlygte, som konstant blinkede. Testen var tilrettelagt som et lodtrækningsstudie, hvor 4.000 cyklister fra Odense deltog – 2.000 fik monteret lygten, og 2.000 var kontrolgruppe. Testen viste signifikante resultater, idet testgruppen havde 47 % færre flerpartsulykker med personskade end kontrolgruppen. Lygterne var udviklet og stillet til rådighed af firmaet Reelight. I 2017 henvendte Jochum Kirsebom fra Reelight (www.reelight.dk) sig til Trafikforskningsgruppen med henblik på at gentage forsøget fra 2005, men nu med en ny generation af kørelys, der lyser langt kraftigere end 2005-lygterne. Efter en periode, hvor projektet blev planlagt, og der blev skaffet finansiering til Trafikforskningsgruppens deltagelse i projektet, blev projektet igangsat i 2020. Lygterne blev også denne gang stillet til rådighed af Reelight, og igen blev projektet planlagt i tæt samarbejde med Odense Kommune, mens deltagelse denne gang ikke blev begrænset til indbyggere i Odense. Trafikforskningsgruppen vil gerne takke Troels Andersen og Tanja Bruntse Andersen, begge fra Odense Kommune, for hjælpen med planlægningen af projektet. Vi vil også gerne takke Reelight for at stille lygterne til rådighed, men også for at respektere den armslænge, der nødvendigvis har måttet være mellem producenten af lygten og dem, der evaluerer lygten. Endelig vil vi gerne takke A.P. Møller Fonden og Det Nissenske Familiefond for økonomisk støtte til projektet, uden hvilken projektet ikke ville have været muligt.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lahrmann, Harry","Christensen, Michelle Cederstrøm","Tallaksen, Anders Brogaard","Tønning, Charlotte","Larsen, Mette Kathrine","Madsen, Tanja Kidholm Osmann","Rasmussen, Line Røjkjær","Olesen, Anne Vingaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-064044"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Sikkerhed","Trafik","Ulykker"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"projekt cykelliv en undersøgelse af den sikkerhedsmæssige effekt af kørelys på cykler","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/515256123/Projekt_Cykelliv.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-064044","ids":["aau-30579b3a-3e03-4da7-8c0a-f7b5c2ed684f"],"keyword":["Cykellygter","Sikkerhed","Trafik","Ulykker"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3537B659CF4413586DC0BEA0CE7A477B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/515256123/Projekt_Cykelliv.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Civil and Environmental Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Traffic Research Group","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, CITS"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Harry","key":"lahrmannpau","last":"Lahrmann","locid":"7e1bc853-b677-467c-87ae-54b08116b7e4","name":"Lahrmann, Harry","orcid":"0000-0001-6339-4586","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michelle Cederstrøm","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"ee6729ff-07b6-45cb-b75e-b462106ba574","name":"Christensen, Michelle Cederstrøm","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Brogaard","key":"tallaksenpau","last":"Tallaksen","locid":"db5117b0-e079-499a-9e09-2738abc003f6","name":"Tallaksen, Anders Brogaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"tønningpau","last":"Tønning","locid":"f1d118d0-05c0-4c0e-b005-3038109659a4","name":"Tønning, Charlotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Kathrine","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"148d7797-8067-4e4a-8c4e-88c0abcc9934","name":"Larsen, Mette Kathrine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tanja Kidholm Osmann","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"e7bda905-fb0a-4545-9140-cad6d9b45c73","name":"Madsen, Tanja Kidholm Osmann","orcid":"0000-0002-0513-752X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Røjkjær","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"b172f930-ea77-4806-a3d9-edbbe7fb8df7","name":"Rasmussen, Line Røjkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-4533-8748","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Vingaard","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"2452b28f-e318-4c14-947b-42e0dd07d1a3","name":"Olesen, Anne Vingaard","orcid":"0000-0002-1503-8269","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["25973118"],"issue":"02","pages":"30","place":"Aalborg","publisher":"Institut for Byggeri, By og Miljø (BUILD), Aalborg Universitet","repno":"BUILD Rapport, No. 02","series":"BUILD Rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-30579b3a-3e03-4da7-8c0a-f7b5c2ed684f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Projekt Cykelliv : en undersøgelse af den sikkerhedsmæssige effekt af kørelys på cykler","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-064044","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The reported infection rates, and the burden of severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus-2 (SARS-CoV-2) in low- and middle-income countries, including sub-Saharan Africa, are relatively low compared to Europe and America, partly due to limited testing capabilities. Unlike many countries, in Tanzania, neither mass screening nor restrictive measures such as lockdowns have been implemented to date. The prevalence of SARS-CoV-2 infection in rural mainland Tanzania is largely unknown. METHODS: Between April and October 2021, we conducted a cross-sectional study to assess anti-SARS-CoV-2 seroprevalence among mother-child pairs ( n=634 children, n=518 mothers) in a rural setting of north-eastern Tanzania. FINDINGS: We found a very high prevalence of anti-SARS-CoV-2 antibody titres with seroprevalence rates ranging from 29% among mothers and 40% among children, with a dynamic peak in seropositivity incidence at the end of July/early in August being revealed. Significant differences in age, socioeconomic status and body composition were associated with seropositivity in mothers and children. No significant associations were observed between seropositivity and comorbidities, including anaemia, diabetes, malaria, and HIV. INTERPRETATIONS: The SARS-CoV-2 transmission in a rural region of Tanzania during 2021 was high, indicating a much higher infection rate in rural Tanzania compared to that reported in the UK and USA during the same period. Ongoing immune surveillance may be vital to monitoring the burden of viral infection in rural settings without access to molecular genotyping where a load of communicable diseases may mask COVID-19. Surveillance could be implemented in tandem with the intensification of vaccination strategies.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Msemo, Omari Abdul","Pérez-Alós, Laura","Minja, Daniel T R","Hansen, Cecilie Bo","Gesase, Samwel","Mtove, George","Mbwana, Joyce","Larsen, Victoria Marie Linderod","Bøgestad, Emilie Caroline Skuladottir","Grunnet, Louise Groth","Christensen, Dirk Lund","Bygbjerg, Ib Christian","Burgner, David","Schmiegelow, Christentze","Garred, Peter","Hjort, Line"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-516095"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Tanzania"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Institute for Medical Research Tanga","University of Melbourne"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high anti sars cov 000000000002 seroprevalence among unvaccinated mother child pairs from a rural setting of north eastern tanzania during the second wave of covid 000000000019","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijregi.2022.11.011","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-516095","identifier":[{"id":"85150900933","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36466214","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9709504","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-cd5f8ffc-5dc6-4e09-a416-1796a61ba680"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A765EE71E43C9C5A3F7F507C790B2B67"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/329206549/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijregi.2022.11.011","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"tz","key":"national institute for medical research tanga","loc":["Tanzania","Africa"],"name":"National Institute for Medical Research Tanga","used":1},{