{"abstract":"This study explored salivary fluoride levels following toothbrushing with 5000 and 1450 ppm fluoride toothpaste and determined the decline in salivary fluoride levels following the return from 5000 to 1450 ppm fluoride toothpaste. The study was a randomised, controlled double-blind parallel clinical trial (n = 24/group) measuring salivary fluoride five times during a 3-week trial phase involving 2×/day use of 5000 or 1450 ppm fluoride toothpaste, and five times during an ensuing 2-week wash-out phase where all participants used 1450 ppm toothpaste. Salivary fluoride was measured using a fluoride electrode and data were analysed using multilevel mixed-effects linear regression. Baseline salivary fluoride geometric means were 0.014 and 0.016 ppm for the 1450 and 5000 ppm groups, while the values at the end of the trial phase were 0.023 and 0.044 ppm, respectively. During the trial phase, except at baseline, differences between groups were statistically significant. The salivary fluoride levels for the 5000 ppm group remained statistically significantly higher than for the 1450 ppm group only at the first measurement in the wash-out phase (≈30 h after the last 5000 ppm brushing), indicating that higher salivary fluoride levels resulting from use of 5000 ppm are sustained only as long as the brushing habit continues.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Staun Larsen, Line","Nyvad, Bente","Bælum, Vibeke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-675132"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Staun Larsen, Line"],"keyword":["Dental caries","Fluorides","Humans","Saliva","Toothbrushing","Topical"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"salivary fluoride levels after daily brushing with 000000005000 ppm fluoride toothpaste a randomised controlled clinical trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/eos.12934","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-675132","identifier":[{"id":"37127433","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85157976963","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-700b985f-89d6-49d4-b7b1-c59bd47c1ce0"],"keyword":["dental caries","fluorides","humans","saliva","toothbrushing","topical"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A6F5A5AF40F636D32157F6270FC286B3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/407778863/European_J_Oral_Sciences_-_2023_-_Staun_Larsen_-_Salivary_fluoride_levels_after_daily_brushing_with_5000_ppm_fluoride.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/eos.12934","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L.","key":"staunlarsenpau","last":"Staun Larsen","locid":"35e2ae60-25db-4a15-893f-dc8906e2bccf","name":"Staun Larsen, Line","name_org":"Staun Larsen, L.","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-5884","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"B.","key":"nyvadpau","last":"Nyvad","locid":"f0fda280-eb7a-42d4-93f0-45f26e30fc45","name":"Nyvad, Bente","name_org":"Nyvad, B.","orcid":"0000-0002-9545-0447","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"V.","key":"baelumpau","last":"Baelum","locid":"fa28bbda-971e-4463-be61-3dcc358973b2","name":"Bælum, Vibeke","name_org":"Baelum, V.","orcid":"0000-0002-2195-8053","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37127433"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/eos.12934","issn":["09098836","13977555"],"issn_org":["09098836"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Journal of Oral Sciences","paperid":"e12934","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Oral Sciences","volume":"131"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85157976963"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-700b985f-89d6-49d4-b7b1-c59bd47c1ce0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Salivary fluoride levels after daily brushing with 5000 ppm fluoride toothpaste : A randomised, controlled clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-675132","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Mental illness is common among refugees displaced by conflict and war. While evidence points to the relatively good health in terms of longevity of migrants resettled in the destination country, less is known about the mortality of the most vulnerable migrants with a trauma-related diagnosis alone and those with an additional comorbid psychotic disorder. This study aimed to provide an overview of the number and mortality of foreign-born individuals diagnosed with Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder or Enduring Personality Change after a Catastrophic Event (PTSD/EPCACE), a psychotic disorder or both. METHODS: A nationwide register-based cohort study, including residents in Denmark, followed from 1 January 1995 to 31 December 2016. The exposure was PTSD/EPCACE and psychotic disorders as well as region of origin. Relative all-cause mortality was estimated using Cox proportional hazards regression models and calculated for migrants with one or both groups of disorders compared to those from the same region without the disorder. RESULTS: During the study period, 6,580,000 individuals (50.4% women) were included in the cohort. Of these 1,249,654 (50.5% women) died during follow-up. For men and women from the former Yugoslavia, the Middle East and Northern Africa, a PTSD/EPCACE diagnosis alone or with comorbid psychotic disorder was not associated with increased mortality after adjusting for region of origin. A psychotic disorder alone, however, was associated with an increased mortality rate. CONCLUSION: Despite the severity of many refugees' traumatic experiences, a diagnosis of a trauma-related psychiatric disorder did not appear to increase the mortality rates.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bager, Line","Agerbo, Esben","Skipper, Niels","Larsen, Janne Tidselbak","Laursen, Thomas Munk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-682170"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bager, Line"],"keyword":["Migrants","Mortality","Psychosis","Refugees"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"are migrants diagnosed with a trauma related disorder at risk of premature mortality a register based cohort study in denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmh.2023.100197","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-682170","identifier":[{"id":"37496744","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85164988190","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10365948","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-0b86000d-c4dd-4413-8255-a772d84aa310"],"keyword":["Migrants","Mortality","Psychosis","Refugees","Traumatic stress disorders"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E87CB7ECBFA432EF24377B604D0CFB73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmh.2023.100197","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/379635986/1-s2.0-S2666623523000478-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - National Centre for Register-based Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"bagerpau","last":"Bager","locid":"e7f7965c-9e17-4e02-9bca-3aa929f290db","name":"Bager, Line","orcid":"0000-0003-2184-2808","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben","key":"agerbopau","last":"Agerbo","locid":"5b08ed69-ad64-469f-a5b3-3407bf3c4b04","name":"Agerbo, Esben","orcid":"0000-0002-2849-524X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"skipperpau","last":"Skipper","locid":"36663df9-fd9e-485b-8bd1-13719a01832b","name":"Skipper, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5766-4420","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janne Tidselbak","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5e35426b-5cd7-438a-a11a-bfd44f63fbdf","name":"Larsen, Janne Tidselbak","orcid":"0000-0002-0385-1017","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Munk","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"366752b6-7172-46ab-9feb-f8f7eadce49f","name":"Laursen, Thomas Munk","orcid":"0000-0001-6934-1784","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37496744"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmh.2023.100197","issn":["26666235"],"journal":"Journal of Migration and Health","paperid":"100197","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Migration and Health","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164988190"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0b86000d-c4dd-4413-8255-a772d84aa310"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Are migrants diagnosed with a trauma-related disorder at risk of premature mortality? : A register-based cohort study in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-682170","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Staun Larsen, Line"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-700220"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Human","Retsodontologi"],"level":"pop","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bidmærkeanalyse","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-700220","ids":["au-e65602cd-cf4d-4de1-84b0-40bcc3c23bc7"],"keyword":["bidmærkeanalyse","human","retsodontologi"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0C4C351770FBF6EE067E4302792414E7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Ecology","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Forensic Medicine, Department of Forensic Medicine - Department of Forensic Medicine - Forensic Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"staunlarsenpau","last":"Staun Larsen","locid":"35e2ae60-25db-4a15-893f-dc8906e2bccf","name":"Staun Larsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-5884","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00399353","24458112"],"issn_org":["00399353"],"issue":"8","journal":"Tandlægebladet","pages":"678-685","publisher":"Tandlægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Tandlægebladet","volume":"127"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e65602cd-cf4d-4de1-84b0-40bcc3c23bc7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Bidmærkeanalyse","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-700220","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Collaborative processes framed through the exploration of reflective practice-based learning’s theoretical basis and pedagogical innovation theory are presented to exemplify how our interdisciplinary project team has approached the development of reflective practice-based learning in physical learning spaces. The project on which the poster is based seeks to manifest RPL physically to activate experience, thinking, and action in a student-initiated learning space. The project will develop RPL in the space “Reflekzonen”, which is a part of the UCN Innovation House. Based on divergent educational culture and practice, understood as the many disciplines that UCN educates for, and reflective practice-based learning as a potentially convergent meeting point in these educational cultures and practices, the poster is about how we in the interdisciplinary project team have methodically worked to move from divergent professional starting points for a more convergent understanding of educational development in physical spaces based on RPL and innovation. Specifically, the poster outlines the work processes that we in the interdisciplinary project team have gone through in developing RPL in the physical learning space. It is an emergent process, where we have used the social innovation theory; Theory U by Otto Scharmer as a process framework for collaboration. The poster aims to exemplify methodological approaches to interdisciplinary collaboration, where reflective practice-based learning and pedagogical innovation enrich the collaboration process. The poster seeks to convey how we have worked with RPL and innovation through processes that are based on elements from “Experience, thinking, and action” and Theory U.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Petersen, Inge-Kathrine","Stenderup, Mogens Larsen","Larsen-Zarechnova, Maria","Schou, Ditte Vejby","Madsen, Anja Emilie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-715115"],"event":{"end":"2023-11-22","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2023-11-20","title":"European Conference on Reflective Practice-based Learning 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Refleksiv praksislæring","academy educations","internships","learning educational science and teaching","professional bachelor programmes"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reflekzonen the collaborative development of rpl in innovative learning spaces","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://aauforlag.dk/produkt/proceedingsudgivelser/proceedings-for-the-european-conference-on-reflective-practice-based-learning-2023#info-tabs","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-715115","ids":["ucn-3ab52709-3fd6-4831-81aa-c13d73eef627"],"keyword":["Refleksiv praksislæring","academy educations","internships","learning, educational science and teaching","professional bachelor programmes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8912A8E6B4D4EACB7C4B8C19DE379921"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, UCN Enhed for Refleksiv Praksislæring"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Inge-Kathrine","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1e79fbfb-5c13-4c84-9912-2f7e1dd859ea","name":"Petersen, Inge-Kathrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens Larsen","key":"stenderuppau","last":"Stenderup","locid":"1eec9838-71ba-495b-82f0-cc1025509274","name":"Stenderup, Mogens Larsen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"larsenzarechnovapau","last":"Larsen-Zarechnova","locid":"4b586840-bb93-46b7-a766-a596812ebbdf","name":"Larsen-Zarechnova, Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-7298-8914","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte Vejby","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"2179122b-e98f-46bf-84ee-52325241f680","name":"Schou, Ditte Vejby","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja Emilie","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"85f082e3-1fe1-4e2a-b18e-d498795e8370","name":"Madsen, Anja Emilie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marianne","key":"georgsenpedh","last":"Georgsen","name":"Georgsen, Marianne","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Susanne","key":"daupedh","last":"Dau","name":"Dau, Susanne","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Line Helverskov","key":"hornpedh","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Line Helverskov","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788775730315"],"pages":"27-28","publisher":"Aalborg Universitetsforlag","status":"p","subtitle":"Aalborg, November 20th-22nd 2023","title":"Proceedings for the European Conference on Reflective Practice-based Learning 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-3ab52709-3fd6-4831-81aa-c13d73eef627"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Reflekzonen – the collaborative development of RPL in innovative learning spaces","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-715115","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Currently, SARS-CoV-2 have been detected in farmed mink in 13 different countries. Due to the high susceptibility and transmissibility among mink, great concerns of mink serving as a reservoir to generate novel variants with unknown virulence and antigenic properties arose. These concerns have consequently resulted in entire mink productions being culled and banned. This study investigates the post-vaccination antibody response in the Canadian farmed mink vaccinated with a commercial Index spike protein-based vaccine, approved for use in cats, and compares the antibody response to that observed post infection in Danish farmed mink. Blood samples were obtained from 50 mink at the Canadian Centre for Fur Animal Research (CCFAR), Dalhousie University (Truro, Canada). The sera were initially analyzed for antibodies by enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA), and selected sera was subsequently tested in a virus neutralization tests. The levels of neutralizing antibodies were evaluated for an ancestral D614G strain and a recent circulating SARS-CoV-2 variant of concern (Omicron BA.4). The results revealed that the vaccine induced a strong antibody response in mink by reaching antibody titer levels of up to 1:12800 in the ELISA. Moreover, high levels of neutralizing antibodies were obtained, and despite the great level of genetic differences between the ancestral and Omicron BA.4 strains, the vaccinated mink showed high levels of cross-reacting neutralizing antibodies. Interestingly, the antibody levels towards SARS-CoV-2 in the Canadian vaccinated mink were significantly higher than observed in recently SARS-CoV-2 infected Danish mink and equal to anamnestic responses following re-infection. In conclusion, the vaccine used in the Canadian farmed mink was able to induce a strong and broad-reacting antibody response in mink, which could limit the spread of SARS-CoV-2 in farmed mink and thereby reduce the risk of mink serving as a SARS-CoV-2 reservoir for human infections.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Line Gram","Larsen, Lars Erik","Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","Miar, Younes","Lassuniére, Ria","Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","Ryt-Hansen, Pia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739188"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dalhousie University"],"keyword":["Antibody response","Cross protection","Mink","Neogale vison","SARS CoV 2","Vaccination"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigation of the sars cov 000000000002 post vaccination antibody response in canadian farmed mink","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vaccine.2023.10.073","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-739188","identifier":[{"id":"37932134","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85175869721","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-60294411-f0bc-49fb-9fe8-21a2d0ee070c"],"keyword":["Antibody response","Cross-protection","Mink","Neogale vison","SARS-CoV-2","Vaccination"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-842A9E8E6CBA4F49D5B7F4D6A46CC621"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/390194228/1_s2.0_S0264410X23012884_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vaccine.2023.10.073","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"dalhousie university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Dalhousie University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line Gram","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"11549d14-c45d-43b0-923a-f08c66e86bce","name":"Hansen, Line Gram","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas Bruun","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Younes","key":"miarpau","last":"Miar","name":"Miar, Younes","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ria","key":"lassuniérepau","last":"Lassuniére","name":"Lassuniére, Ria","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Sværke","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37932134"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.vaccine.2023.10.073","issn":["0264410X","13552732"],"issn_org":["0264410X"],"issue":"49","journal":"Vaccine","pages":"7387-7394","status":"p","title":"Vaccine","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175869721"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-60294411-f0bc-49fb-9fe8-21a2d0ee070c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Investigation of the SARS-CoV-2 post-vaccination antibody response in Canadian farmed mink","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739188","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To measure anxiety levels in women aged ≥45 years undergoing diagnostic large loop excision of the transformation zone (LLETZ) at the first colposcopy visit. Design: Longitudinal study. Setting: Three colposcopy clinics in the Central Denmark Region. Population: Women aged ≥45 years undergoing diagnostic LLETZ. Methods: Women completed the State–Trait Anxiety Inventory (STAI) and Short Form 12 (mental and physical health) questionnaires before, immediately after, and at 1 and 6 months after LLETZ. Main outcome measures: STAI state anxiety median scores were calculated and stratified by health status, by letter with information about screening result and by LLETZ results. Results: Of 109 eligible women, 11 were excluded, leaving 98 women for the final analyses. Response rates ranged from 84.7% to 100%. Overall, state anxiety levels were low; however, a decrease was observed from before to immediately after the LLETZ (33.4 vs 29.3, p< 0.001). The anxiety levels remained stable up to 6 months after LLETZ. Women with poor mental health were more likely to have higher anxi-ety levels compared with women with good mental health (before LLETZ, RR 3.77, 95% CI 2.12–6.70; 1 month after LLETZ, RR 3.37, 95% CI 1.59–7.15; 6 months after LLETZ, RR 1.93, 95%CI 1.06–3.51). Conclusions: Overall, colposcopy and diagnostic LLETZ in women aged ≥45 years were not associated with high levels of anxiety. Anxiety levels were highest before col-poscopy, and the women seemed to experience immediate relief afterwards. Women with poor mental health had the highest anxiety levels throughout the study, which might call for special attention.K EY WOR DSanxiety, cervical cancer screening, colposcopy, LLETZ, postmenopausal women, STAI","author_count":6,"contributors":["Gustafson, Line Winther","Larsen, Mette Bach","Hammer, Anne","Petersen, Lone Kjeld","Andersen, Berit","Bor, Isil Pinar"],"cuid":["S02-088.63-018959"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Gustafson, Line Winther"],"keyword":["Anxiety","Anxiety etiology","Cervical cancer screening","Colposcopy","Colposcopy methods","Female","Humans","LLETZ","Longitudinal Studies","Postmenopausal women","Pregnancy","STAI","Uterine Cervical Dysplasia diagnosis","Uterine Cervical Neoplasms diagnosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"levels of anxiety in women aged 000000000045 years undergoing diagnostic large loop excision of the transformation zone a longitudinal study","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1471-0528.17299","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["First, the authors want to acknowledge the participating women. Second, we give special thanks to secretary Marianne R. Pedersen at the Department of Public Health Programmes, Regional Hospital Randers, Denmark, for her valuable help with the questionnaires. Grants from the Health Research Foundation of Central Denmark Region (A3234), Dagmar Marshalls Foundation, Fabricant Einar Willumsens Mindelegat, Else and Mogens Wedell‐Wedellsborgs Foundation and the AP Moller Foundation (18‐L‐0124) funded this project. In addition LWG recieved a travel grant from Danish Cancer Society. None of the funders had an influence on the scientific process, including the decision to submit the article for publication."],"id":"S02-088.63-018959","identifier":[{"id":"85139755296","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10091992","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36161454","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-56922fd5-306a-4b92-9bf6-4de9069e45e5","sdu-9ccb156c-5a99-4b60-9f62-1f67553284ac"],"keyword":["Anxiety/etiology","Colposcopy/methods","Female","Humans","LLETZ","Longitudinal Studies","Pregnancy","STAI","Uterine Cervical Dysplasia/diagnosis","Uterine Cervical Neoplasms/diagnosis","anxiety","anxiety, cervical cancer screening, colposcopy, LLETZ, postmenopausal women, STAI","cervical cancer screening","colposcopy","postmenopausal women"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6DA3881856D1A3BF94979F6D5024C947"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/216166374/BJOG_2022_Gustafson_Levels_of_anxiety_in_women_aged_45_years_undergoing_diagnostic_large_loop_excision_of_the.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1471-0528.17299","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/409575457/BJOG_-_2022_-_Gustafson_-_Levels_of_anxiety_in_women_aged_45_years_undergoing_diagnostic_large_loop_excision_of_the.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Public Health Programs, Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Gynaecology and Obstetrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Winther","key":"gustafsonpau","last":"Gustafson","locid":"b35cf260-4016-4f8f-887c-c15a1110e496","name":"Gustafson, Line Winther","orcid":"0000-0003-4149-4708","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Bach","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"40b0a541-1654-4488-a108-499a4097e34a","name":"Larsen, Mette Bach","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne","key":"hammerpau","last":"Hammer","locid":"2ca0e215-d566-4dd7-9095-6e30d8506b18","name":"Hammer, Anne","orcid":"0000-0002-4616-9827","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone Kjeld","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"000a791a-6685-4ef0-b286-f342dd3ad555","name":"Petersen, Lone Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0002-1424-6170","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Berit","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"4f64dc11-e5ca-4037-bbad-8ca533d841e4","name":"Andersen, Berit","orcid":"0000-0003-4074-6504","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Isil Pinar","key":"borpau","last":"Bor","locid":"dffefbfe-7c80-4f4b-8491-ab78fc11eb22","name":"Bor, Isil Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-5841-5418","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36161454"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1471-0528.17299","issn":["01407686","14700328"],"issn_org":["14700328"],"issue":"2","journal":"BJOG","pages":"192-200","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"BJOG","title_org":"BJOG: An International Journal of Obstetrics and Gynaecology","volume":"130"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139755296"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-56922fd5-306a-4b92-9bf6-4de9069e45e5","sdu-9ccb156c-5a99-4b60-9f62-1f67553284ac"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Levels of anxiety in women aged ≥ 45 years undergoing diagnostic large loop excision of the transformation zone : A longitudinal study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.63-018959","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Mental health of trauma-affected refugees is an understudied area, resulting in inadequate and poorer treatment outcomes. To address this, more high-quality treatment studies that include predictive analyses, long-term evaluations, cultural adaptations, and take account for comorbidities, are needed. Moreover, given the complex intertwining of refugees' health with post-migration stressors and other social factors, it is crucial to examine the social determinants of refugee mental health. The Danish Trauma Database for Refugees (DTD) is a multicenter research database uniting six national centers that provide outpatient treatment for trauma-affected refugees. Through the database, we collect clinical and sociodemographic data from approximately 1200 refugees annually and will merge the database with Danish population register data. The purpose of the DTD is two-fold; clinical and research. The DTD offers data-driven guidance for routine clinical treatment planning of the individual patient, as well as exceptional research opportunities for testing treatment interventions in clinical settings, with larger sample sizes, and more representative heterogeneity of the population. Complex analyses of risk and protective factors, barriers, access to treatment, and societal and transgenerational aspects of trauma are possible with the DTD. This conceptual paper introduces the DTD, the historical background, the development process and implementation strategy, and the associated challenges with developing and running a multicenter database. Most importantly, it highlights the clinical and research potential of the DTD for advancing the understanding and treatment of trauma-affected refugees.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Thøgersen, Marie Høgh","Bager, Line","Bangsgaard, Sofie Grimshave","Palic, Sabina","Auning-Hansen, Mikkel","Møller, Stine Bjerrum","Larsen, Kirstine Bruun","Tækker, Louise","Jensen, Bo Søndergaard","Bothe, Søren","Nordin, Linda"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-686054"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Thøgersen, Marie Høgh"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Ambulatory Care","DTD","Database","Denmark epidemiology","Humans","Mental health","Migration","PTSD","Psychotherapy","Refugees","Trauma","Treatment","multicenter research"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-DIG"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["The Rehabilitation Center for Trauma Survivors (RCT)"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-DIG","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the danish trauma database for refugees dtd a multicenter database collaboration overcoming the challenges and enhancing mental health treatment and research for refugees","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph20166611","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-686054","identifier":[{"id":"37623194","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85168694928","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10454926","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-d0cf35ba-0985-47c8-bd0d-35aa1eef47f9","sdu-791add5d-f312-42f0-9e82-9bdf337f030d"],"keyword":["Ambulatory Care","DTD","Denmark/epidemiology","Humans","Mental Health","PTSD","Psychotherapy","database","migration","multicenter research","refugees","trauma","treatment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-88EE0A1968DDF65B88B3F9F89A9A8DFE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph20166611","version":"Published Version"