{"abstract":"https://iofos2023.com/assets/files/IOFOS_abstracts.pdf","author_count":4,"contributors":["Staun Larsen, Line","Johansen, Jane Vestergaard","Duncker, Hannah Sophie Antonia","Bindslev, Dorthe Arenholt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-709534"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-08","place":"Dubrovnik, hr","start":"2023-09-06","title":"Trienial I.O.F.O.S. Congres of Forensic Odonto-Stomatology","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Staun Larsen, Line"],"keyword":["Identifikation","Retsodontologi","fluorescens"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"composite restorations visualized by uv light","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-709534","ids":["au-e02d7dbf-d775-4ff8-8168-3c148f55f74a"],"keyword":["UV-lyskilde","fluorescens","identifikation","kompositfyldninger","retsodontologi"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-45CC8B449502900667E7CB8E16DCDD7B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Forensic Medicine, Department of Forensic Medicine - Department of Forensic Medicine - Forensic Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"staunlarsenpau","last":"Staun Larsen","locid":"35e2ae60-25db-4a15-893f-dc8906e2bccf","name":"Staun Larsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-5884","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane Vestergaard","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Jane Vestergaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hannah Sophie Antonia","key":"dunckerpau","last":"Duncker","name":"Duncker, Hannah Sophie Antonia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorthe Arenholt","key":"bindslevpau","last":"Bindslev","locid":"a95ac976-ed75-421f-a895-8fc5ec9c62c0","name":"Bindslev, Dorthe Arenholt","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e02d7dbf-d775-4ff8-8168-3c148f55f74a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Composite restorations visualized by UV light","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-709534","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Delayed diagnosis of common variable immunodeficiency (CVID) remains a serious problem. We investigated whether some diseases diagnosed during out-patient visits or admission to hospitals could act as indicator conditions for CVID diagnosis. Methods: In this nested case–control study, we identified 128 cases diagnosed with CVID in Denmark (1999–2013) and 640 age-, gender-, and region-matched controls. We obtained data on diseases diagnosed at hospitals in the five years before CVID diagnosis from The National Hospital Registry. We grouped hospital diagnoses in 33 major disease categories and 210 subcategories. We used conditional logistic regression to calculate the odds ratios (OR) and 95% confidence intervals (CI) to estimate associations between disease exposure and subsequent CVID. Results: During the five years preceding a CVID diagnosis, cases had four times as many hospital contacts as the controls (p < 0.001). A diagnosis in 18 major disease categories showed a significant OR for subsequent diagnosis of CVID. The most substantial association with a subsequent CVID diagnosis was a diagnosis of lower respiratory tract infections (OR: 29.9; 95% CI: 14.2–63.2) and lung diseases (35.1; 15.0–82.5). We observed a similar association when we removed the last year before diagnosis from analysis and overall, in the years < 1, ≥ 1–3, and ≥ 3–5 before diagnosis, although the absolute number of exposures was small. Twenty-eight specific diseases displayed an at least 3-fold risk of subsequent CVID diagnosis. Conclusion: Targeted screening for antibody deficiency in patients diagnosed with specific diseases associated with CVID may lead to earlier CVID diagnosis and treatment and thereby potentially reduced morbidity and mortality.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Dahl, Christina","Petersen, Inge","Ilkjær, Frederik V.","Westh, Lena","Katzenstein, Terese L.","Hansen, Ann Brit E.","Nielsen, Thyge L.","Larsen, Carsten Schade","Johansen, Isik S.","Rasmussen, Line D."],"cuid":["S03-100.00-742048"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Dahl, Christina"],"keyword":["CVID","Case Control Studies","Common Variable Immunodeficiency diagnosis","Diagnostic delay","Early Diagnosis","Humans","Indicators","Odds Ratio","PID","Registries","Secondary health care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"missed opportunities to diagnose common variable immunodeficiency a population based case control study identifying indicator diseases for common variable immunodeficiency","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10875-023-01590-9","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors of this study greatly appreciate the work of all the physicians who have provided data on the CVID patients, as well as the patients included in this study and the Danish adult CVID cohort. This study could not have been completed without the help of the Danish adult CVID cohort."],"id":"S03-100.00-742048","identifier":[{"id":"85172990220","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37770805","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10661759","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-c7e4d1ef-692f-46e7-9136-6af41a11b99b","ku-21cfcb0c-0673-48af-9be6-2ba47e8dfd45","sdu-65ad27e8-e3e7-4073-8fda-2bfa87679587"],"keyword":["CVID","Case-Control Studies","Common Variable Immunodeficiency/diagnosis","Early Diagnosis","Humans","Odds Ratio","PID","Registries","diagnostic delay","indicators","secondary health care"],"lang":"Eng