L.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 4","first":"Ann-Brit E.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"29b6e1f5-8374-4247-a7bd-76de887cc30d","name":"Hansen, Ann-Brit Eg","name_org":"Hansen, Ann-Brit E.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Thyge L.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Thyge L.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten S.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"2435cb82-03bd-498b-909d-1ef0e99443fe","name":"Larsen, Carsten Schade","name_org":"Larsen, Carsten S.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Isik S.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"d7a439ff-f0ad-43c9-80d8-a269647e1886","name":"Johansen, Isik Somuncu","name_org":"Johansen, Isik S.","orcid":"0000-0002-2189-9823","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line D.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"a0349aeb-56d9-4984-86b0-4829aee2a04b","name":"Rasmussen, Line Dahlerup","name_org":"Rasmussen, Line D.","orcid":"0000-0003-0853-0893","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37770805"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10875-023-01590-9","issn":["02719142","15732592"],"issn_org":["02719142"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of Clinical Immunology","pages":"2104-2114","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Immunology","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85172990220"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c7e4d1ef-692f-46e7-9136-6af41a11b99b","ku-21cfcb0c-0673-48af-9be6-2ba47e8dfd45","sdu-65ad27e8-e3e7-4073-8fda-2bfa87679587"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Missed Opportunities to Diagnose Common Variable Immunodeficiency : a Population-Based Case–Control Study Identifying Indicator Diseases for Common Variable Immunodeficiency","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-742048","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In patients with intracerebral hemorrhage (ICH) and prevalent atrial fibrillation (AF), the optimal stroke prevention strategy is unclear. We sought to estimate the risk of cerebrovascular events among ICH survivors with AF. METHODS: We used the Danish Stroke Registry to identify patients with incident ICH and prevalent AF between 2003 and 2018. Key inclusion/exclusion criteria of the PRESTIGE-AF (Prevention of Stroke in Intracerebral hemorrhage Survivors With Atrial Fibrillation) trial were applied. Cumulative incidence of recurrent ICH, cerebrovascular ischemic event, and all-cause death were investigated after one year. RESULTS: A total of 1885 patients (median age 80.0 years; 47.6% females) were included in the study. We observed 191 cerebrovascular events and 650 all-cause deaths, and more cerebrovascular ischemic events (N=63) than recurrent ICH events (N=40). Risks of recurrent ICH, cerebrovascular ischemic event, and all-cause death were 1.5%, 3.2%, and 30.3%, respectively, among patients not exposed to OAC during follow-up. The cumulative incidences were 2.8% for recurrent ICH, 3.2% for cerebrovascular ischemic events, and 22.0% for all-cause death among patients initiating/resuming OAC during follow-up. CONCLUSIONS: We observed a high risk of cerebrovascular ischemic events and a very high risk of all-cause death at one year after the incident ICH. The results of ongoing clinical trials are warranted to determine optimal stroke prevention treatment among ICH survivors with concomitant AF.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Peter Brønnum","Melgaard, Line","Overvad, Thure Filskov","Jensen, Martin","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Lip, Gregory Y H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-059565"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["PRESTIGE-AF Consortium"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","University of Liverpool"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Anticoagulants","Anticoagulants therapeutic use","Atrial Fibrillation complications","Atrial fibrillation","Cerebral Hemorrhage complications","Cohort Studies","Epidemiology","Female","Hemorrhagic stroke","Humans","Ischemic stroke","Male","Risk Factors","Stroke etiology","Survivors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of cerebrovascular events in intracerebral hemorrhage survivors with atrial fibrillation a nationwide cohort study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/STROKEAHA.121.038331","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-059565","identifier":[{"id":"85133307904","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35414198","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-2093c699-965c-4ecc-9ac9-5930b1d33e87"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Anticoagulants/therapeutic use","Atrial Fibrillation/complications","Cerebral Hemorrhage/complications","Cohort Studies","Female","Humans","Male","Risk Factors","Stroke/etiology","Survivors","anticoagulants","atrial fibrillation","epidemiology","hemorrhagic stroke","ischemic stroke"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9EFFFC95F1FCEF980C2CA5197597535B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/482615985/STROKEAHA.121.038331.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/STROKEAHA.121.038331","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg