{"abstract":"Purpose: To investigate the socio-economic status of families affected by childhood cataract and to assess how the socio-economic status is affected by cataract diagnosis. Materials and methods: Children born between 2000 and 2017, seen between the age 0 and 10 years in the same period at Rigshospitalet or Aarhus University Hospital for cataract (N = 485), were included and compared to a matched children group without cataract (N = 4358). Socio-economic status was evaluated by the parents’ income, employment, education, marital status and family structure. Results: Parents of children with cataract were more likely to have a low yearly income (OR = 1.60, 95% CI (1.12–2.27)), be out of work (OR = 1.74, 95% CI (1.34–2.26)) and have basic education as the highest attained education (OR = 1.64, 95% CI (1.27–2.13)) prior to diagnosis. This social gradient was not affected by the diagnosis. In addition, a higher number of children with cataract lived in multi-family residencies (13.8% versus 8% in group of children without cataract) and they had a greater number of siblings (6.2% had ≥4 siblings versus 2.1% in group of children without cataract). Conclusion: Families affected by childhood cataract have a lower socio-economic status and educational background even before cataract is diagnosed but the diagnosis does not aggravate the differences between these families and the background population. The lower socio-economic status and parental educational background should be taken into consideration in the management of these families.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Al-Bakri, Moug","Bach-Holm, Daniella","Larsen, Dorte Ancher","Siersma, Volkert","Kessel, Line"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-018726"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Al-Bakri, Moug"],"keyword":["Childhood cataract","Socio economic status","congenital cataract"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socio economic status in families affected by childhood cataract","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85101977863","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-018726","identifier":[{"id":"85101977863","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33666374","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-52db12c6-ec46-4209-b2bd-074da8c9dd0f","ku-1ebad699-1809-4aec-921d-082921080dff"],"keyword":["childhood cataract","congenital cataract","socio-economic status"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-69FEC66A102C303AC63E67A199A1C19A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Moug","key":"albakripau","last":"Al-Bakri","locid":"b088ca79-9c7d-45b1-8c4a-1c9289aedf65","name":"Al-Bakri, Moug","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Daniella","key":"bachholmpau","last":"Bach-Holm","locid":"8b33b618-7a43-481a-a590-79dc9de2bc11","name":"Bach-Holm, Daniella","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Ancher","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5e903371-0f65-473a-ad66-1a909c98a776","name":"Larsen, Dorte Ancher","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Volkert","key":"siersmapau","last":"Siersma","locid":"70f90acb-f0b0-4ffc-b7f2-a86ca85ac96d","name":"Siersma, Volkert","orcid":"0000-0003-1941-2681","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33666374"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.14768","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"183-188","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"100"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101977863"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-52db12c6-ec46-4209-b2bd-074da8c9dd0f","ku-1ebad699-1809-4aec-921d-082921080dff"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Socio-economic status in families affected by childhood cataract","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-018726","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Staun Larsen, Line","Nyvad, Bente","Bælum, Vibeke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-239257"],"event":{"end":"2022-07-02","place":"Cagliari, it","start":"2022-06-29","title":"ORCA: 69th Congress of the European Organization for Caries Research","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fluoride","ORCA","Saliva"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of 000000000005 000000000000 ppm fluoride toothpaste on salivary fluoride a randomized controlled clinical trial abstract","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-239257","ids":["au-c0a45326-458d-4c7e-b1a3-ce1e5ae175b9"],"keyword":["Caries research","High-dossage fluoride toothpaste","Non-operative caries control","ORCA","fluoride","saliva"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-025C3AF329FCB64AE747D20912E7E672"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Ecology and Caries Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"staunlarsenpau","last":"Staun Larsen","locid":"35e2ae60-25db-4a15-893f-dc8906e2bccf","name":"Staun Larsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-5884","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bente","key":"nyvadpau","last":"Nyvad","locid":"f0fda280-eb7a-42d4-93f0-45f26e30fc45","name":"Nyvad, Bente","orcid":"0000-0002-9545-0447","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vibeke","key":"bælumpau","last":"Bælum","locid":"fa28bbda-971e-4463-be61-3dcc358973b2","name":"Bælum, Vibeke","orcid":"0000-0002-2195-8053","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c0a45326-458d-4c7e-b1a3-ce1e5ae175b9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effect of 5,000 ppm fluoride toothpaste on salivary fluoride: a randomized, controlled clinical trial : (abstract)","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-239257","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Ectopic liver fat deposition, resulting from impaired subcutaneous adipose tissue expandability, may represent an age-dependent key feature linking low birth weight (LBW) with increased risk of type 2 diabetes (T2D). We examined whether presumably healthy early middle-aged, non-obese LBW subjects exhibit increased liver fat content, whether increased liver fat in LBW is associated with the severity of dysmetabolic traits and finally whether such associations may be confounded by genetic factors. Methods: Using 1H magnetic resonance spectroscopy, we measured hepatic fat content in 26 early middle-aged, non-obese LBW and 22 BMI-matched normal birth weight (NBW) males. Endogenous glucose production was measured by stable isotopes, and a range of plasma adipokine and gut hormone analytes were measured by multiplex ELISA. Genetic risk scores were calculated from genome-wide association study (GWAS) data for birth weight, height, T2D, plasma cholesterol and risk genotypes for non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD). Results: The LBW subjects had significantly increased hepatic fat content compared with NBW controls (P= 0.014), and 20% of LBW vs no controls had overt NAFLD. LBW subjects with NAFLD displayed widespread metabolic changes compared with NBW and LBW individuals without NAFLD, including hepatic insulin resistance, plasma adipokine and gut hormone perturbations as well as dyslipidemia. As an exception, plasma adiponectin levels were lower in LBW subjects both with and without NAFLD as compared to NBW controls. Genetic risk for selected differential traits did not differ between groups. Conclusion: Increased liver fat content including overt NAFLD may be on the critical path linking LBW with increased risk of developing T2D in a non-genetic manner.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Brøns, Charlotte","Thuesen, Anne Cathrine B.","Elingaard-Larsen, Line Ohrt","Justesen, Louise","Jensen, Rasmus Tanderup","Henriksen, Nicolai S.","Juel, Helene Bæk","Størling, Joachim","Ried-Larsen, Mathias","Sparks, Lauren M.","van Hall, Gerrit","Danielsen, Else Rubæk","Hansen, Torben","Vaag, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-415011"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["Advent Health","All Global Affiliations"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increased liver fat associates with severe metabolic perturbations in low birth weight men","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-415011","identifier":[{"id":"000802046600009","type":"wos"},{"id":"85128001820","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35212643","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2429f1f5-e06c-4ac1-aeab-1295111f872a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49BAA5405196A4ED187644D333B0355F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Hanse