 University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Neonatal complications and neurophysiological development in twins - a long-term follow-up study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.82-001809","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Infrequent deviants in a rapid sequence of sounds elicit a negative cortical potential over the frontocentral midline (mismatch negativity, MMN) followed by a positive deflection (P3a). Both cortical potentials are consistently attenuated in patients with schizophrenia (SZ), and, to a lesser degree, in patients with bipolar disorder (BP). Objective: Since it is unclear when MMN and P3a deficits arise relative to the emergence of symptoms, we examined whether MMN and P3a alterations are already detectable in children with familial high risk. Methods: Using 128-channel electroencephalography, we recorded auditory MMN and P3a evoked by a deviation in sound duration, frequency, or both in 51 children with familial high-risk for SZ (FHR-SZ), 41 children with familial high-risk for BP (FHR-BP), and 39 population-based children (PBC) at a mean age of 12.10. Results: MMN amplitude evoked by a duration deviant was larger in children with FHR-BP compared to PBC and FHR-SZ. P3a amplitude in response to a duration ∗ frequency deviant was larger in children with FHR-BP compared to children with FHR-SZ, but not compared to PBC. MMN- and P3a-peak latency did not differ between groups. Conclusions: At an age of around 12 years, children with FHR-BP display enhanced neural sensitivity to change detection of duration deviants, while FHR-SZ showed a normal response pattern. Longitudinal recordings in high-risk children during adolescence are required to elucidate the temporal trajectories of MMN and P3a responses and how they relate to the emergence of first clinical symptoms in SZ and BP.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ver Loren van Themaat, Anna Hester","Oranje, Bob","Larsen, Kit Melissa","Tomasevic, Leo","Korsgaard Johnsen, Line","Thorup, Anne Amalie Elgaard","Plessen, Kerstin Jessica","Siebner, Hartwig Roman","Nordentoft, Merete"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-423477"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lausanne"],"keyword":["Electroencephalography","Mismatch negativity","Neurodevelopment","Offspring"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mismatch negativity and p000000000003a amplitude in children with familial high risk of schizophrenia or bipolar disorder a danish register based eeg study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-423477","identifier":[{"id":"35797883","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85134611314","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-32775db7-9a99-43cb-92ea-de897980548e"],"keyword":["Electroencephalography","Mismatch negativity","Neurodevelopment","Offspring"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EF8C03FF063A630FA2B960E5DFF339EB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Child and Adolescent Mental Health Centre","Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"university of lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lausanne","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Hester","key":"verlorenvanthemaatpau","last":"Ver Loren van Themaat","name":"Ver Loren van Themaat, Anna Hester","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bob","key":"oranjepau","last":"Oranje","name":"Oranje, Bob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kit Melissa","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Kit Melissa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Leo","key":"tomasevicpau","last":"Tomasevic","name":"Tomasevic, Leo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Line","key":"korsgaardjohnsenpau","last":"Korsgaard Johnsen","locid":"b9ee691d-486a-49ce-b35a-766d5dc2daba","name":"Korsgaard Johnsen, Line","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne Amalie","key":"elgaardthoruppau","last":"Elgaard Thorup","locid":"c70ccbcc-b880-4352-919d-08595d91ed2b","name":"Thorup, Anne Amalie Elgaard","name_org":"Elgaard Thorup, Anne Amalie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Kerstin Jessica","key":"plessenpau","last":"Plessen","name":"Plessen, Kerstin Jessica","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hartwig Roman","key":"siebnerpau","last":"Siebner","locid":"d9ed8669-a16b-429a-86ed-353ef481bb72","name":"Siebner, Hartwig Roman","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Merete","key":"nordentoftpau","last":"Nordentoft","locid":"6d0fe19c-7c81-463b-8bc8-822d71584b69","name":"Nordentoft, Merete","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35797883"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.schres.2022.06.035","issn":["09209964","15732509"],"issn_org":["09209964"],"journal":"Schizophrenia Research","pages":"187-194","status":"p","title":"Schizophrenia Research","volume":"246"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134611314"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-32775db7-9a99-43cb-92ea-de897980548e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mismatch negativity and P3a amplitude in children with familial high risk of schizophrenia or bipolar disorder – A Danish register-based EEG study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-423477","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"On the online forum Virtuous Paedophiles, experiences of being sexually attracted to children are discussed based on the belief that ‘adult-child sex’ is wrong. Having explored the forum’s culture of support, advice, and negotiations, we find that the stigmatised paedophile character limits both the understanding of being a paedophile and the ability to remain virtuous. Additionally, ideas about the paedophile character allow the formation of a counter discourse: the virtuous paedophile character. We argue that the justifications used in the forum differ from those in pro-contact communities and that the forum can help paedophiles be offense-free.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Marie Haarmark","Aaskov, Line","Larsen, Jørgen Elm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-485625"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Faculty of Social Sciences","Online community","Stigma"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"when virtuous paedophiles meet online a sociological study of a paedophile community","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-485625","identifier":[{"id":"85097789410","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9a39e0dd-7208-4472-b92e-54ab17885685"],"keyword":["Faculty of Social Sciences","non-offending","online community","paedophile","stigma","virtuous"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ACA9351FAE7D42EFC944FA099F851A10"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Sociology, Department of Sociology, Study Council"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie H","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b000adc6-342b-4b51-ab4c-4b0626e29e31","name":"Nielsen, Marie Haarmark","name_org":"Nielsen, Marie H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"aaskovpau","last":"Aaskov","locid":"a9c1b20a-a9e8-4680-95e9-13bf95624016","name":"Aaskov, Line","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen E","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"4e3ad6db-0b82-4b5e-8631-79f10207977d","name":"Larsen, Jørgen Elm","name_org":"Larsen, Jørgen E","orcid":"0000-0002-8604-7509","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1363460720979306","issn":["13634607","14617382"],"issn_org":["13634607"],"issue":"5-6","journal":"Sexualities","pages":"598-614","status":"p","title":"Sexualities","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097789410"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9a39e0dd-7208-4472-b92e-54ab17885685"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"When virtuous paedophiles meet online : A sociological study of a paedophile community","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-485625","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"SARS-CoV-2 vaccines are crucial in controlling COVID-19, but knowledge of which factors determine waning immunity is limited. We examined antibody levels and T-cell gamma-interferon release after two doses of BNT162b2 vaccine or a combination of ChAdOx1-nCoV19 and BNT162b2 vaccines for up to 230 days after the first dose. Generalized mixed models with and without natural cubic splines were used to determine immunity over time. Antibody responses were influenced by natural infection, sex, and age. IgA only became significant in naturally infected. A one-year IgG projection suggested an initial two-phase response in those given the second dose delayed (ChAdOx1/BNT162b2) followed by a more rapid decrease of antibody levels. T-cell responses correlated significantly with IgG antibody responses. Our results indicate that IgG levels will drop at different rates depending on prior infection, age, sex, T-cell response, and the interval between vaccine injections. Only natural infection mounted a significant and lasting IgA response.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Pérez-Alós, Laura","Armenteros, Jose Juan Almagro","Madsen, Johannes Roth","Hansen, Cecilie Bo","Jarlhelt, Ida","Hamm, Sebastian Rask","Heftdal, Line Dam","Pries-Heje, Mia","Møller, Dina Leth","Fogh, Kamille","Hasselbalch, Rasmus Bo","Rosbjerg, Anne","Brunak, Søren","Sørensen, Erik","Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","Bayarri-Olmos, Rafael","Hilsted, Linda Maria","Iversen, Kasper","Bundgaard, Henning","Nielsen, Susanne Dam","Garred, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-496887"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Antibodies Viral","BNT162 Vaccine","COVID 19 Vaccines","COVID 19 prevention control","Humans","SARS CoV 2","Vaccination","Vaccines Inactivated","Viral Vaccines"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling of waning immunity after sars cov 000000000002 vaccination and influencing factors","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29225-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-496887","identifier":[{"id":"35347129","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000774213100017","type":"wos"},{"id":"85127250506","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8960902","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-ad2b6932-a7d4-40c0-a401-a5edadb563fa"],"keyword":["Antibodies, Viral","BNT162 Vaccine","COVID-19 Vaccines","COVID-19/prevention & control","Humans","SARS-CoV-2","Vaccination","Vaccines, Inactivated","Viral Vaccines"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B13126F4EA468893D4CED4E5F7C974BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/303803985/s41467_022_29225_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29225-4","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Laura","key":"pérezalóspau","last":"Pérez-Alós","locid":"d2298b3a-c2a2-4ee7-9acf-81c70030dc5a","name":"Pérez-Alós, Laura","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jose Juan Almagro","key":"armenterospau","last":"Armenteros","locid":"2ef303c4-c8c5-4339-8254-9ea0f5545752","name":"Armenteros, Jose Juan Almagro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Johannes Roth","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Johannes Roth","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cecilie Bo","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"47a06331-2df1-4a5f-81b3-e582da0e70e6","name":"Hansen, Cecilie Bo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ida","key":"jarlheltpau","last":"Jarlhelt","name":"Jarlhelt, Ida","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sebastian Rask","key":"hammpau","last":"Hamm","locid":"fda23bba-aa98-4ad7-979d-f28d0045abde","name":"Hamm, Sebastian Rask","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Line Dam","key":"heftdalpau","last":"Heftdal","name":"Heftdal, Line Dam","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mia Marie","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","locid":"f6ffd512-b0c2-4a0b-be43-5fc299240ae2","name":"Pries-Heje, Mia","name_org":"Pries-Heje, Mia Marie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dina Leth","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"8d5cc577-14db-4efa-9db9-72b979611644","name":"Møller, Dina Leth","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kamille","key":"foghpau","last":"Fogh","name":"Fogh, Kamille","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus Bo","key":"hasselbalchpau","last":"Hasselbalch","locid":"8dfc4eeb-90da-420f-bf73-bc70213d98ab","name":"Hasselbalch, Rasmus Bo","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"rosbjergpau","last":"Rosbjerg","locid":"362a8e3b-6cb9-4