Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8e3cd5f6-4f6e-4a0e-a9c0-fd6597118ce5","ku-9f8b0c77-36ac-473c-b6b6-21a0ee392bf9","sdu-c87f7e98-5dc0-4403-95cf-3c56fe6f6ec6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Increased Incidence of Mental Disorders in Children with Cataract : Findings from a Population-based Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-023027","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Dette kapitel adresserer sammenhængen mellem meningsfuld aktivitet, sundhed, livskvalitet og velvære fra et aktivitetsvidenskabeligt perspektiv. Kapitlet indeholder en gennemgang af begrebernes definitioner, særkende og anvendelse i aktivitetsvidenskaben samt en kritisk diskussion af disse. Herudover vil deres indbyrdes samspil foldes ud og underbygges at nordisk aktivitetsvidenskabelig forskning. Meningsfulde aktiviteters betydning for forebyggelse og sundhedsfremmende indsatser belyses ud fra nordiske studier og kapitlet afsluttes med en perspektivering, implikationer for fremtidig forskning samt refleksionsspørgsmål.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lindahl-Jacobsen, Line Elisabeth","Jessen-Winge, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-389657"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Medier kommunikation og sprog","meningsfulde aktiviteter"],"level":"edu","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"meningsfulde aktiviteters betydning for sundhed og velvære","src":["kp"],"src-code":["DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-389657","ids":["kp-8d1290a9-cb94-48ea-b573-7da764074a40"],"keyword":["Medier, kommunikation og sprog","meningsfulde aktiviteter"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C8AC55A0CB2CD374AE877082198E71EE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["University College Absalon"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for sundhedsuddannelser - Dekan, Ergoterapeutuddannelsen","Sundhed for børn og voksne – Institut for Terapeut og Jordemoderuddannelser, Arbejdsliv - Bedre forebyggelse og behandling af skader og sygdomme der påvirker arbejdsevnen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Elisabeth","key":"lindahljacobsenpau","last":"Lindahl-Jacobsen","name":"Lindahl-Jacobsen, Line Elisabeth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"jessenwingepau","last":"Jessen-Winge","locid":"7dfa3576-802e-4e52-960f-4b818d167e17","name":"Jessen-Winge, Christina","orcid":"0000-0001-8323-8863","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanne Kaae","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Hanne Kaae","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Sofie Bach","key":"schoupedh","last":"Schou","name":"Schou, Anne Sofie Bach","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Larsen","key":"mærskpedh","last":"Mærsk","name":"Mærsk, Jesper Larsen","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"2.","isbn":["9788702325546"],"pages":"83-105","place":"København","publisher":"Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Nordisk aktivitetsvidenskab"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-8d1290a9-cb94-48ea-b573-7da764074a40"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"Meningsfulde aktiviteters betydning for sundhed og velvære","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-389657","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Nitrogen fertilisation contributes significantly to the atmospheric increase of nitrous oxide (N2O). Application of nitrification inhibitors (NIs) is a promising strategy to mitigate N2O emissions and improve N-use efficiency in agricultural systems. This study investigated the effect of NI, 3,4-dimethylpyrazol phosphate (DMPP) on N2O mitigation from spring barley and spring oilseed rape. Manual and automatic chamber methodologies were used to capture spatial and temporal variability in N2O emissions. In a second experiment, we study the effect of N fertiliser levels without NI (0 %, 50 %, 100 %, 150 % and 200 % of recommended amount of N fertiliser), as well as 100 % of N with NI on N2O emissions in spring barley. The automated chamber measurements showed dynamics of N2O changes throughout the season, including positive and negative peaks that were unobservable with manual chambers due to low temporal resolution. Although not significant, application of NI tended to reduce N2O emissions. The reduction was on average 16 % in spring barley and 58 % in spring oilseed rape in manual chamber measurements. However, N2O reduction was 108 % in continuous automatic chamber measurements in spring barley. The N2O EFs for the growing season were very low (0.025 % to 0.148 %), with a greater reduction in EF in spring oilseed rape (76 %) than in spring barley (32 %) with NI application. A positive correlation (R = 80 %) was observed between N fertiliser levels and N2O emissions. Crop yield and crop N uptake were not significantly affected by the use of NI. This study highlighted that NI can reduce N2O emissions, but the reduction effects are plot, crop and microclimate specific. Long-term experiments with continuous plot-scale measurements are needed to capture and optimise N2O mitigation effect of NIs across wide variability in soils and microclimates in agroecosystems.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Tariq, Azeem","Larsen, Klaus Steenberg","Hansen, Line Vinther","Jensen, Lars Stoumann","Bruun, Sander"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-517421"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agricultural soils","Mitigation","Nitrification inhibitor","Nitrous oxide"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of nitrification inhibitor dmpp on nitrous oxide emissions from agricultural fields automated and manual measurements","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.157650","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-517421","identifier":[{"id":"000926442800012","type":"wos"},{"id":"35907541","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85135160668","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cf87eb09-8432-4c36-9e2b-d80d81986215"],"keyword":["Agricultural soils","Automatic chambers","Mitigation","Nitrification inhibitor","Nitrous oxide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-57FCB9C93AA7990DE5E0D7978603A071"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.157650","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/316149008/1_s2.0_S0048969722047489_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant and Soil Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Azeem","key":"tariqpau","last":"Tariq","locid":"653a23fb-0563-44c5-9582-fc665b5b2b21","name":"Tariq, Azeem","orcid":"0000-0002-6132-2391","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus Steenberg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"412c996e-9d8d-4985-97b1-6b2502331595","name":"Larsen, Klaus Steenberg","orcid":"0000-0002-1421-6182","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Vinther","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"99992d9f-8b1f-4f8a-abab-90af1aa9af50","name":"Hansen, Line Vinther","orcid":"0000-0001-6734-9440","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Stoumann","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"42c2f2f0-5a77-47db-994c-85731e64ba92","name":"Jensen, Lars Stoumann","orcid":"0000-0002-1446-2084","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sander","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"5880b143-364d-4b44-bb5f-340230798d28","name":"Bruun, Sander","orcid":"0000-0002-2233-5122","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35907541"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.157650","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","paperid":"157650","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"847"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135160668"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cf87eb09-8432-4c36-9e2b-d80d81986215"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of nitrification inhibitor (DMPP) on nitrous oxide emissions from agricultural fields : Automated and manual measurements","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-517421","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Skaarup, Line","Gätz, Natalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-648007"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the dark side of occupation","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-648007","ids":["ucl-6c46e8dd-c37b-450a-84ed-ef20f1d55f24"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-01B90E3D1FFB67E6AA345BAF19CE1996"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Ergoterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"skaaruppau","last":"Skaarup","locid":"edffb414-8eee-44f2-a093-9cb29a9403da","name":"Skaarup, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"gätzpau","last":"Gätz","name":"Gätz, Natalie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanne Kaae","key":"kristensenpedh","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Hanne Kaae","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Sofie Bach","key":"schoupedh","last":"Schou","name":"Schou, Anne Sofie Bach","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Larsen","key":"mærskpedh","last":"Mærsk","name":"Mærsk, Jesper Larsen","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"2","isbn":["9788702325546"],"pages":"313-330","place":"København","publisher":"Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Nordisk aktivitetsvidenskab"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-6c46e8dd-c37b-450a-84ed-ef20f1d55f24"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"The dark side of occupation","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-648007","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background In recent years, significant research efforts have focused on identifying modifiable risk factors to be leveraged for dementia prevention. Sleep is required for memory consolidation and normal brain functioning, and various mechanisms are proposed between poor sleep quality and cognitive impairment. Several studies have examined the role of sleep disturbances as a risk factor for dementia; however, most of these studies have involved smaller cohorts and short time intervals, and often rely on retrospective surveys and self-reported exposure data. Our aim was to examine the association between sleep disorders and late-onset dementia in an entire population. Method In a nationwide cohort with a 40-year follow up, we linked nationwide population data with information on hospital-based sleep disorder diagnoses and late-onset dementia from the extensive Danish health registers. Incidence rate ratios (IRR) were calculated using Poisson regression analysis. Analyses were adjusted for age, sex, calendar year, education, and somatic and psychiatric comorbidities. Result The cohort consisted of 1,491,276 people. Those with any hospital-diagnosed sleep disorder had a 17% higher risk of dementia (IRR 1.17, 95% CI 1.11-1.24) compared to people with no sleep disorder diagnosis. The highest risk was found for men with ‘other specific disorders’ (e.g. insomnia, hypersomnia, non-organic sleep disorders) with an IRR of 2.00 (95% CI 1.71-2.32). The risk of dementia was significantly increased 0 to 5 years after sleep disorder diagnosis (IRR 1.35, 95% CI 1.25-1.47), while the association after 5 years or more was non-significant (1.05, 95% CI 0.97-1.13). Conclusion Our findings indicate an increased short-term risk of dementia following a hospital-based sleep disorder diagnosis, while we found weaker evidence of a long-term risk. While this may indicate that sleep disorders could be early symptoms of dementia as well as a risk factor, further research is needed to evaluate sleep disorders as potential early symptoms of dementia, risk factors for dementia, or both, and characterize how this may change at different points along the dementia course. Increased knowledge of the role of sleep disorders in dementia could help inform efforts towards diagnosing dementia in the early stages of the disease or even in dementia prevention.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Damsgaard, Line","Janbek, Janet","Larsen, Thomas Munk","Erlangsen, Annette","Spira, Adam P","Waldemar, Gunhild"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-732459"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Australian National University","Johns Hopkins University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sleep disorders and incident dementia a nationwide observational cohort study alzheimer s dement","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-732459","ids":["ku-d070b5cd-4b89-4684-8e51-1f262038642f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B329F307939A9D076D2454A84B23C1DF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"johns hopkins university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Johns Hopkins University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"au","key":"australian national university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Australian National University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"damsgaardpau","last":"Damsgaard","name":"Damsgaard, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janet","key":"janbekpau","last":"Janbek","name":"Janbek, Janet","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas Munk","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Thomas Munk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 4","first":"Annette","key":"erlangsenpau","last":"Erlangsen","name":"Erlangsen, Annette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Adam P","key":"spirapau","last":"Spira","name":"Spira, Adam P","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Gunhild","key":"waldemarpau","last":"Waldemar","locid":"becd5a62-33b3-405e-8c6e-36a9578512d6","name":"Waldemar, Gunhild","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/alz.063813","issn":["15525260","15525279"],"issn_org":["15525260"],"issue":"Supplement 11","journal":"Alzheimer's & Dementia","status":"p","title":"Alzheimer's & Dementia","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d070b5cd-4b89-4684-8e51-1f262038642f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sleep disorders and incident dementia: a nationwide observational cohort study : Alzheimer's Dement","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-732459","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Genetic variants within nearly 1000 loci are known to contribute to modulation of blood lipid levels. However, the biological pathways underlying these associations are frequently unknown, limiting understanding of these findings and hindering downstream translational efforts such as drug target discovery. RESULTS: To expand our understanding of the underlying biological pathways and mechanisms controlling blood lipid levels, we leverage a large multi-ancestry meta-analysis (N = 1,654,960) of blood lipids to prioritize putative causal genes for 2286 lipid associations using six gene prediction approaches. Using phenome-wide association (PheWAS) scans, we identify relationships of genetically predicted lipid levels to other diseases and conditions. We confirm known pleiotropic associations with cardiovascular phenotypes and determine novel associations, notably with cholelithiasis risk. We perform sex-stratified GWAS meta-analysis of lipid levels and show that 3-5% of autosomal lipid-associated loci demonstrate sex-biased effects. Finally, we report 21 novel lipid loci identified on the X chromosome. Many of the sex-biased autosomal and X chromosome lipid loci show pleiotropic associations with sex hormones, emphasizing the role of hormone regulation in lipid metabolism. CONCLUSIONS: Taken together, our findings provide insights into the biological mechanisms through which associated variants lead to altered lipid levels and potentially cardiovascular disease risk.","author_count":543,"contributors":["Kanoni, Stavroula","Graham, Sarah E.","Wang, Yuxuan","Surakka, Ida","Ramdas, Shweta","Zhu, Xiang","Clarke, Shoa L.","Bhatti, Konain Fatima","Vedantam, Sailaja","Winkler, Thomas W.","Locke, Adam E.","Marouli, Eirini","Zajac, Greg J.M.","Wu, Kuan Han H.","Ntalla, Ioanna","Hui, Qin","Klarin, Derek","Hilliard, Austin T.","Wang, Zeyuan","Xue, Chao","Thorleifsson, Gudmar","Helgadottir, Anna","Gudbjartsson, Daniel F.","Holm, Hilma","Olafsson, Isleifur","Hwang, Mi Yeong","Han, Sohee","Akiyama, Masato","Sakaue, Saori","Terao, Chikashi","Kanai, Masahiro","Zhou, Wei","Brumpton, Ben M.","Rasheed, Humaira","Havulinna, Aki S.","Veturi, Yogasudha","Pacheco, Jennifer Allen","Rosenthal, Elisabeth A.","Lingren, Todd","Feng, Qi Ping","Kullo, Iftikhar J.","Narita, Akira","Takayama, Jun","Martin, Hilary C.","Hunt, Karen A.","Trivedi, Bhavi","Haessler, Jeffrey","Giulianini, Franco","Bradford, Yuki","Miller, Jason E.","Campbell, Archie","Lin, Kuang","Millwood, Iona Y.","Rasheed, Asif","Hindy, George","Faul, Jessica D.","Zhao, Wei","Weir, David R.","Turman, Constance","Huang, Hongyan","Graff, Mariaelisa","Choudhury, Ananyo","Sengupta, Dhriti","Mahajan, Anubha","Brown, Michael R.","Zhang, Weihua","Yu, Ketian","Schmidt, Ellen M.","Pandit, Anita","Gustafsson, Stefan","Yin, Xianyong","Luan, Jian'an","Zhao, Jing Hua","Matsuda, Fumihiko","Jang, Hye Mi","Yoon, Kyungheon","Medina-Gomez, Carolina","Pitsillides, Achilleas","Hottenga, Jouke Jan","Wood, Andrew R.","Ji, Yingji","Gao, Zishan","Haworth, Simon","Yousri, Noha A.","Mitchell, Ruth E.","Chai, Jin Fang","Aadahl, Mette","Bjerregaard, Anne A.","Yao, Jie","Manichaikul, Ani","Hwu, Chii Min","Hung, Yi Jen","Warren, Helen R.","Ramirez, Julia","Bork-Jensen, Jette","Kårhus, Line L.","Goel, Anuj","Sabater-Lleal, Maria","Noordam, Raymond","Mauro, Pala","Matteo, Floris","McDaid, Aaron F.","Marques-Vidal, Pedro","Wielscher, Matthias","Trompet, Stella","Sattar, Naveed","Møllehave, Line T.","Munz, Matthias","Zeng, Lingyao","Huang, Jianfeng","Yang, Bin","Poveda, Alaitz","Kurbasic, Azra","Lamina, Claudia","Forer, Lukas","Scholz, Markus","Galesloot, Tessel E.","Bradfield, Jonathan P.","Ruotsalainen, Sanni E.","Daw, EWarwick","Zmuda, Joseph M.","Mitchell, Jonathan S.","Fuchsberger, Christian","Christensen, Henry","Brody, Jennifer A.","Vazquez-Moreno, Miguel","Feitosa, Mary F.","Wojczynski, Mary K.","Wang, Zhe","Preuss, Michael H.","Mangino, Massimo","Christofidou, Paraskevi","Verweij, Niek","Benjamins