://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-085.71-703806","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Aims: Rare variants in the glucokinase gene (GCK) cause Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young (MODY2/GCK-MODY). We investigated the prevalence of GCK variants, phenotypic characteristics, micro- and macrovascular disease at baseline and follow-up, and treatment among individuals with and without pathogenic GCK variants. Methods: This is a cross-sectional study in a population-based cohort of 5,433 individuals without diabetes (Inter99 cohort) and in 2,855 patients with a new clinical diagnosis of type 2 diabetes (DD2 cohort) with sequencing of GCK. Phenotypic characteristics, presence of micro- and macrovascular disease and treatment information were available for patients in the DD2 cohort at baseline and after an average follow-up of 7.4 years. Results: Twenty-two carriers of potentially deleterious GCK variants were found among patients with type 2 diabetes compared to three among 5,433 nondiabetic individuals [OR = 14.1 (95 % CI 4.2; 47.0), p = 8.9*10-6]. Patients with type 2 diabetes carrying GCK variants had significantly lower waist circumference, hip circumference and BMI, compared to non-carriers. Three GCK variant carriers with diabetes had microvascular complications during follow-up. Conclusions: Approximately 0.8% of Danish patients with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes carry non-synonymous variants in GCK and resemble patients with GCK-MODY. Glucose-lowering treatment cessation should be considered in this subset of diabetes patients.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Gjesing, Anette P.","Engelbrechtsen, Line","Cathrine B. Thuesen, Anne","Have, Christian T.","Hollensted, Mette","Grarup, Niels","Linneberg, Allan","Steen Nielsen, Jens","Christensen, Lotte Brix","Thomsen, Reimar Wernich","Johansson, Kristoffer E.","Cagiada, Matteo","Gersing, Sarah","Hartmann-Petersen, Rasmus","Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","Vaag, Allan","Sørensen, Henrik Toft","Brandslund, Ivan","Beck-Nielsen, Henning","Pedersen, Oluf","Rungby, Jørgen","Hansen, Torben"],"cuid":["S03-094.00-017947"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Gjesing, Anette P.","Hansen, Torben"],"keyword":["Complications","Cross Sectional Studies","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 diagnosis","Glucokinase","Glucokinase genetics","Heterozygote","Humans","MODY","Macrovascular","Microvascular","Monogenic diabetes","Mutation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000014 fold increased prevalence of rare glucokinase gene variant carriers in unselected danish patients with newly diagnosed type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2022.110159","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-094.00-017947","identifier":[{"id":"36400171","type":"pmid"},{"id":"001010866400006","type":"wos"},{"id":"85143917075","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-48e449f1-fb13-42d7-8dfe-ef06fc7bfc8d","ku-f58ec4b8-1b28-4dba-a363-62a66a09597a","sdu-8134ce27-b9c2-4b87-865e-6ec0e65f02d6"],"keyword":["Complications","Cross-Sectional Studies","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/diagnosis","Glucokinase","Glucokinase/genetics","Heterozygote","Humans","MODY","Macrovascular","Microvascular","Monogenic diabetes","Mutation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-26774479B68DDB4DE52D8F3C535E5D18"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/