","first":"Gitte","key":"johannesenpedh","last":"Johannesen","name":"Johannesen, Gitte","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","isbn":["9788712066767"],"pages":"119-132","publisher":"Gad","status":"p","title":"Energibesparende metoder og energiforvaltning i hverdagen"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-d4aaa94a-993e-4d19-93c0-618cced40a51"],"src":["AB University College Absalon"],"title":"Energibesparende tilgange til mennesker med psykiatriske problemstillinger","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-555485","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Early maternal cancer and fertility treatment each increase the risk for adverse birth outcomes, but the joint effect of these outcomes has not yet been reported. Thus, the aim was to assess the individual and joint effect of maternal cancer and fertility treatment on the risk for adverse birth outcomes. Methods: This population-based cohort study included 5487 live-born singletons identified in the Danish Medical Birth Register (1994–2016) of mothers with previous cancer (<40 years) recorded in the Danish Cancer Registry (1955–2014). We randomly selected 80,262 live-born singletons of mothers with no cancer <40 years matched to mothers with cancer by birth year and month. We calculated odds ratios (ORs) for preterm birth, low birth weight (LBW) (<2500 g) and small for gestational age (SGA), mean differences in birth weight in grams, and additional cases of preterm birth (gestational age<259 days) per 100,000 person-years. Multiplicative and additive interaction of maternal cancer and fertility treatment was compared with outcomes of children conceived naturally to mothers with no maternal cancer (reference group). Findings: Among 84,332 live-born singletons, increased ORs for preterm birth were observed among children born to mothers with previous cancer (1·48, 95% confidence interval [CI] 1·33–1.65) or after fertility treatment (1·43, 95% 1·28–1–61), with 22 additional cases of preterm birth among both group of children (95% CI 15–29; 95% CI 14–30). In the joint analyses, the OR for SGA for children born after fertility treatment to mothers with previous cancer was similar to that of the reference group (OR 1·02, 95% CI 0·72–1·44, P for interaction=0·52). Children with both exposures had increased ORs for LBW (1·86, 95% CI 1·17–2·96, P for interaction=0·06) and preterm birth (2·31, 955 CI 1·66–3·20, P for interaction = 0·56), with 61 additional cases of preterm birth (95% CI 27–95, P for interaction=0.26) over that of children in the reference group. The mean birth weight was also lower in children born to mothers with both exposures (-140 g, 95% CI -215; -65) (P for interaction=0.06) but decreased to -22 g (95% CI -76; 31) after adjustment for GA. Interpretation: Although we did not find any statistically significant additive interaction between maternal cancer and fertility treatment, children born after fertility treatment of mothers with previous cancer were at increased risk for adverse birth outcomes. Thus, pregnant women with both exposures need close follow-up during pregnancy. Funding: The Danish Cancer Society and the Danish Childhood Cancer Foundation.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Everhøj, Cathrine","Norsker, Filippa Nyboe","Rechnitzer, Catherine","Licht, Sofie de Fine","Nielsen, Thomas T.","Kjær, Susanne K.","Jensen, Allan","Hargreave, Marie","Christensen, Jane","Belmonte, Federica","Urhoj, Stine Kjaer","Strandberg-Larsen, Katrine","Winther, Jeanette Falck","Kenborg, Line"],"cuid":["S02-098.25-018204"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Kenborg, Line"],"keyword":["Birth outcomes","Cohort study","Early onset cancer","Fertility treatment","Population based","Survivorship"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of early maternal cancer and fertility treatment on the risk of adverse birth outcomes","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eclinm.2022.101369","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.25-018204","identifier":[{"id":"35399810","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8987408","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85127304713","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-4bea665f-2c53-4acf-b4c8-e6c8232b6779","ku-9dda2ab6-3493-4603-a93d-a5d4bf9e57dc"],"keyword":["Birth outcomes","Cohort study","Early onset cancer","Fertility treatment","Population-based","Survivorship"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A6B7C3903825977D71A0A8FBD01EE41C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/303586085/Effects.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eclinm.2022.101369","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cathrine","key":"everhøjpau","last":"Everhøj","name":"Everhøj, Cathrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Filippa Nyboe","key":"norskerpau","last":"Norsker","name":"Norsker, Filippa Nyboe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Catherine","key":"rechnitzerpau","last":"Rechnitzer","name":"Rechnitzer, Catherine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie de Fine","key":"lichtpau","last":"Licht","name":"Licht, Sofie de Fine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas T.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Thomas T.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Susanne K","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","name_org":"Kjær, Susanne K","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Allan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"hargreavepau","last":"Hargreave","name":"Hargreave, Marie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jane","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Federica","key":"belmontepau","last":"Belmonte","name":"Belmonte, Federica","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Stine Kjaer","key":"urhøjpau","last":"Urhøj","locid":"a9791d78-26b7-4a43-a897-7d2c93a258c5","name":"Urhoj, Stine Kjaer","name_org":"Urhøj, Stine Kjaer","orcid":"0000-0002-2069-9723","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Katrine","key":"strandberglarsenpau","last":"Strandberg-Larsen","locid":"5a443538-3866-40a3-b93e-b4d4be24a83a","name":"Strandberg-Larsen, Katrine","orcid":"0000-0001-7061-3767","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette F.","key":"wintherpau","last":"Winther","locid":"11ca8ef7-98c5-4eed-9dbe-3b44124f948b","name":"Winther, Jeanette Falck","name_org":"Winther, Jeanette F.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"kenborgpau","last":"Kenborg","name":"Kenborg, Line","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35399810"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.eclinm.2022.101369","issn":["25895370"],"journal":"EClinicalMedicine","paperid":"101369","publisher":"The Lancet Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"EClinicalMedicine","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127304713"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4bea665f-2c53-4acf-b4c8-e6c8232b6779","ku-9dda2ab6-3493-4603-a93d-a5d4bf9e57dc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of early maternal cancer and fertility treatment on the risk of adverse birth outcomes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.25-018204","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: In early 2021, the SARS-CoV-2 lineage B.1.1.7 (Alpha variant) became dominant across large parts of the world. In Denmark, comprehensive and real-time test, contact-tracing, and sequencing efforts were applied to sustain epidemic control. Here, we use these data to investigate the transmissibility, introduction, and onward transmission of B.1.1.7 in Denmark. Methods: We analyzed a comprehensive set of 60,178 SARS-CoV-2 genomes generated from high-throughput sequencing by the Danish COVID-19 Genome Consortium, representing 34% of all positive cases in the period 14 November 2020 to 7 February 2021. We calculated the transmissibility of B.1.1.7 relative to other lineages using Poisson regression. Including all 1976 high-quality B.1.1.7 genomes collected in the study period, we constructed a time-scaled phylogeny, which was coupled with detailed travel history and register data to outline the introduction and onward transmission of B.1.1.7 in Denmark. Results: In a period with unchanged restrictions, we estimated an increased B.1.1.7 transmissibility of 58% (95% CI: [56%, 60%]) relative to other lineages. Epidemiological and phylogenetic analyses revealed that 37% of B.1.1.7 cases were related to the initial introduction in November 2020. The relative number of cases directly linked to introductions varied between 10 and 50% throughout the study period. Conclusions: Our findings corroborate early estimates of increased transmissibility of B.1.1.7. Both substantial early expansion when B.1.1.7 was still unmonitored and continuous foreign introductions contributed considerably to case numbers. Finally, our study highlights the benefit of balanced travel restrictions and self-isolation procedures coupled with comprehensive surveillance efforts, to sustain epidemic control in the face of emerging variants.","author_count":94,"contributors":["Michaelsen, Thomas Yssing","Bennedbæk, Marc","Christiansen, Lasse E.","Jørgensen, Mia S.F.","Møller, Camilla H.","Sørensen, Emil Aarre","Knutsson, Simon","Brandt, Jakob","Nymann, Thomas","Chiche-Lapierre, Clarisse","Collados, Emilio Fuster","Sørensen, Trine","Petersen, Celine","Le, Vang","Sereika, Mantas","Hansen, Frederik Teilfeldt","Rasmussen, Morten","Fonager, Jannik","Karst, Søren M.","Marvig, Rasmus L.","Stegger, Marc","Sieber, Raphael N.","Skov, Robert","Legarth, Rebecca","Krause, Tyra G.","Fomsgaard, Anders","Andersen, Kasper Skytte","Andersen, Martin Hjorth","Berg, Amalie","Bielidt, Susanne R.","Mølvang Dall, Sebastian","Dvarionaite, Erika","Hove Hansen, Susan","Jørgensen, Vibeke Rudkjøbing","Kirkegaard, Rasmus Hansen","Saei, Wagma","Nicolajsen, Trine B.","Østergaard, Stine Karstenskov","Brøndum, Rasmus Froberg","Bøgsted, Martin","Hose, Katja","Sagi, Tomer","Pakanec, Miroslaw","Fuglsang-Damgaard, David","Mølvadgaard, Mette","Krarup, Henrik","Svarrer, Christina W.","Christiansen, Mette T.","Ingham, Anna C.","Johannesen, Thor B.","Basterrechea, Martín","Lilje, Berit","Ellegaard, Kirsten","Matusevicius, Povilas","Christoffersen, Lars B.","Tang, Man Hung E.","Ng, Kim L.","Edslev, Sofie M.","Baig, Sharmin","Larsen, Ole H.","Skipper, Kristian A.","Vang, Søren","Handberg, Kurt J.","Nielsen, Marc T.K.","Kobel, Carl M.","Andersen, Camilla","Tarpgaard, Irene H.","Ellermann-Eriksen, Svend","Castruita, José A.S.","Schneider, Uffe V.","Jacobsen, Nana G.","Andersen, Christian","Pedersen, Martin S.","Schønning, Kristian","Kirkby, Nikolai","Nielsen, Lene","Nilsson, Line L.","Friis, Martin B.","Sundelin, Thomas","Hansen, Thomas A.","Skov, Marianne N.","Sydenham, Thomas V.","Nielsen, Xiaohui C.","Schouw, Christian H.","Jensen, Anders","Marmolin, Ea S.","Coia, John E.","Andersen, Dorte T.","Albertsen, Mads"],"cuid":["S04-093.49-010787"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corpau":["Danish Covid-19 Genome Consortium","The Danish COVID-19 Genome Consortium (DCGC)"],"corresponding_author":["Albertsen, Mads"],"keyword":["COVID 19 epidemiology","Denmark epidemiology","Humans","Phylogeny","SARS CoV 2 genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction and transmission of sars cov 000000000002 lineage b 000000000001 000000000001 000000000007 alpha variant in denmark","src":["aau","dtu","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13073-022-01045-7","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work would not have been possible without the Danish COVID-19 Genome Consortium (DCGC); a full list of contributing consortium members can be found in Additional file 1. We gratefully acknowledge the Danish hospitals for local sequencing and data sharing. Thanks to all data contributors from outside Denmark, including the authors and their originating laboratories responsible for obtaining the specimens, as well as their submitting laboratories for generating the genetic sequence and metadata and sharing it via the GISAID Initiative. A full acknowledgement table is provided in Additional file 2. We would like to acknowledge the people at Data Integration and Analysis (DIAS), Statens Serum Institute, for managing and maintaining the national MiBa database which much of this work is based on. Thanks to the people at the Danish Patient Safety Authority for providing us with detailed travel records of SARS-CoV-2 positive cases. Thanks to Anna Zhukova, Institut Pasteur for modifying the pastML software to better fit our needs upon request. Finally, sincere thanks to Edyth Parker, Scripps Research, for insightful phylogenetic discussions."],"id":"S04-093.49-010787","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9064402","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35505393","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85129997318","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e1d96822-d59b-45a3-b51f-6e36f19b02d1","dtu-d4ee83d3-1835-45e8-ad47-e535115bd0ce","ku-51b0d01b-2672-480d-b31c-e83ffa63c4d4","sdu-43413a40-3fef-478a-bbab-354d2e418a06"],"keyword":["COVID-19/epidemiology","Denmark/epidemiology","Humans","Phylogeny","SARS-CoV-2/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-6B2D322F513D0D7725F93C1C169BC517"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/281354429/s13073_022_01045_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/518917951/s13073_022_01045_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13073-022-01045-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/203034876/s13073_022_01045_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.1101/2021.06.04.21258333v1","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC0","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/318706852/Introduction_and_transmission.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering 