{"abstract":"The inherent flexibility of intrinsically disordered proteins (IDPs) makes it difficult to interpret experimental data using structural models. On the other hand, molecular dynamics simulations of IDPs often suffer from force-field inaccuracies, and long simulation times or enhanced sampling methods are needed to obtain converged ensembles. Here, we apply metainference and Bayesian/Maximum Entropy reweighting approaches to integrate prior knowledge of the system with experimental data, while also dealing with various sources of errors and the inherent conformational heterogeneity of IDPs. We have measured new SAXS data on the protein α-synuclein, and integrate this with simulations performed using different force fields. We find that if the force field gives rise to ensembles that are much more compact than what is implied by the SAXS data it is difficult to recover a reasonable ensemble. On the other hand, we show that when the simulated ensemble is reasonable, we can obtain an ensemble that is consistent with the SAXS data, but also with NMR diffusion and paramagnetic relaxation enhancement data.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ahmed, Mustapha Carab Hussein","Skaanning, Line K.","Jussupow, Alexander","Newcombe, Estella A.","Kragelund, Birthe B.","Camilloni, Carlo","Langkilde, Annette Eva","Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-407672"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technical University of Munich","University of Milan"],"keyword":["Intrinsically disordered protein","Molecular Dynamics Simulation","NMR","Protein","Small angle X ray scattering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"refinement of α synuclein ensembles against saxs data comparison of force fields and methods","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmolb.2021.654333","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-407672","identifier":[{"id":"33968988","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8100456","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85105396641","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-17dd0215-6819-4e6c-9467-f8b547950847"],"keyword":["NMR","intrinsically disordered protein","molecular dynamics simulation","protein","small-angle X-ray scattering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D5C9D05C432B88DE23F4E034D3DB67B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmolb.2021.654333","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/262899107/Refinement_of_Synuclein_Ensembles_Against_SAXS_Data.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Biomolecular Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Milan","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mustapha Carab","key":"ahmedpau","last":"Ahmed","locid":"8628fdb3-4498-453e-894d-fd61ac2384c2","name":"Ahmed, Mustapha Carab Hussein","name_org":"Ahmed, Mustapha Carab","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line K.","key":"skaanningpau","last":"Skaanning","locid":"4ecba80b-1625-4277-839c-7dbf9202cb48","name":"Skaanning, Line K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Alexander","key":"jussupowpau","last":"Jussupow","name":"Jussupow, Alexander","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Estella A.","key":"newcombepau","last":"Newcombe","locid":"5b66f39e-fa99-400a-8bbc-675a49d7ef09","name":"Newcombe, Estella A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birthe B.","key":"kragelundpau","last":"Kragelund","locid":"c3a5d42e-5e73-4af3-94f9-22550bb7c499","name":"Kragelund, Birthe B.","orcid":"0000-0002-7454-1761","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Carlo","key":"camillonipau","last":"Camilloni","name":"Camilloni, Carlo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annette E.","key":"langkildepau","last":"Langkilde","locid":"fda7c2aa-b668-457b-a00a-1b95892123c2","name":"Langkilde, Annette Eva","name_org":"Langkilde, Annette E.","orcid":"0000-0003-2467-4205","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kresten","key":"lindorfflarsenpau","last":"Lindorff-Larsen","locid":"be20a4d8-92c4-44b9-9dfb-b6ad6471a58c","name":"Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","orcid":"0000-0002-4750-6039","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33968988"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmolb.2021.654333","issn":["2296889X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Molecular Biosciences","paperid":"654333","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Molecular Biosciences","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105396641"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-17dd0215-6819-4e6c-9467-f8b547950847"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Refinement of α-Synuclein Ensembles Against SAXS Data : Comparison of Force Fields and Methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://loca