{"abstract":"Background: The COVID-19 pandemic has changed various spheres of health care. General practitioners (GPs) have widely replaced face-to-face consultations with telephone or video consultations (VCs) to reduce the risk of COVID-19 transmission. Using VCs for health service delivery is an entirely new way of practicing for many GPs. However, this transition process has largely been conducted with no formal guidelines, which may have caused implementation barriers. This study presents a rapid cycle coproduction approach for developing a guide to assist VC implementation in general practice. Objective: The aim of this paper is to describe the developmental phases of the VC guide to assist general practices in implementing VCs and summarize the evaluation made by general practice users. Methods: The development of a guide for VC in general practice was structured as a stepped process based on the coproduction and prototyping processes. We used an iterative framework based on rapid qualitative analyses and interdisciplinary collaborations. Thus, the guide was developed in small, repeated cycles of development, implementation, evaluation, and adaptation, with a continuous exchange between research and practice. The data collection process was structured in 3 main phases. First, we conducted a literature review, recorded observations, and held informal and semistructured interviews. Second, we facilitated coproduction with stakeholders through 4 workshops with GPs, a group interview with patient representatives, and individual revisions by GPs. Third, nationwide testing was conducted in 5 general practice clinics and was followed by an evaluation of the guide through interviews with GPs. Results: A rapid cycle coproduction approach was used to explore the needs of general practice in connection with the implementation of VC and to develop useful, relevant, and easily understandable guiding materials. Our findings suggest that a guide for VCs should include advice and recommendations regarding the organization of VCs, the technical setup, the appropriate target groups, patients' use of VCs, the performance of VCs, and the arrangements for booking a VC. Conclusions: The combination of coproduction, prototyping, small iterations, and rapid data analysis is a suitable approach when contextually rich, hands-on guide materials are urgently needed. Moreover, this method could provide an efficient way of developing relevant guide materials for general practice to aid the implementation of new technology beyond the pandemic period.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sandbæk, Amanda","Christensen, Line Due","Larsen, Lotte Lykke","Christensen, Nina Primholdt","Kofod, Frida Greek","Guassora, Ann Dorrit","Merrild, Camilla Hoffmann","Hvidt, Elisabeth Assing"],"cuid":["S04-098.49-010067"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Line Due"],"keyword":["Communication","Coproduction","General practice","Implementation science","Intervention development","Rapid analysis","Remote Consultation","Resource guide","Video consultation","Workshop"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"guidance for implementing video consultations in danish general practice rapid cycle coproduction study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/27323","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by Innovation Fund Denmark. The funding source had no role in the design, analysis, and interpretation of the data or in the writing of the paper."],"id":"S04-098.49-010067","identifier":[{"id":"34821560","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8663649","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85120169799","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d21f8aac-8a70-4767-b17a-e48d56b0e6e6","au-a9957f8b-a94b-4cd7-a6e7-7a5c8cbd0c17","ku-aba0fa4c-7999-452a-8c84-6bc3e9770c6d","sdu-f1696247-d928-4e6c-95f2-c688a5630a52"],"keyword":["Communication","Coproduction","General practice","Implementation science","Intervention development","Rapid analysis","Remote consultation","Resource guide","Video consultation","Workshop"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-AA9026F0D5C534E9A6D45BDE832BC464"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/455320270/Sandb_k_et_al._2021_._Guidance_for_Implementing_Video_Consultations_in_Danish_General_Practice_Rapid_Cycle_Coproduction_Study.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/27323","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/195201922/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/291124167/Guidance_for_implementing_video_consultations_in_danish_general_practice.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg universi