{"abstract":"AIMS: To describe the risks of thromboembolism and major bleeding complications in anticoagulated patients with atrial fibrillation (AF) and native aortic or mitral valvular heart disease using data reflecting clinical practice. METHODS AND RESULTS: Descriptive cohort study of anticoagulated patients with incident AF and native aortic or mitral valvular heart disease, identified in nationwide Danish registries from 2000 to 2018. A total of 10 043 patients were included, of which 5190 (51.7%) patients had aortic stenosis, 1788 (17.8%) patients had aortic regurgitation, 327 (3.3%) patients had mitral stenosis, and 2738 (27.3%) patients had mitral regurgitation. At 1 year after AF diagnosis, the risk of thromboembolism was 4.6% in patients with mitral stenosis taking a vitamin K antagonist (VKA), and 2.6% in patients with aortic stenosis taking a VKA or non-vitamin K antagonist oral anticoagulant (NOAC). For patients with aortic or mitral regurgitation, the risks of thromboembolism ranged between 1.5%-1.8% in both treatment groups. For the endpoint of major bleeding, the risk was ∼5.5% in patients with aortic stenosis or mitral stenosis treated with a VKA, and 3.3-4.0% in patients with aortic or mitral regurgitation. For patients treated with a NOAC, the risk of major bleeding was 3.7% in patients with aortic stenosis and ∼2.5% in patients with aortic or mitral regurgitation. CONCLUSION: When using data reflecting contemporary clinical practice, our observations suggested that 1 year after a diagnosis of AF, anticoagulated patients with aortic or mitral valvular heart disease had dissimilar risk of thromboembolism and major bleeding complications. Specifically, patients with aortic stenosis or mitral stenosis were high-risk subgroups. This observation may guide clinicians regarding intensity of clinical follow-up.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Melgaard, Line","Overvad, Thure Filskov","Jensen, Martin","Lip, Gregory Y H","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Nielsen, Peter Brønnum"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-080624"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Melgaard, Line"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","University of Liverpool"],"keyword":["Anticoagulation","Atrial fibrillation","Bleeding complications","Thromboembolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thromboembolism and bleeding complications in anticoagulated patients with atrial fibrillation and native aortic or mitral valvular heart disease a descriptive nationwide cohort study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85104209941&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-080624","identifier":[{"id":"85104209941","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32003787","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-692f7362-355e-4e0e-89ad-5fec7f34b12e"],"keyword":["Anticoagulation","Atrial fibrillation","Bleeding complications","Native valvular heart disease","Thromboembolism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7ADA6A1297451ECB924B02604F3038B7"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Cardiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Anæstesi, Børn, Kredsløb og Kvinder","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of liverpool","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Liverpool","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"liverpool heart and chest hospital nhs foundation trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"melgaardpau","last":"Melgaard","locid":"88687b9c-5b56-4584-a89a-89fdeca4fd54","name":"Melgaard, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thure Filskov","key":"overvadpau","last":"Overvad","locid":"63d282a2-85c6-4f40-a01b-f4cc59ec37f5","name":"Overvad, Thure Filskov","orcid":"0000-0001-8096-0236","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d5770e98-1d04-4d3b-aa8c-49c951b21eb0","name":"Jensen, Martin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y H","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Bjerregaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a3c6747f-b9db-488b-8eb9-887d38742880","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Brønnum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3ce5c24a-cc41-4e4c-a071-9a41f036faf8","name":"Nielsen, Peter Brønnum","orcid":"0000-0003-2922-6970","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32003787"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjcvp/pvaa008","issn":["20556837"],"issue":"FI1","journal":"European Heart Journal - Cardiovascular Pharmacotherapy","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal - Cardiovascular Pharmacotherapy","title_org":"European heart journal. Cardiovascular pharmacotherapy","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104209941"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-692f7362-355e-4e0e-89ad-5fec7f34b12e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Thromboembolism and bleeding complications in anticoagulated patients with atrial fibrillation and native aortic or mitral valvular heart disease : A descriptive nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-080624","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"For prospective investigation of drugs and metabolites in archaeological and contemporary dental calculus, a sensitive, broadly applicable ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry method using pneumatically assisted electrospray ionisation (UHPLC-ESI-MS/MS) was developed. The dental calculus was treated with citric acid and the dissolution extracts were cleaned using weak and strong polymeric cation-exchange sorbents. The method was validated on hydroxyapatite for the analysis of 67 drugs and metabolites. Typically, the lower limits of quantification were in the range of 0.01–0.05 ng for the sample mass extracted. The general applicability of the method was tested using dental calculus material sampled from 10 corpses undergoing forensic autopsy. The calculus material was washed several times before dissolution to remove residual substances originating from saliva, gingival crevicular fluid and blood. The wash extracts and the calculus samples (cleaned calculus material) were analysed using the same instrumental conditions. The dry mass of the calculus samples ranged from 1 to 10 mg. The total number of drug detections was 131 in the dental calculus samples and 117 in the whole blood samples. From the analyses of the wash extracts and calculus samples, it was proven that drug residues were trapped in the interior of the calculus material. In 82 of the drug detections, the drug concentrations were higher in the dental calculus than in the blood. Among substances detected in the dental calculus but not in the blood were cocaine, heroin, 6-MAM and THCA-A.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sørensen, Lambert Kristiansen","Hasselstrøm, Jørgen Bo","Staun Larsen, Line","Bindslev, Dorthe Arenholt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-253517"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Lambert Kristiansen"],"keyword":["Alkaloids","Caffeine","Cannabinoids","Cocaine","Dental calculus","Drugs","LC MS MS","Nicotine","Opioids"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"entrapment of drugs in dental calculus detection validation based on test results from post mortem investigations","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85097870925","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-253517","identifier":[{"id":"85097870925","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33341470","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d99413f7-9119-49e2-94ae-b864b5965cda"],"keyword":["Alkaloids","Caffeine","Cannabinoids","Cocaine","Dental calculus","Drugs","LC-MS/MS","Nicotine","Opioids"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-90802D74C5BCDA065B2AA259CDC8EE1B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Forensic Medicine, Department of Forensic Medicine - Retskemisk"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lambert Kristiansen","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"8cf45c89-ac2d-4ef2-a97c-20eec9f71a8e","name":"Sørensen, Lambert Kristiansen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Bo","key":"hasselstrømpau","last":"Hasselstrøm","locid":"c4351988-ff77-42bc-9a7a-5a329fe8d98b","name":"Hasselstrøm, Jørgen Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5928-9238","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country"