esper Larsen","key":"mærskpau","last":"Mærsk","locid":"498dd3b8-2091-4d8a-8316-14799fe80c52","name":"Mærsk, Jesper Larsen","orcid":"0000-0002-5290-7937","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"lacourpau","last":"laCour","name":"laCour, Karen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Elisabeth Ejlersen","key":"wæhrenspau","last":"Wæhrens","name":"Wæhrens, Eva Elisabeth Ejlersen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Line","key":"lindahljacobsenpedh","last":"Lindahl-Jacobsen","name":"Lindahl-Jacobsen, Line","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe Varning","key":"poulsenpedh","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Dorthe Varning","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788712061762"],"pages":"185-194","publisher":"Gad","status":"p","title":"Ergoterapi og fysioterapi i den palliative praksis"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Universities","University College Absalon","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-ed27fd72-59cd-43ef-8b38-ddd0739b5c85"],"src":["AB University College Absalon"],"title":"Aktivitetsvidenskabelige perspektiver på hverdagsliv og ergoterapeutisk brug af aktivitet til mennesker med livstruende sygdom","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-555769","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Osteogenesis imperfecta (OI) is a rare, hereditary disease affecting collagen type-1 in connective tissue. Collagen type-1 is a substantial component of dentine, and it is speculated, whether affected dentine could cause altered mesiodistal tooth dimension possibly affecting restorative treatment regimen. Therefore, the aim of the present study was to measure mesiodistal tooth dimensions in individuals with OI and compare them with healthy controls. Materials and methods: Fifty-seven individuals aged 20–77 years with OI type 1–4 were included and 70 control patients aged 11–34 years were drawn from an orthodontic database. Mesiodistal tooth dimensions of all tooth types, except third molars, were measured in mm (two decimals) on digital 3 D-models of the tooth-bearing arches. Results: Multilevel mixed-effects linear regression analysis showed that mesiodistal tooth dimension on average was 0.17 mm (95% CI = (−0.33; −0.01)) reduced for the OI group compared to controls. The analysis revealed variation between tooth types; incisors and first premolars were most affected and molars minimally affected. Conclusions: The mesiodistal tooth dimension in individuals diagnosed with OI is significantly smaller compared to healthy controls, which should be taken into consideration in the restorative treatment planning of individuals with OI, although the magnitude of the deviation is relatively small. The results on mesiodistal tooth dimensions of the present controls may be used as a standard for comparisons in future studies on tooth dimensions.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Staun Larsen, Line","Thuesen, Kirstine Juhl","Gjørup, Hans","Dahl, Jannie","Væth, Michael","Dalstra, Michel","Haubek, Dorte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-271330"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Staun Larsen, Line"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Basel"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Bicuspid","Child","Cross Sectional Studies","Dental Arch","Dentinogenesis imperfecta","Digital Model","Humans","Incisor","Middle Aged","Osteogenesis imperfecta","Tooth","Young Adult","tooth dimension","tooth size"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reduced mesiodistal tooth dimension in individuals with osteogenesis imperfecta a cross sectional study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00016357.2020.1836391","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-271330","identifier":[{"id":"000583823200001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85094131909","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33103531","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f8e904c6-ab66-4539-b13c-962eb95bb5a7"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Bicuspid","Child","Cross-Sectional Studies","Dental Arch","Humans","Incisor","Middle Aged","Young Adult","collagen diseases","dentinogenesis imperfecta","digital model","osteogenesis imperfecta","plaster model","tooth","tooth dimension","tooth size"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0EA6CEB7F8226AB4EDCC2FB444A5DCAB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00016357.2020.1836391","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/274249486/00016357.2020.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Ecology and Caries Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"university of basel","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Basel","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"staunlarsenpau","last":"Staun Larsen","locid":"35e2ae60-25db-4a15-893f-dc8906e2bccf","name":"Staun Larsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-5884","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirstine Juhl","key":"thuesenpau","last":"Thuesen","name":"Thuesen, Kirstine Juhl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"gjøruppau","last":"Gjørup","locid":"09e05c36-ee41-48dd-ab77-12b82e3ea6db","name":"Gjørup, Hans","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannie","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"ff28625c-4331-45c8-9c95-035c52847347","name":"Dahl, Jannie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"væthpau","last":"Væth","locid":"b646a6f8-cf55-4b01-9c73-f252a48f9fdd","name":"Væth, Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michel","key":"dalstrapau","last":"Dalstra","locid":"e8ed52b4-5c3f-4216-9b0d-b30dff189fa4","name":"Dalstra, Michel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte","key":"haubekpau","last":"Haubek","locid":"5810b477-1799-4dc4-b619-5c04fe335800","name":"Haubek, Dorte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33103531"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00016357.2020.1836391","issn":["00016357","15023850"],"issn_org":["00016357"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Odontologica Scandinavica","pages":"262-267","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Odontologica Scandinavica","volume":"79"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85094131909"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f8e904c6-ab66-4539-b13c-962eb95bb5a7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Reduced mesiodistal tooth dimension in individuals with osteogenesis imperfecta : a cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-271330","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Cloud-Radio Access Network (C-RAN) is seen as a key enabler of energy efficient mobile networks, as it limits the energy consumption at the cell site and provides capacity sharing for multiple cells. C-RAN splits the traditional mobile base station's functional composition into three units, connected by a fronthaul and midhaul network, which together with the backhaul network forms the crosshaul network. This work investigates the crosshaul network energy consumption by the use of network simulations. Network simulations are used to model a realistic user behavior, and provide information about network energy consumption in different scenarios. This work presents results from the simulation of a model implemented by different C-RAN functional compositions. The simulation results can predict the energy consumption in the crosshaul network under realistic application loads. Results illustrate that when scaling up the network, it is more energy efficient to use a functional composition with much processing before transmission on the cross haul network. Results show a 40 times variation in energy consumption among possible scenarios and thus, this work enlighten the importance of choosing the right functional split.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Ruepp, Sarah Renée","Berger, Michael Stübert","Christiansen, Henrik L."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-308957"],"event":{"end":"2021-12-08","place":"Melbourne, au","start":"2021-12-06","title":"17<sup>th</sup> IEEE International Conference on Green Computing and Communications","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Crosshaul","Ethernet","Fronthaul","Functional split","Green Networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy consumption modelling of next generation mobile crosshaul networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85127376687","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-308957","identifier":[{"id":"85127376687","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0e878302-e3db-4e2e-8d4e-806205f7ea88"],"keyword":["Crosshaul","Ethernet","Fronthaul","Functional split","Green Networks","Midhaul"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-69D9D65C3772AFDCBB9624329359F20D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["TDC NET A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line M.P.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","name_org":"Larsen, Line M.P.","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sarah","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","name_org":"Ruepp, Sarah","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael S.","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","locid":"7b367889-bde0-4e40-893f-0a22e4d32371","name":"Berger, Michael Stübert","name_org":"Berger, Michael S.","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-7261","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik L.","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Henrik L.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ithings-greencom-cpscom-smartdata-cybermatics53846.2021.00036","isbn":["9781665417624"],"pages":"153-160","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2021 IEEE Congress on Cybermatics: 14th IEEE International Conferences on Internet of Things, iThings 2021, 17th IEEE International Conference on Green Computing and Communications, GreenCom 2021, 2021 IEEE International Conference on Cyber Physical and Social Computing, CPSCom 2021 and 7th IEEE International Conference on Smart Data, SmartData 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127376687"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","tdc net a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0e878302-e3db-4e2e-8d4e-806205f7ea88"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Energy Consumption Modelling of Next Generation Mobile Crosshaul Networks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-308957","year":"2021","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: While underlying mechanisms and pathways of social inequalities in cancer survival have been extensively examined in adults, this is less so for children with cancer. Hypothesized mechanisms include prediagnostic utilization of and navigation through the health care system, which may differ by socioeconomic resources of the families. In this nationwide register-based study we investigated the association between measures of family socioeconomic position in relation to prediagnostic health care contacts and stage of disease at diagnosis in children with cancer in Denmark. Methods: We identified all children diagnosed with a cancer at ages 0–15 years in 1998–2016 (N = 3043) from the Danish Childhood Cancer Registry. We obtained comprehensive information on measures of socioeconomic position, parental health and prediagnostic contacts to both general practitioners and hospitals 24 months prior to diagnosis from various national registries. We fitted multivariable conditional logistic regression models for the association of family socioeconomic and health-related variables with firstly, frequent health care contacts and secondly, advanced stage. Results: We found higher odds ratios (OR) of frequent both overall and emergency health care contacts in the last 3 months before diagnosis in children from households with short parental education and mixed affiliation to work market, when compared to children with high family socioeconomic position. Further, children of parents with depression or of non-Western origin, respectively, had higher OR for frequent overall and emergency contacts. We found no association between socioeconomic position, parental health and stage of disease. Conclusion: Families with socioeconomic disadvantage, non-Western origin or depression more frequently utilize prediagnostic health care services, both generally and in the acute setting, indicating that some disadvantaged families may struggle to navigate the health care system when their child is sick. Reassuringly, this was not reflected in disparities in stage at diagnosis. In order to improve the diagnostic process and potentially reduce health care contacts, attention and support should be given to families with a high number of health care contacts over a short period of time.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pedersen, Line Hjøllund","Erdmann, Friederike","Aalborg, Gitte Lerche","Hjalgrim, Lisa Lyngsie","Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Winther, Jeanette Falck","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-425977"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz"],"keyword":["Childhood","Childhood cancer","Denmark","Diagnosis","Register study","STAGE","Social inequality","Socioeconomic position"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socioeconomic position and prediagnostic health care contacts in children with cancer in denmark a nationwide register study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-021-08837-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-425977","identifier":[{"id":"85117299500","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8518314","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34649500","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-36c48b00-abfc-477a-9457-73eeb9f5d3ed"],"keyword":["Childhood","Childhood cancer","Denmark","Diagnosis","Prediagnostic contacts","Register study","Social inequality","Socioeconomic position","Stage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FD70BC07D5A35AF15BDEED13A068860D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-021-08837-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/284087074/s12885_021_08837_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"johannes gutenberg university mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line Hjøllund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"80ce3db1-0709-4cf5-91c6-abb970ef7aa5","name":"Pedersen, Line Hjøllund","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Friederike","key":"erdmannpau","last":"Erdmann","name":"Erdmann, Friederike","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Gitte Lerche","key":"aalborgpau","last":"Aalborg","name":"Aalborg, Gitte Lerche","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Lisa Lyngsie","key":"hjalgrimpau","last":"Hjalgrim","name":"Hjalgrim, Lisa Lyngsie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne Bækgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"88b48e37-454f-41e8-a110-a385dce66a6e","name":"Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kjeld","key":"schmiegelowpau","last":"Schmiegelow","locid":"6ce2f948-244d-4f19-82aa-f08a71289674","name":"Schmiegelow, Kjeld","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jeanette Falck","key":"wintherpau","last":"Winther","name":"Winther, Jeanette Falck","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne Oksbjerg","key":"daltonpau","last":"Dalton","locid":"84d10468-fe5d-4cc7-952f-1d89d961390f","name":"Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34649500"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12885-021-08837-x","issn":["14712407"],"journal":"BMC Cancer","paperid":"1104","status":"p","title":"BMC Cancer","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117299500"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-36c48b00-abfc-477a-9457-73eeb9f5d3ed"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Socioeconomic position and prediagnostic health care contacts in children with cancer in Denmark : a nationwide register study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-425977","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This article explores the staging of the Hop On–Hop Off buses, bus-tour and actual embodied performances enacted by tourists on the move. We draw on a performance-inspired terminology to explore the co-production of mundane tourist experiences. Following calls for not making moral judgements or belittling sightseeing tourists and understanding the mundane dimensions of tourist practice, we conduct empathetic research with and about them. We also draw on performance metaphors to highlight the staged and scripted nature of these tours. However, to disavow assumptions that sightseeing is a uniform, fully choreographed practice, we identify different practices and motives within an otherwise much-scripted practice. We show that Hop On–Hop Off practices potentially undermine distinctions within tourism theory between (1) individual tourism and mass tourism, (2) self-directed active mobility (such as walking) and designed passive mobility (such as the sightseeing bus), (3) bubbles and local neighbourhoods and (4) gazing and glancing.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Larsen, Jonas","Bastos, Mónica Sylvia Gomes","Hansen, Line Isselin Skovslund","Hevink, Lieke Maureen","Jostova, Katerina","Smagurauskaite, Dovile"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-560014"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Movement","Performances sightseeing buses","Tourism mobilities","Tourist bubbles"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bubble wrapped sightseeing mobilities hop on hop off bus experiences in copenhagen","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-560014","identifier":[{"id":"85104073580","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-3bdbcf8e-2f06-4282-9e8b-59821931f5a0"],"keyword":["Movement","Performances sightseeing buses","Tourism mobilities","Tourist bubbles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-11AA289441A0D3574E0504E36B9E092F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Space, Place, Mobility and Urban Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1cb27156-b919-462a-9243-4ab2d8f87f26","name":"Larsen, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0002-8208-8119","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mónica Sylvia Gomes","key":"bastospau","last":"Bastos","name":"Bastos, Mónica Sylvia Gomes","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Isselin Skovslund","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Line Isselin Skovslund","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lieke Maureen","key":"hevinkpau","last":"Hevink","name":"Hevink, Lieke Maureen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katerina","key":"jostovapau","last":"Jostova","name":"Jostova, Katerina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dovile","key":"smagurauskaitepau","last":"Smagurauskaite","name":"Smagurauskaite, Dovile","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/14687976211007383","issn":["14687976","17413206"],"issn_org":["14687976"],"issue":"3","journal":"Tourist Studies","pages":"387-403","status":"p","title":"Tourist Studies","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104073580"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-3bdbcf8e-2f06-4282-9e8b-59821931f5a0"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Bubble-Wrapped Sightseeing Mobilities : Hop-On Hop-Off Bus Experiences in Copenhagen","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-560014","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To examine whether medications used to treat rheumatoid arthritis (RA)/chronic inflammatory bowel disease (IBD), or factors related to the assisted reproductive technology (ART) procedures, impact the success of ART. In women with RA/IBD, initial studies have shown a reduced chance of a live-born child after ART. DESIGN: Cohort study. SETTING: Nationwide Danish health registries. PATIENTS: All Danish women with a fresh embryo transfer from January 1, 2006, through 2018. The cohorts comprised 1,824 embryo transfers in women with RA/IBD and 97,191 embryo transfers in women without RA/IBD. INTERVENTIONS: Observational, noninterventional study. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE: Live birth per fresh embryo transfer. RESULTS: The chance of a live birth in women with RA/IBD receiving ART, compared with other women receiving ART, had an adjusted odds ratio (OR) of 0.79 (95% confidence interval [CI], 0.68-0.91). Prescribed corticosteroids before embryo transfer were positively associated with a live-born child (adjusted OR, 1.21; 95% CI, 1.12-1.31), while the use of antiinflammatory/immunosuppressive agents did not have significant importance. Intracytoplasmic sperm injection was associated with a reduced chance (adjusted OR, 0.94; 95% CI, 0.90-0.97). Type of hormone treatment protocol did not have significant importance, and transfer at the blastocyst stage was positively associated with a live-born child (adjusted OR, 1.54; 95% CI, 1.46-1.62). CONCLUSIONS: In women with RA and/or IBD, prescribed corticosteroid before embryo transfer and embryo transfer at the blastocyst stage were associated with successful ART. Intracytoplasmic sperm injection was associated with a slightly reduced chance. Antiinflammatory/immunosuppressive agents and type of hormone protocols did not have significant importance.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nørgård, Bente Mertz","Wod, Mette","Larsen, Michael Due","Friedman, Sonia","Jølving, Line Riis","Fedder, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-626403"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nørgård, Bente Mertz"],"country":["Norway","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard Medical School","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of medical therapies and factors related to treatment procedures in women with rheumatoid arthritis and inflammatory bowel disease receiving assisted reproduction a nationwide cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fertnstert.2021.07.1198","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-626403","identifier":[{"id":"85113319576","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34433518","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b98ebe23-d038-4f1e-a7e0-34ddfea373d4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-29CE9FCC1F45A5CAD724712F3230DCF1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fertnstert.2021.07.1198","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/200117982/1_s2.0_S0015028221017970_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Epidemiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"harvard medical school","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard Medical School","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Mertz","key":"nørgårdpau","last":"Nørgård","locid":"3d41d6fb-8f1c-4899-9ebd-b72f88e3935d","name":"Nørgård, Bente Mertz","orcid":"0000-0002-9514-3033","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"wodpau","last":"Wod","locid":"3e5c725a-e68c-422a-af38-8562c2fce953","name":"Wod, Mette","orcid":"0000-0001-9765-7321","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Due","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3de91a40-2cd5-40f2-b680-9ef23b0778cf","name":"Larsen, Michael Due","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-2481","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sonia","key":"friedmanpau","last":"Friedman","locid":"90853ab4-d45c-494e-978e-466b9d70d775","name":"Friedman, Sonia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Riis","key":"jølvingpau","last":"Jølving","locid":"524924f0-2e37-4535-9dd3-59630ea8c815","name":"Jølving, Line Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-7433-7656","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"fedderpau","last":"Fedder","locid":"51b716fd-ee92-46ef-8d70-04bf8995c772","name":"Fedder, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-5383-5501","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34433518"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fertnstert.2021.07.1198","issn":["00150282","15462501"],"issn_org":["00150282"],"issue":"6","journal":"Fertility and Sterility","pages":"1492-1500","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fertility and Sterility","volume":"116"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85113319576"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b98ebe23-d038-4f1e-a7e0-34ddfea373d4"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The impact of medical therapies and factors related to treatment procedures in women with rheumatoid arthritis and inflammatory bowel disease receiving assisted reproduction : a nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-626403","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Manifestations and outcomes of severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) infection are not well documented in patients with common variable immunodeficiency disorder (CVID). Methods: A Danish nationwide retrospective clinician-reported survey. Results: Eleven patients with CVID and SARS-CoV-2 infection were identified. The median age was 50 years (range 22–72). All were on immunoglobulin replacement therapy. Eight patients had other pre-existing co-morbidities. Three patients were asymptomatic during the SARS-CoV-2 infection while seven developed mild coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19). One patient had more severe disease with hypoxia and required oxygen therapy. This patient had multiple co-morbidities including well known risk factors for severe COVID-19. All patients recovered. Conclusions: The results suggest that CVID may not be a risk factor for severe COVID-19. However, further monitoring of this immunodeficient population is needed to confirm our observation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Drabe, Camilla Heldbjerg","Hansen, Alastair","Rasmussen, Line Dahlerup","Larsen, Olav Ditlevsen","Møller, Axel","Mogensen, Trine H.","Helweg-Larsen, Jannik","Katzenstein, Terese L"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-041983"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Drabe, Camilla Heldbjerg"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Common Variable Immunodeficiency","Common Variable Immunodeficiency complications","Covid 19","Denmark epidemiology","Humans","Inborn errors of immunity","Middle Aged","Morbidity","Primary immunodeficiency","Retrospective Studies","SARS CoV 2","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low morbidity in danish patients with common variable immunodeficiency disorder infected with severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 000000000002","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85112236286","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["CD: financial grants for research: Takeda; AEH: financial grants for research and a teaching salary: CSL Behring; THM is funded by a grant from The Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF21OC0067157); TLK: advisory board member or lecturer for Bristol-Myers Squibb, GlaxoSmithKline/ViiV, Jannsen, Merck Sharp & Dohme, Gilead Sciences, Chiesi, Vertex, CSLBehring, Shire and Takeda; research grant from Gilead Sciences; has participated in immunodeficiency conferences sponsored by CSLBehring, Shire and Takeda. LDR, ODL, AM, JHL: no competing interests."],"id":"S02-100.00-041983","identifier":[{"id":"34375571","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85112236286","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-45608c6c-d6e7-4e73-88d2-6142a39149c4","sdu-0fb943cd-5e34-4052-8203-27dc2f57c5d7"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","COVID-19","Common Variable Immunodeficiency/complications","Denmark/epidemiology","Humans","Middle Aged","Morbidity","Retrospective Studies","SARS-CoV-2","Young Adult","common variable immunodeficiency","inborn errors of immunity","primary immunodeficiency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-630DEEDDF479454CE379C00724011D3E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen