"Thórarinsson, Thorkell Lindberg","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Skjold","key":"tjørnløvpau","last":"Tjørnløv","locid":"a7c7b798-3999-4e50-862e-76ccfe24d56d","name":"Tjørnløv, Rune Skjold","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"17","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"wilsonpau","last":"Wilson","name":"Wilson, Simon","rank":39,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Igor","key":"eulaerspau","last":"Eulaers","locid":"f3d7c96b-a468-4a6c-a6ab-99223effd52a","name":"Eulaers, Igor","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33246245"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envint.2020.106178","issn":["01604120","18736750"],"issn_org":["01604120"],"journal":"Environment International","paperid":"106178","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Environment International","volume":"146"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096719039"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-90c994eb-4b93-4d10-9c2e-a5a653150839"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A risk assessment of the effects of mercury on Baltic Sea, Greater North Sea and North Atlantic wildlife, fish and bivalves","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-211914","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The binding of the major stress-inducible human 70-kDa heat shock protein (Hsp70) to the anionic phospholipid bis-(monoacylglycero)-phosphate (BMP) in the lysosomal membrane is crucial for its impact on cellular pathology in lysosomal storage disorders. However, the conformational features of this protein-lipid complex remain unclear. Here, we apply hydrogen–deuterium exchange mass spectrometry (HDX-MS) to describe the dynamics of the full-length Hsp70 in the cytosol and its conformational changes upon translocation into lysosomes. Using wild-type and W90F mutant proteins, we also map and discriminate the interaction of Hsp70 with BMP and other lipid components of the lysosomal membrane. We identify the N-terminal of the nucleotide binding domain (residues 87–118) as the primary orchestrator of BMP interaction. We show that the conformation of this domain is significantly reorganized in the W90F mutant, explaining its inability to stabilize lysosomal membranes. Overall, our results reveal important new molecular details of the protective effect of Hsp70 in lysosomal storage diseases, which, in turn, could guide future drug development.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Calvaresi, Valeria","Truelsen, Line T.","Larsen, Sidsel B.","Petersen, Nikolaj H. T.","Kirkegaard, Thomas","Rand, Kasper D"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-470556"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"conformational dynamics of free and membrane bound human hsp000000000070 in model cytosolic and endo lysosomal environments","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-021-02892-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-470556","identifier":[{"id":"34876699","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85120971403","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8651726","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-80cff831-1983-49cd-867c-32aadfd167a0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6E9DF510512646B261DE1CB512F4BD99"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/288114788/s42003_021_02892_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-021-02892-7","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Protein Analyse"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Orphazyme"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Valeria","key":"calvaresipau","last":"Calvaresi","locid":"9483f28d-cfc5-4115-9270-c591596f6780","name":"Calvaresi, Valeria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line T.","key":"truelsenpau","last":"Truelsen","name":"Truelsen, Line T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sidsel B.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Sidsel B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nikolaj H. T.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Nikolaj H. T.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"kirkegaardpau","last":"Kirkegaard","name":"Kirkegaard, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper D.","key":"randpau","last":"Rand","locid":"77e991c1-455a-49fc-bc8a-1f1f7804e8e9","name":"Rand, Kasper D","name_org":"Rand, Kasper D.","orcid":"0000-0002-6337-5489","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34876699"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s42003-021-02892-7","issn":["23993642"],"journal":"Communications Biology","paperid":"1369","status":"p","title":"Communications Biology","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85120971403"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","orphazyme"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-80cff831-1983-49cd-867c-32aadfd167a0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Conformational dynamics of free and membrane-bound human Hsp70 in model cytosolic and endo-lysosomal environments","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-470556","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The Danish National Register of assisted reproductive technology (ART) was initially established in 1994. The register comprises complete information on all ART procedures in public and private clinics in Denmark from 2013 and onwards, including baseline information on the cause of infertility and a number of health-related patient characteristics. The register enables monitoring and research on infertility treatment and reproductive topics in single women or couples seeking assisted reproduction, and the register is thus a key component of the Danish health information system within human reproduction. We aimed to provide an updated description of the register including advantages and pitfalls when using the register for reproductive epidemiological research, and a description of the accessibility for researchers. The Danish ART register is a valuable tool for epidemiological research. However, the inherent strengths and limitations ought to be in perspective when designing studies and interpreting the study results. Reports with annually aggregated data on ART treatments, can be accessed on the Danish Health Data Authority web page and researchers may obtain access to individual pseudonomized data via secure servers at the Danish Health Data Authority and Statistics Denmark.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jølving, Line Riis","Erb, Karin","Nørgård, Bente Mertz","Fedder, Jens","Larsen, Michael Due"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-589255"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jølving, Line Riis"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technology","Clinical epidemiology","Medical Record Linkage","Population based registries","Reproductive Epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Ukendt"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the danish national register of assisted reproductive technology content and research potentials","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85103542349","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-589255","identifier":[{"id":"33796977","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85103542349","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-382e9659-2ef4-4259-bc27-0ccd2f738d2c"],"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technology","Clinical epidemiology","Danish health registries","Medical record linkage","Population based registries","Reproductive epidemiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1171789E1AA7C0CD330D5DDF2A8BF1BE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Epidemiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Ukendt"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Riis","key":"jølvingpau","last":"Jølving","locid":"524924f0-2e37-4535-9dd3-59630ea8c815","name":"Jølving, Line Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-7433-7656","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"erbpau","last":"Erb","name":"Erb, Karin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Mertz","key":"nørgårdpau","last":"Nørgård","locid":"3d41d6fb-8f1c-4899-9ebd-b72f88e3935d","name":"Nørgård, Bente Mertz","orcid":"0000-0002-9514-3033","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"fedderpau","last":"Fedder","locid":"51b716fd-ee92-46ef-8d70-04bf8995c772","name":"Fedder, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-5383-5501","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Due","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3de91a40-2cd5-40f2-b680-9ef23b0778cf","name":"Larsen, Michael Due","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-2481","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33796977"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10654-021-00742-8","issn":["03932990","15737284"],"issn_org":["03932990"],"issue":"4","journal":"European Journal of Epidemiology","pages":"445-452","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Epidemiology","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85103542349"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-382e9659-2ef4-4259-bc27-0ccd2f738d2c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Danish National Register of assisted reproductive technology : content and research potentials","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-589255","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This report is based on an empirical study of online teaching during the lockdown of further education institutions. In the spring due to the COVID-19 pandemic. The project was a collaborative effort between Aalborg Universitet (AAU), Aarhus Universitet (AU), professionshøjskolen Absalon (PHA), Danmarks Medie- og Journalisthøjskole (DMJX), Roskilde Universitet (RUC), Syddansk Universitet (SDU), UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole (UCL), UC SYD, Professionshøjskolen UCN (UCN) og Via University Collage (VIA). Therefore, the study acquired broad insight into online teaching across several institutions. The aim of the study was to gather experiences and describe the practices that were established during the lockdown with regard to digitally supported teaching and learning. The first lockdown was unexpected and therefore the practices established during this period are not generalizable to situations other than ‘emergency teaching’ but the study will point towards possibilities within the realm of online teaching based on the experiences from the lockdown in spring. The report is extensive, covering the resources available in the institutions before and during the lockdown, the theoretical framework for the study, design and analysis in order to answer four central research questions: 1) Which variation of digitally supported didactical practices have been established across institution types and subject areas? 2) How do students experience the different practices and how do these impact different students e.g. in relation to experienced learning, learning strategies and mastery experiences? 3) How do teachers experience different practices and how do these impact the different teachers, their relations to their students as well as their experience of professional satisfaction? 4) How do the digitally supported practices affect a. collaboration between students and b. collaboration between teachers and students? The study further consists of four parts: a survey amongst 85.000 students across 9 institutions, a survey amongst 6.000 teachers across the same 9 institutions, an interview study with strategically selected respondents from the two survey studies and mapping of the institution’s systematic landscabes and organizational resources in relation to reorganization of classes to online teaching.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Georgsen, Marianne","Qvortrup, Ane","Buus, Lillian","Andersen, Ina Solveig Kjær","Asmussen, Ida Skytte","Bak, Carsten Kronborg","Dalsgaard, Christian","Geisnæs, Dorthe","Graf, Stefan Ting","Gundersen, Peter","Gynther, Karsten","Helverskov Horn, Line","Tapdrup Jensen, Søren","Jørgensen, Asbjørn","Jørnø, Rasmus Leth","Kjærgaard, Thomas","Konnerup, Ulla","Knude Larsen, Inger","Larsen, Søren","Lorentzen, Rasmus Fink","Lyngsø, Anita","Marinos, Nicolas","Nielsen, Steen","Nortvig, Anne-Mette","Dyhrberg O'Neill, Lotte","Aagaard Pallesen, Thomas","Petersson, Morten","Puck, Morten Rasmus","Rasmussen, Fie","Riis, Marianne","Ruge, Dorte","Spejlborg Sejersen, Thomas","Skovbjerg, Annegrete","Troelsen, Rie","Svenstrup Sverregaard, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-656409"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blended learning","Covid 19","Didactics","Didaktik","Learning","Læring","Læring pædagogik og undervisning","Online teaching","Online undervisning"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-DMJX","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-DMJX","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"erfaringer og oplevelser med online undervisning på 000000000009 videregående uddannelsesinstitutioner i foråret 000000002020