":"Iversen","locid":"558df261-ca9f-440a-8bee-7d38813c253f","name":"Iversen, Kasper","name_org":"Iversen, Kasper Karmark","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"garredpau","last":"Garred","locid":"854d72a7-c955-43b5-b455-b7ea1f9bcb1e","name":"Garred, Peter","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34237190"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/joim.13366","issn":["09546820","09557873"],"issn_org":["09546820"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Internal Medicine","pages":"1272-1274","status":"p","title":"Journal of Internal Medicine","volume":"290"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111854759"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-799164c6-e27f-4fcb-bb68-5f9842eec6db"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Antibody-dependent neutralizing capacity of the SARS-CoV-2 vaccine BNT162b2 with and without previous COVID-19 priming","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-466226","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Assisted reproductive technology (ART) treatments in women with underlying chronic diseases have become increasingly frequent. The objective of this review is to provide an overview of the literature examining the chance of having a live born child after ART in women with chronic diseases, compared to other women receiving ART. We focused on some of the most prevalent chronic diseases in women during their reproductive years, ie ulcerative colitis, Crohn’s disease, rheumatoid arthritis, multiple sclerosis, epilepsy, hyperthyroidism, hypothyroidism, and diabetes mellitus. Secondly, we studied the chance of successful implantation. The literature search was performed in the database Pubmed.gov. including all studies published before October 2020. Title and abstracts of 58 papers were reviewed, 37 papers were excluded and other 8 studies were excluded after full-text evaluation. Only 13 papers were eligible for review. Results indicate that women with ulcerative colitis, Crohn’s disease, rheumatoid arthritis, hyperthyroidism, and diabetes mellitus type 2 might have problems with low implantation rate or early embryo development during ART. On the contrary, the few studies on women with hypothyroidism, diabetes mellitus type 1, and epilepsy suggest an equivalent chance of a live birth compared to other women undergoing ART. A possible explanation behind these differences could reside in the disease-specific dysregulation of the innate or adaptive immune system. To our knowledge, this is the first review on ART in women with chronic diseases, and it has disclosed that the evidence in this area is indeed sparse. We encourage others to examine live birth after ART in women with chronic diseases.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nørgård, Bente Mertz","Catalini, Laura","Jølving, Line Riis","Larsen, Michael Due","Friedman, Sonia","Fedder, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-615235"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nørgård, Bente Mertz"],"country":["Norway","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brigham and Women's Hospital","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technology","Diabetes mellitus","Epilepsy","Inflammatory Bowel Diseases","Multiple sclerosis","Rheumatoid arthritis","Thyroid disease"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the efficacy of assisted reproduction in women with a wide spectrum of chronic diseases a review","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S310795","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-615235","identifier":[{"id":"85111787037","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8236837","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34194244","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-9299ff07-b0df-4e51-8d88-8ad98ef035bc"],"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technology","Diabetes mellitus","Epilepsy","Inflammatory bowel diseases","Multiple sclerosis","Rheumatoid arthritis","Thyroid disease"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9840D65C609D4623CD1ADF9EAE18F89B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/185030709/CLEP_310795_the_efficacy_of_assisted_reproduction_in_women_with_a_wide_s.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S310795","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Epidemiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"brigham and women s hospital","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Brigham and Women's Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Mertz","key":"nørgårdpau","last":"Nørgård","locid":"3d41d6fb-8f1c-4899-9ebd-b72f88e3935d","name":"Nørgård, Bente Mertz","orcid":"0000-0002-9514-3033","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"catalinipau","last":"Catalini","locid":"1c31a2fa-9fcb-4830-850e-9bb8dec6b9f2","name":"Catalini, Laura","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Riis","key":"jølvingpau","last":"Jølving","locid":"524924f0-2e37-4535-9dd3-59630ea8c815","name":"Jølving, Line Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-7433-7656","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Due","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3de91a40-2cd5-40f2-b680-9ef23b0778cf","name":"Larsen, Michael Due","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-2481","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sonia","key":"friedmanpau","last":"Friedman","locid":"90853ab4-d45c-494e-978e-466b9d70d775","name":"Friedman, Sonia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"fedderpau","last":"Fedder","locid":"51b716fd-ee92-46ef-8d70-04bf8995c772","name":"Fedder, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-5383-5501","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34194244"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2147/clep.s310795","issn":["11791349"],"journal":"Clinical Epidemiology","pages":"477-500","publisher":"Dove Medical Press","status":"p","title":"Clinical Epidemiology","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111787037"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-9299ff07-b0df-4e51-8d88-8ad98ef035bc"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The efficacy of assisted reproduction in women with a wide spectrum of chronic diseases – a review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-615235","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Aims: In the Danish population, we examined whether patients treated with thiopurines, methotrexate, systemic corticosteroids, anti-tumour necrosis factor (TNF)-α agents, anti-interleukin therapeutic agents, selective immunosuppressive agents and cyclosporine/tacrolimus had an increased risk of hospitalization for COVID- 19, compared to the background population. Methods: A nationwide cohort study including all people alive in Denmark on 1 March 2020. Exposed patients constituted those exposed to thiopurines (n = 5484), methotrexate (n = 17 977), systemic corticosteroids (n = 55 868), anti-TNF-α agents (n = 17 857), anti-interleukin therapeutic agents (n = 3744), selective immunosuppressive agents (n = 3026) and cyclosporine/tacrolimus (n = 1143) in a period of 12 months prior to 1 March 2020 (estimated time of outbreak in Denmark). We estimated the adjusted risk of hospitalization for COVID-19 for patients treated with the above-mentioned categories of medications, compared to the rest of the population. Results: The adjusted odds ratios of hospitalization in patients treated with corticosteroids and cyclosporine/tacrolimus were 1.64 (95% confidence interval [CI] 1.35 to 2.00) and 4.75 (95% CI 1.96 to 11.49), respectively. The risks of hospitalization in patients treated with thiopurines, methotrexate, and anti-TNF-α agents, were 1.93 (95% CI 0.91 to 4.08), 0.74 (95% CI 0.43 to 1.28), 1.00 (95% CI 0.52 to 1.94), respectively. The number of outcomes in patients treated with anti-interleukin therapeutic agents and selective immunosuppressive agents was too small for analysis. Conclusion: Patients treated with systemic corticosteroids and cyclosporine/tacrolimus had a significantly increased risk of being hospitalized for COVID-19. Our study does not uncover whether the increased risk is related to the drug itself, the underlying condition for which the patient is treated or other factors.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nørgård, Bente Mertz","Nielsen, Jan","Knudsen, Torben","Nielsen, Rasmus Gaardskær","Larsen, Michael Due","Jølving, Line Riis","Kjeldsen, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-624160"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nørgård, Bente Mertz"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Biologics","Clinical epidemiology","Covid 19","Hospitalization","Pharmacoepidemiology","Thiopurines"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hospitalization for covid 000000000019 in patients treated with selected immunosuppressant and immunomodulating agents compared to the general population a danish cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/174822297/bcp.14622.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-624160","identifier":[{"id":"85097029718","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33098713","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b1d250eb-ade5-457d-b025-fbcac0cfdc48"],"keyword":["COVID-19","biologics","clinical epidemiology","hospitalization","immunosuppressive","pharmacoepidemiology","thiopurines"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-770B2F93C1A1DEE95B21DB56CCE891A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/174822297/bcp.14622.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Epidemiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Mertz","key":"nørgårdbentemertzpau","last":"Nørgård","locid":"3d41d6fb-8f1c-4899-9ebd-b72f88e3935d","name":"Nørgård, Bente Mertz","orcid":"0000-0002-9514-3033","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"nielsenjanpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"014149d9-906e-4c74-ac91-2ffd5cd77a49","name":"Nielsen, Jan","orcid":"0000-0002-7634-6812","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben","key":"knudsentorbenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"afa15e36-ab82-4894-89c0-b8802310b50b","name":"Knudsen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0003-0726-0115","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Gaardskaer","key":"nielsenrasmusgaardskærpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1bfc1ab1-a1de-4993-8f2c-535fe756143b","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus Gaardskær","name_org":"Nielsen, Rasmus Gaardskaer","orcid":"0009-0000-5912-003X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Due","key":"larsenmichaelduepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3de91a40-2cd5-40f2-b680-9ef23b0778cf","name":"Larsen, Michael Due","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-2481","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Riis","key":"jølvinglineriispau","last":"Jølving","locid":"524924f0-2e37-4535-9dd3-59630ea8c815","name":"Jølving, Line Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-7433-7656","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"kjeldsenjenspau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"4893b496-ebc1-4498-92aa-836500b4cb45","name":"Kjeldsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-8148-6572","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33098713"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcp.14622","issn":["02643774","03065251"],"issn_org":["03065251"],"issue":"4","journal":"British Journal of Clinical Pharmacology","pages":"2111-2120","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Clinical Pharmacology","volume":"87"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097029718"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b1d250eb-ade5-457d-b025-fbcac0cfdc48"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Hospitalization for COVID-19 in patients treated with selected immunosuppressant and immunomodulating agents, compared to the general population : a Danish cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-624160","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this study was to examine the values of movement and physical activity (MoPA) using government policy documents (e.g., laws and curricula) on early childhood education and care (ECEC) from Denmark, Finland, Iceland, Norway, and Sweden. This descriptive, comparative study was designed based on curriculum theory and used word count and content analyses to identify similarities and differences in the occurrence of MoPA in the ECEC policies of Nordic countries. Seven terms were identified as MoPA-related in Nordic policy documents. These terms occurred in various content contexts: development, environment, expression, health and well-being, learning and play, albeit sparsely. MoPA was referred to as both a goal in and of itself and as a means of achieving other goals (e.g., learning or development in another area). Formulations specifically dedicated to MoPA as a goal were present in the Danish and Finnish curricula and, to some extent, also in the Norwegian curriculum, while the Icelandic and Swedish curricula mentioned MoPA mostly as a means. Findings indicated that MoPA, which is important for children’s development, health, and well-being, is a low-priority value, to varying degrees, in the ECEC policies enacted by Nordic countries and the guidance provided to educators and stakeholders therein is inexplicit.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Sollerhed, Ann Christin","Olesen, Line Grønholt","Froberg, Karsten","Soini, Anne","Sääkslahti, Arja","Kristjánsdóttir, Gudrún","Vilhjálmsson, Rúnar","Fjørtoft, Ingunn","Larsen, Robert","Ekberg, Jan Eric"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-632318"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sollerhed, Ann Christin"],"country":["Finland","Iceland","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University","University of Iceland","University of Jyväskylä","University of South-Eastern Norway"],"keyword":["Children","Curriculum","Early childhood education and care","Education","Movement","Nordic","Physical activity","Preschool"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Hogskolan Kristianstad"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"movement and physical activity in early childhood education and care policies of five nordic countries","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph182413226","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-632318","identifier":[{"id":"34948837","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85121119074","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8706902","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-ce47942f-b1d0-45f5-bd6a-1ef01878b4e2"],"keyword":["Children","Curriculum","Early childhood education and care","Education","Movement","Nordic","Physical activity","Preschool"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-61C090DA17F96A691AD26BD2D47A813A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/195812901/ijerph_18_13226.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph182413226","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Hogskolan Kristianstad"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3n