"Sääkslahti, Arja","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Gudrún","key":"kristjánsdóttirpau","last":"Kristjánsdóttir","name":"Kristjánsdóttir, Gudrún","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rúnar","key":"vilhjálmssonpau","last":"Vilhjálmsson","name":"Vilhjálmsson, Rúnar","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingunn","key":"fjørtoftpau","last":"Fjørtoft","name":"Fjørtoft, Ingunn","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Robert","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Eric","key":"ekbergpau","last":"Ekberg","name":"Ekberg, Jan Eric","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34948837"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ijerph182413226","issn":["16604601","16617827"],"issn_org":["16617827"],"issue":"24","journal":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","paperid":"13226","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121119074"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ce47942f-b1d0-45f5-bd6a-1ef01878b4e2"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Movement and physical activity in early childhood education and care policies of five nordic countries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-632318","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Assistive technologies in care work are expected to alleviate the challenges related to population aging, namely the pressure on public budgets and a shortage of care professionals. This study examines how various stakeholders view the potentials of assistive technology in an institutionalized care setting in Denmark. Method: Using ethnographic field observations, interviews, and document analysis, we explore the residents’, the staff’s, and the municipality’s perspectives on the technologies and analyze whether they live up to the stated expectations. Results: We identify three parallel narratives representing each of the stakeholder’s perspectives. The municipality’s triple-win narrative emphasizes expected gains in terms of efficiency, improved working conditions, and better quality of care. The staff’s ambiguity narrative contains both negative views regarding the motive for using technologies to save resources and positive accounts of how technologies have reduced work-related pain. The residents’ limited agency narrative reflects an internalization of the staff’s perspectives. Conclusions: We conclude that, despite both the staff and the municipality highlighting the residents’ well-being and comfort as important outcomes of assistive technologies, the residents’ wishes have limited influence on whether and, if so, how assistive technologies are used.IMPLICATIONS FOR REHABILITATION Different stakeholders’ views on assistive technology vary and are closely connected to their respective institutional interests and roles. These perspectives are important for a successful implementation of assistive technologies. Understanding the positions of staff and older care recipients, and differentiating between their respective perspectives can help both scholars and product developers understand the potentials and risks of AT in a more nuanced way.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Siren, Anu","Amilon, Anna","Larsen, Gabriela K.","Mehlsen, Line"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-664413"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Assistive technology","CARE","Narrative","Nursing home","Stakeholders"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the promise of assistive technology in institutionalized old age care economic efficiency improved working conditions and better quality of care","src":["vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85073794274","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-664413","identifier":[{"id":"85073794274","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["vive-a242d008-67d6-4f3a-a9da-4882fab66674"],"keyword":["Assistive technology","Care","Narrative","Nursing home","Stakeholders"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-30B927E0E57A16598469E4AA0073DB98"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","namevar":["VIVE - The Danish Center for Social Science Research, VIVE Work and Late Life"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-VIVE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anu","key":"sirenpau","last":"Siren","locid":"fc91aa1f-ce67-45f0-9f61-2a17400b0938","name":"Siren, Anu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna","key":"amilonpau","last":"Amilon","locid":"39fe7edd-14c3-4c68-9c69-f829260a988a","name":"Amilon, Anna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gabriela K.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"18502d23-075b-42d6-bdf8-ba2b333d27d0","name":"Larsen, Gabriela K.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"mehlsenpau","last":"Mehlsen","locid":"91e3d90f-6ac3-4896-9036-45bc13d7d853","name":"Mehlsen, Line","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17483107.2019.1659862","issn":["17483107","17483115"],"issn_org":["17483107"],"journal":"Disability and Rehabilitation: Assistive Technology","pages":"483-489","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Disability and Rehabilitation: Assistive Technology","volume":"16(5)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073794274"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["vive-a242d008-67d6-4f3a-a9da-4882fab66674"],"src":["VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"The promise of assistive technology in institutionalized old age care : Economic efficiency, improved working conditions, and better quality of care?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-664413","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Mærsk, Jesper Larsen","Handberg, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-083.33-014477"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Sundhed ernæring og livskvalitet"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sårbare grupper og social ulighed i den palliative og rehabiliterende indsats til mennesker med livstruende sygdomme","src":["au","pha"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-083.33-014477","ids":["au-1a0adb40-fb7d-4c94-9f79-42d754d5dfbd","pha-6944d9ef-abbf-480b-8584-317718c77666"],"keyword":["Sundhed, ernæring og livskvalitet"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-45C5C973794702C63693E7E9C45A0853"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Sundhed, Social og Engineeringområdet, Absalon - Hverdagsliv og Sundhed","Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Sundhed, Social og Engineeringområdet, Ergoterapeutuddannelsen - Næstved"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Klinisk Socialmedicin og Rehabilitering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Danish Rehabilitation Centre for Neuromuscular Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Larsen","key":"mærskpau","last":"Mærsk","locid":"498dd3b8-2091-4d8a-8316-14799fe80c52","name":"Mærsk, Jesper Larsen","orcid":"0000-0002-5290-7937","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"handbergpau","last":"Handberg","locid":"282bd838-2f69-4679-9331-15174eec2360","name":"Handberg, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-1378-2449","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Line","key":"lindahljacobsenpedh","last":"Lindahl-Jacobsen","name":"Lindahl-Jacobsen, Line","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe","key":"varningpoulsenpedh","last":"Varning Poulsen","name":"Varning Poulsen, Dorthe","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1. udg.","isbn":["9788712061762"],"pages":"205-210","place":"København","publisher":"Gad","status":"p","title":"Ergoterapi og fysioterapi i den palliative praksis"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University College Absalon","University Colleges","danish rehabilitation centre for neuromuscular diseases"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1a0adb40-fb7d-4c94-9f79-42d754d5dfbd","pha-6944d9ef-abbf-480b-8584-317718c77666"],"src":["AB University College Absalon","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Sårbare grupper og social ulighed i den palliative og rehabiliterende indsats til mennesker med livstruende sygdomme","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.33-014477","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Early diagnosis is crucial for the treatment of childhood cancer as it in some cases can prevent progression of disease and improve prognoses. However, childhood cancer can be difficult to diagnose and barriers to early diagnosis are multifactorial. New knowledge about factors influencing the pathway to diagnosis contribute to a deeper understanding of the mechanisms that influence this time span. Qualitative research in the field is sparse but can be expected to lead to additional useful insights that could contribute to efforts shorten time to diagnosis. The purpose of this study was to explore parents’ experiences of the pathway to diagnosis in the time between their noticing bodily or behavioural changes and their child’s diagnosis. Methods: The study is a qualitative interview study carried out in large Danish hospital. Thirty-two interviews with a total of 46 parents of children with cancer were included for analysis. The children were diagnosed with haematological cancers (n = 17), solid tumours (n = 9) or brain tumours (n = 6). Data were analysed applying the theoretical model of pathways to treatment and an inductive-deductive approach. A revised ‘diagnostic triage’ model was developed and validated by member checking. Results: The pathway to diagnosis was influenced by various factors which we present as consistent parts of a new diagnostic triage model. Each factor impacts the level of urgency assigned to bodily and behavioural changes by parents, general practitioners and specialists. The model of diagnostic triage was developed and validated to understand mechanisms influencing time from the point parents notice changes in their child to diagnosis. The model identifies dynamic movement between parental triage in everyday life and professional triage in a healthcare system, both affecting appraisal and case escalation according to: 1) the nature of bodily and behavioural changes, 2) parental intuition, 3) social relations, 4) professional-child-parent interaction, and 5) specialist-child-parent interaction. Conclusions: Diagnostic triage is a model which explains mechanisms that shape the pathway to diagnosis. It is a contribution aimed at supporting the clinical diagnostic process, that ultimately could ensure more timely testing, referral and diagnosis, and also a novel theoretical framework for future research on diagnostic pathways.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Pedersen, Line Hjøllund","Wahlberg, Ayo","Cordt, Marie","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-394641"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Childhood cancer","Early Diagnosis","MODEL","Parent","Primary care","Qualitative Research","Secondary Care","Theory development","Triage"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parent s perspectives of the pathway to diagnosis of childhood cancer a matter of diagnostic triage","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12913-020-05821-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-394641","identifier":[{"id":"33092610","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85093832048","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7584100","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-01ede940-f667-4f2f-998e-25904694b23a"],"keyword":["Childhood cancer","Diagnostic pathway","Early diagnosis","Model","Parent","Primary care","Qualitative research","Secondary care","Theory development","Triage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6CCF74993F76236BF15B06635DC75458"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12913-020-05821-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250966061/s12913_020_05821_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Asian Dynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line Hjøllund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Line Hjøllund","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ayo","key":"wahlbergpau","last":"Wahlberg","locid":"c1114f6e-8a86-4e8b-a7f7-db6ac7b914d5","name":"Wahlberg, Ayo","orcid":"0000-0001-6862-5208","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie","key":"cordtpau","last":"Cordt","name":"Cordt, Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kjeld","key":"schmiegelowpau","last":"Schmiegelow","locid":"6ce2f948-244d-4f19-82aa-f08a71289674","name":"Schmiegelow, Kjeld","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Susanne Oksbjerg","key":"daltonpau","last":"Dalton","locid":"84d10468-fe5d-4cc7-952f-1d89d961390f","name":"Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne Bækgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"88b48e37-454f-41e8-a110-a385dce66a6e","name":"Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33092610"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12913-020-05821-2","issn":["14726963"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Health Services Research","paperid":"969","status":"p","title":"BMC Health Services Research","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85093832048"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-01ede940-f667-4f2f-998e-25904694b23a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Parent’s perspectives of the pathway to diagnosis of childhood cancer : a matter of diagnostic triage","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-394641","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Mercaptopurine (6MP) is essential to cure childhood acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL). A liquid 6MP formulation was recently introduced to facilitate oral 6MP administration, especially to children. Its approval and bioequivalence with 6MP tablet were based on comparative pharmacokinetics in 60 healthy adults. Due to potential pharmacokinetic differences between healthy adults and children with ALL, we compared pharmacokinetics of tablet and liquid 6MP formulations in children with ALL. METHODS: Pharmacokinetics of 50 mg 6MP tablet (Puri-Nethol®) and 20 mg/ml 6MP liquid suspension (Xaluprine®) were compared in a non-blinded, random order, single-dose, cross-over study in 16 children with ALL (eight males). 6MP was administered after a 12 h fast, and 6MP plasma concentrations measured consecutively over seven hours post-dose. Pharmacokinetic outcomes were as follows: Area under the curve (AUC), maximum plasma concentration (Cmax), time to maximum plasma concentration (Tmax), and terminal half-life (T½). RESULTS: Liquid 6MP formulation resulted in a 26% lower AUC (p = 0.02) compared with tablet (median 1215 vs. 1805 h × nmol/l). No significant differences were observed for Cmax,Tmax and T½ (p = 0.28, p = 0.09, p = 0.41, respectively). Based on criteria declared by the World Health Organization the results did not establish non-inferiority of liquid 6MP formulation compared with 6MP tablet. CONCLUSION: Non-inferiority of liquid 6MP formulation compared with 6MP tablet was not demonstrated. Yet, maintenance therapy doses are adjusted by degree of myelosuppression and not by 6MP dose. Thus, in spite of a lower bioavailability, a liquid 6MP formulation is still desirable in a clinical setting, especially for children. However, if shifting between 6MP formulation is indicated, dose adjustments should be anticipated to maintain equivalent treatment intensity in children with ALL. The study is registered on clinicaltrials.gov (NCT01906671). Date of registration: 24.07.13.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Larsen, Rikke Hebo","Hjalgrim, Lisa Lyngsie","Grell, Kathrine","Kristensen, Kim","Pedersen, Line Gerner","Brünner, Emilie Damgaard","Als-Nielsen, Bodil","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Nersting, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434929"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pharmacokinetics of tablet and liquid formulations of oral 000000000006 mercaptopurine in children with acute lymphoblastic leukemia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-434929","identifier":[{"id":"32519032","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85086166537","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-45899bf4-1ff7-450b-909a-11ce4938518d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7F979A238956D5B8C6CB098A3B44D42E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"aff