","name":"Nikolajsen, Lone","orcid":"0000-0002-2705-7088","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle","key":"rømerpau","last":"Rømer","locid":"fa53187b-aec8-4015-b3ee-1b8df7fe506f","name":"Rømer, Helle","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maiken Bay","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","name":"Ravn, Maiken Bay","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingerlise","key":"rønfeldtpau","last":"Rønfeldt","locid":"abd0211d-598b-4ef9-bca8-c6597538b635","name":"Rønfeldt, Ingerlise","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1eaf23a5-c12f-437c-8283-3b4af0f57975"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"National Klinisk retningslinje for perioperativ behandling, pleje og tidlig rehabilitering til patienter som får foretaget større benamputationer","type":"Memorandum/Exposition","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-146904","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background Complex treatment, care and rehabilitation require continuous healthcare professional development and maintenance of competencies in collaboration with other professionals. Interprofessional education in childhood cancer involves several groups of healthcare professionals with both general and specific knowledge and skills. Objective To establish consensus on content and interprofessional learning objectives for an interprofessional education in childhood cancer. Design A three-round Delphi survey in Scandinavian childhood cancer departments. Participants Healthcare professionals appointed by their head of departments and head nurses based on their profession and their involvement in continuing professional development. Main outcome measures A prioritised list of interprofessional learning objectives with a mean score of ≥3 on a five-point scale (1=not relevant, 5=extremely relevant). Results 12 childhood cancer departments participated with 30 healthcare professionals: 11 nurses, 10 medical doctors, 5 social workers, 2 physiotherapists and 2 pedagogues. In total, 28 (93%), 25 (83%) and 22 (73%) completed the first, second and third round, respectively. In the first round, we asked open-ended questions and used directed content analysis to analyse 386 statements. We formulated 170 interprofessional learning objectives in six categories: (1) acute life-threatening situations, (2) gastrointestinal toxicities and side effects, (3) pain, (4) palliation, (5) play and activity, and (6) prescription and administration of medicine. The second round resulted in 168 interprofessional learning objectives receiving a mean score of ≥3 on a five-point scale. Final agreement in the third round resulted in a prioritised list of 168 learning objectives. Conclusions Consensus on content and interprofessional learning objectives for an interprofessional education in childhood cancer was established across five groups of healthcare professionals in three countries. Some learning objectives are generic and can be applied in settings other than childhood cancer, where healthcare professionals collaborate to provide patients and families optimal treatment and care.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Topperzer, Martha Krogh","Thellesen, Line","Hoffmann, Marianne","Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","Weibel, Mette","Lausen, Birgitte","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Sørensen, Jette Led"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-481251"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Haematology","Medical education","Oncology","multidisciplinary team care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"establishment of consensus on content and learning objectives for an interprofessional education in childhood cancer a delphi survey","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjpo-2019-000634","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-481251","identifier":[{"id":"32342017","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85083067393","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7173955","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-92f865af-a7ce-4a7d-8cb1-cbd3fc13c2ca"],"keyword":["haematology","medical education","multidisciplinary team-care","oncology","paediatric practice"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B7450D84CEE31C17F75E0715EA47BCCE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjpo-2019-000634","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/251018035/Establishment_of_consensus_on_content.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, No speciality"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martha Krogh","key":"topperzerpau","last":"Topperzer","name":"Topperzer, Martha Krogh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"thellesenpau","last":"Thellesen","name":"Thellesen, Line","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne","key":"hoffmannpau","last":"Hoffmann","name":"Hoffmann, Marianne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne Baekgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"88b48e37-454f-41e8-a110-a385dce66a6e","name":"Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","name_org":"Larsen, Hanne Baekgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette","key":"weibelpau","last":"Weibel","name":"Weibel, Mette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birgitte","key":"lausenpau","last":"Lausen","name":"Lausen, Birgitte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kjeld","key":"schmiegelowpau","last":"Schmiegelow","locid":"6ce2f948-244d-4f19-82aa-f08a71289674","name":"Schmiegelow, Kjeld","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jette Led","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"84ce4092-8277-45c1-89d5-afedea9c65f0","name":"Sørensen, Jette Led","orcid":"0000-0002-7320-2784","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32342017"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjpo-2019-000634","issn":["23999772"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMJ Paediatrics Open","paperid":"e000634","status":"p","title":"BMJ Paediatrics Open","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083067393"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-92f865af-a7ce-4a7d-8cb1-cbd3fc13c2ca"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Establishment of consensus on content and learning objectives for an interprofessional education in childhood cancer : A Delphi survey","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-481251","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"AIMS/HYPOTHESIS: Type 1 and type 2 diabetes are among the most prevalent chronic diseases in women in the fertile years and women with diabetes may experience several reproductive issues. We aimed to examine the chance of biochemical pregnancy, clinical pregnancy and live birth after assisted reproductive technology (ART) treatment in women with type 1 and type 2 diabetes and whether obesity per se influenced the results. METHODS: This nationwide register-based cohort study is based on the Danish ART Registry comprising 594 women with either type 1 diabetes or type 2 diabetes from 2006 to 2017. RESULTS: Relative to women without diabetes, the adjusted OR (95% CI) of a live birth per embryo transfer was 0.50 (0.36, 0.71) in women with type 2 diabetes and 1.10 (0.86, 1.41) in women with type 1 diabetes. CONCLUSIONS/INTERPRETATION: Our data on the efficacy of ART treatment in women with type 1 and type 2 diabetes is the first in this field. When compared with women without diabetes, women with type 1 diabetes had an equivalent chance of a live birth per embryo transfer whereas women with type 2 diabetes had a reduced chance. The findings in women with type 2 diabetes did not seem to be driven by obesity per se as the same pattern was seen in both normal-weight and obese women. Graphical abstract.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Michael Due","Jensen, Dorte Møller","Fedder, Jens","Jølving, Line Riis","Nørgård, Bente Mertz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-590209"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technology","Body Mass Index","Cohort study","Denmark","Embryo Transfer","Epidemiology","In vitro fertilisation","Infertility","Type 1 diabetes","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"live born children after assisted reproduction in women with type 000000000001 diabetes and type 000000000002 diabetes a nationwide cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-020-05193-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-590209","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7406522","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85089115456","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32548699","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-3b44bed4-d1d1-4924-b6ac-3814b0c393ae"],"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technology","Body mass index","Cohort study","Denmark","Embryo transfer","Epidemiology","In vitro fertilisation","Infertility","Type 1 diabetes","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78D235F3BB343B25C7905A2E6070E2F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-020-05193-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170823621/Larsen2020_Article_Live_bornChildrenAfterAssisted.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Epidemiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Due","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3de91a40-2cd5-40f2-b680-9ef23b0778cf","name":"Larsen, Michael Due","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-2481","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a221b393-70f9-4f53-902e-63d1a13f8f60","name":"Jensen, Dorte Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-3298-9824","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"fedderpau","last":"Fedder","locid":"51b716fd-ee92-46ef-8d70-04bf8995c772","name":"Fedder, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-5383-5501","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Riis","key":"jølvingpau","last":"Jølving","locid":"524924f0-2e37-4535-9dd3-59630ea8c815","name":"Jølving, Line Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-7433-7656","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Mertz","key":"nørgårdpau","last":"Nørgård","locid":"3d41d6fb-8f1c-4899-9ebd-b72f88e3935d","name":"Nørgård, Bente Mertz","orcid":"0000-0002-9514-3033","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32548699"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00125-020-05193-6","issn":["0012186X","14320428"],"issn_org":["0012186X"],"issue":"9","journal":"Diabetologia","pages":"1736-1744","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"p","title":"Diabetologia","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089115456"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3b44bed4-d1d1-4924-b6ac-3814b0c393ae"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Live-born children after assisted reproduction in women with type 1 diabetes and type 2 diabetes : a nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-590209","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Preventive health checks targeted at the at-risk population can be a way of preventing noncommunicable diseases. However, evidence on patient preferences for preventive health checks is limited, especially among patients with a high risk of noncommunicable diseases. Objective: To examine patient preferences for preventive health checks in Danish general practice, targeting persons at high risk of a noncommunicable disease. Methods: The method used in this study was a discrete choice experiment (DCE) with five attributes: Assess, advice, agree, assist and arrange. The attributes were inspired by the 5A model for behaviour change counselling but was altered for the purpose of this study to grasp the entirety of the general practice-based intervention. Moreover, the attribute levels were defined to resemble daily clinical practice. The experimental design of the DCE was an efficient Bayesian main effects design and the results were analysed using a random utility theory framework. Results: A total of 148 patients completed the DCE. Patients at high risk of a noncommunicable disease have positive preferences for: Giving brief explanations about own lifestyle, practicing shared decision-making with the general practitioner (GP), follow-up counselling with the GP after the preventive health check and scheduling a new appointment right after the preventive health check. Conclusions: The results provide Danish GPs with evidence on their patients' preferences towards preventive health checks which will enable the GPs to tailor these consultations. Moreover, the results suggest that pre-appointment measures, such as a health profile, may mediate a preference for more action-oriented attributes.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bruun Larsen, Lars","Thilsing, Trine","Pedersen, Line Bjørnskov"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-634613"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bruun Larsen, Lars"],"keyword":["Chronic Disease","Doctor patient relationship","Prevention","Primary care","Risk Assessment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient preferences for preventive health checks in danish general practice a discrete choice experiment among patients at high risk of noncommunicable diseases","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/fampra/cmaa038","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-634613","identifier":[{"id":"32311022","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85093878010","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7750959","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-d65d4d17-e839-45cb-b40c-de93ad4f19c3"],"keyword":["Chronic disease","doctor–patient relationship","lifestyle modification/health behaviour change","prevention","primary care","risk assessment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0A97E1D47BDC3FBB3774FA05568A2D2A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/fampra/cmaa038","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/174648239/cmaa038_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Bruun","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1418e278-0f71-406e-b479-3429aca4b01d","name":"Bruun Larsen, Lars","name_org":"Larsen, Lars Bruun","orcid":"0000-0001-9120-4751","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine","key":"thilsingpau","last":"Thilsing","locid":"6ae25242-1e96-48cf-ab01-cbac26690f6b","name":"Thilsing, Trine","orcid":"0000-0002-2041-2219","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Bjørnskov","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"b2346680-b60a-41e8-9332-304171fab9be","name":"Pedersen, Line Bjørnskov","orcid":"0000-0001-6804-2045","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32311022"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/fampra/cmaa038","issn":["02632136","14602229"],"issn_org":["02632136"],"issue":"5","journal":"Family Practice","pages":"689-694","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Family Practice","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85093878010"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d65d4d17-e839-45cb-b40c-de93ad4f19c3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Patient preferences for preventive health checks in Danish general practice : a discrete choice experiment among patients at high risk of noncommunicable diseases","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-634613","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Genetic testing has become a routine part of the diagnostic workup in children with early onset epilepsies. In the present study, we sought to investigate a cohort of adult patients with epilepsy, to determinate the diagnostic yield and explore the gain of personalized treatment approaches in adult patients. Methods: Two hundred patients (age span = 18-80 years) referred for diagnostic gene panel testing at the Danish Epilepsy Center were included. The vast majority (91%) suffered from comorbid intellectual disability. The medical records of genetically diagnosed patients were mined for data on epilepsy syndrome, cognition, treatment changes, and seizure outcome following the genetic diagnosis. Results: We found a genetic diagnosis in 46 of 200 (23%) patients. SCN1A, KCNT1, and STXBP1 accounted for the greatest number of positive findings (48%). More rare genetic findings included SLC2A1, ATP6A1V, HNRNPU, MEF2C, and IRF2BPL. Gene-specific treatment changes were initiated in 11 of 46 (17%) patients (one with SLC2A1, 10 with SCN1A) following the genetic diagnosis. Ten patients improved, with seizure reduction and/or increased alertness and general well-being. Significance: With this study, we show that routine diagnostic testing is highly relevant in adults with epilepsy. The diagnostic yield is similar to previously reported pediatric cohorts, and the genetic findings can be useful for therapeutic decision-making, which may lead to better seizure control, ultimately improving quality of life.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Johannesen, Katrine M.","Nikanorova, Natalya","Marjanovic, Dragan","Pavbro, Agnieszka","Larsen, Line H.G.","Rubboli, Guido","Møller, Rikke S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-645664"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Johannesen, Katrine M."],"keyword":["ADULTS","Gene panel","Genetic Testing","NGS"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-FILA"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-FILA","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"utility of genetic testing for therapeutic decision making in adults with epilepsy","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170280971/epi.16533.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-645664","identifier":[{"id":"85085014936","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32427350","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-fd326b0e-a657-402b-98e5-538b4db96a03"],"keyword":["NGS","adults","gene panel","genetic testing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-457C64AB86912712251CCFA01209F317"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170280971/epi.16533.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - The Epilepsyhospital Filadelfia, Research Unit of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine (Dianalund)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"filadelfia danish epilepsy hospital","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-FILA","l3nn":"Filadelfia - Danish Epilepsy Hospital","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Filadelfia - Danish Epilepsy Hospital","namevar":["Epilepsihospitalet Filadelfia"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-FILA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Amplexa Genetics A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine M.","key":"johannesenpau","last":"Johannesen","locid":"89bb9eac-d981-4e12-a3d2-29c42f22ea7e","name":"Johannesen, Katrine M.","orcid":"0000-0002-7356-3109","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalya","key":"nikanorovapau","last":"Nikanorova","name":"Nikanorova, Natalya","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dragan","key":"marjanovicpau","last":"Marjanovic","name":"Marjanovic, Dragan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Agnieszka","key":"pavbropau","last":"Pavbro","name":"Pavbro, Agnieszka","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Line H.G.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Line H.G.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Guido","key":"rubbolipau","last":"Rubboli","name":"Rubboli, Guido","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke S.","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"85de2fa9-456c-4427-8c30-7dc1bdd4bcf0","name":"Møller, Rikke S.","orcid":"0000-0002-9664-1448","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32427350"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/epi.16533","issn":["00139580","15281167"],"issn_org":["00139580"],"issue":"6","journal":"Epilepsia","pages":"1234-1239","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Epilepsia","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085014936"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","amplexa genetics a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-fd326b0e-a657-402b-98e5-538b4db96a03"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Utility of genetic testing for therapeutic decision-making in adults with epilepsy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-645664","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The Na+/H+ exchanger-1 (NHE1) supports tumour growth, making NHE1 inhibitors of interest in anticancer therapy, yet their molecular effects are incompletely characterized. Here, we demonstrate that widely used pyrazinoylguanidine-type NHE1 inhibitors potently inhibit growth and survival of cancer cell spheroids, in a manner unrelated to NHE1 inhibition. Cancer and non-cancer cells were grown as 3-dimensional (3D) spheroids and treated with pyrazinoylguanidine-type (amiloride, 5-(N-ethyl-N-isopropyl)-amiloride (EIPA), 5-(N,N-dimethyl)-amiloride (DMA), and 5-(N,N-hexamethylene)-amiloride (HMA)) or benzoylguanidine-type (eniporide, cariporide) NHE1 inhibitors for 2-7 days, followed by analyses of viability, compound accumulation, and stress- and death-associated signalling. EIPA, DMA and HMA dose-dependently reduced breast cancer spheroid viability while cariporide and eniporide had no effect. Although both compound types inhibited NHE1, the toxic effects were NHE1-independent, as inhibitor-induced viability loss was unaffected by NHE1 CRISPR/Cas9 knockout. EIPA and HMA accumulated extensively in spheroids, and this was associated with marked vacuolization, apparent autophagic arrest, ER stress, mitochondrial- and DNA damage and poly-ADP-ribose-polymerase (PARP) cleavage, indicative of severe stress and paraptosis-like cell death. Pyrazinoylguanidine-induced cell death was partially additive to that induced by conventional anticancer therapies and strongly additive to extracellular-signal-regulated-kinase (ERK) pathway inhibition. Thus, in addition to inhibiting NHE1, pyrazinoylguanidines exert potent, NHE1-independent cancer cell death, pointing to a novel relevance for these compounds in anticancer therapy.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rolver, Michala G.","Elingaard-Larsen, Line O.","Andersen, Anne Poder","Counillon, Laurent","Pedersen, Stine Helene Falsig"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-489735"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Côte d'Azur"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pyrazine ring based na sup sup h sup sup exchanger nhe inhibitors potently inhibit cancer cell growth in 000000000003d culture independent of nhe000000000001","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-62430-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-489735","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7118118","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32242030","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85082901388","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a1086f7e-8435-462f-9b51-1cf7a85a48be"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0A71F95E3830BD7EE5B37D6A27E5ED0C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-62430-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/239813350/s41598_020_62430_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Cell Biology and Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"university of côte d azur","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Côte d'Azur","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Michala G.","key":"rolverpau","last":"Rolver","locid":"e61a699a-cf7a-479e-8cf1-9fd071540db0","name":"Rolver, Michala G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Line O.","key":"elingaardlarsenpau","last":"Elingaard-Larsen","locid":"0cdfcf12-6832-4b3a-8454-802e6c5790ff","name":"Elingaard-Larsen, Line O.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne P.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"14758998-867e-4472-8d12-b0974eded710","name":"Andersen, Anne Poder","name_org":"Andersen, Anne P.","orcid":"0000-0002-6693-1524","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Laurent","key":"counillonpau","last":"Counillon","name":"Counillon, Laurent","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stine F.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"1d5a844a-2526-46ea-9662-94eccb5854ea","name":"Pedersen, Stine Helene Falsig","name_org":"Pedersen, Stine F.","orcid":"0000-0002-3044-7714","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32242030"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-020-62430-z","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"5800","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082901388"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a1086f7e-8435-462f-9b51-1cf7a85a48be"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pyrazine ring-based Na<sup>+</sup>/H<sup>+</sup> exchanger (NHE) inhibitors potently inhibit cancer cell growth in 3D culture, independent of NHE1","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-489735","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Omkring 1940 var konservering og restaurering en meget lille del af Nationalmuseets virke. Der var ansat få håndværksuddannede og sidemandsoplærte konservatorer. I løbet af de sidste 80 år har dette ændret sig markant til, at der i dag er en stab på 40-50 årsværk af akademisk uddannede konservatorer, der varetager en lang række forskellige opgaver. Opgaverne består bl.a. i at konservere og restaurere Nationalmuseets genstande, at holde styr på museets magasiner med 42.000 m3 genstande, at overvåge og optimere klimaforholdene i magasiner og udstillinger, at montere genstande i forbindelse med udstillinger samt at administrere museets udlån af genstande til ind- og udland. Hertil kommer, at en betydelig del af museets konservatorer udfører en bred vifte af konserveringsfaglige opgaver for eksterne kunder i ind- og udland. Det er med til at opretholde og udvikle bredden af de konserveringsfaglige specialer til gavn for Nationalmuseet og vores fælles kulturarv. En af Nationalmuseets prominente konservatorer, Børge Brorson Christensen (1913-89), skrev for godt 40 år siden: “Det er en udbredt anskuelse, at er en ting kommet på museum, er den sikret for tid og evighed. Dette er kun en illusion.” Dette udsagn gælder stadig.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bregnhøi, Line","Brajer, Isabelle Eve","Klenz Larsen, Poul","Schmidt, Anne Lisbeth","Strætkvern, Kristiane"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-548462"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"konservering og restaurering på nationalmuseet nationalmuseets arbejdsmark 000000001940 000000002020","src":["kum"],"src-code":["DI-GV-KUM"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-548462","ids":["kum-57f9dedc-da41-4650-8954-86d98e6e183d"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D9E19CD1482AF3B3A3E7E15780925D82"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kum ministry of culture archives museums and royal library denmark","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-KUM","l3nn":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","namevar":["Ministry of Culture Denmark, The National Museum of Denmark","Ministry of Culture Denmark, The National Museum of Denmark, Buildings and Artefacts Conservation"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-KUM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"bregnhøipau","last":"Bregnhøi","locid":"7c75a960-cee9-4786-b01d-27b7ea8589e6","name":"Bregnhøi, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Isabelle","key":"brajerpau","last":"Brajer","locid":"7aeda82b-5f8b-44bf-b448-e5b067544cef","name":"Brajer, Isabelle Eve","name_org":"Brajer, Isabelle","orcid":"0000-0002-8236-8460","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul","key":"klenzlarsenpau","last":"Klenz Larsen","locid":"da7b64a3-e8d7-4599-8114-fc1b9eda46d1","name":"Klenz Larsen, Poul","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Lisbeth","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"0c401f8b-585a-4743-83e6-23f7f44984fd","name":"Schmidt, Anne Lisbeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristiane","key":"strætkvernpau","last":"Strætkvern","locid":"6edb86b7-91bc-4889-b3f4-dde13c25ae56","name":"Strætkvern, Kristiane","orcid":"0009-0008-1649-9076","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"kristianmadsenpedh","last":"Kristian Madsen","name":"Kristian Madsen, Per","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ingeborg","key":"zachorathpedh","last":"Zacho Rath","name":"Zacho Rath, Ingeborg","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ingrid","key":"wasspedh","last":"Wass","name":"Wass, Ingrid","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["978 87 408 3303 4"],"pages":"149-177","place":"Odense","publisher":"Syddansk Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"Nationalmuseets Arbejdsmark 1940-2020"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kum-57f9dedc-da41-4650-8954-86d98e6e183d"],"src":["KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark"],"title":"Konservering og restaurering på Nationalmuseet: Nationalmuseets Arbejdsmark 1940-2020","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-548462","year":"2020","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: ECG changes after revascularization predicts improved outcome for patients with ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI). Worst lead residual (WLR) ST deviation and resolution of worst lead ST elevation (rST elevation) are simple measures that can be obtained early after PCI. The objective of the current study was to investigate whether simple ECG measures, obtained one hour following PCI, could predict cardiac magnetic resonance (CMR)-derived myocardial salvage index (MSI), infarct size (IS), and microvascular obstruction (MVO) in patients with STEMI included in the MITOCARE trial. Methods: The MITOCARE trial included 165 patients with a first-time STEMI presenting within six hours of symptom onset. The current analysis included patients that had an ECG recorded at baseline and one hour after PCI and underwent CMR imaging after 3–5 days. Independent core laboratories determined WLR ST deviation, rST elevation, and the CMR variables (MSI, IS, and MVO). Results: 83 patients with a mean age of 61 years were included. 83.1% were males and 41% had anterior infarctions. In logistic regression models, WLR ST deviation was a statistically significant predictor of IS (OR 2.2, 95% CI 1.3–3.8) and MVO (OR 2.8, 95% CI 1.5–5.2), but not of MSI (OR 0.8, 95% CI 0.5–1.2). rST elevation showed a trend toward a significant association with IS (OR 0.3, 95% CI 0.1–1.0), but not with the other CMR variables. Conclusion: WLR ST deviation one hour after PCI was a predictor of IS and MVO. WLR ST deviation, a measure easily obtained from ECGs following PCI, may provide important prognostic information in patients with STEMI.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Stensjøen, Anne Line","Hommerstad, Anders","Halvorsen, Sigrun","Arheden, Håkan","Engblom, Henrik","Erlinge, David","Larsen, Alf Inge","Sejersten Ripa, Maria","Clemmensen, Peter","Atar, Dan","Hall, Trygve S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-584828"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Stensjøen, Anne Line"],"country":["Germany","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Oslo University Hospital","Stavanger University hospital","University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","University of Bergen","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Cardiac magnetic resonance","Cardiology","Electrocardiography","ST elevation myocardial infarction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"worst lead st deviation and resolution of st elevation at one hour for prediction of myocardial salvage infarct size and microvascular obstruction in patients with st elevation myocardial infarction treated with primary percutaneous coronary intervention","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/anec.12784","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The MITOCARE project was supported by the European Union under the 7th Framework Programme ‐ Grant Agreement HEALTH‐2010‐261034. The current study did not receive any additional grants from funding agencies in the public, commercial, or not‐for‐profit sectors."],"id":"S01-000.00-584828","identifier":[{"id":"32592427","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85087295809","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7679835","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-287d6ae8-14cc-4119-813b-fbf75c061777"],"keyword":["ST-elevation myocardial infarction","cardiac magnetic resonance","cardiology","electrocardiography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BA51A