{"abstract":"We propose a novel method to co-train deep convolutional neural networks for data sets of differing position specific data. This is an advantage in chemometrics where individual measurements represent exact chemical compounds, e.g. for given wavelengths, and thus signals cannot be translated or resized without disturbing their interpretation. Our approach outperforms transfer learning for three small data sets co-trained with a medium sized data set.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Jacob Søgaard","Clemmensen, Line Katrine Harder"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-375126"],"event":{"end":"2020-05-08","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2020-05-04","title":"2020 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deep learning","Spectroscopic data","Transfer learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"weight sharing and deep learning for spectral data","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85089224015","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The research is partially funded by BIOPRO (www.biopro.nu) which is financed by the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF), Region Zealand (Denmark) and BIOPRO partners. The research is partially funded by BIOPRO (www.biopro.nu) which is financed by the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF), Region Zealand (Denmark) and BIOPRO partners. The Innovation Fund Denmark grant 5153-00004B “DABAI – Danish Center for Big Data Analytics driven Innovation” is thanked for the support for travel and conference expenses. We would like to acknowledge the Walloon Agricultural Research Centre (CRA-W, Chaussée de Namur 15, 5030 Gembloux, Belgium) for providing the test data for the Chimiometrie 2018 and 2019 data sets used in the study."],"id":"S01-000.00-375126","identifier":[{"id":"85089224015","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ebce48f0-dc48-4030-b036-0eaf5aa4ea96"],"keyword":["Co-training","Deep Learning","Spectroscopic data","Transfer Learning","Weight Sharing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6A43FEA104B3AF668423A5D184BE4F90"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Statistics and Data Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Sogaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e187fab0-e41e-4d83-95fa-a47ceb325653","name":"Larsen, Jacob Søgaard","name_org":"Larsen, Jacob Sogaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"4e7ff76e-13f9-4365-83b1-d10bab96517b","name":"Clemmensen, Line Katrine Harder","name_org":"Clemmensen, Line","orcid":"0000-0001-5527-5798","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icassp40776.2020.9053918","eisbn":["9781509066315"],"issn":["15206149"],"pages":"4227-4231","publisher":"IEEE","series":"ICASSP, IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing - Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2020 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089224015"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ebce48f0-dc48-4030-b036-0eaf5aa4ea96"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Weight Sharing and Deep Learning for Spectral Data","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-375126","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Gut microbiota composition correlates strongly with essential disease parameters in the oxazolone-induced mouse model for atopic dermatitis. The phenotype of this model can be transferred to germ-free mice with a gut microbiota transplant to achieve high and low responding mice. Therefore, the production of high responding mice through gut microbiota transplantation may be seen as a tool to reduce group sizes or increase power in intervention studies by increasing effect size. We sought to determine whether high responding mice respond to a common treatment in the same way as low responding mice. We hypothesized that while high responding mice would exhibit a higher clinical score than low responding mice before treatment, the clinical parameters would be similar in both groups after betamethasone treatment. Dermatitis was induced with oxazolone in barrier bred Swiss Webster mice, and a high responding and a low responding donor was selected based upon clinical and pathologic scores, as confirmed by monitoring a range of ear tissue cytokines. Feces from these donors were transplanted to pregnant germ-free Swiss Webster dams, and subsequently to their offspring. Although the overall effect of betamethasone on the clinical dermatitis score and ear thickness was rather small, the high responding recipients had significantly higher clinical dermatitis score and ear thickness than the low responding recipients before treatment, and these differences vanished after betamethasone treatment. We conclude that high responding recipients can be treated to a clinical level comparable with the low responding recipients.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Debes, Karina Poulsdóttir","Evdina, Nathalie A","Laigaard, Ann","Larsen, Julie M","Zachariassen, Line F.","Hansen, Camilla Hartmann Friis","Hansen, Axel Kornerup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-452376"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"betamethasone treatment for atopic dermatitis in gut microbiota transplanted mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7024782/pdf/cm20200006.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-452376","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7024782","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31744592","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85088884707","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-628723f4-5f99-4808-82ad-14b89e8be179"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7C41C7B6E54785C586C0E3A8F01C1021"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7024782/pdf/cm20200006.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Lifepharm","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Preclinical Disease Biology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, The Graduate Programme for In Vivo Pharmacology and Experimental Animals"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Karina P","key":"debeskarinapoulsdóttirpau","last":"Debes","locid":"a2ae489f-2e5e-4ae7-8ec6-52dceeddd040","name":"Debes, Karina Poulsdóttir","name_org":"Debes, Karina P","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Nathalie A","key":"evdinanathalieapau","last":"Evdina","locid":"f015741b-9224-44c3-b547-08144351be94","name":"Evdina, Nathalie A","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ann","key":"laigaardannpau","last":"Laigaard","locid":"1333015e-a5a0-4fbb-9e8b-6974cf20b1c6","name":"Laigaard, Ann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julie M","key":"larsenjuliempau","last":"Larsen","locid":"98df10b8-e185-4735-89bd-e3226a2ffb7d","name":"Larsen, Julie M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line F","key":"zachariassenlinefpau","last":"Zachariassen","locid":"cdafe75d-cfc9-4fca-adfe-20ae0c542b57","name":"Zachariassen, Line F.","name_org":"Zachariassen, Line F","orcid":"0000-0001-5425-9841","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla H F","key":"hansencamillahartmannfriispau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d7f25dbd-3efc-483b-9805-8909e9597652","name":"Hansen, Camilla Hartmann Friis","name_org":"Hansen, Camilla H F","orcid":"0000-0002-1860-385X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Axel K","key":"hansenaxelkorneruppau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ecc439ea-5c9b-4e25-814a-3ee8960bc0d0","name":"Hansen, Axel Kornerup","name_org":"Hansen, Axel K","orcid":"0000-0003-1575-2507","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31744592"],"pub":{"doi":"10.30802/aalas-cm-18-000136","issn":["15320820"],"issue":"1","journal":"Comparative Medicine","pages":"6-15","status":"p","title":"Comparative Medicine","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088884707"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-628723f4-5f99-4808-82ad-14b89e8be179"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Betamethasone Treatment for Atopic Dermatitis in Gut Microbiota Transplanted Mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-452376","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Introduction The use of capsule endoscopy has become an approved method in small bowel diagnostics, but the same level of integration is not seen in large bowel diagnostics. We will use colon capsule endoscopy (CCE) as a filter test in colorectal cancer (CRC) screening between the faecal immunochemical test (FIT) and colonoscopy. We aim to investigate the clinical performance, population acceptability, and economic implications of the procedure in a large-scale clinical trial. Methods and analysis We will randomly allocate 124 214 Danish citizens eligible for participation in the national CRC screening programme within the Region of Southern Denmark to either an intervention group or a control group. Prior to submitting a FIT, citizens randomised to the intervention group will be informed about their opportunity to undergo CCE, instead of colonoscopy, if the FIT is positive. Suspected cancers; >3 adenomas <10 mm in size, 1 adenoma >10 mm in size or >4 adenomas regardless of size, detected during CCE will generate an invitation to colonoscopy as per regular screening guidelines, whereas citizens with suspected low risk polyps will re-enter the biennial screening programme. Citizens with no CCE findings will be excluded from screening for 8 years. In the control group, citizens will follow standard screening procedures. Ethics and dissemination All participants must consent prior to capsule ingestion. All collected data will be handled and stored in accordance with current data protection legislation. Approvals from the regional ethics committee (ref. S-20190100) and the Danish data protection agency have been obtained (ref. 19/29858). Trial registration details The study has been registered with ClinicalTrials.gov under: NCT04049357.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Kaalby, Lasse","Deding, Ulrik","Kobaek-Larsen, Morten","Havshoi, Anne Line Volden","Zimmermann-Nielsen, Erik","Thygesen, Marianne Kirstine","Kroijer, Rasmus","Bjørsum-Meyer, Thomas","Baatrup, Gunnar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-601558"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Colorectal adenomas","Colorectal cancer screening","diagnostic and therapeutic endoscopy"],"level":"pop","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"colon capsule endoscopy in colorectal cancer screening a randomised controlled trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjgast-2020-000411","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-601558","identifier":[{"id":"85087561843","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32601101","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7326244","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-63160c90-0ca9-4adb-a534-2288922e7632"],"keyword":["colorectal adenomas","colorectal cancer screening","diagnostic and therapeutic endoscopy"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-756424D964281080C084BB7BFBB6F8EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/171295078/e000411.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjgast-2020-000411","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse","key":"kaalbypau","last":"Kaalby","locid":"0c8d2c97-bb94-4040-883e-f9d93c5f4327","name":"Kaalby, Lasse","orcid":"0000-0002-6721-3604","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"dedingpau","last":"Deding","locid":"ac9881cb-949b-4427-bf3e-8badf8905e2d","name":"Deding, Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0002-8263-2989","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"kobaeklarsenpau","last":"Kobaek-Larsen","locid":"0f383fcc-0bd7-4c47-93b8-911d024157d6","name":"Kobaek-Larsen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-5097-9283","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Line Volden","key":"havshoipau","last":"Havshoi","name":"Havshoi, Anne Line Volden","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"zimmermannnielsenpau","last":"Zimmermann-Nielsen","locid":"da8d9e1e-6b1a-4778-a74b-853dff2f5d52","name":"Zimmermann-Nielsen, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7385-4969","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne K.","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","locid":"b71406f7-073f-4c45-920c-5984da19b5c8","name":"Thygesen, Marianne Kirstine","name_org":"Thygesen, Marianne K.","orcid":"0000-0002-1811-7405","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"kroeijerpau","last":"Kroeijer","locid":"c26556ac-04a1-4ee4-b5aa-6e230c1679b2","name":"Kroijer, Rasmus","name_org":"Kroeijer, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0003-4358-7916","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"bjørsummeyerpau","last":"Bjørsu