{"abstract":"Research question: Multiple sclerosis is predominant in women during the childbearing years and, in case of problems with conceiving naturally, assisted reproductive technology (ART) becomes relevant. The efficacy of ART treatment in women with multiple sclerosis has not previously been studied. Our aim was to examine the chance of a liveborn infant after an embryo transfer in women with multiple sclerosis and to examine whether corticosteroids before embryo transfer had a beneficial effect. Design: This cohort study is based on nationwide Danish health registries, including all women who underwent embryo transfers between 1 January 1995 to 31 December 2017. The exposed cohort comprised 2267 embryo transfers in women with multiple sclerosis and the unexposed cohort comprised 200,684 in women without multiple sclerosis. Multilevel logistic regression analysis was used to compute the crude and the adjusted risk estimates. Results: A total of 21.97% of the embryo transfers in women with multiple sclerosis resulted in a liveborn infant compared with 24.17% in women without multiple sclerosis, and the adjusted odds ratio was 0.91 (95% CI 0.81 to 1.02). The adjusted odds ratio of live birth in women with multiple sclerosis using corticosteroids before embryo transfer was 0.90 (95% CI 0.49 to 1.68), compared with women with multiple sclerosis receiving no corticosteroids. Conclusion: The chance of a live birth was not decreased in women with multiple sclerosis undergoing ART compared with women without multiple sclerosis. The use of corticosteroids had no effect on the result. These novel results on ART treatment are useful when counselling women with multiple sclerosis undergoing assisted reproduction.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jølving, Line Riis","Larsen, Michael Due","Fedder, Jens","Nørgård, Bente Mertz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-624090"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technology","Chronic Disease","Clinical epidemiology","In vitro fertilization","Multiple sclerosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"live birth in women with multiple sclerosis receiving assisted reproduction","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85083357828","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-624090","identifier":[{"id":"85083357828","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32317230","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b196e936-8fb7-4294-bec4-ed4ae1f7ba82"],"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technology","Chronic disease","Clinical epidemiology","In vitro fertilization","Multiple sclerosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EB6F335FCF788090ED88A06F72F97117"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Epidemiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Riis","key":"jølvingpau","last":"Jølving","locid":"524924f0-2e37-4535-9dd3-59630ea8c815","name":"Jølving, Line Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-7433-7656","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Due","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3de91a40-2cd5-40f2-b680-9ef23b0778cf","name":"Larsen, Michael Due","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-2481","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"fedderpau","last":"Fedder","locid":"51b716fd-ee92-46ef-8d70-04bf8995c772","name":"Fedder, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-5383-5501","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Mertz","key":"nørgårdpau","last":"Nørgård","locid":"3d41d6fb-8f1c-4899-9ebd-b72f88e3935d","name":"Nørgård, Bente Mertz","orcid":"0000-0002-9514-3033","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32317230"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.rbmo.2020.01.013","issn":["14726483","14726491"],"issn_org":["14726483"],"issue":"5","journal":"Reproductive BioMedicine Online","pages":"711-718","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Reproductive BioMedicine Online","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083357828"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b196e936-8fb7-4294-bec4-ed4ae1f7ba82"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Live birth in women with multiple sclerosis receiving assisted reproduction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-624090","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Research question: The question of interest for this study was to examine the chance of a live birth following assisted reproductive technology (ART) treatment in women with epilepsy compared with women without epilepsy. In sub-analyses, the chance of biochemical and clinical pregnancies, and the impact of antiepileptic drugs (AED) treatment prior to embryo transfer, was analysed. Design: This register-based cohort study was based on the Danish ART register comprising all women who underwent embryo transfer during 2006 to 2017, which included 730 ART treatments in 264 women with a history of epilepsy, and 128,387 ART treatments in 42,938 women without epilepsy. Adjustments were made for comorbidity, women's age, calendar year, type of infertility treatment and cause of infertility. A possible impact of AED use at the time of embryo transfer was studied in a sub-analysis. The primary outcome was live birth within a period of 140–308 days after the date of embryo transfer. Results: The adjusted odds ratio for a live birth per embryo transfer in women with epilepsy, relative to women without epilepsy, was 1.06 (95% confidence interval [CI] 0.88–1.28). The adjusted odds ratio for a live birth among users of an AED was 1.22 (95% CI 0.77–1.92) relative to women who had stopped the use of AED prior to embryo transfer. Conclusions: The chances of a live birth per embryo transfer were similar in women with and without epilepsy. These are novel and reassuring findings on the efficacy of infertility treatment in women with epilepsy.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Michael Due","Jølving, Line Riis","Fedder, Jens","Nørgård, Bente Mertz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-628229"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Michael Due"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technology","Clinical epidemiology","Epilepsy","IVF","Infertility","Reproduction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the efficacy of assisted reproductive treatment in women with epilepsy","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85091526996","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors thank Cecilie Johannessen Landmark, Department of Life Sciences and Health, OlsoMet, Oslo, Norway, for assistance and discussions of methods. The study was supported by the Research Foundation of the Region of Southern Denmark, and the Free Research Foundation at Odense University Hospital, Denmark."],"id":"S01-000.00-628229","identifier":[{"id":"32978071","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85091526996","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-bfdf963a-324b-4446-b8a4-6d910f4e086e"],"keyword":["Assisted reproductive technology","Clinical epidemiology","Epilepsy","IVF","Infertility","Reproduction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6F644B499692B40B82510DE6A251329A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Epidemiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Due","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3de91a40-2cd5-40f2-b680-9ef23b0778cf","name":"Larsen, Michael Due","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-2481","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Riis","key":"jølvingpau","last":"Jølving","locid":"524924f0-2e37-4535-9dd3-59630ea8c815","name":"Jølving, Line Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-7433-7656","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"fedderpau","last":"Fedder","locid":"51b716fd-ee92-46ef-8d70-04bf8995c772","name":"Fedder, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-5383-5501","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Mertz","key":"nørgårdpau","last":"Nørgård","locid":"3d41d6fb-8f1c-4899-9ebd-b72f88e3935d","name":"Nørgård, Bente Mertz","orcid":"0000-0002-9514-3033","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32978071"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.rbmo.2020.07.019","issn":["14726483","14726491"],"issn_org":["14726483"],"issue":"6","journal":"Reproductive BioMedicine Online","pages":"1015-1022","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Reproductive BioMedicine Online","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091526996"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bfdf963a-324b-4446-b8a4-6d910f4e086e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The efficacy of assisted reproductive treatment in women with epilepsy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-628229","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Abnormal blood compositions can lead to abnormal blood flow which can influence the macular vasculature. Optical coherence tomography angiography (OCTA) makes it possible to study the macular vasculature and potential vascular abnormalities induced by hematological disorders. Here, we investigate vascular changes in control subjects and in hematologic patients before and after treatment. Since these changes are small, they are difficult to notice in the OCTA images. To quantify vascular changes, we propose a method for combined capillary registration, dictionary-based segmentation and local density estimation. Using this method, we investigate three patients and five controls, and our results show that we can detect small changes in the vasculature in patients with large changes in blood composition.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Engberg, Astrid Margareta Elisabet","Amini, Abdullah","Willerslev, Anne","Larsen, Michael","Sander, Birgit","Kessel, Line","Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","Dahl, Vedrana Andersen"],"cuid":["S02-089.60-037134"],"event":{"acronym":"ISBI","end":"2020-04-07","place":"Iowa City, us","start":"2020-04-03","title":"17th IEEE International Symposium on Biomedical Imaging, ISBI 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Microvasculature","OCTA","Quantification"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"automated quantification of macular vasculature changes from octa images of hematologic patients","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/290689836/Automated_Quantification_of_Macular_Vasculature_Changes_from_OCTA_Images_of_Hematologic_Patients_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-089.60-037134","identifier":[{"id":"85085861908","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-c9712b46-eefc-47e5-9dc5-8ed87235182f","ku-fc5f913c-0f77-4b74-9319-39dc2dd9a36a"],"keyword":["Microvasculature","OCTA","Quantification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6EDC6CC62B622B6AC38CA8C4A6E49950"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/204987775/ISBI20_0099_FI.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/290689836/Automated_Quantification_of_Macular_Vasculature_Changes_from_OCTA_Images_of_Hematologic_Patients_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Visual Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Glostrup University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Astrid Margareta Elisabet","key":"engbergastridmargaretaelisabetpau","last":"Engberg","locid":"0b563644-5d5e-4a34-bd56-c5181cfbac16","name":"Engberg, Astrid Margareta Elisabet","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Astrid M.E.","key":"engbergastridmepau","last":"Engberg","name":"Engberg, Astrid M.E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Abdullah","key":"aminiabdullahpau","last":"Amini","name":"Amini, Abdullah","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"willerslevannepau","last":"Willerslev","name":"Willerslev, Anne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Michael","key":"larsenmichaelpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgit","key":"sanderbirgitpau","last":"Sander","name":"Sander, Birgit","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Line","key":"kessellinepau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bjørholm","key":"dahlandersbjorholmpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"c2bad3c8-b172-481b-bb99-d3c2bc4004ef","name":"Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","name_org":"Dahl, Anders Bjørholm","orcid":"0000-0002-0068-8170","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders B.","key":"dahlandersbpau","last":"Dahl","name":"Dahl, Anders B.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vedrana Andersen","key":"dahlvedranaandersenpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"aced0c8f-957d-4bb3-9725-e410e42328f8","name":"Dahl, Vedrana Andersen","orcid":"0000-0001-6734-5570","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vedrana A.","key":"dahlvedranaapau","last":"Dahl","name":"Dahl, Vedrana A.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/isbi45749.2020.9098441","eisbn":["9781538693308"],"isbn":["9781538693308"],"issn":["19457928"],"pages":"1987-1991","publisher":"IEEE","series":"Proceedings - International Symposium on Biomedical Imaging","status":"p","title":"2020 IEEE 17th International Symposium on Biomedical Imaging"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085861908"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c9712b46-eefc-47e5-9dc5-8ed87235182f","ku-fc5f913c-0f77-4b74-9319-39dc2dd9a36a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Automated Quantification of Macular Vasculature Changes from OCTA Images of Hematologic Patients","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.60-037134","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The majority of acutely admitted older medical patients are multimorbid, receive multiple drugs, and experience a complex treatment regime. To be able to optimize treatment and care, we need more knowledge of the association between different patterns of multimorbidity and healthcare utilization and the complexity thereof. The purpose was therefore to investigate patterns of multimorbidity in a Danish national cohort of acutely hospitalized medical patients aged 65 and older and to determine the association between these multimorbid patterns with the healthcare utilization and complexity. Patients and Methods: Longitudinal cohort study of 129,900 (53% women) patients. Latent class analysis (LCA) was used to develop patterns of multimorbidity based on 22 chronic conditions ascertained from Danish national registers. A latent class regression was used to test for differences in healthcare utilization and healthcare complexity among the patterns measured in the year leading up to the index admission. Results: LCA identified eight distinct multimorbid patterns. Patients belonging to multimorbid patterns including the major chronic conditions; diabetes and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease was associated with higher odds of healthcare utilization and complexity than the reference pattern (\"Minimal chronic conditions\"). The pattern with the highest number of chronic conditions did not show the highest healthcare utilization nor complexity. Conclusion: Our study showed that chronic conditions cluster together and that these patterns differ in healthcare utilization and complexity. Patterns of multimorbidity have the potential to be used in epidemiological studies of healthcare planning but should be confirmed in other population-based studies.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Juul-Larsen, Helle Gybel","Christensen, Line Due","Bandholm, Thomas","Andersen, Ove","Kallemose, Thomas","Jørgensen, Lillian Mørch","Petersen, Janne"],"cuid":["S02-095.18-014758"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Acute hospitalization","Chronic conditions","Latent class analysis","Multimorbidity","Older medical patients"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patterns of multimorbidity and differences in healthcare utilization and complexity among acutely hospitalized medical patients gt 000000000065 years a latent class approach","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S226586","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.18-014758","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7053819","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85081034056","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000519251200001","type":"wos"},{"id":"32184671","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1dc16403-64a1-433b-84d4-836ed8461850","ku-cc9ceb06-d747-4fc2-ad32-47d7241611ac"],"keyword":["Acute hospitalization","Chronic conditions","Latent class analysis","Multimorbidity","Older medical patients"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EE66C33FEB916A9C4C0B9A08A22B16B6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/238540657/clep_226586_patterns_of_multimorbidity_and_differences_in_healthcare_uti.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S226586","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Helle Gybel","key":"juullarsenpau","last":"Juul-Larsen","name":"Juul-Larsen, Helle Gybel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Due","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"aa0cb857-7506-4c63-8f8d-1f94fd25fc99","name":"Christensen, Line Due","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"bandholmpau","last":"Bandholm","locid":"b95f1a84-201a-4df5-ba46-de16a9ce8d60","name":"Bandholm, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ove","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"251ac7c3-391a-4cd6-8696-6d5f1ee26911","name":"Andersen, Ove","orcid":"0000-0002-2274-548X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"kallemosepau","last":"Kallemose","name":"Kallemose, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lillian Morch","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","locid":"5793b7cf-716f-4067-9abd-3a9c2bd61997","name":"Jørgensen, Lillian Mørch","name_org":"Jorgensen, Lillian Morch","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janne","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1cb72724-54f8-4ca1-a201-bfa4a354a129","name":"Petersen, Janne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32184671"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2147/clep.s226586","issn":["11791349"],"journal":"Clinical Epidemiology","pages":"245-259","publisher":"Dove Medical Press Ltd","status":"p","title":"Clinical Epidemiology","title_org":"Clinical epidemiology","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081034056"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1dc16403-64a1-433b-84d4-836ed8461850","ku-cc9ceb06-d747-4fc2-ad32-47d7241611ac"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Patterns of Multimorbidity and Differences in Healthcare Utilization and Complexity Among Acutely Hospitalized Medical Patients (&gt;= 65 Years) - A Latent Class Approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.18-014758","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: State Trait Anxiety Inventory (STAI) scale was developed in the 1980's and has been widely used both in clinical settings and in research. However the Danish version of STAI has not been validated. The aim of this study was to assess the validity and reliability of STAI - state anxiety scale in Danish women aged 45 years and older with abnormal cervical cancer screening results. Methods: Women ≥45 years referred with an abnormal cervical cytology and healthy volunteers (n = 12) underwent cognitive interview after completing STAI. Further, STAI was sent out in an electronic questionnaire to women (n = 109) seen at the gynecological department with abnormal cervical cancer screening test during 2018. Validity and reliability of STAI was evaluated according to the Consensus-based Standards for the selection of health Measurement Instruments (COSMIN) checklist by examining internal consistency, test-retest reliability, measurement error, floor and ceiling, construct validity and content validity. Results: In the cognitive interviews the content validity was evaluated to be very good. The internal consistency of the scale was excellent with Cronbach's α = 0.93. Test-retest reliability was good with an intra-class correlation coefficient of 0.80 and the systematic difference between test-retest results was negligible. The construct validity was good. Conclusion: To our best knowledge, this is the first validation study of the Danish translation of STAI-state anxiety scale. This version of STAI demonstrates an acceptable reliability and validity when used in a gynecological setting.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Gustafson, Line Winther","Gabel, Pernille","Hammer, Anne","Lauridsen, H. H.","Petersen, L. K.","Andersen, Berit","Bor, Isil Pinar","Larsen, Mette Bach"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013029"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Gustafson, Line Winther"],"keyword":["Abnormal cervical screening test","Agreement","Anxiety","FORM","INTRACLASS CORRELATION COEFFICIENTS","Information","Questionnaire","State trait anxiety inventory","Validation and reliability"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validity and reliability of state trait anxiety inventory in danish women aged 000000000045 years and older with abnormal cervical screening results","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12874-020-00982-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-013029","identifier":[{"id":"85084030937","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000530144100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7178932","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32326886","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-05e584bd-e936-4cea-a9b1-b842c1831d75","sdu-d1a4923a-58e7-4edb-a8bc-51844faf5028"],"keyword":["AGREEMENT","ATTENDING COLPOSCOPY","Abnormal cervical screening test","Anxiety","FORM","INFORMATION","INTRACLASS CORRELATION-COEFFICIENTS","Questionnaire","State trait anxiety inventory","Validation and reliability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9A3D150DA51E492730A98A13AA17CA97"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12874-020-00982-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170146988/s12874_020_00982_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl