of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik V.","key":"ilkjærpau","last":"Ilkjær","locid":"533c0fab-76a0-4691-b8c9-149c6fe51caf","name":"Ilkjær, Frederik Veitland","name_org":"Ilkjær, Frederik V.","orcid":"0000-0003-3647-7209","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line D.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"a0349aeb-56d9-4984-86b0-4829aee2a04b","name":"Rasmussen, Line Dahlerup","name_org":"Rasmussen, Line D.","orcid":"0000-0003-0853-0893","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raquel","key":"martiniguacelpau","last":"Martin-Iguacel","locid":"458ec645-67fa-48e3-b302-2239bd857531","name":"Martin-Iguacel, Raquel","orcid":"0000-0003-3543-1970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"6c54d03c-7758-4ac9-b27a-c606f993066f","name":"Westh, Lena","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Terese L","key":"katzensteinpau","last":"Katzenstein","locid":"7ff54094-7ab3-471a-89d8-575332708b34","name":"Katzenstein, Terese L","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Ann-Brit E","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"29b6e1f5-8374-4247-a7bd-76de887cc30d","name":"Hansen, Ann-Brit Eg","name_org":"Hansen, Ann-Brit E","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Thyge L.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Thyge L.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 6 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten S.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"2435cb82-03bd-498b-909d-1ef0e99443fe","name":"Larsen, Carsten Schade","name_org":"Larsen, Carsten S.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Isik S.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"d7a439ff-f0ad-43c9-80d8-a269647e1886","name":"Johansen, Isik Somuncu","name_org":"Johansen, Isik S.","orcid":"0000-0002-2189-9823","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31372799"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10875-019-00666-9","issn":["02719142","15732592"],"issn_org":["02719142"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Clinical Immunology","pages":"641-652","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Immunology","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070107086"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6062907b-f158-4769-a18c-dea77c1198ff","ku-7113fadb-073a-4c5a-ad2a-10123d0d243b","sdu-6bb5761c-9780-45d1-9056-7f488ae35f9c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"How to Identify Common Variable Immunodeficiency Patients Earlier : General Practice Patterns","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-019665","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Substantial interest has been directed towards stroke risk stratification in patients with atrial fibrillation (AF) but prior studies have focused on AF without significant valvular heart disease (VHD), so-called 'non-valvular AF'. A formal validation exercise addressing stroke risks in relation to the CHA2DS2-VASc risk factor(s) in AF patients with VHD is lacking. Also, the use of the HAS-BLED score in anticoagulated patients with VHD has not been previously studied. The aim of this study was to investigate stroke and bleeding rates in AF patients with VHD in relation to the CHA2DS2-VASc and HAS-BLED scores. We conducted a nationwide cohort study. VHD were categorized based on the 2017 joint European consensus document definition, i.e. Evaluated Heartvalves, Rheumatic or Artificial (EHRA) categorization, as follows: (i) EHRA Type 1 VHD, which refers to AF patients with 'VHD needing therapy with a Vitamin K antagonist (VKA)', thus including severe native mitral stenosis and prosthetic mechanical heart valves and (ii) EHRA Type 2 VHD, which refers to AF patients with 'VHD needing therapy with a VKA or a non-VKA oral anticoagulant (NOAC)', thus including all other forms of VHD. We identified 25 818 AF patients with VHD with EHRA Type 2 in 90% (n = 23 253). Thromboembolism and bleeding events increased with increasing CHA2DS2-VASc and HAS-BLED scores, whether with 1 or 2.5 years follow-up. EHRA Type 1 outcomes: The predictive value of CHA2DS2-VASc score for thromboembolism was modest, c-indexes 0.62 (0.55-0.70) at 1 year. The predictive value of the HAS-BLED score for bleeding was also modest being 0.59 (0.53-0.65) at 1 year. EHRA Type 2 outcomes: The predictive value of CHA2DS2-VASc score for thromboembolism was modest, c-indexes 0.63 (0.60-0.65) at 1 year. The predictive value of the HAS-BLED score for bleeding was also modest being 0.59 (0.53-0.65) at 1 year. This is the first validation of CHA2DS2-VASc and HAS-BLED scores in AF patients with VHD (so-called 'valvular AF') using the new EHRA classification. Both scores are modestly predictive of thromboembolism and bleeding events in VHD, respectively. Event rates increased with increasing risk factors as evident by increasing CHA2DS2-VASc and HAS-BLED score points, consistent with performance of these clinical scores in 'non-valvular AF' patients.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lip, Gregory Y H","Jensen, Martin","Melgaard, Line","Skjøth, Flemming","Nielsen, Peter Brønnum","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-097140"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Birmingham"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Bleeding","Stroke","Valvular heart disease"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stroke and bleeding risk scores in patients with atrial fibrillation and valvular heart disease evaluating valvular heart disease in a nationwide cohort study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85059498542&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-097140","identifier":[{"id":"85059498542","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29986001","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-a28e8f36-1ef2-47fc-82dc-ff116aa17dba"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Bleeding","EHRA classification","Stroke","Valvular heart disease"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-017F83AD803B6FE574BFDAAB56F2565A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Birmingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y H","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d5770e98-1d04-4d3b-aa8c-49c951b21eb0","name":"Jensen, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"melgaardpau","last":"Melgaard","locid":"88687b9c-5b56-4584-a89a-89fdeca4fd54","name":"Melgaard, Line","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"skjøthpau","last":"Skjøth","locid":"6166e832-f5f5-47be-82bb-07962be7c943","name":"Skjøth, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0003-2975-647X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Brønnum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3ce5c24a-cc41-4e4c-a071-9a41f036faf8","name":"Nielsen, Peter Brønnum","orcid":"0000-0003-2922-6970","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Bjerregaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a3c6747f-b9db-488b-8eb9-887d38742880","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29986001"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/europace/euy151","issn":["10995129","10996044"],"issn_org":["10995129"],"issue":"1","journal":"Europace","pages":"33-40","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Europace","title_org":"Europace : European pacing, arrhythmias, and cardiac electrophysiology : journal of the working groups on cardiac pacing, arrhythmias, and cardiac cellular electrophysiology of the European Society of Cardiology","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059498542"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a28e8f36-1ef2-47fc-82dc-ff116aa17dba"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Stroke and bleeding risk scores in patients with atrial fibrillation and valvular heart disease : evaluating 'valvular heart disease' in a nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-097140","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The aim was to measure and compare fluoride concentrations in oral mucosa and saliva following a single brushing with either 1,450 or 5,000 ppm fluoride toothpaste. Fourteen healthy participants provided saliva and oral mucosa samples in the morning before tooth brushing. Then participants brushed their teeth with 1,450 ppm fluoride toothpaste, and saliva and mucosa samples were collected after 1, 2, 4, and 6 h. The experiment was repeated 3–7 days later with 5,000 ppm fluoride toothpaste. All samples were analyzed for fluoride using an ion-selective electrode adapted for microanalysis. Pre-brushing fluoride concentrations were higher in mucosa (mean1,450 0.26 ppm and mean5,000 0.20 ppm) than in saliva (mean1,450 0.08 ppm and mean5,000 0.07 ppm). The mean fluoride concentrations increased in both mucosa and saliva following a single brushing with both 1,450 ppm (meanmuc1,450 (1 h) 1.15 ppm, meansal1,450 (1 h) 0.33 ppm) and 5,000 ppm fluoride toothpaste (meanmuc5,000 (1 h) 3.21 ppm and meansal5,000 (1 h) 0.90 ppm). At 6 h, the fluoride concentrations had returned to pre-brushing levels. Across the 6-h sampling period the fluoride concentration in saliva was statistically significantly 1.4 times higher following brushing with 5,000 ppm compared with 1,450 ppm fluoride toothpaste. For mucosa, this ratio was only 1.1 and not statistically significant. In conclusion, the fluoride level in oral buccal mucosa is higher than in saliva and follows the same fluoride clearance pattern as in saliva. Over the initial 6-h period following a single tooth brushing, the ratio of the fluoride concentration in mucosa to that in saliva is independent of the fluoride concentrations in the toothpastes used.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Staun Larsen, Line","Bælum, Vibeke","Richards, Alan","Nyvad, Bente"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-135735"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Human","Mouth Mucosa","Saliva","Toothpastes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fluoride in saliva and oral mucosa after brushing with 000000000001 000000000450 or 000000000005 000000000000 ppm fluoride toothpaste","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85069795782","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-135735","identifier":[{"id":"85069795782","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31307037","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0b4a9402-351c-49b7-b829-07222ab6c089"],"keyword":["Dentifrices","Human","Mouth mucosa","Saliva","Toothpastes","Topical fluorides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6C881D9AA46127C37489D8028673D33A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Ecology and Caries Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"staunlarsenpau","last":"Staun Larsen","locid":"35e2ae60-25db-4a15-893f-dc8906e2bccf","name":"Staun Larsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-5884","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vibeke","key":"baelumpau","last":"Baelum","locid":"fa28bbda-971e-4463-be61-3dcc358973b2","name":"Bælum, Vibeke","name_org":"Baelum, Vibeke","orcid":"0000-0002-2195-8053","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alan","key":"richardspau","last":"Richards","locid":"2b845949-43a7-481b-b04e-d301d661433b","name":"Richards, Alan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bente","key":"nyvadpau","last":"Nyvad","locid":"f0fda280-eb7a-42d4-93f0-45f26e30fc45","name":"Nyvad, Bente","orcid":"0000-0002-9545-0447","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31307037"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000501264","issn":["00086568","1421976X"],"issn_org":["00086568"],"issue":"6","journal":"Caries Research","pages":"675-681","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Caries Research","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069795782"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0b4a9402-351c-49b7-b829-07222ab6c089"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Fluoride in Saliva and Oral Mucosa after Brushing with 1,450 or 5,000 ppm Fluoride Toothpaste","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-135735","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Presbyopia, i.e. the loss of accommodative amplitude with age, results from increasing stiffness and thickness of the lens and leads to inability of the lens to change shape, refractive power and focus of the eye in response to the contraction of the ciliary muscle inside the eye. Multiple remedies are available, the most common being reading glasses. Alternative options include a monovision combination of monofocal lenses or the use of multifocal lenses, in the form of contact lenses or intraocular implant lenses, corneal implants or corneal refractive surgery. This review provides an update on current options and their limitations.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Mohamud, Ahmed","Erichsen, Jesper","Kessel, Line","Holm, Lars Morten","Larsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-543698"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cornea","Eyeglasses","Humans","Lenses Intraocular","Visual Acuity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"presbyopibehandling","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/videnskab/presbyopibehandling","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-543698","identifier":[{"id":"85061153640","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30722817","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-fbb7da6c-213a-4e7a-807c-9290cd7d4c74"],"keyword":["Cornea","Eyeglasses","Humans","Lenses, Intraocular","Presbyopia/therapy","Visual Acuity"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-20A0AF974C806AFDEBD83E76E7000C99"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l