{"abstract":"Purpose: To provide a detailed electroclinical description and expand the phenotype of PIGT-CDG, to perform genotype–phenotype correlation, and to investigate the onset and severity of the epilepsy associated with the different genetic subtypes of this rare disorder. Furthermore, to use computer-assisted facial gestalt analysis in PIGT-CDG and to the compare findings with other glycosylphosphatidylinositol (GPI) anchor deficiencies. Methods: We evaluated 13 children from eight unrelated families with homozygous or compound heterozygous pathogenic variants in PIGT. Results: All patients had hypotonia, severe developmental delay, and epilepsy. Epilepsy onset ranged from first day of life to two years of age. Severity of the seizure disorder varied from treatable seizures to severe neonatal onset epileptic encephalopathies. The facial gestalt of patients resembled that of previously published PIGT patients as they were closest to the center of the PIGT cluster in the clinical face phenotype space and were distinguishable from other gene-specific phenotypes. Conclusion: We expand our knowledge of PIGT. Our cases reaffirm that the use of genetic testing is essential for diagnosis in this group of disorders. Finally, we show that computer-assisted facial gestalt analysis accurately assigned PIGT cases to the multiple congenital anomalies–hypotonia–seizures syndrome phenotypic series advocating the additional use of next-generation phenotyping technology.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Bayat, Allan","Knaus, Alexej","Juul, Annika Wollenberg","Dukic, Dejan","Gardella, Elena","Charzewska, Agnieszka","Clement, Emma","Hjalgrim, Helle","Hoffman-Zacharska, Dorota","Horn, Denise","Horton, Rachel","Hurst, Jane A.","Josifova, Dragana","Larsen, Line H.G.","Lascelles, Karine","Obersztyn, Ewa","Pagnamenta, Alistair","Pal, Deb K.","Pendziwiat, Manuela","Ryten, Mina","Taylor, Jenny","Vogt, Julie","Weber, Yvonne","Krawitz, Peter M.","Helbig, Ingo","Kini, Usha","Møller, Rikke S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-614702"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["the DDD Study Group"],"corresponding_author":["Bayat, Allan"],"country":["Germany","Poland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Birmingham Women’s Hospital","Campus Kiel","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","Children's Hospital of Philadelphia","Eberhard Karls University of Tübingen","Great Ormond Street Hospital","Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust","Institute of Mother and Child Department of Molecular Genetics","King's College London","Oxford University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","UCL Queen Square Institute of Neurology","University Hospital Bonn","University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust","University of Oxford","Wellcome Trust Centre for Human Genetics"],"keyword":["Epilepsy","Genotype phenotype","congenital disorder of glycosylation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-FILA"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-FILA","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pigt cdg a disorder of the glycosylphosphatidylinositol anchor description of 000000000013 novel patients and expansion of the clinical characteristics","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170256040/PIGT_CDG_a_disorder_of_the_glycosylphosphatidylinositol_anchor_description_of.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-614702","identifier":[{"id":"85064261102","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30976099","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-90d835c1-e0fc-421f-a4b2-48a53de3f297"],"keyword":["PIGT-CDG","computer-assisted facial gestalt analysis","congenital disorder of glycosylation","epilepsy","genotype–phenotype"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-492F9EF1D92646DC183E6803D06EA6A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170256040/PIGT_CDG_a_disorder_of_the_glycosylphosphatidylinositol_anchor_description_of.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - The Epilepsyhospital Filadelfia, Research Unit of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine (Dianalund)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Hvidovre Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university hospital bonn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital Bonn","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"pl","key":"institute of mother and child department of molecular genetics","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Institute of Mother and Child Department of Molecular Genetics","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"great ormond street hospital","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Great Ormond Street Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Resea