","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"molleruppedh","last":"Mollerup","name":"Mollerup, Charlotte","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9878779171237"],"pages":"26-45","place":"København","publisher":"Multivers","status":"p","subtitle":"Proust og Psyken","title":"Proust Bulletin","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cf0aa46e-7776-46cb-9e6d-200903a39997"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Den Sunkne Katedral : Proust og psyken","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-517149","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"As a result of elevated metabolic rates and net acid extrusion in the rapidly proliferating cancer cells, solid tumours are characterized by a highly acidic microenvironment, while cancer cell intracellular pH is normal or even alkaline. Two-dimensional (2D) cell monocultures, which have been used extensively in breast cancer research for decades, cannot precisely recapitulate the rich environment and complex processes occurring in tumours in vivo. The use of such models can consequently be misleading or non-predictive for clinical applications. Models mimicking the tumour microenvironment are particularly pivotal for studying tumour pH homeostasis, which is profoundly affected by the diffusion-limited conditions in the tumour. To advance the understanding of the mechanisms and consequences of dysregulated acid-base homeostasis in breast cancer, clinically relevant models that incorporate the unique microenvironment of these tumours are required. The development of three-dimensional (3D) cell cultures has provided new tools for basic research and pre-clinical approaches, allowing the culture of breast cancer cells under conditions that closely resemble tumour growth in a living organism. Here we provide an overview of the main 3D techniques relevant for breast cancer cell culture. We discuss the advantages and limitations of the classical 3D models as well as recent advances in 3D culture techniques, focusing on how these culture methods have been used to study acid-base transport in breast cancer. Finally, we outline future directions of 3D culture technology and their relevance for studies of acid-base transport.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Czaplinska, Dominika","Elingaard-Larsen, Line O.","Rolver, Michala G.","Severin, Marc","Pedersen, Stine Helene Falsig"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-532552"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["3D culture","Cyst","Organoid","Spheroid","Tumour microenvironment","pH homeostasis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000003d multicellular models to study the regulation and roles of acid base transporters in breast cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-532552","identifier":[{"id":"85077016332","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31803922","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e8f6e0d1-6427-4d78-927d-41437c4320c0"],"keyword":["3D culture","cyst","organoid","pH homeostasis","spheroid","tumour microenvironment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-36F337288427D1C4B41E7D844940A6A5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Cell Biology and Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Dominika","key":"czaplinskapau","last":"Czaplinska","locid":"1c75644f-5972-4a16-81a1-cd00de53fd8e","name":"Czaplinska, Dominika","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Line O.","key":"elingaardlarsenpau","last":"Elingaard-Larsen","locid":"0cdfcf12-6832-4b3a-8454-802e6c5790ff","name":"Elingaard-Larsen, Line O.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michala G.","key":"rolverpau","last":"Rolver","locid":"e61a699a-cf7a-479e-8cf1-9fd071540db0","name":"Rolver, Michala G.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marc","key":"severinpau","last":"Severin","locid":"80dda290-a7ff-4ec9-a493-19f28c411