{"abstract":"Three-dimensional spheroids of cancer cells are important tools for both cancer drug screens and for gaining mechanistic insight into cancer cell biology. The power of this preparation lies in its ability to mimic many aspects of the in vivo conditions of tumors while being fast, cheap, and versatile enough to allow relatively high-throughput screening. The spheroid culture conditions can recapitulate the physico-chemical gradients in a tumor, including the increasing extracellular acidity, increased lactate, and decreasing glucose and oxygen availability, from the spheroid periphery to its core. Also, the mechanical properties and cell-cell interactions of in vivo tumors are in part mimicked by this model. The specific properties and consequently the optimal growth conditions, of 3D spheroids, differ widely between different types of cancer cells. Furthermore, the assessment of cell viability and death in 3D spheroids requires methods that differ in part from those employed for 2D cultures. Here we describe several protocols for preparing 3D spheroids of cancer cells, and for using such cultures to assess cell viability and death in the context of evaluating the efficacy of anticancer drugs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rolver, Michala G.","Elingaard-Larsen, Line O.","Pedersen, Stine Helene Falsig"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-476241"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["3D cell culture","Anti cancer therapy","Breast cancer","Cancer research","Cell viability","Chemotherapy","Drug treatment","Immunohistochemistry","Issue 148","Pancreatic cancer","Propidium iodide","Spheroids"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessing cell viability and death in 000000000003d spheroid cultures of cancer cells","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/be22/9f9fadbff6e7330c9e1b8910861e71362083.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-476241","identifier":[{"id":"31259899","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85068964018","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8a8370a6-02ea-429f-b1fc-f8d060da646a"],"keyword":["3D cell culture","Anti-cancer therapy","Breast cancer","Cancer Research","Cell viability","Chemotherapy","Drug treatment","Hanging drop","Immunohistochemistry","Issue 148","Pancreatic cancer","Propidium iodide","Reconstituted basement membrane","Spheroids"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-6DB3328D5C1BA136C2474BBDE19D82B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/be22/9f9fadbff6e7330c9e1b8910861e71362083.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Cell Biology and Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Michala G.","key":"rolverpau","last":"Rolver","locid":"e61a699a-cf7a-479e-8cf1-9fd071540db0","name":"Rolver, Michala G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Line O.","key":"elingaardlarsenpau","last":"Elingaard-Larsen","locid":"0cdfcf12-6832-4b3a-8454-802e6c5790ff","name":"Elingaard-Larsen, Line O.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stine F.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"1d5a844a-2526-46ea-9662-94eccb5854ea","name":"Pedersen, Stine Helene Falsig","name_org":"Pedersen, Stine F.","orcid":"0000-0002-3044-7714","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31259899"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3791/59714","issn":["1940087X"],"issue":"148","journal":"Journal of Visualized Experiments","paperid":"e59714","status":"p","title":"Journal of Visualized Experiments","volume":"2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068964018"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8a8370a6-02ea-429f-b1fc-f8d060da646a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Assessing Cell Viability and Death in 3D Spheroid Cultures of Cancer Cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-476241","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"For decades, the research on reproductive consequences in women with inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) has focused on short-term outcomes, including adverse pregnancy outcomes (eg, abruptio placenta, placenta previa, preeclampsia/eclampsia) and adverse birth outcomes (eg, small for gestational age, preterm birth, and congenital malformations). The long-term health outcomes of the children of parents with IBD have been studied to a much lesser extent, and there is a critical research gap in understanding the influence of parental IBD on long-term outcomes. In this review, we propose the reasons for this lack of evidence and highlight the weakest areas of the research on the impact of parental IBD on offspring health. We will focus on health outcomes in children of parents with IBD from an age of 1 year through childhood, adolescence, and adulthood.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nørgård, Bente Mertz","Jølving, Line Riis","Larsen, Michael Due","Friedman, Sonia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-645280"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nørgård, Bente Mertz"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brigham and Women's Hospital","Harvard Medical School"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Child","Child Development","Child Preschool","Female","Health outcomes","Humans","Infant","Inflammatory Bowel Diseases complications","Inflammatory bowel disease","Long term outcomes","Parents","Pregnancy","Pregnancy Complications etiology","Pregnancy Outcome epidemiology","Quality of Life","Reproduction","Time Factors","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parental ibd and long term health outcomes in the offspring","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/156478524/Parental_IBD_and_long_term_health_outcomes_in_the_offspring.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-645280","identifier":[{"id":"85069981035","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30624631","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-fbef0ab5-f146-4c96-b428-66c35592c7c3"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Child","Child Development","Child, Preschool","Female","Health outcomes","Humans","Infant","Inflammatory Bowel Diseases/complications","Inflammatory bowel disease","Long-term outcomes","Parents","Pregnancy","Pregnancy Complications/etiology","Pregnancy Outcome/epidemiology","Quality of Life","Reproduction","Time Factors","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-749ED1AF20FE96EAEED6AB1C11A4C410"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/156478524/Parental_IBD_and_long_term_health_outcomes_in_the_offspring.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Epidemiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"brigham and women s hospital","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Brigham and Women's Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"harvard medical school","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard Medical School","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":nu