Leif","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rashmi","key":"prasadrashmipau","last":"Prasad","name":"Prasad, Rashmi","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","first":"John","key":"lusingujohnpau","last":"Lusingu","locid":"cda7aa04-4ac5-43ec-a446-0d8f8fd30037","name":"Lusingu, John","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christentze","key":"schmiegelowchristentzepau","last":"Schmiegelow","locid":"c40efab4-c1ea-469a-a17a-fd7296acaf7c","name":"Schmiegelow, Christentze","orcid":"0000-0002-9360-9741","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ib C","key":"bygbjergibchristianpau","last":"Bygbjerg","locid":"acec49c2-8e30-45f6-8785-19112c22d379","name":"Bygbjerg, Ib Christian","name_org":"Bygbjerg, Ib C","orcid":"0000-0001-9100-2754","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31122967"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2018-024861","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"5","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e024861","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066836958"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-785861ea-a0a8-4567-891b-7659e86f3e53","ku-e33603f7-311d-413e-bd87-669ad2274461"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"FOETAL for NCD - FOetal Exposure and Epidemiological Transitions : The role of Anaemia in early Life for Non-Communicable Diseases in later life: A prospective preconception study in rural Tanzania","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.88-021462","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To evaluate the prevalence of amblyopia and associated biometric factors in Danish children. Methods: Determination of best-corrected visual acuity (BCVA) using ETDRS charts, non-cycloplegic subjective refractioning guided by automated refractometry, axial length and corneal curvature, fundus photography and optical coherence tomography (OCT) in 1335 children from the population-based Copenhagen Child Cohort 2000 (CCC2000) Eye Study. Birth data were obtained from the Danish Medical Birth Registry. Results: The mean (±SD) age of children was 11.7 (±0.4) years, and 47% were boys. Amblyopia prevalence was 1.5 (95% CL 0.8–2.2) %. Unilateral amblyopic eyes [BCVA < 80 ETDRS letters (0.8 snellen) and ≥2 lines difference between the eyes] was 0.6 (95% CL 0.3–1.0) mm shorter, 1.34 (95% CL 0.30–2.37) D more hyperopic and had 0.79 (95% CL 0.14–1.44) D more astigmatism compared with fellow eyes. Compared with the right eyes of the non-amblyopic children, unilateral amblyopic eyes were 1.0 (95% CL 0.5–1.6) mm shorter, 2.48 (95% CL 1.11–3.86) D more hyperopic, 1.09 (95% CL 0.43–1.75) D more astigmatic and had a 47 (95% CL 13–81) μm thicker subfoveal choroid. Conclusion: Amblyopia was found in 1.5% of Danish children born 22 years after the inception of the nationwide preschool visual screening programme. Amblyopia was associated with anisometropia, astigmatism, a thicker subfoveal choroid and a history of childhood strabismus.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Mathias Henning","Munch, Inger Christine","Li, Xiao Qiang","Skovgaard, Anne Mette","Olsen, Else Marie","Larsen, Michael","Kessel, Line"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-043629"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Mathias Hvidtfelt"],"keyword":["Amblyopia","Amblyopia diagnosis","Axial length","Child","Children","Choroidal thickness","Cohort study","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Male","Population Surveillance","Prevalence","Tomography Optical Coherence","Urban Population","Visual Acuity","corneal curvature"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"visual acuity and amblyopia prevalence in 000000000011 to 000000000012 year old danish children from the copenhagen child cohort 000000002000","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170612470/aos.13842.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-043629","identifier":[{"id":"30280496","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000456872000007","type":"wos"},{"id":"85054342373","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7905e7a2-4853-4be4-805f-662c82a93ef8","sdu-75551b26-22e4-457c-94a0-614bc7dd3284"],"keyword":["Amblyopia/diagnosis","Child","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Male","Population Surveillance","Prevalence","Tomography, Optical Coherence","Urban Population","amblyopia","axial length","children","choroidal thickness","cohort study","corneal curvature","visual acuity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8AF859327B0DA994F23132974DBB6BF5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170612470/aos.13842.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and