{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Staun Larsen, Line","Richards, Alan","Nyvad, Bente"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-208548"],"event":{"end":"2018-07-07","place":"København, dk","start":"2018-07-04","title":"65th Congress of the European Organisation for Caries Research","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Mucosa","Saliva","fluorid"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fluoride on the oral mucosa and in saliva a pilot study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85045767287","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-208548","identifier":[{"id":"85045767287","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29672290","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-8ad62191-9125-4c0a-b793-f2442e3b0540"],"keyword":["fluorid","mucosa","saliva"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-5-6-C0CABC5E1F3A5F22F88133683FEAD96B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Pediatric Dentistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"staunlarsenpau","last":"Staun Larsen","locid":"35e2ae60-25db-4a15-893f-dc8906e2bccf","name":"Staun Larsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-5884","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alan","key":"richardspau","last":"Richards","locid":"2b845949-43a7-481b-b04e-d301d661433b","name":"Richards, Alan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bente","key":"nyvadpau","last":"Nyvad","locid":"f0fda280-eb7a-42d4-93f0-45f26e30fc45","name":"Nyvad, Bente","orcid":"0000-0002-9545-0447","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29672290"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000488302","issn":["00086568","1421976X"],"issn_org":["00086568"],"issue":"6","journal":"Caries Research","pages":"491","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Caries Research","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8ad62191-9125-4c0a-b793-f2442e3b0540"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Fluoride on the Oral Mucosa and in Saliva – A Pilot Study","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-208548","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Pacing the way towards 5G has lead researchers and industry in the direction of centralized processing known from Cloud-Radio Access Networks (C-RAN). In C-RAN research, a variety of different functional splits is presented by different names and focusing on different directions. The functional split determines how many Base Station (BS) functions to leave locally, close to the user, with the benefit of relaxing fronthaul network bitrate and delay requirements, and how many functions to centralize with the possibility of achieving greater processing benefits. This work presents for the first time a comprehensive overview systematizing the different work directions for both research and industry, while providing a detailed description of each functional split option and an assessment of the advantages and disadvantages. This work gives an overview of where the most effort has been directed in terms of functional splits, and where there is room for further studies. The standardization currently taking place is also considered and mapped into the research directions. It is investigated how the fronthaul network will be affected by the choice of functional split, both in terms of bitrates and latency, and as the different functional splits provide different advantages and disadvantages, the option of flexible functional splits is also looked into.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Checko, Aleksandra","Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316423"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt"],"keyword":["C RAN","Crosshaul","Fronthaul","Functional split","Industry","Network architecture","Standardization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a survey of the functional splits proposed for 000000000005g mobile crosshaul networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/COMST.2018.2868805","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316423","identifier":[{"id":"85053421589","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-27dc6285-f04b-46fa-bb34-855a9db84d3d"],"keyword":["C-RAN","Crosshaul","Fronthaul","Functional Split","Industry","Network architecture.","Standardization","X-haul"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D1558BB98EACFFEF2FDE0BDEC2EB1A01"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/COMST.2018.2868805","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/158484230/hkkr_08479363.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/204172085/08479363.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Radiocomp ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Maria","key":"pyndtlarsenpau","last":"Pyndt Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","name_org":"Pyndt Larsen, Line Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksandra","key":"checkopau","last":"Checko","name":"Checko, Aleksandra","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Lehrmann","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"f3aec174-d663-4d97-aaa0-81cd6f4493a9","name":"Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9558-3493","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/comst.2018.2868805","issn":["1553877X"],"issue":"1","journal":"IEEE Communications Surveys and Tutorials","pages":"146-172","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Communications Surveys and Tutorials","title_org":"I E E E Communications Surveys and Tutorials","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053421589"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","radiocomp aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-27dc6285-f04b-46fa-bb34-855a9db84d3d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A Survey of the Functional Splits Proposed for 5G Mobile Crosshaul Networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316423","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This work considers how network slicing can use the network architecture Cloud-Radio Access Network (C-RAN) as an enabler for the required prerequisite network virtualization. Specifically this work looks at a segment of the C-RAN architecture called the fronthaul network. The fronthaul network required for network slicing needs to be able to dynamically assign capacity where it is needed. Deploying a fronthaul network faces a trade-off between fronthaul bitrate, flexibility, and complexity of the local equipment close to the user. This work relates the challenges currently faced in C-RAN research to the network requirements in network slicing. It also shows how using a packet-switched fronthaul for network slicing will bring great advantages and enable the use of different functional splits, while the price to pay is a minor decrease in fronthaul length due to latency constraints.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Berger, Michael Stübert","Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-324795"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fronthaul for cloud ran enabling network slicing in 000000000005g mobile networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2018/4860212","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-324795","identifier":[{"id":"85053421228","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-43fd12f7-7cfc-4dd4-baca-a137f67e57a2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EC5B20298F375BFC0A0CA6BABEF6A258"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/152923275/4860212.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2018/4860212","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line M. P.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","name_org":"Larsen, Line M. P.","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Stübert","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","locid":"7b367889-bde0-4e40-893f-0a22e4d32371","name":"Berger, Michael Stübert","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-7261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Lehrmann","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"f3aec174-d663-4d97-aaa0-81cd6f4493a9","name":"Christiansen, Henrik Lehrmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9558-3493","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1155/2018/4860212","issn":["15308669","15308677"],"issn_org":["15308669"],"journal":"Wireless Communications and Mobile Computing","paperid":"4860212","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Wireless Communications and Mobile Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053421228"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-43fd12f7-7cfc-4dd4-baca-a137f67e57a2"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fronthaul for Cloud-RAN Enabling Network Slicing in 5G Mobile Networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-324795","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we investigate the planning of operating rooms at Rigshospitalet, a large Danish hospital. Each operation must be assigned to a specific operating room and also be scheduled for a specific time while taking into account clinical guidelines. Both elective and emergency operations are included, such that the elective operations are planned while still taking potential emergency operations into consideration. Furthermore, the duration of each operation is uncertain. The aim is to construct robust operating room schedules that minimise overtime work and release unused capacity. Due to the uncertainty associated with arrival of emergency patients and also the duration of each operation, a deterministic model is not suitable for this problem. Therefore, we develop a stochastic model where operation duration can vary and where the arrivals of emergency patients are unknown. The stochastic model is computationally heavy, so two mixed integer programming based heuristics denoted 2-Step Relax-and-Fix and All Open Relax-and-Fix are developed to solve the problem. The computational study is based on an extensive dataset compromising 304 days. The heuristics give good results with half of the operating rooms having less than 8 min of overtime work. To test the robustness of the solutions we carry out a simulated implementation of the operation plans. The simulation shows that the heuristic solutions are fairly robust. In general, results show a clear potential for implementing the method for planning and scheduling of operating rooms at Rigshospitalet.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kroer, Line Ravnskjær","Foverskov, Karoline","Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","Hansen, Aske Skouboe","Larsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-378503"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Jesper"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"planning and scheduling operating rooms for elective and emergency surgeries with uncertain duration","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/150862536/MELJU_1_s2.0_S2211692317300188_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-378503","identifier":[{"id":"85045836717","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f725dbea-1080-438b-a562-150d2eba2954"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-03C2AB034301CD792FA9140E59A0B71B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/150862536/MELJU_1_s2.0_S2211692317300188_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Ravnskjær","key":"kroerpau","last":"Kroer","name":"Kroer, Line Ravnskjær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline","key":"foverskovpau","last":"Foverskov","name":"Foverskov, Karoline","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"vilhelmsenpau","last":"Vilhelmsen","locid":"6ceebc69-a38c-4b56-9070-23135aa491c6","name":"Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-8260-6791","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aske Skouboe","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"18f81523-2d28-483e-9428-7f115bc2c75d","name":"Hansen, Aske Skouboe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d1af4d26-e92b-414c-b534-25b2b607a0d9","name":"Larsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9119-3586","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.orhc.2018.03.006","issn":["22116923"],"journal":"Operations Research for Health Care","pages":"107-119","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Operations Research for Health Care","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045836717"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f725dbea-1080-438b-a562-150d2eba2954"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Planning and scheduling operating rooms for elective and emergency surgeries with uncertain duration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-378503","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Type VII collagen is the main component of the anchoring fibrils connecting the basement membrane to the underlying interstitial matrix. Mutations in the type VII collagen gene cause dystrophic epidermolysis bullosa. Increased levels of type VII collagen in the skin have been reported in patients with systemic sclerosis (SSc), whereas reduced levels in the airways have been related to asthma. This indicates that type VII collagen plays an important part in upholding tissue integrity and that its remodeling may lead to pathological states. The aim of this study was to investigate the role of type VII collagen remodeling in fibroproliferative disorders. We produced monoclonal antibody targeting a specific fragment of type VII collagen (C7M) released to the systemic circulation and developed a neo-epitope specific competitive enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA). Biological relevance was evaluated in serum from patients with SSc or chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). The C7M ELISA was technically robust and specific for the C7M neo-epitope. Serum C7M levels were significantly elevated in two cohorts of patients with SSc and in patients with COPD as compared with healthy individuals (P < 0.0001). The C7M ELISA enabled quantification of type VII collagen turnover in serum. Elevated serum C7M levels indicated that the turnover rate of type VII collagen was significantly increased in patients with SSc or COPD, suggesting a pathological role. Thus, the C7M ELISA may become useful in future investigations of type VII collagen turnover in fibroproliferative disorders, and it may prove a valuable tool for evaluating novel anti-fibrotic drugs.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Sand, Jannie M.B.","Lamy, Patricia","Juhl, Pernille","Siebuhr, Anne Sofie","Iversen, Line V.","Nawrocki, Arkadiusz","Larsen, Martin Røssel","Domsic, Robyn T.","Franchimont, Nathalie","Chavez, Juan","Karsdal, Morten A.","Leeming, Diana J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-642189"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sand, Jannie M.B."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Biogen Inc.","University of Pittsburgh"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","COPD","ELISA","Extracellular matrix","Systemic sclerosis","type VII collagen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NBIO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NBIO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of a neo epitope specific assay for serological assessment of type vii collagen turnover and its relevance in fibroproliferative disorders","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85045390819","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank Peter Lange, Gerd Martinez, and Anne-Kirstine Midjord (Hvidovre Hospital, Denmark) for their invaluable contribution to obtaining the COPD cohort. Funding: This work was supported by The Danish Research Foundation, which was not involved in the study design, data analysis, article preparation, or decision to publish. Part of the study was sponsored by Biogen."],"id":"S01-000.00-642189","identifier":[{"id":"29493258","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85045390819","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-f0f8ef7a-2d48-4c33-bacc-a8c27ce1441e"],"keyword":["COPD","ELISA","biomarkers","extracellular matrix","systemic sclerosis","type VII collagen"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F637A1D1CE8B78951878E71BAD6511C8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"nordic biosc