{"abstract":"Previously, it has been reported that melanopsin-mediated pupillary light response (PLR), measured with pupillometry, is reduced in patients with idiopathic intracranial hypertension (IIH), indicating the clinical utility of the tool in the diagnosis of IIH. In the current study, the authors aimed to measure the PLR in 13 treatment-naive patients with new-onset IIH and 13 healthy controls. In contrast to the previous report, which was based on patients with longstanding IIH (n = 13), the authors found no significant difference in the melanopsin-mediated PLR (p = 0.48).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ba-Ali, Shakoor","Jensen, Rigmor Højland","Larsen, Line Sofie","Lund-Andersen, Henrik","Hamann, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-513269"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["IIH","Melanopsin","Pupillary light reflex","Pupillometry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the melanopsin mediated pupillary light response is not changed in patients with newly diagnosed idiopathic intracranial hypertension","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5858859/pdf/ioph-42-02-1344251.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-513269","identifier":[{"id":"29563950","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85027855404","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5858859","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-c8b292c8-d4a6-479f-ad00-7656f1bc1f64"],"keyword":["IIH","PIPR","ipRGCs","melanopsin","pupillary light reflex","pupillometry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-91E57EE4C4DDA377A63BC0D8AC05B6FA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5858859/pdf/ioph-42-02-1344251.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Shakoor","key":"baalipau","last":"Ba-Ali","name":"Ba-Ali, Shakoor","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rigmor Højland","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ba001bf1-101a-4d39-b06f-d5c44f83da58","name":"Jensen, Rigmor Højland","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Line Sofie","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Line Sofie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"lundandersenpau","last":"Lund-Andersen","locid":"5277856f-b771-4658-bb2f-b292ec78ee6f","name":"Lund-Andersen, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steffen","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","locid":"4e7d48fd-1aa8-4703-94ec-8ae85794b7d7","name":"Hamann, Steffen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29563950"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/01658107.2017.1344251","issn":["01658107","1744506X"],"issn_org":["01658107"],"issue":"2","journal":"Neuro-Ophthalmology","pages":"65-72","status":"p","title":"Neuro-Ophthalmology","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85027855404"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c8b292c8-d4a6-479f-ad00-7656f1bc1f64"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Melanopsin-Mediated Pupillary Light Response Is Not Changed in Patients with Newly Diagnosed Idiopathic Intracranial Hypertension","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-513269","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The definition of “complicated grief” has long been debated. On the one hand, it has been used to describe a broad range of difficult and prolonged grief reactions following the death of a loved one. That is, reactions like severe and persistent symptoms of grief, physical and psychiatric illnesses, and untimely death. On the other hand, complicated grief has been used to describe a more specific form of pathological grief. This condition has also been called prolonged grief, traumatic grief, and pathological grief. Sometime in 2018, the WHO is due to publish a revised version of the ICD-11, which will likely include a diagnosis of “Prolonged Grief Disorder” (in Danish “Vedvarende Sorglidelse”). This article proposes that complicated grief retains its definition as a broad term, describing grief reactions which do not follow a natural progression but instead become prolonged and impairing. That is, we argue that complicated grief is an “umbrella term” which encompasses maladaptive grief reactions in the form of 1) prolonged grief disorder, 2) loss-related depression, PTSD, and anxiety, and 3) somatic illnesses. We also focus on the current research findings pertaining to the anticipated and more narrow grief diagnosis, “prolonged grief disorder”. We will discuss the proposed diagnostic criteria, how to differentiate it from depression and PTSD, and recommendations for treatment.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Lene","Lauritzen, Line Rettig","O'Connor, Maja"],"cuid":["S02-092.86-021107"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["The Danish National Center for Grief"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kompliceret sorg og vedvarende sorglidelse begrebsmæssig adskillelse og sammenhæng","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/psyke/article/download/112158/161068/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.86-021107","ids":["au-735876ca-ece2-4bb8-8fdf-2b5bffb1f6c3","ku-dc6284e3-2cd6-4721-b5f7-9ade55427040"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-382DF0B7B401ECE39852C4141C0B919B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/psyke/article/download/112158/161068/","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["The Danish National Center for Grief"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Psychology, Department of Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Lene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Line Rettig","key":"lauritzenpau","last":"Lauritzen","locid":"096df799-2e84-47fd-986d-b57e1d756afd","name":"Lauritzen, Line Rettig","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"oconnorpau","last":"O'Connor","locid":"1173473f-f95b-473d-bc15-f8b8c026b6b9","name":"O'Connor, Maja","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-8633","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01071211"],"issue":"1","journal":"Psyke & Logos","pages":"15-36","publisher":"Dansk Psykologisk Forlag","status":"p","title":"Psyke & Logos","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-735876ca-ece2-4bb8-8fdf-2b5bffb1f6c3","ku-dc6284e3-2cd6-4721-b5f7-9ade55427040"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Kompliceret sorg og vedvarende sorglidelse : Begrebsmæssig adskillelse og sammenhæng","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.86-021107","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: The 22q11.2 deletion syndrome confers a markedly increased risk for schizophrenia. 22q11.2 deletion carriers without manifest psychotic disorder offer the possibility to identify functional abnormalities that precede clinical onset. Since schizophrenia is associated with a reduced cortical gamma response to auditory stimulation at 40 Hz, we hypothesized that the 40 Hz auditory steady-state response (ASSR) may be attenuated in nonpsychotic individuals with a 22q11.2 deletion. Methods: Eighteen young nonpsychotic 22q11.2 deletion carriers and a control group of 27 noncarriers with comparable age range (12-25 years) and sex ratio underwent 128-channel EEG. We recorded the cortical ASSR to a 40 Hz train of clicks, given either at a regular inter-stimulus interval of 25 ms or at irregular intervals jittered between 11 and 37 ms. Results: Healthy noncarriers expressed a stable ASSR to regular but not in the irregular 40 Hz click stimulation. Both gamma power and inter-trial phase coherence of the ASSR were markedly reduced in the 22q11.2 deletion group. The ability to phase lock cortical gamma activity to regular auditory 40 Hz stimulation correlated with the individual expression of negative symptoms in deletion carriers (ρ = -0.487, P = .041). Conclusions: Nonpsychotic 22q11.2 deletion carriers lack efficient phase locking of evoked gamma activity to regular 40 Hz auditory stimulation. This abnormality indicates a dysfunction of fast intracortical oscillatory processing in the gamma-band. Since ASSR was attenuated in nonpsychotic deletion carriers, ASSR deficiency may constitute a premorbid risk marker of schizophrenia.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Larsen, Kit Melissa","Pellegrino, Giovanni","Birknow, Michelle Rosgaard","Kjær, Trine Nørgaard","Baaré, William Frans Christiaan","Didriksen, Michael","Olsen, Line","Werge, Thomas","Mørup, Morten","Siebner, Hartwig Roman"],"cuid":["S02-095.64-037545"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["22q11 2 deletion syndrome","EEG","Gamma band","Journal Article","Oscillations","Schizophrenia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-LUND"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-LUND","DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000022q000000000011 000000000002 deletion syndrome is associated with impaired auditory steady state gamma response","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/schbul/sbx058","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.64-037545","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5815132","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28521049","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85044918612","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-dc611711-99e7-452e-8184-ac9625f8ae6d","ku-1e9027e7-6401-47e7-afed-f5024885e509"],"keyword":["22q11.2 deletion syndrome","EEG","Gamma band","Journal Article","Oscillations","Schizophrenia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9469660FCF34CCEA34D0333C4E8B2334"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/schbul/sbx058","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/186676721/sbx058.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/134178229/sbx058.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)","Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denm