{"abstract":"Standard infrared spectroscopy techniques are well-developed and widely used. However, they typically require milligrams of sample and can involve time-consuming sample preparation. A promising alternative is represented by nanomechanical infrared spectroscopy (NAM-IR) based on the photothermal response of a nanomechanical resonator, which enables the chemical analysis of picograms of analyte directly from a liquid solution in only a few minutes. Herein, we present NAM-IR using perforated membranes (filters). The method was tested with the pharmaceutical compound indomethacin to successfully perform a chemical and morphological analysis on roughly 100 pg of sample. With an absolute estimated sensitivity of 109±15 fg, the presented method is suitable for ultrasensitive vibrational spectroscopy.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kurek, Maksymilian","Carnoy, Matthias","Larsen, Peter Emil","Nielsen, Line Hagner","Hansen, Ole","Rades, Thomas","Schmid, Silvan","Boisen, Anja"],"cuid":["S02-092.86-032611"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","TU Wien"],"keyword":["Crystallization","IR spectroscopy","Journal Article","Nanomechanics","Nanoparticles"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nanomechanical infrared spectroscopy with vibrating filters for pharmaceutical analysis","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/179892595/PP_Nanomechanical_Infrared_Spectroscopy_with_Vibrating_Filters_for_Pharm.._.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-092.86-032611","identifier":[{"id":"28266106","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85014729669","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-01e16958-b43e-4117-a936-3a2b0044e6fa","ku-54d59565-01d4-474d-8f64-2fec6d335428"],"keyword":["IR spectroscopy","Journal Article","crystallization","nanomechanics","nanoparticles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F9093B68E9E15092E57BDAA293B45B7B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/179892595/PP_Nanomechanical_Infrared_Spectroscopy_with_Vibrating_Filters_for_Pharm.._.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, Nanoprobes"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Design and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"tu wien","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"TU Wien","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maksymilian","key":"kurekpau","last":"Kurek","locid":"cc2e7ba8-55af-4e5d-94f0-b78a868454c4","name":"Kurek, Maksymilian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"carnoypau","last":"Carnoy","name":"Carnoy, Matthias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Emil","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"32b8c221-c511-48f7-894a-c1f3616c8eeb","name":"Larsen, Peter Emil","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Hagner","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a9a7a51b-9e8f-40cc-b691-6e64d62e7765","name":"Nielsen, Line Hagner","orcid":"0000-0002-3789-4816","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8d678857-a721-4f7f-9a33-1dadb7401ce4","name":"Hansen, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-6090-8323","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"radespau","last":"Rades","locid":"e3c9db98-a0f8-4161-911f-d6ffdccbfdc6","name":"Rades, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7521-6020","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Silvan","key":"schmidpau","last":"Schmid","name":"Schmid, Silvan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anja","key":"boisenpau","last":"Boisen","locid":"898c472f-7fe0-4454-83d8-564450caa2cb","name":"Boisen, Anja","orcid":"0000-0002-9918-6567","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28266106"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/anie.201700052","issn":["14337851","15213773"],"issn_org":["14337851"],"issue":"14","journal":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","pages":"3901-3905","status":"p","title":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","title_org":"Angewandte Chemie (International ed. in English)","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85014729669"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-01e16958-b43e-4117-a936-3a2b0044e6fa","ku-54d59565-01d4-474d-8f64-2fec6d335428"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nanomechanical Infrared Spectroscopy with Vibrating Filters for Pharmaceutical Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.86-032611","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The first use of thiosemicarbazone-based organocatalysis was demonstrated on both tetrahydropyranylation and 2-deoxygalactosylation reactions. The organocatalysts were optimised using kinetics-based selection. The best catalyst outperformed previously reported thiourea catalysts for tetrahydropyranylation by 50-fold. Hammett investigations of both the organocatalyst and the substrate indicate an oxyanion hole-like reaction mechanism.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Dennis","Langhorn, Line M.","Akselsen, Olivia M.","Nielsen, Bjarne E.","Pittelkow, Michael"],"cuid":["S02-097.80-034991"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Pittelkow, Michael"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thiosemicarbazone organocatalysis tetrahydropyranylation and 000000000002 deoxygalactosylation reactions and kinetics based mechanistic investigation","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c7sc03366d","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.80-034991","identifier":[{"id":"000415877000011","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC5853554","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85034828020","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29568444","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-687507ed-a96b-4e6c-99f6-914c90bd3a5c","ku-034eb4eb-e81b-4bc9-b99f-235e7279dd05"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6FA28091163A5233CA6CCB37A606E7AA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/142123728/c7sc03366d.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.