{"abstract":"In this paper we demonstrate a method for novelty detection of foreign objects in food products using grating-based multimodal X-ray imaging. With this imaging technique three modalities are available with pixel correspondence, enhancing organic materials such as wood chips, insects and soft plastics not detectable by conventional X-ray absorption radiography. We conduct experiments, where several food products are imaged with common foreign objects typically found in the food processing industry. To evaluate the benefit from using this multi-contrast X-ray technique over conventional X-ray absorption imaging, a novelty detection scheme based on well known image- and statistical analysis techniques is proposed. The results show that the presented method gives superior recognition results and highlights the advantage of grating-based imaging.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Einarsdottir, Hildur","Emerson, Monica Jane","Clemmensen, Line Katrine Harder","Scherer, Kai","Willer, Konstantin","Bech, Martin","Larsen, Rasmus","Ersbøll, Bjarne Kjær","Pfeiffer, Franz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-367854"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technical University of Munich"],"keyword":["Dark field imaging","Foreign object detection","Novelty detection","Phase contrast imaging","Texture analysis","X ray radiography"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novelty detection of foreign objects in food using multi modal x ray imaging","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84959333129","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-367854","identifier":[{"id":"84959333129","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d3cbcdbe-c2b8-4d11-aac6-143e5ca32ce1"],"keyword":["Dark-field imaging","Foreign object detection","Novelty detection","Phase-contrast imaging","Texture analysis","X-ray radiography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-09A0D8E38A16B07AE57FCF19991F725B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Statistics and Data Analysis","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Visual Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hildur","key":"einarsdottirpau","last":"Einarsdottir","locid":"dccfa572-37b6-4c51-88bb-bb9027af3f68","name":"Einarsdottir, Hildur","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Monica Jane","key":"emersonpau","last":"Emerson","locid":"18088a3b-c6da-487d-91aa-50377eaebd31","name":"Emerson, Monica Jane","orcid":"0000-0002-6428-9646","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Katrine Harder","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"4e7ff76e-13f9-4365-83b1-d10bab96517b","name":"Clemmensen, Line Katrine Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-5527-5798","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kai","key":"schererpau","last":"Scherer","name":"Scherer, Kai","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Konstantin","key":"willerpau","last":"Willer","name":"Willer, Konstantin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"bechpau","last":"Bech","name":"Bech, Martin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"b3ea098f-fc7a-48a0-94ae-ae033577d7f1","name":"Larsen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0001-8507-0523","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne Kjær","key":"ersbøllpau","last":"Ersbøll","locid":"c2cd9e9b-b4fe-432e-8d5c-6b4b82e775d4","name":"Ersbøll, Bjarne Kjær","orcid":"0000-0003-1262-7890","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Franz","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","name":"Pfeiffer, Franz","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.foodcont.2016.02.023","issn":["09567135","18737129"],"issn_org":["09567135"],"issue":"September","journal":"Food Control","pages":"39-47","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Food Control","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84959333129"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d3cbcdbe-c2b8-4d11-aac6-143e5ca32ce1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Novelty detection of foreign objects in food using multi-modal X-ray imaging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-367854","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: Changes in body composition in cancer patients during chemotherapy are associated with treatment related toxicities or mortalities. Thus, it is relevant to identify accessible, relatively inexpensive, portable and reliable tools for evaluation of body composition in cancer patients during the course of their treatments. Objective: To examine relationships between single cross-sectional thighs magnetic resonance imaging (MRI), skeletal muscle mass (SM) as reference and multi-frequency bioelectrical impedance analysis (BIA) fat free mass (FFM) in patients with colorectal cancer undergoing chemotherapy. Design: In an observational, prospective study we examine the relationships between single cross-sectional thighs MRI (T1-weighted (1.5 T) SM compared to FFM BIA (8-electrodes multi-frequency Tanita MC780MA)) and FFM skin-fold thickness (ST) (4-points (Harpenden, Skinfold Caliper)) and SM equation for non-obese persons from Lee et al. 2000 (L2000) (based on age, height, weight, sex and race). FFM and SM (kg) were calculated based on either area (MRI) or weight. Results: 18 CRC patients (10 males and 8 females) with mean (SD) age 67 yr (6) were measured at baseline, and 13 were available for follow-up. BIA overestimated FFM kg for all 31 measurements with mean (SD) 18.0 kg (6.0) compared to the MRI. ST overestimated FFM kg with mean 12.4 kg (6.2) and L2000 underestimated SM kg in 18 measurements and overestimated in 13 with a total mean of −4.3 kg (6.8). Conclusions BIA and ST were the best alternatives to MRI as they showed constant and thereby correctable errors. The equation, L2000, carried the smallest average measurement error but it was non-constant.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Palle, Stine Skov","Tang Møllehave, Line","Kadkhoda, Zahra Taheri","Johansen, Susanne","Larsen, Lisbeth","Hansen, Janne Willer","Jensen, Nikolaj K G","Elingaard, Anette O","Møller, Alice H","Larsen, Karen","Andersen, Jens Rikardt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-428920"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bioelectrical impedance analysis","Body composition","Colorectal cancer","Fat free mass","Magnetic Resonance Imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multi frequency bioelectrical impedance analysis bia compared to magnetic resonance imaging mri for estimation of fat free mass in colorectal cancer patients treated with chemotherapy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-428920","identifier":[{"id":"28531456","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84993990000","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3b74f51b-d5bf-4613-95eb-e18745657567"],"keyword":["Bioelectrical impedance analysis","Body composition","Colorectal cancer","Fat-free mass","Magnetic resonance imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1608477E517CE94D81860DC29984646"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Stine Skov","key":"pallestineskovpau","last":"Palle","name":"Palle, Stine Skov","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"tangmøllehavelinepau","last":"Tang Møllehave","name":"Tang Møllehave, Line","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Zahra Taheri","key":"kadkhodazahrataheripau","last":"Kadkhoda","name":"Kadkhoda, Zahra Taheri","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Susanne","key":"johansensusannepau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Susanne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lisbeth","key":"larsenlisbethpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Lisbeth","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Janne Willer","key":"hansenjannewillerpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Janne Willer","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nikolaj K G","key":"jensennikolajkgpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Nikolaj K G","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anette O","key":"elingaardanetteopau","last":"Elingaard","name":"Elingaard, Anette O","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Alice H","key":"mølleralicehpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Alice H","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Karen","key":"larsenkarenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Karen","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Jens Rikardt","key":"andersenjensrikardtpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a94b3044-927f-46fa-ba5e-d829d4259fe4","name":"Andersen, Jens Rikardt","orcid":"0000-0003-3503-8474","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28531456"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clnesp.2016.09.003","issn":["24054577"],"journal":"Clinical Nutrition ESPEN","pages":"8-15","status":"p","title":"Clinical Nutrition ESPEN","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84993990000"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3b74f51b-d5bf-4613-95eb-e18745657567"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multi-frequency bioelectrical impedance analysis (BIA) compared to magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) for estimation of fat-free mass in colorectal cancer patients treated with chemotherapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-428920","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To assess the prevalence of somatic MTOR mutations in focal cortical dysplasia (FCD) and of germline MTOR mutations in a broad range of epilepsies. METHODS: We collected 20 blood-brain paired samples from patients with FCD and searched for somatic variants using deep-targeted gene panel sequencing. Germline mutations in MTOR were assessed in a French research cohort of 93 probands with focal epilepsies and in a diagnostic Danish cohort of 245 patients with a broad range of epilepsies. Data sharing among collaborators allowed us to ascertain additional germline variants in MTOR. RESULTS: We detected recurrent somatic variants (p.Ser2215Phe, p.Ser2215Tyr, and p.Leu1460Pro) in the MTOR gene in 37% of participants with FCD II and showed histologic evidence for activation of the mTORC1 signaling cascade in brain tissue. We further identified 5 novel de novo germline missense MTOR variants in 6 individuals with a variable phenotype from focal, and less frequently generalized, epilepsies without brain malformations, to macrocephaly, with or without moderate intellectual disability. In addition, an inherited variant was found in a mother-daughter pair with nonlesional autosomal dominant nocturnal frontal lobe epilepsy. CONCLUSIONS: Our data illustrate the increasingly important role of somatic mutations of the MTOR gene in FCD and germline mutations in the pathogenesis of focal epilepsy syndromes with and without brain malformation or macrocephaly.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Møller, Rikke S.","Weckhuysen, Sarah","Chipaux, Mathilde","Marsan, Elise","Taly, Valerie","Bebin, E Martina","Hiatt, Susan M","Prokop, Jeremy W","Bowling, Kevin M","Mei, Davide","Conti, Valerio","de la Grange, Pierre","Ferrand-Sorbets, Sarah","Dorfmüller, Georg","Lambrecq, Virginie","Larsen, Line H G","LeGuern, Eric","Guerrini, Renzo","Rubboli, Guido","Cooper, Gregory M","Baulac, Stéphanie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-601153"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"germline and somatic mutations in the mtor gene in focal cortical dysplasia and epilepsy","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1212/NXG.0000000000000118","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-601153","identifier":[{"id":"85012104030","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27830187","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5089441","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-61acaf38-505a-454d-85c9-99a966e31ba2"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E6A2EC576B06313048F695F039AB0993"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/124974976/Germline_and_somatic_mutations_in_the_MTOR_gene_in_focal_cortical_dysplasia_and_epilepsy.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1212/NXG.0000000000000118","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5089441/pdf/NG2016003145.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - The Epilepsyhospital Filadelfia"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Amplexa Genetics A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke S","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"85de2fa9-456c-4427-8c30-7dc1bdd4bcf0","name":"Møller, Rikke S.","name_org":"Møller, Rikke S","orcid":"0000-0002-9664-1448","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"weckhuysenpau","last":"Weckhuysen","name":"Weckhuysen, Sarah","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathilde","key":"chipauxpau","last":"Chipaux","name":"Chipaux, Mathilde","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Elise","key":"marsanpau","last":"Marsan","name":"Marsan, Elise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Valerie","key":"talypau","last":"Taly","name":"Taly, Valerie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"E Martina","key":"bebinpau","last":"Bebin","name":"Bebin, E Martina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Susan M","key":"hiattpau","last":"Hiatt","name":"Hiatt, Susan M","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeremy W","key":"prokoppau","last":"Prokop","name":"Prokop, Jeremy W","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kevin M","key":"bowlingpau","last":"Bowling","name":"Bowling, Kevin M","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Davide","key":"meipau","last":"Mei","name":"Mei, Davide","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Valerio","key":"contipau","last":"Conti","name":"Conti, Valerio","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pierre","key":"delagrangepau","last":"de la Grange","name":"de la Grange, Pierre","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"ferrandsorbetspau","last":"Ferrand-Sorbets","name":"Ferrand-Sorbets, Sarah","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Georg","key":"dorfmüllerpau","last":"Dorfmüller","name":"Dorfmüller, Georg","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Virginie","key":"lambrecqpau","last":"Lambrecq","name":"Lambrecq, Virginie","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Line H G","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Line H G","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Eric","key":"leguernpau","last":"LeGuern","name":"LeGuern, Eric","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Renzo","key":"guerrinipau","last":"Guerrini","name":"Guerrini, Renzo","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Guido","key":"rubbolipau","last":"Rubboli","locid":"1b44634c-91ac-41f6-bd79-7c3199ea6f5d","name":"Rubboli, Guido","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregory M","key":"cooperpau","last":"Cooper","name":"Cooper, Gregory M","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Stéphanie","key":"baulacpau","last":"Baulac","name":"Baulac, Stéphanie","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27830187"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1212/nxg.0000000000000118","issn":["23767839"],"issue":"6","journal":"Neurology: Genetics","paperid":"e118","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Neurology: Genetics","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85012104030"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","amplexa genetics a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-61acaf38-505a-454d-85c9-99a966e31ba2"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Germline and somatic mutations in the MTOR gene in focal cortical dysplasia and epilepsy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-601153","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To delineate phenotypic heterogeneity, we describe the clinical features of a cohort of patients with GABRA1 gene mutations. METHODS: Patients with GABRA1 mutations were ascertained through an international collaboration. Clinical, EEG, and genetic data were collected. Functional analysis of 4 selected mutations was performed using the Xenopus laevis oocyte expression system. RESULTS: The study included 16 novel probands and 3 additional family members with a disease-causing mutation in the GABRA1 gene. The phenotypic spectrum varied from unspecified epilepsy (1), juvenile myoclonic epilepsy (2), photosensitive idiopathic generalized epilepsy (1), and generalized epilepsy with febrile seizures plus (1) to severe epileptic encephalopathies (11). In the epileptic encephalopathy group, the patients had seizures beginning between the first day of life and 15 months, with a mean of 7 months. Predominant seizure types in all patients were tonic-clonic in 9 participants (56%) and myoclonic seizures in 5 (31%). EEG showed a generalized photoparoxysmal response in 6 patients (37%). Four selected mutations studied functionally revealed a loss of function, without a clear genotype-phenotype correlation. CONCLUSIONS: GABRA1 mutations make a significant contribution to the genetic etiology of both benign and severe epilepsy syndromes. Myoclonic and tonic-clonic seizures with pathologic response to photic stimulation are common and shared features in both mild and severe phenotypes.","author_count":46,"contributors":["Johannesen, Katrine M.","Marini, Carla","Pfeffer, Siona","Møller, Rikke S.","Dorn, Thomas","Niturad, Christina","Gardella, Elena","Weber, Yvonne","Søndergård, Marianne","Hjalgrim, Helle","Nikanorova, Mariana","Becker, Felicitas","Larsen, Line H G","Dahl, Hans A","Maier, Oliver","Mei, Davide","Biskup, Saskia","Klein, Karl M","Reif, Philipp S","Rosenow, Felix","Elias, Abdallah F","Hudson, Cindy","Helbig, Katherine L","Schubert-Bast, Susanne","Scordo, Maria R","Craiu, Dana","Djémié, Tania","Hoffman-Zacharska, Dorota","Caglayan, Hande","Helbig, Ingo","Serratosa, Jose","Striano, Pasquale","De Jonghe, Peter","Weckhuysen, Sarah","Suls, Arvid","Muru, Kai","Talvik, Inga","Talvik, Tiina","Muhle, Hiltrud","Borggraefe, Ingo","Rost, Imma","Guerrini, Renzo","Lerche, Holger","Lemke, Johannes R","Rubboli, Guido","Maljevic, Snezana"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-635425"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phenotypic spectrum of gabra000000000001 from generalized epilepsies to severe epileptic encephalopathies","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84987678754","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-635425","identifier":[{"id":"84987678754","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27521439","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-d93878bf-eef4-458a-8cac-ab87c2aae797"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-53676B2C3181838DCD0451A40B9AD931"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - The Epilepsyhospital Filadelfia"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine","key":"johannes