{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The risk of ischemic stroke, systemic thromboembolism, and all-cause death among heart failure patients previously diagnosed with diabetes mellitus is poorly described. We evaluated the risk of these endpoints among heart failure patients without diagnosed atrial fibrillation according to the presence of diabetes mellitus. METHODS: Population-based nationwide cohort study of non-anticoagulated patients diagnosed with incident heart failure during 2000-2012, identified by record linkage between nationwide registries in Denmark. We calculated relative risks after 1year to evaluate the association between diabetes and risk of events in 39,357 heart failure patients, among whom 18.1% had diabetes. Analysis took into account competing risks of death. RESULTS: Absolute risks of all endpoints were higher in patients with diabetes compared to patients without diabetes after 1-year follow-up (ischemic stroke: 4.1% vs. 2.8%; systemic thromboembolism: 11.9% vs. 8.6%; all-cause death: 22.1% vs. 21.4%). Diabetes was significantly associated with an increased risk of ischemic stroke (adjusted relative risk [RR]: 1.27, 95% confidence interval [CI]: 1.07-1.51); systemic thromboembolism (RR: 1.20, 95% CI: 1.11-1.30); and all-cause death (RR: 1.17, 95% CI: 1.11-1.23). Additionally, time since diabetes diagnosis was associated with higher adjusted cumulative incidences of ischemic stroke, systemic thromboembolism, and all-cause death (p for trend, p<0.001). CONCLUSIONS: Among heart failure patients without atrial fibrillation, diabetes was associated with a significantly increased risk of ischemic stroke, systemic thromboembolism, and all-cause death compared to those without diabetes, even after adjustment for concomitant cardiovascular risk factors. Increased focus on secondary prevention in heart failure patients with diabetes may be warranted.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Melgaard, Line","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Søgaard, Peter","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Lip, Gregory Y H","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-080829"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City Hospital in Birmingham","University of Birmingham"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diabetes mellitus and risk of ischemic stroke in patients with heart failure and no atrial fibrillation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-080829","identifier":[{"id":"84961572517","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26874450","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000372530700001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-69e51b01-d13c-4384-a2fb-1a96d661e100"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FE874AA829D397D0C6EF9E917BB5B2FD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Birmingham","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"city hospital in birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"City Hospital in Birmingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"melgaardpau","last":"Melgaard","locid":"88687b9c-5b56-4584-a89a-89fdeca4fd54","name":"Melgaard, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"gorstrasmussenpau","last":"Gorst-Rasmussen","locid":"2aa85786-c0b1-42ec-93d4-eb7a75696409","name":"Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"30606c01-a86b-4eee-90ef-b4268fedaee9","name":"Søgaard, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Hvilsted","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"20cfd847-7f3e-4c77-88c0-32d3432496ed","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y H","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Bjerregaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a3c6747f-b9db-488b-8eb9-887d38742880","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26874450"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijcard.2016.02.004","issn":["01675273","18741754"],"issn_org":["01675273"],"journal":"International Journal of Cardiology","pages":"1-6","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cardiology","volume":"209"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961572517"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-69e51b01-d13c-4384-a2fb-1a96d661e100"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Diabetes mellitus and risk of ischemic stroke in patients with heart failure and no atrial fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-080829","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This work investigates different network design considerations with respect to energy-efficiency, under green-field resilient multi-layer network deployment. The problem of energy efficient, reliable multi-layer network design is known to result in different trade-offs between key performance measures. In this complex problem, considerations such as client traffic granularity, applied grooming policies and multi-layer resiliency add even more complexity. A commercially available network planning tool is used to investigate the interplay between different methods for resilient capacity planning in multi-layer networks and performance measures such as network resource utilization, availability, agility to traffic fluctuations and energy consumption. A green-field network deployment scenario is considered, where different resiliency methods, design methodologies and grooming strategies are applied. Switching off low-utilized transport links has been investigated via a pro-active re-routing applied during the network planning. Our analysis shows that design factors such as the applied survivability strategy and the applied planning method have higher impact on the key performance indicators compared to the pro-active re-routing under the investigated network deployment scenarios. Power consumption reduction between 9,7% (when applying pro-active re-routing) and 65,7% (when applying a more suitable design methodology) have been demonstrated.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Fagertun, Anna Manolova","Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","Ruepp, Sarah Renée"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-338958"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-15","place":"Halmstad, se","start":"2016-09-13","title":"8th International Workshop on Resilient Networks Design and Modeling","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Energy consumption","Energy efficiency","Multi layer","Network Planning","Optical fiber cables","Optical fiber networks","Optical fibers","Optical switches","Planning","Resiliency"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design considerations for energy efficient resilient multi layer networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84999885201","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-338958","identifier":[{"id":"84999885201","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-734874fe-5873-4552-8bdb-5ca5d9d7675b"],"keyword":["Energy consumption","Energy efficiency","Optical fiber cables","Optical fiber networks","Optical fibers","Optical switches","Planning","multi-layer","network planning","resiliency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C2192DC72A6F5F5466DDC34CC9E0A2D9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna Manolova","key":"fagertunpau","last":"Fagertun","locid":"4113ef4f-ae5e-409d-98d3-6b7f503e7b0c","name":"Fagertun, Anna Manolova","orcid":"0000-0003-3464-3226","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Pyndt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"e76034cd-61d0-43dd-8c6d-0aa95c672b80","name":"Larsen, Line Maria Pyndt","name_org":"Hansen, Line Pyndt","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-5851","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah Renée","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/rndm.2016.7608267","isbn":["9781467390231"],"pages":"51-57","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2016 8th International Workshop on Resilient Networks Design and Modeling"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84999885201"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-734874fe-5873-4552-8bdb-5ca5d9d7675b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Design considerations for energy efficient, resilient, multi-layer networks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-338958","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Antisense peptide nucleic acid (PNA) oligomers constitute a novel class of potential antibiotics that inhibit bacterial growth via specific knockdown of essential gene expression. However, discovery of efficient, nontoxic delivery vehicles for such PNA oligomers has remained a challenge. In the present study we show that antimicrobial peptides (AMPs) with an intracellular mode of action can be efficient vehicles for bacterial delivery of an antibacterial PNA targeting the essential acpP gene. The results demonstrate that buforin 2-A (BF2-A), drosocin, oncocin 10, Pep-1-K, KLW-9,13-a, (P59→W59)-Tat48-60, BF-2A-RXR, and drosocin-RXR are capable of transporting PNA effectively into E. coli (MICs of 1-4 μM). Importantly, presence of the inner-membrane peptide transporter SbmA was not required for antibacterial activity of PNA-AMP conjugates containing Pep-1-K, KLW-9,13-a, or drosocin-RXR (MICs of 2-4 μM).","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Anna Mette","Vedel, Line","Larsen, Camilla Josephine","Yavari, Niloofar","Nielsen, Peter E.","Franzyk, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-457453"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antibacterial peptide nucleic acid antimicrobial peptide pna amp conjugates antisense targeting of fatty acid biosynthesis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-457453","identifier":[{"id":"26938833","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84965017823","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6b396019-a1ca-46ad-b3de-7ced4d47330c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E9FEA03F7DB1A78F25D23294718CD313"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Mette","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5e81b7fd-9d07-4dc6-8a5e-20d5fa6cc0d0","name":"Hansen, Anna Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-1162-8592","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gitte","key":"bonkepau","last":"Bonke","locid":"2a30ceee-2443-4a22-9599-6b9171ab1461","name":"Vedel, Line","name_org":"Bonke, Gitte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla Josephine","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Camilla Josephine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niloofar","key":"yavaripau","last":"Yavari","locid":"60d57251-0ca0-4c34-8dde-53422b4f03e4","name":"Yavari, Niloofar","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter E.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"74cb6e41-3bfc-4d0a-a0df-7bd8fa9c2856","name":"Nielsen, Peter E.","orcid":"0000-0001-8771-330X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"franzykpau","last":"Franzyk","locid":"5120ce68-6886-4ac8-8178-310a47d19261","name":"Franzyk, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2822-1927","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26938833"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.bioconjchem.6b00013","issn":["10431802","15204812"],"issn_org":["10431802"],"issue":"4","journal":"Bioconjugate Chemistry","pages":"863-867","status":"p","title":"Bioconjugate Chemistry","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84965017823"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6b396019-a1ca-46ad-b3de-7ced4d47330c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Antibacterial Peptide Nucleic Acid-Antimicrobial Peptide (PNA-AMP) Conjugates : Antisense Targeting of Fatty Acid Biosynthesis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-457453","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Benign familial infantile seizures (BFIS), paroxysmal kinesigenic dyskinesia (PKD), and their combination - known as infantile convulsions and paroxysmal choreoathetosis (ICCA) - are related autosomal dominant diseases. PRRT2 (proline-rich transmembrane protein 2 gene) has been identified as the major gene in all three conditions, found to be mutated in 80-90% of familial and 30-35% of sporadic cases. METHODS: We searched for the genetic defect in PRRT2-negative, unrelated families with BFIS or ICCA using whole exome or targeted gene panel sequencing, and performed a detailed clinico-neurophysiological workup. RESULTS: In three families with a total of 16 affected members, we identified the same, co-segregating heterozygous missense mutation (c.4447G>A; p.E1483K) in SCN8A, encoding a voltage-gated sodium channel. A founder effect was excluded by linkage analysis. All individuals but one had normal cognitive and motor milestones, neuroimaging and interictal neurological status. Fifteen affected members presented with afebrile focal or generalized tonic-clonic seizures during the first-second year of life; 5 of them experienced single unprovoked seizures later on. One patient had seizures only at school age. All patients stayed otherwise seizure-free, most without medication. Interictal EEG was normal in all cases but two. Five/16 patients developed additional brief paroxysmal episodes in puberty, either dystonic/dyskinetic or \"shivering\" attacks, triggered by stretching, motor initiation or by emotional stimuli. In one case, we recorded typical PKD spells by video-EEG-polygraphy, documenting a cortical involvement. INTERPRETATION: Our study establishes SCN8A as a novel gene in which a recurrent mutation causes BFIS/ICCA, expanding the clinical-genetic spectrum of combined epileptic and dyskinetic syndromes. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":36,"contributors":["Gardella, Elena","Becker, Felicitas","Møller, Rikke S","Schubert, Julian","Lemke, Johannes R","Larsen, Line Hg","Eiberg, Hans","Nothnagel, Michael","Thiele, Holger","Altmüller, Janine","Syrbe, Steffen","Merkenschlager, Andreas","Bast, Thomas","Steinhoff, Bernhard J","Nürnberg, Peter","Mang, Yang","Bakke Møller, Louise","Gellert, Pia","Heron, Sarah","Dibbens, Leanne","Weckhuysen, Sarah","Dahl, Hans Atli","Biskup, Saskia","Tommerup, Niels","Hjalgrim, Helle","Lerche, Holger","Beniczky, Sándor","Weber, Yvonne G"],"cuid":["S03-097.90-017963"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Child","Child Preschool","Female","Genetic Predisposition to Disease genetics","Humans","Male","Mutation genetics","NAV1 6 Voltage Gated Sodium Channel genetics","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-FILA"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-FILA","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"benign infantile seizures and paroxysmal dyskinesia caused by an scn000000000008a mutation","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84960424771","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.90-017963","identifier":[{"id":"000371896800009","type":"wos"},{"id":"84960424771","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26677014","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-490f1c52-2eaf-4420-ad93-27989858d4c1","ku-d27cad24-a517-4651-af3b-7e4894b21a4c","sdu-0b5b1464-2a7f-4fee-be06-0a386c024c2b"],"keyword":["Child","Child, Preschool","Chorea/diagnosis","Epilepsy, Benign Neonatal/diagnosis","Female","Genetic Predisposition to Disease/genetics","Humans","Male","Mutation/genetics","NAV1.6 Voltage-Gated Sodium Channel/genetics","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-3768440D9C22836BB29454CA4AC05367"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - The Epilepsyhospital Filadelfia"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Amplexa Genetics A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Medical Genetics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"filadelfia danish epilepsy hospital","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-FILA","l3nn":"Filadelfia - Danish Epilepsy Hospital","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Filadelfia - Danish Epilepsy Hospital","namevar":["Epilepsihospitalet Filadelfia"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-FILA","u