ubboli, G","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"first":"Deb K","key":"paldebkpau","last":"Pal","name":"Pal, Deb K","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans A","key":"dahlhansapau","last":"Dahl","locid":"47a1b0bc-064a-4f1b-a102-6e455ba8a743","name":"Dahl, Hans A","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27781031"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000448369","issn":["16618769","16618777"],"issn_org":["16618769"],"issue":"4","journal":"Molecular Syndromology","pages":"210-219","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Molecular Syndromology","title_org":"Molecular syndromology","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84983748486"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Companies","Private Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","amplexa genetics a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dd314d09-2b25-429d-af98-529df3543826","ku-c6f6d84c-b9df-437a-a5cf-d5858a6536f3","sdu-0316c54c-130b-46cf-ae1b-7d1cee865485"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Gene Panel Testing in Epileptic Encephalopathies and Familial Epilepsies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-028709","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The present paper is an account of a design-based action research study. The research question focused on how to create a pedagogical concept for ICT-supported peer interaction that enabled cross-age students to share experiences and knowledge in relation to internships. Internships in higher education are a natural booster of the elusive concept of professional identity. Students return from internships with a better understanding of what they do, know and are professionally. The learning that takes place for the intern remains individual and is only shared with a supervisor. The present study is based on the idea that internship students’ individual learning could be shared with younger peers through online interaction. In the context of a bachelor programme in Northern Denmark, the concept was implemented as discussion forums embedded in the local LMS. In these forums, the students engaged in discussions of professional matters and accounts of daily practices in internships. The analysis of the forum interactions, a survey and a focus group interview revealed that the students perceived the concept as a meaningful activity. The key findings centered on issues regarding: responsibility, relevance and roles. The students felt a strong sense of responsibility toward each other in providing meaningful content and frequent activity and replies to posts, which served as a source of motivation. The question of relevance relates strongly to the timing of the activity, as well as clear expectations and purpose. To the cross-age students, tutor/tutee roles could have provided further direction and purpose of the interaction, but this was not initially part of the concept. This research gave insight into the creation of a pedagogical cross-age concept supported by ICT that could benefit practitioners and researchers in higher education.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Gudiksen, Maria Boel Klok","Horn, Line Helverskov","Knudsen, Torben Broe","Larsen, Louise Landbo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-106674"],"event":{"acronym":"ECEL","end":"2016-10-28","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2016-10-27","title":"ECEL 2016: 15th European Conference on e-learning","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a pedagogical design for ict supported cross age peer interaction","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.academic-bookshop.com/shop/search.php?pagefile=ourshop&pageid=2351980&q=ecel&searchbutton=%3CSPAN%3E%3CSPAN%3EGo%21%3C%2FSPAN%3E%3C%2FSPAN%3E","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-106674","identifier":[{"id":"85000766319","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c31e9b26-9b2d-423b-aa3b-8e8115d3f654"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-6349C5EF1E21899D347335A1FBF3AC8D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["University College of Northern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, D4Learning: Digital, Dialogic, Democratic, Development. Research on Innovative IT-integrating Learning Processes (Learning)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Boel Klok","key":"gudiksenpau","last":"Gudiksen","name":"Gudiksen, Maria Boel Klok","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Helverskov","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","locid":"80066097-b69a-49ec-a31e-b0e7f1f95d7d","name":"Horn, Line Helverskov","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Broe","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Torben Broe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Landbo","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Louise Landbo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jarmila","key":"novotnápedh","last":"Novotná","name":"Novotná, Jarmila","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Antonín","key":"janaíkpedh","last":"Janaík","name":"Janaík, Antonín","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781911218173"],"isbn":["9781911218180"],"pages":"249-255","publisher":"Academic Conferences International (ACI)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 15th European Conference on e-Learning ECEL 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85000766319"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Universities","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c31e9b26-9b2d-423b-aa3b-8e8115d3f654"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Pedagogical Design for ICT-Supported Cross-age Peer Interaction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-106674","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"User-generated information types (ratings and reviews) are highly used when booking hotel rooms on Online Travel Agency (OTA) websites. The impact of user-generated information on decision-making is often investigated through quantitative research, thereby not examining in depth how and why travelers use this information. This paper therefore presents a qualitative study conducted to achieve a deeper understanding. We investigated the use of reviews and average rating in a hotel-booking-context through a laboratory experiment, which involved a task of examining a hotel on a pre-designed OTA website followed by an interview. We processed the data from the interview, and the analysis resulted in a model generalizing the use of reviews and average rating in the deliberation phase of a hotel-booking. The findings are overall consistent with related research. Yet, beyond this, the qualitative approach has given some deep insights that expand the knowledge in the field.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Buus, Line Thomassen","Jensen, Charlotte Thodberg","Jessen, Anne Mette Karnøe","Jørgensen, Lotte Ishoy","Laursen, Jeanette Kølbæk","Larsen, Lars Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-114345"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-31","place":"Florida, us","start":"2016-07-27","title":"AHFE 2016 International Conference on The Human Side of Service Engineering","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of reviews and average rating on hotel booking intention a qualitative study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.springer.com/us/book/9783319419466","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-114345","identifier":[{"id":"84986275756","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-dd15e631-7aa0-4639-bcbf-a0c1684acf5a"],"keyword":["Hotel-booking · Decision-making · Review · Rating · User-generated information · eWOM · Qualitative research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5C97E812312DDC803AA05AED70C148B3"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Thomassen","key":"buuspau","last":"Buus","locid":"fd782d71-0dbc-40e2-91a6-0c8c5fb347fc","name":"Buus, Line Thomassen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Thodberg","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"adc3b813-9e0e-4d97-b35b-4d1199ed57c4","name":"Jensen, Charlotte Thodberg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Mette Karnøe","key":"jessenpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"950393a4-7515-4c14-84dc-400ec9cb7ea7","name":"Jessen, Anne Mette Karnøe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte Ishoy","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"d8a45a67-e7ea-41b8-bb01-69d97b98639c","name":"Jørgensen, Lotte Ishoy","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeanette Kølbæk","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"a0d11ecf-766c-499d-b4d2-e09cd34ad856","name":"Laursen, Jeanette Kølbæk","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Bo","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"0f770a4f-bd24-4330-be1e-877e6b58f6c3","name":"Larsen, Lars Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-0509-2165","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tareq Z.","key":"ahrampedh","last":"Ahram","name":"Ahram, Tareq Z.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Waldemar","key":"karwowskipedh","last":"Karwowski","name":"Karwowski, Waldemar","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-41947-3_30","eisbn":["9783319419473"],"isbn":["9783319419466"],"issn":["16153871"],"pages":"319-331","publisher":"Springer Publishing Company","series":"Advances in Intelligent Systems and Computing","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the AHFE 2016 International Conference on The Human Side of Service Engineering, July 27-31, 2016, Florida, USA","title":"Advances in The Human Side of Service Engineering"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84986275756"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dd15e631-7aa0-4639-bcbf-a0c1684acf5a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Impact of Reviews and Average Rating on Hotel-Booking-Intention : A Qualitative Study","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-114345","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: Hypertension is a major risk factor for development of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD). Although lowering blood pressure with antihypertensive drugs reduces the increased risk of ASCVD, residual increased risk still remains, suggesting that hypertension may cause chronic changes that promote atherosclerosis. Thus, we tested the hypothesis that hypertension increases the susceptibility to atherosclerosis in mice even after a period of re-established normotension. Methods: We used the 2-kidney, 1-clip (2K1C) technique to induce angiotensin-driven renovascular hypertension, and overexpression of the proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 9 (PCSK9) gene to cause severe hypercholesterolemia and atherosclerosis. Results: First, we performed 2K1C (n = 8) or sham surgery (n = 9) in PCSK9 transgenic mice before they were fed a high fat diet for 14 weeks. As expected, 2K1C did not affect cholesterol levels, but induced cardiac hypertrophy and significantly increased the atherosclerotic lesion area compared to sham mice (1.8 fold, p < 0.01). Next, we performed 2K1C (n = 13) or sham surgery (n = 14) in wild-type mice but removed the clipped/sham-operated kidney after 10 weeks to eliminate hypertension, and subsequently induced hypercholesterolemia by way of adeno-associated virus-mediated hepatic gene transfer of PCSK9 combined with high-fat diet. After 14 weeks of hypercholesterolemia, atherosclerotic lesion areas were not significantly different in mice with or without prior 2K1C hypertension (0.95 fold, p = 0.35). Conclusion: Renovascular hypertension in mice does not induce pro-atherogenic changes that persist beyond the hypertensive phase. These results indicate that hypertension only promotes atherogenesis when coinciding temporally with hypercholesterolemia.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","Nilsson, Line","Larsen, Tore G","Espeseth, Eirild","Bek, Marie","Bjørklund, Martin Mæng","Hagensen, Mette K","Wolff, Anne","Gunnersen, Stine","Füchtbauer, Ernst-Martin","Boedtkjer, Ebbe","Bentzon, Jacob Fog"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-253392"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atherosclerosis","Hypertension","PCSK9"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prior renovascular hypertension does not predispose to atherosclerosis in mice","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84963619579","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-253392","identifier":[{"id":"84963619579","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27100924","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d956e0eb-418d-453f-8124-c45d18868eaf"],"keyword":["Atherosclerosis","Hypertension","PCSK9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2E5BEB074E08CB9DD1D9B947B0B90457"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Bødtker","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"f995af52-018b-4fa9-a398-c1bdc7ab1bd0","name":"Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"ec88681d-da88-4113-aeb1-d437e44aec34","name":"Nilsson, Line","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tore G","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"8deac003-89b6-4cf7-bc60-e43502450523","name":"Larsen, Tore G","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eirild","key":"espesethpau","last":"Espeseth","locid":"8a57d73b-150e-431f-977f-56b23fb77bd4","name":"Espeseth, Eirild","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"bekpau","last":"Bek","name":"Bek, Marie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin M","key":"bjørklundpau","last":"Bjørklund","locid":"296bc88d-5b12-43fb-bca4-47a7bfc1b096","name":"Bjørklund, Martin Mæng","name_org":"Bjørklund, Martin M","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette K","key":"hagensenpau","last":"Hagensen","locid":"2dad0671-9960-48b6-b2d3-c9c4c5b94f74","name":"Hagensen, Mette K","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"wolffpau","last":"Wolff","locid":"40919c5b-04a9-4004-848d-736a519a5f55","name":"Wolff, Anne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine","key":"gunnersenpau","last":"Gunnersen","locid":"c720151e-efad-42e7-8a65-91ce512ffe95","name":"Gunnersen, Stine","orcid":"0000-0002-0342-2220","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ernst-Martin","key":"füchtbauerpau","last":"Füchtbauer","locid":"aae550a1-5156-4de4-ac28-c6df3b08384c","name":"Füchtbauer, Ernst-Martin","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ebbe","key":"boedtkjerpau","last":"Boedtkjer","locid":"cf192eb0-d018-4de8-89ce-f392ec8e8d68","name":"Boedtkjer, Ebbe","orcid":"0000-0002-5078-9279","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob F","key":"bentzonpau","last":"Bentzon","locid":"b19cdb97-a953-43ff-ad51-19d0a680caed","name":"Bentzon, Jacob Fog","name_org":"Bentzon, Jacob F","orcid":"0000-0002-3020-5002","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27100924"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.atherosclerosis.2016.03.030","issn":["00219150","15675688"],"issn_org":["00219150"],"journal":"Atherosclerosis","pages":"157-63","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"Atherosclerosis","volume":"249"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963619579"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d956e0eb-418d-453f-8124-c45d18868eaf"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prior renovascular hypertension does not predispose to atherosclerosis in mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-253392","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Formation of insoluble aggregates in acidic whey protein isolate (WPI) beverages during storage is a quality concern. Earlier studies showed that changes in processing methods from 95 °C for 180 s–120 °C for 20 s could prevent it. In the present study, WPI drinks were stored for up to 12 months and insoluble aggregates formed in re-solubilised WPI and its liquid phase analysed by proteomics. Insoluble aggregates were found to be enriched in caseinomacropeptides (CMP). Increased peptide formation by weak acid hydrolysis, especially of CMP, was found at 120 °C. Further enhanced hydrolysis of CMP was obtained by deamidation as well as by the presence of the genetic variant A of CMP. Batch variations may therefore be assigned to variations in CMP as well as variations in the distribution of genetic variants of A and B in different WPI batches used for the production of the WPI products.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Le, Thao Thi Thu","Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary","Villumsen, Nanna Stengaard","Kristiansen, Gitte Hald","Ravn Nielsen, Line","B. Nielsen, Søren","Hammershøj, Marianne","Larsen, Lotte Bach"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-259765"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aggregates","Proteomics","Whey protein"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using proteomics to characterise storage induced aggregates in acidic whey protein isolate drinks","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84961223621","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-259765","identifier":[{"id":"84961223621","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e4719714-3663-45e1-80e0-be99e76e3f04"],"keyword":["aggregates","proteomics","whey protein"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-430CFC5BCD3A1B1FCE32867AF35203A6"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Food Science, Department of Food Science - Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"arla foods","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ARLA","l3nl":"Arla Foods","l3nn":"Arla Foods","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Arla Foods","namevar":["Arla Foods"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ARLA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thao Thi Thu","key":"lepau","last":"Le","locid":"f114fe35-c2f1-437d-b00b-8beded4747a9","name":"Le, Thao Thi Thu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Drud","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"030ede5c-2e12-40c1-9d0c-543f0c5ffadf","name":"Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary","name_org":"Nielsen, Søren Drud","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna Stengaard","key":"villumsenpau","last":"Villumsen","locid":"45a4023b-95a1-44a9-9923-86230284ddee","name":"Villumsen, Nanna Stengaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte Hald","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"82722678-5af2-4c59-9536-648f555c249a","name":"Kristiansen, Gitte Hald","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"ravnnielsenpau","last":"Ravn Nielsen","name":"Ravn Nielsen, Line","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"bnielsenpau","last":"B. Nielsen","name":"B. Nielsen, Søren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne","key":"hammershøjpau","last":"Hammershøj","locid":"483a27e1-b030-4e4b-8441-76424c064fed","name":"Hammershøj, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0001-9297-6526","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte Bach","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"204d7240-6828-4ee0-8ef5-77a4a2ac92d4","name":"Larsen, Lotte Bach","orcid":"0000-0001-9674-0107","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.idairyj.2016.01.028","issn":["09586946","18790143"],"issn_org":["09586946"],"journal":"International Dairy Journal","pages":"39-46","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"International Dairy Journal","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961223621"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Arla Foods","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e4719714-3663-45e1-80e0-be99e76e3f04"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Using proteomics to characterise storage-induced aggregates in acidic whey protein isolate drinks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-259765","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"At a hospital in Denmark around 40 midwives support the pregnancy of approx. 6000 pregnant women every year. Their role is to monitor the pregnancies and prepare the women for labour. Based on the due date of a woman, authority guidelines prescribe specific and mostly rather narrow time windows within which the pregnant woman should have consultations with a midwife. Therefore, once a pregnant woman enters the system, here sequence of consultations for the time period until labour is fairly fixed. There is a clear goal that, as far as possible, each pregnant woman should see the same midwife at every consultation. Every week the newly arrived pregnant women are assigned an arbitrary free time slot belonging to a specific midwife. In turn this midwife is expected to have consultations with this woman in specific weeks according to the authority guidelines. This random assignment of pregnant woman to specific midwives, without any concern to the midwives? future schedules, means that each midwife has a very unbalanced workload over the year. Furthermore, it means that there is an imbalance between the workloads of the different midwifes. The aim of this project is therefore to devise a method that can make a fair distribution of pregnant women among the midwives. The distribution should result in a balanced work load for each midwife and a balanced work load among the midwives while at the same time making sure that the time windows for consultations are not violated.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Græse, Line","Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","Larsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-374818"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-07","place":"Poznan, pl","start":"2016-07-03","title":"28th European Conference on Operational Research","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"planning of midwives","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-374818","ids":["dtu-eac12fc6-69b7-44f8-9b8d-277e185ee6e4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-590EF1F2ADDBFAD5018A032658A87DB7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"græsepau","last":"Græse","name":"Græse, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"vilhelmsenpau","last":"Vilhelmsen","locid":"6ceebc69-a38c-4b56-9070-23135aa491c6","name":"Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-8260-6791","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d1af4d26-e92b-414c-b534-25b2b607a0d9","name":"Larsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9119-3586","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-eac12fc6-69b7-44f8-9b8d-277e185ee6e4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Planning of Midwives","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-374818","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Purpose. To describe associations between retinal vessel diameters and cardiovascular risk markers and mortality. Methods. The present study included 908 persons aged 30 to 60 years. Vessel diameters were expressed as central retinal venular equivalent (CRVE) and central retinal arteriolar equivalent (CRAE). Multiple linear regression analyses and Cox regression models were used. Results. Multiple linear regression analyses showed that narrower CRAE was associated with higher systolic blood pressure, age, and higher HDL cholesterol, whereas wider CRAE and CRVE were associated with smoking. Narrower CRVE was associated with higher HDL cholesterol. In an age-adjusted model, associations between wider CRVE and risk of ischemic heart disease were found (P < 0.001). Wider CRVE was associated with all-cause mortality (HR = 2.02, P = 0.033) in a model adjusted for age, gender, and blood pressure. However, the association was not statistically significant after additional adjustment for smoking. Conclusions. The associations between retinal vessel diameters and known cardiovascular risk factors were confirmed. All-cause mortality was not associated with retinal vessel diameters when adjusting for relevant confounders.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Drobnjak, Dragana","Munch, Inger Christine","Glümer, Charlotte","Faerch, Kristine","Kessel, Line","Larsen, Michael","Veiby, Nina C B B"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-502575"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"retinal vessel diameters and their relationship with cardiovascular risk and all cause mortality in the inter000000000099 eye study a 000000000015 year follow up","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2016/6138659","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-502575","identifier":[{"id":"28053777","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85008931766","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5174182","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-b6c36dce-7cdc-4c62-8c5b-931c616fba5c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-30F07AE3267C08EDEDDF387CCD712A60"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2016/6138659","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Dragana","key":"drobnjakpau","last":"Drobnjak","name":"Drobnjak, Dragana","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inger Christine","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","locid":"a1af1ee5-c4b4-44d8-a7af-b7c1ce0882ac","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"glümerpau","last":"Glümer","name":"Glümer, Charlotte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristine","key":"faerchpau","last":"Faerch","name":"Faerch, Kristine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nina C B B","key":"veibypau","last":"Veiby","name":"Veiby, Nina C B B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28053777"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1155/2016/6138659","issn":["00071161","14682079"],"issn_org":["2090004X"],"journal":"British Journal of Ophthalmology","pages":"1-8","paperid":"6138659","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Ophthalmology","volume":"2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85008931766"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b6c36dce-7cdc-4c62-8c5b-931c616fba5c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Retinal Vessel Diameters and Their Relationship with Cardiovascular Risk and All-Cause Mortality in the Inter99 Eye Study : A 15-Year Follow-Up","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-502575","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Many weight-loss programs in children are performed without specific foci on training both physical fitness and motor skills. The aim of this study was to describe the effect of a one-year weight-loss program on children's motor skills and physical fitness. METHODS: Participants included 115 overweight fifth-grade children (12.0 years) randomized into either a Day-Camp Intervention Arm (DCIA), with a subsequent family-based support program or a low-intense Standard Intervention Arm (SIA). Physical fitness was assessed by vertical jump, hand grip strength, and a progressive cardio-respiratory fitness test. Motor skills were assessed by the Movement Assessment Battery for Children - second edition (M-ABC-2), age band 3. RESULTS: Loss to follow-up after 52 weeks was 19 % and 32 % in the DCIA and SIA, respectively. Balance skills were improved post-camp, but not after 52 weeks in children from the DCIA compared to the SIA. Contrary to the expected, children from the SIA improved aiming and catching skills relative to the DCIA children. Overall z-scores of the physical fitness components and cardio-respiratory fitness improved more in children from the DCIA compared to children from the SIA. CONCLUSION: In conclusion, the day-camp intervention led to improvements in physical fitness but not in motor skills compared to the standard intervention. Including both motor skills and physical fitness could advantageously be considered in future immersive intervention programmes. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Clinicaltrials NCT01574352, March 26, 2012 (retrospectively registered).","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Kristian Traberg","Huang, Tao","Runge, Lisbeth","Olesen, Line Grønholt","Andersen, Lars Bo","Møller, Niels Christian"],"cuid":["S02-083.45-049721"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["China","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian School of Sport Sciences","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","Sogn og Fjordane University College"],"keyword":["Børn","Children","Journal Article","Motor Skills","Motorik","Multi component intervention","Obesity","Overvægt","Overweight","Physical Fitness","RCT","Svær overvægt","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of a multi component camp based weight loss program on children s motor skills and physical fitness a randomized controlled trial","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12887-016-0627-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.45-049721","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4946099","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84978224636","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27416906","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-fda8460a-9367-432b-bd58-7c4aa561f302","ucl-66f4f95e-b763-4240-8513-d8383e3638f9"],"keyword":["Børn","Children","Fysisk fitness","Journal Article","Motor skills","Motorik","Multi-component intervention","Obesity","Overvægt","Overweight","Physical fitness","RCT","Svær overvægt","Weight loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6505946B3C539B2EC2068C227A1A27DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4946099/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12887-016-0627-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/123472282/The_effect_of_a_multi_component_camp_based_weight_loss_program_on_children_s.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, RICH - Research In Childhood Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Exercise Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Pædagogik og Samfund, Anvendt Forskning i Pædagogik og Samfund"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"norwegian school of sport sciences","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian School of Sport Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"no","key":"sogn og fjordane university college","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Sogn og Fjordane University College","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Traberg","key":"larsenkristiantrabergpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d0e5d5a1-d1e7-4e78-9b2b-97efa080bc24","name":"Larsen, Kristian Traberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3918-6645","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lisbeth Runge","key":"larsenlisbethrungepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5e6862b3-bad8-4a63-aebf-424468603937","name":"Larsen, Lisbeth Runge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tao","key":"huangtaopau","last":"Huang","locid":"05bff937-3953-4e47-87a3-d60bf0e0ad1b","name":"Huang, Tao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth Runge","key":"rungelisbethpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f8ec914f-7057-4cec-907a-ea5e23bef6e0","name":"Runge, Lisbeth","name_org":"Larsen, Lisbeth Runge","orcid":"0000-0002-4378-7785","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Grønholt","key":"olesenlinegrønholtpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"e9ad7180-8cce-4e88-9707-18dedc4c73e0","name":"Olesen, Line Grønholt","orcid":"0000-0002-6588-8878","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Bo","key":"andersenlarsbopau","last":"Andersen","locid":"e868e64f-3441-4506-8f4c-25f0a72c1e73","name":"Andersen, Lars Bo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Christian","key":"møllernielschristianpau","last":"Møller","locid":"f453a8f3-668c-40a5-bcf2-d05243a89418","name":"Møller, Niels Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-5842-5595","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27416906"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12887-016-0627-5","issn":["14712431"],"journal":"BMC Pediatrics","paperid":"91","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Pediatrics","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978224636"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-fda8460a-9367-432b-bd58-7c4aa561f302","ucl-66f4f95e-b763-4240-8513-d8383e3638f9"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"The effect of a multi-component camp-based weight-loss program on children's motor skills and physical fitness : a randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.45-049721","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Sustainable agricultural production on coarse sandy soil is constrained by the restricted growth of roots, and poor water and nutrient retention. Amending the soil with biochar can reduce these problems, but the processes involved are not known in detail. We investigated in the laboratory the effects of two fine-grained gasification biochars made of straw (LTST) and other materials (LTSN) and of one fast pyrolysis straw biochar (FPST) on pore-size distribution and soil compressibility when added to coarse sandy subsoil. Water retention and therefore pore-size distribution were affected systematically. All biochars converted drainable pore space with pore diameters in the range 60-300 mu m into water-retaining pores of size 0.2-60 mu m, which was taken as an estimate of available water capacity (AWC). Effects were linear over the whole range of biochar (0-4% by mass). The effect of LTST and LTSN on AWC (3.6% by volume per % biochar) was about 70% larger than the effect of the somewhat coarser FPST biochar (2.1% by volume per % biochar). The compression index increased linearly with biochar content without any significant effects from the type of biochar. The common least squares estimate of the slope was 21.2kgm(-3)%(-1) by weight. The results reflect a strong interaction at the microscopic scale between biochar and soil rather than intrinsic properties of the added biochar. How fine-grained biochars added to sandy soil affect water retention and soil compressibility. Such combined effects have not been investigated previously in coarse sandy subsoil. Pore space was changed from drainable to water retaining, and the soil became easier to compress. Fine-grained biochars were more efficient than a coarser biochar in changing the pore space.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Petersen, C. T.","Hansen, E.","Larsen, H. H.","Hansen, L. V.","Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","Hauggaard-Nielsen, H."],"cuid":["S03-099.03-037137"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["AMENDMENT","Carbon sequestration","Denmark","Retention","Soil"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pore size distribution and compressibility of coarse sandy subsoil with added biochar","src":["dtu","ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84994910715","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-099.03-037137","identifier":[{"id":"000388477100002","type":"wos"},{"id":"84994910715","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-c9acd5ba-ac21-44df-a847-30167c61eafc","ku-2d262a4e-5cd6-4ae5-ba70-0bc4cf68f112","ruc-40a3cdd0-2191-4ea3-b288-24e4be91d691"],"keyword":["AMENDMENT","CARBON SEQUESTRATION","DENMARK","RETENTION","SOIL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-122F54FA5A8E566F3317E30875BE6FE4"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Environmental Chemistry and Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CHEC Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten Tilbæk","key":"petersencarstentilbækpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1a96f560-f27c-4ca0-b48a-6130456a37b8","name":"Petersen, Carsten Tilbæk","orcid":"0000-0001-7574-0351","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Emilie Marie Øst","key":"hansenemiliemarieøstpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"4f706025-c34b-4d0f-b819-4c4e27dcdb6a","name":"Hansen, Emilie Marie Øst","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"E.","key":"hansenepau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"H. H.","key":"larsenhhpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, H. H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"L. V.","key":"hansenlinevintherpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"99992d9f-8b1f-4f8a-abab-90af1aa9af50","name":"Hansen, Line Vinther","name_org":"Hansen, L. V.","orcid":"0000-0001-6734-9440","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"ahrenfeldtjesperpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","locid":"9fef4394-4b16-4061-8cc6-0da0fe3996b3","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3999-5864","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J.","key":"ahrenfeldtjpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","name":"Ahrenfeldt, J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"hauggaardnielsenhenrikpau","last":"Hauggaard-Nielsen","locid":"0bc8cc02-9199-4a75-9e51-7dd5ceba9583","name":"Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-8929-9691","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"H.","key":"hauggaardnielsenhpau","last":"Hauggaard-Nielsen","name":"Hauggaard-Nielsen, H.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ejss.12383","issn":["13510754","13652389"],"issn_org":["13510754"],"issue":"6","journal":"European Journal of Soil Science","pages":"726-736","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Soil Science","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994910715"],"sdg":["2. Zero Hunger","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c9acd5ba-ac21-44df-a847-30167c61eafc","ku-2d262a4e-5cd6-4ae5-ba70-0bc4cf68f112","ruc-40a3cdd0-2191-4ea3-b288-24e4be91d691"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Pore-size distribution and compressibility of coarse sandy subsoil with added biochar","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.03-037137","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The present study examines responses to 10 weeks of aerobic training and/or erythropoiesis-stimulating agent (ESA) treatment on maximal oxygen uptake ((V) over dotO(2)max). Thirty-six healthy, untrained men were randomly assigned to sedentary-placebo (n = 9), sedentary-ESA (SE) (n = 9), training-placebo (TP) (n = 10), or training-ESA (TE) (n = 8). The participants were treated subcutaneously once weekly with ESA (darbepoietin-alpha, week 1-3; 40 mu g and week 4-10; 20 mu g) or a placebo for 10 weeks. The training consisted of supervised cycling 3 times per week for 1 hour at an average of 65% of maximal watt, with a progressive overload during the intervention period. (V) over dotO(2)max, wattmax, and hematological values were measured throughout the study. In addition, the total training workload and estimated energy consumption were recorded after each training session. ESA treatment increased hemoglobin (similar to 11 and similar to 14%, p <0.001) and hematocrit (similar to 12 and similar to 13%, p <0.001) in the SE and TE groups, respectively. The relative (but not absolute) increases in (V) over dotO(2)max were more pronounced (p <0.01) in TE (27 +/- 6%), compared with SE (15 +/- 4%) but not TP (19 +/- 4%), indicating that training is superior to ESA in stimulating (V) over dotO(2)max in untrained men. The increased oxygen uptake in the TE group did not result in higher absolute training workloads than in the TP group. In untrained men, training exhibits a greater stimulus for improvements in (V) over dotO(2)max than ESA treatment, without pronounced additive effects, which is supported by similar average training workloads and energy consumption in TP and TE. Thus, in untrained men, training alone seems sufficient to induce improvement in (V) over dotO(2)max.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sieljacks, Peter","Thams, Line","Nellemann, Birgitte","Larsen, Mads Sørensen","Vissing, Kristian","Christensen, Britt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-217878"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Comparative Study","Darbepoetin alfa","Erythropoietin","Exercise","Hematinics","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Oxygen Consumption","Randomized Controlled Trial","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparative effects of aerobic training and erythropoietin on oxygen uptake in untrained humans","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84982794707","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-217878","identifier":[{"id":"000380752800031","type":"wos"},{"id":"84982794707","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26694499","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9b671b06-65bf-4e6f-bfc9-a23c50a8a32a"],"keyword":["Adult","Comparative Study","Darbepoetin alfa","Erythropoietin","Exercise","Hematinics","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Oxygen Consumption","Randomized Controlled Trial","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CBDFCCE49D0595B8C06A59641F9A146A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Sport Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"sieljackspau","last":"Sieljacks","locid":"027fade5-fd85-47ba-ac29-636265797645","name":"Sieljacks, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"thamspau","last":"Thams","name":"Thams, Line","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"nellemannpau","last":"Nellemann","locid":"d715ca68-7276-407b-a149-14c985b93afe","name":"Nellemann, Birgitte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Sørensen","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7614c2e7-5a5d-4796-ad6d-6bd3b41a1e99","name":"Larsen, Mads Sørensen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian","key":"vissingpau","last":"Vissing","locid":"2a18fabb-7859-4d82-9b88-25be869db47c","name":"Vissing, Kristian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Britt","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"818501d4-b691-497c-b25b-b792b1040bc0","name":"Christensen, Britt","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26694499"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1519/jsc.0000000000001314","issn":["10648011","15334287"],"issn_org":["10648011"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of Strength and Conditioning Research","pages":"2307-2317","publisher":"NSCA National Strength and Conditioning Association","status":"p","title":"Journal of Strength and Conditioning Research","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84982794707"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9b671b06-65bf-4e6f-bfc9-a23c50a8a32a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Comparative Effects of Aerobic Training and Erythropoietin on Oxygen Uptake in Untrained Humans","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-217878","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background Infections with the three feline haemotropic mycoplasmas Mycoplasma haemofelis, Candidatus Mycoplasma haemominutum and Candidatus Mycoplasma turicensis cause feline infectious anemia. The purpose of this study was to investigate the prevalence of carriage of feline haemoplasma in Danish cats in different age groups. The presence was detected by a conventional polymerase chain reaction (PCR) assay on blood samples as well as by real-time PCR (RT-PCR). Results The study revealed a prevalence of 14.9% Candidatus Mycoplasma haemominutum positive cats and 1.5% Mycoplasma haemofelis positive cats. No cats were found positive for Candidatus Mycoplasma turicensis. The results showed a statistically significant higher prevalence in older (>8 years) cats compared to younger cats and a higher prevalence among domestic cats compared to purebred cats. As part of this study, we developed a cloning strategy to obtain Danish positive controls of haemoplasma 16S rRNA. Conclusion From convenience-sampled cats in Denmark, we found that 16.4% were carriers of feline haemotropic mycoplasmas. Haemoplasma was mostly found in older and domestic cats. The prevalence found in Denmark is similar to that found in several other European countries.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rosenqvist, Maja Benedicte","Meilstrup, Ann-Katrine Helene","Larsen, Jesper","Olsen, John Elmerdahl","Jensen, Asger Lundorff","Thomsen, Line Elnif"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-503489"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Prevalence","Real time PCR","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence of feline haemoplasma in cats in denmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13028-016-0260-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-503489","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5103603","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84994845387","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27832803","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000388328200002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-b8594c1c-97d3-425a-820a-4026e0000cdd"],"keyword":["Conventional PCR","Feline haemoplasma","Prevalence","Real-time PCR","Risk factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FE4DFB5DABA688AA678CFAD3E6120423"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13028-016-0260-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/170079259/art_3A10.1186_2Fs13028_016_0260_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maja Benedicte","key":"rosenqvistpau","last":"Rosenqvist","locid":"4a2e3607-4709-4853-970e-2adf2f7737bb","name":"Rosenqvist, Maja Benedicte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ann-Katrine Helene","key":"meilstruppau","last":"Meilstrup","locid":"594a718c-00ec-4757-9e91-220a8584ca88","name":"Meilstrup, Ann-Katrine Helene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"4c1f078a-c093-405a-9812-257e0d717095","name":"Larsen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"John Elmerdahl","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d7f792e1-ac2c-4d67-8887-3615a3a98edb","name":"Olsen, John Elmerdahl","orcid":"0000-0001-6225-6587","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Asger Lundorff","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"82070307-d574-4caa-961a-ed2dc20528d8","name":"Jensen, Asger Lundorff","orcid":"0000-0003-2048-9221","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Elnif","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"e8fab8c4-e7bb-404b-81dc-910f78e64ff0","name":"Thomsen, Line Elnif","orcid":"0000-0001-5460-9178","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27832803"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13028-016-0260-1","issn":["0044605X","17510147"],"issn_org":["0044605X"],"journal":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","paperid":"78","status":"p","title":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","title_org":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica (Online)","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994845387"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b8594c1c-97d3-425a-820a-4026e0000cdd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prevalence of feline haemoplasma in cats in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-503489","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Purpose – It is important within public health goals to promote adolescents’ mental health and to reduce socioeconomic inequalities in mental health. Among adults there are indications that the socioeconomic pattern of low positive mental health (PMH) differs from the socioeconomic pattern of high PMH. Knowledge regarding the social epidemiology of PMH among young people is lacking. The purpose of this paper is to examine the socioeconomic patterning of aspects of low and high PMH among adolescents. Design/methodology/approach – The Health Behaviour in School-aged Children Methodology Development Study 2012 provided data on 3,670 adolescents aged 11-15 in two municipalities in Denmark. Socioeconomic differences in aspects of low and high PMH (self-esteem, social competence and self-efficacy) were investigated by calculating sex-specific prevalence of PMH in socioeconomic groups measured by parents’ occupational social class. Using multi-level logistic regression analyses, odds ratios for low and high PMH compared to moderate PMH were estimated. Findings – In age-adjusted analyses there seemed to be a graded relationship with increasing odds for low PMH with decreasing socioeconomic position, but no indication of a socioeconomic patterning of high PMH. The prevalence of high self-esteem and high self-efficacy was higher among boys than girls. High social competence and high self-efficacy increased with age. Research limitations/implications – Public health research has primarily focused on risk factors and mental health problems. Research highlighting more detailed aspects of PMH is needed. Originality/value – The socioeconomic pattern of high PMH may be different from the socioeconomic pattern of low PMH.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Line","Stewart-Brown, Sarah","Vinther-Larsen, Mathilde","Meilstrup, Charlotte","Holstein, Bjørn Evald","Koushede, Vibeke"],"cuid":["S03-092.50-735476"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"a