{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Le, Thao Thi Thu","Villumsen, Nanna Stengaard","Møller, Hanne Søndergård","Ravn Nielsen, Line","Bang Nielsen, Søren","Hammershøj, Marianne","Larsen, Lotte Bach"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-274035"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-02","place":"Papendal, nl","start":"2015-09-30","title":"9th NIZO Dairy Conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proteomic investigation of aggregates formed during storage of whey protein drinks","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-274035","ids":["au-fda84f54-9462-4cce-81c4-48ed29a3bb21"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6C9A522D1BB446E6EDB286FFAF2DB56D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Food Science, Department of Food Science - Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"arla foods","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ARLA","l3nl":"Arla Foods","l3nn":"Arla Foods","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Arla Foods","namevar":["Arla Foods"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ARLA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thao Thi Thu","key":"lepau","last":"Le","locid":"f114fe35-c2f1-437d-b00b-8beded4747a9","name":"Le, Thao Thi Thu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna Stengaard","key":"villumsenpau","last":"Villumsen","locid":"45a4023b-95a1-44a9-9923-86230284ddee","name":"Villumsen, Nanna Stengaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Søndergård","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"ee4bfcda-2bdc-4dd6-90cc-3c3d00e2dbad","name":"Møller, Hanne Søndergård","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"ravnnielsenpau","last":"Ravn Nielsen","name":"Ravn Nielsen, Line","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"bangnielsenpau","last":"Bang Nielsen","name":"Bang Nielsen, Søren","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne","key":"hammershøjpau","last":"Hammershøj","locid":"483a27e1-b030-4e4b-8441-76424c064fed","name":"Hammershøj, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0001-9297-6526","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte Bach","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"204d7240-6828-4ee0-8ef5-77a4a2ac92d4","name":"Larsen, Lotte Bach","orcid":"0000-0001-9674-0107","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Arla Foods","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fda84f54-9462-4cce-81c4-48ed29a3bb21"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Proteomic investigation of aggregates formed during storage of whey protein drinks","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-274035","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Immunomodulatory host defense peptides (HDPs) are considered to be lead compounds for novel anti-sepsis and anti-inflammatory agents. However, development of drugs based on HDPs has been hampered by problems with toxicity and low bioavailability due to in vivo proteolysis. Here, a subclass of proteolytically stable HDP mimics consisting of lipidated α-peptide/β-peptoid oligomers was investigated for their effect on neutrophil function. The most promising compound, Pam-(Lys-βNSpe)6-NH2, was shown to inhibit formyl peptide receptor 2 (FPR2) agonist-induced neutrophil granule mobilization and release of reactive oxygen species. The potency of Pam-(Lys-βNSpe)6-NH2 was comparable to that of PBP10, the most potent FPR2-selective inhibitor known. The immunomodulatory effects of structural analogues of Pam-(Lys-βNSpe)6-NH2 emphasized the importance of both the lipid and peptidomimetic parts. By using imaging flow cytometry in primary neutrophils and FPR-transfected cell lines we found that a fluorescently labelled analogue of Pam-(Lys-βNSpe)6-NH2 interacted selectively with FPR2. Furthermore the interaction between Pam-(Lys-βNSpe)6-NH2 and FPR2 was found to prevent binding of the FPR2-specific activating peptide agonist Cy5-WKYMWM, while the binding of a FPR1-selective agonist was not inhibited. To our knowledge, Pam-(Lys-βNSpe)6-NH2 is the first HDP mimic found to inhibit activation of human neutrophils via direct interaction with FPR2. Hence, we consider Pam-(Lys-βNSpe)6-NH2 to be a convenient tool in the further dissection of the role of FPR2 in inflammation and homeostasis as well as for investigation of the importance of neutrophil stimulation in anti-infective therapy involving HDPs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Skovbakke, Sarah Line","Heegaard, Peter M. H.","Larsen, Camilla J.","Franzyk, Henrik","Forsman, Huamei","Dahlgren, Claes"],"cuid":["S02-098.50-037157"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Anti inflammatory","Formyl peptide receptors","G protein coupled receptors","Host defense peptides","Neutrophils"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the proteolytically stable peptidomimetic pam lys ßnspe sub 000000000006 sub nh sub 000000000002 sub selectively inhibits human neutrophil activation via formyl peptide receptor 000000000002","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bcp.2014.11.004","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.50-037157","identifier":[{"id":"25462815","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84920718913","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ca72f537-82b5-4f42-b8c9-f8eb9989d299","ku-25742f42-83e0-408e-a12e-b0d935b51d7e"],"keyword":["Anti-inflammatory","Formyl peptide receptors","G-protein-coupled receptors","Host defense peptides","Neutrophils"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-69427DBC07B4B676B723642C60FC98B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bcp.2014.11.004","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/102674783/1_s2.0_S0006295214006613_main.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":2014},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Natural Products and Peptides"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Immunology and Vaccinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah Line","key":"skovbakkepau","last":"Skovbakke","locid":"6c43699f-79b1-42e1-bc75-5783c8024f41","name":"Skovbakke, Sarah Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter M. H.","key":"heegaardpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"f15c1dfb-4275-4369-9b2b-2af936d2e0e6","name":"Heegaard, Peter M. H.","orcid":"0000-0003-4506-4932","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla J.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Camilla J.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"franzykpau","last":"Franzyk","locid":"5120ce68-6886-4ac8-8178-310a47d19261","name":"Franzyk, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2822-1927","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Huamei","key":"forsmanpau","last":"Forsman","name":"Forsman, Huamei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Claes","key":"dahlgrenpau","last":"Dahlgren","name":"Dahlgren, Claes","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25462815"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bcp.2014.11.004","issn":["00062952","18732968"],"issn_org":["00062952"],"issue":"2","journal":"Biochemical Pharmacology","pages":"182-195","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biochemical Pharmacology","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84920718913"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ca72f537-82b5-4f42-b8c9-f8eb9989d299","ku-25742f42-83e0-408e-a12e-b0d935b51d7e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Proteolytically Stable Peptidomimetic Pam-(Lys-ßNSpe)<sub>6</sub>-NH<sub>2</sub> Selectively Inhibits Human Neutrophil Activation via Formyl Peptide Receptor 2","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.50-037157","year":"2015","yearsub":2015}
{"abstract":"Importance: The CHA2DS2-VASc score (congestive heart failure, hypertension, age ≥75 years [doubled], diabetes, stroke/transient ischemic attack/thromboembolism [doubled], vascular disease [prior myocardial infarction, peripheral artery disease, or aortic plaque], age 65-75 years, sex category [female]) is used clinically for stroke risk stratification in atrial fibrillation (AF). Its usefulness in a population of patients with heart failure (HF) is unclear. Objective: To investigate whether CHA2DS2-VASc predicts ischemic stroke, thromboembolism, and death in a cohort of patients with HF with and without AF. Design, Setting, and Population: Nationwide prospective cohort study using Danish registries, including 42 987 patients (21.9% with concomitant AF) not receiving anticoagulation who were diagnosed as having incident HF during 2000-2012. End of follow-up was December 31, 2012. Exposures: Levels of the CHA2DS2-VASc score (based on 10 possible points, with higher scores indicating higher risk), stratified by concomitant AF at baseline. Analyses took into account the competing risk of death. Main Outcomes and Measures: Ischemic stroke, thromboembolism, and death within 1 year after HF diagnosis. Results: In patients without AF, the risks of ischemic stroke, thromboembolism, and death were 3.1% (n = 977), 9.9% (n = 3187), and 21.8% (n = 6956), respectively; risks were greater with increasing CHA2DS2-VASc scores as follows, for scores of 1 through 6, respectively: (1) ischemic stroke with concomitant AF: 4.5%, 3.7%, 3.2%, 4.3%, 5.6%, and 8.4%; without concomitant AF: 1.5%, 1.5%, 2.0%, 3.0%, 3.7%, and 7% and (2) all-cause death with concomitant AF: 19.8%, 19.5%, 26.1%, 35.1%, 37.7%, and 45.5%; without concomitant AF: 7.6%, 8.3%, 17.8%, 25.6%, 27.9%, and 35.0%. At high CHA2DS2-VASc scores (≥4), the absolute risk of thromboembolism was high regardless of presence of AF (for a score of 4, 9.7% vs 8.2% for patients without and with concomitant AF, respectively; overall P<.001 for interaction). C statistics and negative predictive values indicate that the CHA2DS2-VASc score performed modestly in this HF population with and without AF (for ischemic stroke, 1-year C statistics, 0.67 [95% CI, 0.65-0.68] and 0.64 [95% CI, 0.61-0.67], respectively; 1-year negative predictive values, 92% [95% CI, 91%-93%] and 91% [95% CI, 88%-95%], respectively). Conclusions and Relevance: Among patients with incident HF with or without AF, the CHA2DS2-VASc score was associated with risk of ischemic stroke, thromboembolism, and death. The absolute risk of thromboembolic complications was higher among patients without AF compared with patients with concomitant AF at high CHA2DS2-VASc scores. However, predictive accuracy was modest, and the clinical utility of the CHA2DS2-VASc score in patients with HF remains to be determined.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Melgaard, Line","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Lane, Deidre A","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Lip, Gregory Y H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-054337"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessment of the cha000000000002ds000000000002 vasc score in predicting ischemic stroke thromboembolism and death in patients with heart failure with and without atrial fibrillation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-054337","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000360840700015","type":"wos"},{"id":"26318604","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84941625442","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0eb4a28a-09ba-45a2-a38a-03f69de3bc9f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-725B979272E032E64624906562442DDF"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"melgaardpau","last":"Melgaard","locid":"88687b9c-5b56-4584-a89a-89fdeca4fd54","name":"Melgaard, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"gorstrasmussenpau","last":"Gorst-Rasmussen","locid":"2aa85786-c0b1-42ec-93d4-eb7a75696409","name":"Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Deidre A","key":"lanepau","last":"Lane","name":"Lane, Deidre A","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Hvilsted","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"20cfd847-7f3e-4c77-88c0-32d3432496ed","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Bjerregaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a3c6747f-b9db-488b-8eb9-887d38742880","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y H","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26318604"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jama.2015.10725","issn":["00987484","01851160"],"issn_org":["00987484"],"issue":"10","journal":"JAMA  The Journal of the American Medical Association","pages":"1030-1038","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA  The Journal of the American Medical Association","title_org":"JAMA: The Journal of the American Medical Association","volume":"314"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84941625442"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0eb4a28a-09ba-45a2-a38a-03f69de3bc9f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Assessment of the CHA2DS2-VASc Score in Predicting Ischemic Stroke, Thromboembolism, and Death in Patients With Heart Failure With and Without Atrial Fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-054337","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Stroke in patients with heart failure is associated with poor outcomes. Risk stratification schemes may improve clinical decision making in this patient population. This study investigated whether female sex is a risk factor for stroke in patients with heart failure in sinus rhythm. METHODS: This is a population-based cohort study of patients diagnosed with heart failure during 2000 to 2012, identified by record linkage between nationwide Danish registries. Our primary outcome was stroke, and secondary outcome was thromboembolic event. We used relative risks (RRs) after 1 and 5 years to compare males with females within each of the following age groups: 50 to 59 years, 60 to 69 years, 70 to 79 years, 80 to 89 years, and 90+ years. Analyses took into account the competing risks of death. RESULTS: During the study period, 84,142 patients were diagnosed with heart failure, of which 39,946 (47.5%) were females. At 5-year follow-up, female sex was associated with a lower risk of stroke compared with males (adjusted overall hazard ratio 0.91, 95% CI 0.85-0.96). The observed lower risks of stroke in females were not present in the older age groups, where the competing risk of death was substantial among males in particular. When considering a more broadly defined thromboembolic end point, a decreased risk among females persisted across nearly all age groups after 5-year follow-up (adjusted overall hazard ratio 0.93, 95% CI 0.91-0.96). CONCLUSIONS: We found an association between female sex and decreased stroke risk in patients with heart failure, which persisted after adjustment for concomitant cardiovascular risk factors. The association was attenuated with increasing age, possibly because of competing risks of death.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Melgaard, Line","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Lip, Gregory Y H","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-068402"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City Hospital in Birmingham","University of Birmingham"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"female sex is associated with a lower risk of stroke in patients with heart failure","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-068402","identifier":[{"id":"25728730","type":"pmid"},{"id":"WOS:000351486800012","type":"wos"},{"id":"84926171158","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3f6af908-d10f-45d0-a433-d09070313d92"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D6B106954439431E743388327C8206E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjertemedicin (Kardiologi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Birmingham","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"city hospital in birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"City Hospital in Birmingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L