,"first":"Elvira","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Elvira","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle Rosgaard","key":"birknowpau","last":"Birknow","name":"Birknow, Michelle Rosgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Richardt Møllegaard","key":"jepsenpau","last":"Jepsen","name":"Jepsen, Jens Richardt Møllegaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Charlotte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"skovbypau","last":"Skovby","name":"Skovby, Flemming","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kerstin Jessica","key":"plessenpau","last":"Plessen","name":"Plessen, Kerstin Jessica","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"møruppau","last":"Mørup","locid":"7ffdfaca-76bd-44ec-a98f-13fe4f033b71","name":"Mørup, Morten","orcid":"0000-0003-4985-4368","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ollie","key":"hulmepau","last":"Hulme","name":"Hulme, Ollie","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"William Frans Christiaan","key":"baarepau","last":"Baare","name":"Baare, William Frans Christiaan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"didriksenpau","last":"Didriksen","name":"Didriksen, Michael","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hartwig Roman","key":"siebnerpau","last":"Siebner","name":"Siebner, Hartwig Roman","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"wergepau","last":"Werge","name":"Werge, Thomas","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Line","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26384214"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12888-015-0594-7","issn":["13594184","14765578"],"issn_org":["13594184"],"issue":"1","journal":"Molecular Psychiatry","pages":"1-12","paperid":"15:220","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Molecular Psychiatry","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84941644545"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Lundbeck Pharma","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5f0f1546-d521-4026-a67f-f257667b1b8a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The Danish 22q11 research initiative","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-332880","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Neurodevelopmental brain disorders such as schizophrenia, autism and attention deficit hyperactivity disorder are complex disorders with heterogeneous etiologies. Schizophrenia and autism are difficult to treat and often cause major individual suffering largely owing to our limited understanding of the disease biology. Thus our understanding of the biological pathogenesis needs to be substantiated to enable development of more targeted treatment options with improved efficacy. Insights into the pre-morbid disease dynamics, the morbid condition and the underlying biological disease mechanisms may come from studies of subjects with homogenous etiologies. Breakthroughs in psychiatric genetics have shown that several genetic anomalies predispose for neurodevelopmental brain disorders. We have established a Danish research initiative to study the common microdeletion at chromosome 22q11.2, which is one of the genetic anomalies that confer high risk of schizophrenia, autism and attention deficit hyperactivity disorder. METHODS/DESIGN: The study applies a \"cause-to-outcome\" strategy to identify pre-morbid pathogenesis and underlying biological disease mechanisms of psychosis and secondarily the morbid condition of autism and attention deficit hyperactivity disorder. We use a population based epidemiological design to inform on disease prevalence, environmental risk factors and familial disposition for mental health disorders and a case control study design to map the functional effects across behavioral and neurophysiological traits of the 22q11 deletion in a recruited sample of Danish individuals. DISCUSSION: Identification of predictive pre-morbid clinical, cognitive, functional and structural brain alterations in 22q11 deletion carriers may alter current clinical practice from symptomatic therapy of manifest mental illness into early intervention strategies, which may also be applicable to at risk subjects without known etiology. Hopefully new insights into the biological disease mechanisms, which are mandatory for novel drug developments, can improve the outcome of the pharmacological interventions in psychiatry.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Schmock, Henriette","Vangkilde, Anders","Larsen, Kit Melissa","Fischer, Elvira","Birknow, Michelle Rosgaard","Jepsen, Jens Richardt Møllegaard","Olesen, Charlotte","Skovby, Flemming","Plessen, Kerstin J","Mørup, Morten","Hulme, Ollie","Baaré, William Frans Christiaan","Didriksen, Michael","Siebner, Hartwig Roman","Werge, Thomas","Olsen, Line"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-470661"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Attention Deficit Disorder with Hyperactivity","Autistic Disorder","Case Control Studies","Child","Child Health Services","Chromosome Aberrations","Chromosomes Human Pair 22","Denmark","Humans","Mental Health Services","Research Design","Schizophrenia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the danish 000000000022q000000000011 research initiative","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12888-015-0594-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-470661","identifier":[{"id":"26384214","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4574168","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84941644545","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-80ffa911-ea33-4117-8fc6-b5b3dea9c380"],"keyword":["Attention Deficit Disorder with Hyperactivity","Autistic Disorder","Case-Control Studies","Child","Child Health Services","Chromosome Aberrations","Chromosomes, Human, Pair 22","Denmark","Humans","Mental Health Services","Research Design","Schizophrenia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-EC002C6196AEE738E9F866037CF5F1F2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12888-015-0594-7","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Henriette","key":"schmockpau","last":"Schmock","name":"Schmock, Henriette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"vangkildepau","last":"Vangkilde","name":"Vangkilde, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kit Melissa","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Kit Melissa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elvira","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Elvira","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michelle Rosgaard","key":"birknowpau","last":"Birknow","name":"Birknow, Michelle Rosgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Richardt Møllegaard","key":"jepsenpau","last":"Jepsen","name":"Jepsen, Jens Richardt Møllegaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Charlotte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming","key":"skovbypau","last":"Skovby","locid":"90d3162e-d18d-4a2c-8337-1840876ba49a","name":"Skovby, Flemming","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kerstin Jessica","key":"plessenpau","last":"Plessen","locid":"3c8af5dc-9bd6-4322-b9ba-13715978eaa8","name":"Plessen, Kerstin J","name_org":"Plessen, Kerstin Jessica","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"møruppau","last":"Mørup","name":"Mørup, Morten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ollie","key":"hulmepau","last":"Hulme","name":"Hulme, Ollie","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"William Frans Christiaan","key":"baarépau","last":"Baaré","name":"Baaré, William Frans Christiaan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"didriksenpau","last":"Didriksen","name":"Didriksen, Michael","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hartwig Roman","key":"siebnerpau","last":"Siebner","locid":"d9ed8669-a16b-429a-86ed-353ef481bb72","name":"Siebner, Hartwig Roman","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"wergepau","last":"Werge","locid":"905c01bb-6319-4ce6-a38e-ceb5bf73d2f6","name":"Werge, Thomas","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Line","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Line","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26384214"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12888-015-0594-7","issn":["1471244X"],"journal":"BMC Psychiatry","pages":"1-12","paperid":"220","status":"p","title":"BMC Psychiatry","title_org":"B M C Psychiatry","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84941644545"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-80ffa911-ea33-4117-8fc6-b5b3dea9c380"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Danish 22q11 research initiative","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-470661","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Cataract is the world-leading cause of blindness. In search for a new treatment of cataract we have found that the yellow discolouration of aged human lenses can be photobleached using a non-invasive, infra-red, femtosecond laser treatment. These results were presented in an earlier PlosOne publication. The objective of the study was to characterize the single-photon photobleaching action spectrum of the aged human lens in vitro. METHODS: Ninety-one human donor lenses were irradiated with continuous wave laser light at 375, 405, 420, 445, 457 or 473 nm. Photobleaching was monitored by photography and transmission measurements. RESULTS: The action spectrum peaked at 420 nm followed by, in order of decreasing effect, 445, 457, 473, 405 and 375 nm. Younger and less absorbent lenses showed smaller changes than older and more absorbent lenses. There was a dose-dependent increase in lens transmission with increasing laser irradiation. CONCLUSIONS: For a 75 year old lens an effect corresponding to elimination of 15 years or more of optical ageing was obtained. This study of the spectral characteristics and intensity needed to bleach the human lens with single-photon laser effects found an action-spectrum peak at 420 nm tailing gradually off toward longer wavelengths and more steeply toward shorter wavelengths. The results may be used to guide experiments with two-photon bleaching.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Kessel, Line","Larsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-483516"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Action spectrum","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Aging","Cataract","Humans","Lasers","Lens Crystalline","Light","Middle Aged","Photobleaching","Phototherapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"action spectrum for photobleaching of human lenses by short wavelength visible irradiation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0123732","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-483516","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4401553","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"25884924","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84930011723","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-96b804fc-c639-4764-8620-910138aa2f4a"],"keyword":["Action Spectrum","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Aging","Cataract","Humans","Lasers","Lens, Crystalline","Light","Middle Aged","Photobleaching","Phototherapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8615BD68204A1CB966CD419E6C04626A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0123732","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","name":"Kessel, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25884924"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0123732","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLOS ONE","pages":"1-9","paperid":"e0123732","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84930011723"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-96b804fc-c639-4764-8620-910138aa2f4a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Action spectrum for photobleaching of human lenses by short wavelength visible irradiation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-483516","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":8,"contributors":["Hestbech, Astrid Margrethe","Basse, Lena","Sukonnik, Anastasia Rindholt","Lie, Line Lindenskov","Møllmann, Mathias Theil","Lønborg, Henrik","Larsen, Nikolaj Søgaard","Villadsen, Tenna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-554909"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Didaktik"],"level":"pop","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"didaktik og teknologi i pædagogisk arbejde","src":["pha"],"src-code":["DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-554909","ids":["pha-a46eb149-cf01-4bf3-95a4-aa7133392ea6"],"keyword":["didaktik"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","noi":["Local-1-1-B7AECC322B05E65A44968A1F59541C68"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Pædagogik og Ledelsesområdet, Absalon - Bevægelse, kreativitet og æstetik i pædagogisk arbejde","Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Ledelses og Fællesfunktioner (LOF), Forskning og Innovation, Ledelse og fællesfunktioner Sorø"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid Margrethe","key":"hestbechpau","last":"Hestbech","locid":"6f930212-8774-451d-8812-c26adc3e4389","name":"Hestbech, Astrid Margrethe","orcid":"0009-0009-3217-9213","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"bassepau","last":"Basse","locid":"c8e5719b-f6be-4a60-8075-b05808f0753f","name":"Basse, Lena","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anastasia Rindholt","key":"sukonnikpau","last":"Sukonnik","name":"Sukonnik, Anastasia Rindholt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Lindenskov","key":"liepau","last":"Lie","name":"Lie, Line Lindenskov","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Theil","key":"møllmannpau","last":"Møllmann","name":"Møllmann, Mathias Theil","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"lønborgpau","last":"Lønborg","name":"Lønborg, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikolaj Søgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Nikolaj Søgaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tenna","key":"villadsenpau","last":"Villadsen","name":"Villadsen, Tenna","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788792717320"],"pages":"233-240","publisher":"UCSJ Forlag","status":"p","title":"Velfærd, teknologi og læring i et professionsperspektiv"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-a46eb149-cf01-4bf3-95a4-aa7133392ea6"],"src":["AB University College Absalon"],"title":"Didaktik og teknologi i pædagogisk arbejde","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-554909","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"It seems that social capital in the neighbourhood has the potential to reduce socioeconomic differences in mental health among adolescents. Whether school social capital is a buffer in the association between socioeconomic position and mental health among adolescents remains uncertain. The aim of this study is therefore to examine if the association between socioeconomic position and emotional symptoms among adolescents is modified by school social capital. The Health Behaviour in School-aged Children Methodology Development Study 2012 provided data on 3549 adolescents aged 11-15 in two municipalities in Denmark. Trust in the school class was used as an indicator of school social capital. Prevalence of daily emotional symptoms in each socioeconomic group measured by parents' occupational class was calculated for each of the three categories of school classes: school classes with high trust, moderate trust and low trust. Multilevel logistic regression analyses with parents' occupational class as the independent variable and daily emotional symptoms as the dependent variable were conducted stratified by level of trust in the school class. The prevalence of emotional symptoms was higher among students in school classes with low trust (12.9%) compared to school classes with high trust (7.2%) (p < 0.01). In school classes with low level of trust, the odds ratio for daily emotional symptoms was 1.89 (95% CI 1.25-2.86) in the low socioeconomic group compared to the high socioeconomic group. In school classes characterised by high and moderate trust, there were no statistically significant differences in emotional symptoms between high and low socioeconomic groups. Although further studies are needed, this cross-sectional study suggests that school social capital may reduce mental health problems and diminish socioeconomic inequality in mental health among adolescents.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Line","Koushede, Vibeke","Vinther-Larsen, Mathilde","Bendtsen, Pernille","Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","Due, Pernille","Holstein, Bjørn Evald"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-614887"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"does school social capital modify socioeconomic inequality in mental health a multi level analysis in danish schools","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.socscimed.2015.07.002","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-614887","identifier":[{"id":"26189012","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84937035896","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-91678c9d-cc41-43fe-a0e6-3f8cbb1ea4ac"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1E3464770A13ADD4EE279C108C7AF28"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.socscimed.2015.07.002","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Children health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"70e5e888-ca96-4dae-b64a-36817ddc113b","name":"Nielsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4127-4361","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vibeke","key":"koushedepau","last":"Koushede","locid":"67798c78-14a3-4025-83ec-311b56fc0d15","name":"Koushede, Vibeke","orcid":"0000-0002-7302-1334","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathilde","key":"vintherlarsenpau","last":"Vinther-Larsen","locid":"2ed449a2-142b-47de-9899-efa1dccbd166","name":"Vinther-Larsen, Mathilde","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"bendtsenpau","last":"Bendtsen","locid":"2f10fe8b-e58b-44d8-98bd-7a19dfe9bc1c","name":"Bendtsen, Pernille","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette Kjær","key":"ersbøllpau","last":"Ersbøll","locid":"ba343517-a6c5-47c1-a8ba-4cbe00b7409c","name":"Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-9407-3387","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille","key":"duepau","last":"Due","locid":"3a9676ac-1003-4109-8423-b6f77372721f","name":"Due, Pernille","orcid":"0000-0002-7839-2580","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjørn E","key":"holsteinpau","last":"Holstein","locid":"303aa8e2-44ee-4317-ab4a-8f64355f7bf5","name":"Holstein, Bjørn Evald","name_org":"Holstein, Bjørn E","orcid":"0000-0002-4348-280X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26189012"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.socscimed.2015.07.002","issn":["02779536","18735347"],"issn_org":["02779536"],"issue":"September","journal":"Social Science & Medicine","pages":"35-43","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Social Science & Medicine","volume":"140"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84937035896"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-91678c9d-cc41-43fe-a0e6-3f8cbb1ea4ac"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Does school social capital modify socioeconomic inequality in mental health? : A multi-level analysis in Danish schools","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-614887","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Visible aggregates formed during storage in acidic whey protein isolate (WPI) dispersions represent a challenge to the beverage industry. Batch-to-batch variations are observed that prevents consistent quality and shelf-life prediction. Heat-treatment of WPI dispersions at 120°C for 20s instead of conventional heating at 95°C for 180s often prevents the aggregate formation, and varying levels of divalent cations were proposed to contribute to the observed batch-to-batch variations. In this study, the composition of the visible aggregates was examined. Caseinomacropeptide (CMP) was enriched in the visible aggregates compared with the surrounding clear liquid. Disruption of electrostatic interactions between glycosylated and non-glycosylated CMPs were studied by addition of calcium, acidification, and enzymatic de-sialidation. The treatment strategies each significantly decreased time-dependent turbidity development in acidic WPI dispersions. This suggests that the storage-induced aggregates may be prevented by disruption of electrostatic interactions between negatively-charged sialic acid residues and positively-charged amino acids.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Villumsen, Nanna Stengaard","Jensen, Hanne Bak","Le, Thao Thi Thu","Møller, Hanne Søndergård","Nordvang, Rune Thorbjørn","Ravn Nielsen, Line","Bang Nielsen, Søren","Sørensen, John","Hammershøj, Marianne","Larsen, Lotte Bach"],"cuid":["S02-096.70-015371"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Calcium","Caseinomacropeptide","Sialic acid","Whey protein","Whey protein isolate"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"