{"abstract":"DANMAP (Danish Antimicrobial Resistance Monitoring and Research Program) has monitored antimicrobial resistance and consumption of antimicrobial agents in food animals and in humans in Denmark since 1995. This report describes changes and trends in 2013.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Agersø, Yvonne","Bager, Flemming","Boel, Jeppe","Helwigh, Birgitte","Borck Høg, Birgitte","Jensen, Lars Bogø","de Knegt, Leonardo","Korsgaard, Helle Bisgaard","Larsen, Lars Stehr","Sørensen, Anna Irene Vedel","Dalby, Tine","Hammerum, Anette M.","Hoffmann, Steen","Gaardbo Kuhn, Katrin","Rhod Larsen, Anders","Laursen, Maja","Nielsen, Eva Møller","Olsen, Stefan S.","Petersen, Andreas","Bagger-Skjøt, Line","Skov, Robert L.","Slotved, Hans-Christian","Torpdahl, Mia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-329875"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danmap 000000002013 use of antimicrobial agents and occurrence of antimicrobial resistance in bacteria from food animals food and humans in denmark","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/103485043/DANMAP_2013.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-329875","ids":["dtu-551c507b-7bbf-4d99-b3b8-704bc5509db5"],"lang":"English","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-24882220353267F273508E2C4BF0A249"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.danmap.org/~/media/Projekt%20sites/Danmap/DANMAP%20reports/DANMAP%202013/DANMAP%202013.ashx","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/103485043/DANMAP_2013.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Epidemiology and Microbial Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yvonne","key":"agersøpau","last":"Agersø","locid":"727ec55d-b40c-4ff2-b27e-cc347dbeb7ed","name":"Agersø, Yvonne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Flemming","key":"bagerpau","last":"Bager","locid":"441a0c23-e75b-47f0-9683-afef5d81a701","name":"Bager, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0003-0165-5968","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe","key":"boelpau","last":"Boel","locid":"5867f9ab-f23b-4d3d-88b5-7628e0ecf196","name":"Boel, Jeppe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte","key":"helwighpau","last":"Helwigh","locid":"2d9fbd6d-7113-4463-bc88-b29da7fb762f","name":"Helwigh, Birgitte","orcid":"0000-0003-0442-0195","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte","key":"borckhøgpau","last":"Borck Høg","locid":"40edeaf1-a01a-42a0-bc2c-96edff748fe5","name":"Borck Høg, Birgitte","orcid":"0000-0003-3506-9086","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Bogø","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"9976ddc2-1da0-4f04-9044-cf3bc2ab52ed","name":"Jensen, Lars Bogø","orcid":"0000-0002-0077-1118","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leonardo","key":"deknegtpau","last":"de Knegt","locid":"98305da4-9892-482b-8311-9b2428f0bb42","name":"de Knegt, Leonardo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle","key":"korsgaardpau","last":"Korsgaard","locid":"bd6d48e5-2d2c-4c29-ba33-467ef364767f","name":"Korsgaard, Helle Bisgaard","name_org":"Korsgaard, Helle","orcid":"0000-0001-9257-9889","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Stehr","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3890eace-6277-40f2-b2b5-0b93efc64a92","name":"Larsen, Lars Stehr","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna Irene Vedel","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"8df5f1a9-ab36-43ad-8a29-12adf0f1b106","name":"Sørensen, Anna Irene Vedel","orcid":"0000-0002-3877-4592","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine","key":"dalbypau","last":"Dalby","name":"Dalby, Tine","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette M.","key":"hammerumpau","last":"Hammerum","name":"Hammerum, Anette M.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen","key":"hoffmannpau","last":"Hoffmann","name":"Hoffmann, Steen","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrin","key":"gaardbokuhnpau","last":"Gaardbo Kuhn","name":"Gaardbo Kuhn, Katrin","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rhodlarsenpau","last":"Rhod Larsen","name":"Rhod Larsen, Anders","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","name":"Laursen, Maja","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Møller","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Eva Møller","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan S.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Stefan S.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Andreas","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"baggerskjøtpau","last":"Bagger-Skjøt","name":"Bagger-Skjøt, Line","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert L.","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Robert L.","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans-Christian","key":"slotvedpau","last":"Slotved","name":"Slotved, Hans-Christian","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mia","key":"torpdahlpau","last":"Torpdahl","name":"Torpdahl, Mia","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"106","publisher":"Statens Serum Institut","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-551c507b-7bbf-4d99-b3b8-704bc5509db5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"DANMAP 2013 : Use of antimicrobial agents and occurrence of antimicrobial resistance in bacteria from food animals, food and humans in Denmark","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-329875","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Dairy products have previously been reported to be associated with beneficial effects on body weight and metabolic risk markers. Moreover, primary data from the Diet, Obesity and Genes (DiOGenes) study indicate a weight-maintaining effect of a high-protein-low-glycaemic index diet. The objective of the present study was to examine putative associations between consumption of dairy proteins and changes in body weight and metabolic risk markers after weight loss in obese and overweight adults. Results were based on secondary analyses of data obtained from overweight and obese adults who completed the DiOGenes study. The study consisted of an 8-week weight-loss phase and a 6-month weight-maintenance (WM) phase, where the subjects were given five different diets varying in protein content and glycaemic index. In the present study, data obtained from all the subjects were pooled. Dairy protein intake was estimated from 3 d dietary records at two time points (week 4 and week 26) during the WM phase. Body weight and metabolic risk markers were determined at baseline (week - 9 to - 11) and before and at the end of the WM phase (week 0 and week 26). Overall, no significant associations were found between consumption of dairy proteins and changes in body weight and metabolic risk markers. However, dairy protein intake tended to be negatively associated with body weight gain (P= 0·08; β = - 0·17), but this was not persistent when controlled for total protein intake, which indicates that dairy protein adds no additional effect to the effect of total protein. Therefore, the present study does not report that dairy proteins are more favourable than other proteins for body weight regulation.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bendtsen, Line Quist","Lorenzen, Janne Kunchel","Larsen, Thomas Meinert","van Baak, Marleen","Papadaki, Angeliki","Martinez, J Alfredo","Handjieva-Darlenska, Teodora","Jebb, Susan A","Kunešová, Marie","Pfeiffer, Andreas F H","Saris, Wim H M","Astrup, Arne","Raben, Anne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-407633"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Bulgaria","Czechia","Germany","Greece","Netherlands","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Department of Nutrition, Dietetics and Metabolic Diseases, National Transport Hospital, Sofia","Department of Social Medicine, Preventive Medicine & Nutrition Clinic, University of Crete, Heraklion, Crete","Elsie Widdowson Laboratory, MRC Human Nutrition Research, Cambridge","Maastricht University Medical Center","The Obesity Management Center, Institute of Endocrinology, Prague","University of Navarra"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations between dairy protein intake and body weight and risk markers of diabetes and cvd during weight maintenance","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S0007114513003322","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-407633","identifier":[{"id":"84899736891","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24168904","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-17cc8a22-20c3-44c9-b648-b9869be98e02"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DFF678B0B40DA551C374C2D40AD2C7C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S0007114513003322","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"maastricht university medical center","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Maastricht University Medical Center","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gr","key":"department of social medicine preventive medicine nutrition clinic university of crete heraklion crete","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Department of Social Medicine, Preventive Medicine & Nutrition Clinic, University of Crete, Heraklion, Crete","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"es","key":"university of navarra","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Navarra","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"bg","key":"department of nutrition dietetics and metabolic diseases national transport hospital sofia","loc":["Bulgaria","Europe, EU"],"name":"Department of Nutrition, Dietetics and Metabolic Diseases, National Transport Hospital, Sofia","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"elsie widdowson laboratory mrc human nutrition research cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Elsie Widdowson Laboratory, MRC Human Nutrition Research, Cambridge","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"cz","key":"the obesity management center institute of endocrinology prague","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The Obesity Management Center, Institute of Endocrinology, Prague","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"de","key":"charité universitätsmedizin berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line Quist","key":"bendtsenpau","last":"Bendtsen","locid":"d59f6a91-604e-4dbc-9692-3df71bb7f765","name":"Bendtsen, Line Quist","orcid":"0000-0002-9541-7989","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janne Kunchel","key":"lorenzenpau","last":"Lorenzen","locid":"d8755162-ea5d-46be-b486-15f75a00b42b","name":"Lorenzen, Janne Kunchel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Meinert","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"be620f10-2a0e-430c-94d1-5246c8ef122a","name":"Larsen, Thomas Meinert","orcid":"0000-0001-7621-3131","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marleen","key":"vanbaakpau","last":"van Baak","name":"van Baak, Marleen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Angeliki","key":"papadakipau","last":"Papadaki","name":"Papadaki, Angeliki","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"J Alfredo","key":"martinezpau","last":"Martinez","name":"Martinez, J Alfredo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Teodora","key":"handjievadarlenskapau","last":"Handjieva-Darlenska","name":"Handjieva-Darlenska, Teodora","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Susan A","key":"jebbpau","last":"Jebb","name":"Jebb, Susan A","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Marie","key":"kunešovápau","last":"Kunešová","name":"Kunešová, Marie","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Andreas F H","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","name":"Pfeiffer, Andreas F H","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Wim H M","key":"sarispau","last":"Saris","name":"Saris, Wim H M","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","locid":"5d943631-c9fc-4b63-8aaa-263ba4248735","name":"Astrup, Arne","orcid":"0000-0001-8968-8996","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"rabenpau","last":"Raben","locid":"fdac50bf-ccda-4ed1-b344-0b16301c45e8","name":"Raben, Anne","orcid":"0000-0001-5229-4491","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24168904"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0007114513003322","issn":["00071145","14752662"],"issn_org":["00071145"],"issue":"5","journal":"British Journal of Nutrition","pages":"944-953","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Nutrition","volume":"111"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84899736891"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-17cc8a22-20c3-44c9-b648-b9869be98e02"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Associations between dairy protein intake and body weight and risk markers of diabetes and CVD during weight maintenance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-407633","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This study reports for the 1st time the incidence and interobserver variation of morphologic findings in a series of 34 term placentas from pregnancies with normal outcome used for perfusion studies. Histologic evaluation of placental tissue is challenging, especially when it comes to defining \"normal tissue\" versus \"pathologic lesions.\" A scoring system for registration of abnormal morphologic findings was developed. Light microscopic examination was performed independently by 2 pathologists, and interobserver variation was analyzed. Findings in normal and perfused tissue were compared and selected findings were tested against success parameters from the perfusions. Finally, the criteria for frequent lesions with fair to poor interobserver variation in the nonperfused tissue were revised and reanalyzed. In the perfused tissue, the perfusion artefact \"trophoblastic vacuolization,\" which is believed to represent dilated transtrophoblastic channels, was reproducible and significantly correlated to the perfusion marker \"fetal leakage.\" In longer perfusions, microscopy of the perfused cotyledon revealed bacteria in the fetal vessels. This finding led to an adjustment in the perfusion protocol with addition of antibiotics to the medium. In the \"normal\" tissue, certain lesions were very frequent and showed only fair or poor interobserver agreement. Revised minimum criteria for these lesions were defined and found reproducible. This study has emphasized the value of pathologic examination as a supplement in placental perfusion models. Examination of the perfused cotyledon for trophoblastic vacuolization is recommended as an additional quality marker in perfusion models. The study also underlines the need for exact definitions of abnormality in frequent placental lesions.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Maroun, Lisa Leth","Mathiesen, Line","Hedegaard, Morten","Knudsen, Lisbeth E.","Larsen, Lise Grupe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-480240"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Female","Fetus","Humans","Perfusion","Placenta","Placenta Diseases","Pregnancy","Trophoblasts"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pathologic evaluation of normal and perfused term placental tissue","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2350/12-08-1243-OA.1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-480240","identifier":[{"id":"24945897","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84916941151","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9140dd49-51a4-42a3-9222-5817e59264f6"],"keyword":["Female","Fetus","Humans","Perfusion","Placenta","Placenta Diseases","Pregnancy","Trophoblasts"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0C855A81A42474BDA35103A20BAEB8A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2350/12-08-1243-OA.1","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Environmental Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lisa Leth","key":"marounpau","last":"Maroun","name":"Maroun, Lisa Leth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"58ded241-3a44-4af3-af98-85b0d1c106bf","name":"Mathiesen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-3210-159X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"hedegaardpau","last":"Hedegaard","name":"Hedegaard, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lisbeth E.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"53cd3578-ea67-4e7c-a12a-e4db7c0aecd4","name":"Knudsen, Lisbeth E.","orcid":"0000-0002-9576-1202","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lise Grupe","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"469adb96-7fdb-4d00-af58-645432255915","name":"Larsen, Lise Grupe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24945897"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2350/12-08-1243-oa.1","issn":["10935266","16155742"],"issn_org":["10935266"],"issue":"5","journal":"Pediatric and Developmental Pathology","pages":"330-8","status":"p","title":"Pediatric and Developmental Pathology","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84916941151"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9140dd49-51a4-42a3-9222-5817e59264f6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pathologic evaluation of normal and perfused term placental tissue","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-480240","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Background: Risk medications are frequently associated with adverse events and hospitalisations. Objective: To evaluate a risk medication screening service for in-patients at Danish hospitals. Setting: Danish hospitals. Methods: The study was designed as a controlled, prospective intervention study. Inpatients were screened for the use of five risk medications; anticoagulants, digoxin, methotrexate, NSAIDs and opioids, and during the intervention period recommendations were made by clinical pharmacists according to a standardized intervention scheme. The recommendations were discussed with the physician face-to-face. Main outcome measure: Readmissions within 6 months after discharge. Results: In total, 1,007 control and 775 intervention patients were included in the study. The study found that half of the patients (50 % during the control and 48 % during the intervention period) admitted to Danish hospitals were treated with at least one of the five selected risk medications, significantly more drug related problems (DRPs) were identified during the control period (1.7/patient during the control and 1.4/patient during the intervention period (p < 0.001)), and the acceptance rate of recommendations (62 %) was similar to medication management service studies in the literature (39-100 %). However, no impact on outcome measures was found. The majority (69 %) of the clinical pharmacists reported that they had increased their professional competences by participating in the study, and that a national clinical pharmacy study may be used in promoting and implementing a unique clinical pharmacy service throughout the country (67 %). Conclusion: The study showed that a national screening service for risk medications could help identify and address DRPs. Despite no impact on the selected outcome measures, it is likely that the screening service could be included in a medication management review with further focus on the individual patient to ensure positive outcomes, or that the screening service should be delivered to selected patients groups, who might have maximum benefit of the service.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","Clemmensen, Marianne Hald","Kronborg, Christian","Hedegaard, Ulla","Larsen, Line Hedegaard","Yderstræde, Inger Olsen","Nielsen, Jette Lyngholm","Nielsen, Trine Rune Høgh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-579236"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Clinical pharmacy","Cooperative Behavior","Denmark","Drug Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions","Female","Hospital","Humans","Intervention","Male","Middle Aged","Personal Satisfaction","Pharmacists","Pharmacy Service Hospital","Screening"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of a controlled national collaboration study on a clinical pharmacy service of screening for risk medications","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11096-013-9905-6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-579236","identifier":[{"id":"84899918193","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24346818","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-151539d9-f62f-4cd8-9dc0-2c3ec37b9609"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Clinical pharmacy","Cooperative Behavior","Denmark","Drug-Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions","Female","Hospital","Humans","Intervention","Male","Middle Aged","Personal Satisfaction","Pharmacists","Pharmacy Service, Hospital","Risk medication","Screening"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0A986FE7184B3B51B1F0A8E6ED0A950"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11096-0