{"abstract":"Ultrasmall superparamagnetic iron oxide (USPIO) nanoparticles are currently being used as a magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) contrast agent in vivo, mainly by their passive accumulation in tissues of interest. However, a higher specificity can ideally be achieved when the nanoparticles are targeted towards cell specific receptors and this may also facilitate specific drug delivery by an enhanced target-mediated endocytosis. We report efficient peptide-mediated targeting of magnetic nanoparticles to cells expressing the urokinase plasminogen activator receptor (uPAR), a surface biomarker for poor patient prognosis shared by several cancers including breast, colorectal, and gastric cancers. Conjugation of a uPAR specific targeting peptide onto polyethylene glycol (PEG) coated USPIO nanoparticles by click chemistry resulted in a five times higher uptake in vitro in a uPAR positive cell line compared to nanoparticles carrying a non-binding control peptide. In accordance with specific receptor-mediated recognition, a low uptake was observed in the presence of an excess of ATF, a natural ligand for uPAR. The uPAR specific magnetic nanoparticles can potentially provide a useful supplement for tumor patient management when combined with MRI and drug delivery.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Hansen, Line","Larsen, Esben Kjær Unmack","Nielsen, Erik H","Iversen, Frank","Liu, Zhuo","Thomsen, Karen","Pedersen, Michael","Skrydstrup, Troels","Nielsen, Niels Christian","Ploug, Michael","Kjems, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S02-098.91-021431"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Amino Acid Sequence","Click chemistry","Ferric Compounds","Fluorescent Dyes","HEK293 Cells","Humans","Magnetite Nanoparticles","Microscopy Confocal","Peptides","Polyethylene Glycols","Protein Binding","Receptors Urokinase Plasminogen Activator"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"targeting of peptide conjugated magnetic nanoparticles to urokinase plasminogen activator receptor upar expressing cells","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c3nr32922d","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.91-021431","identifier":[{"id":"23835641","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84881501276","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7804499a-617a-4f89-adf7-ac9de52b0060","ku-a69f9800-9ee9-4877-a4ca-244665f6ee24"],"keyword":["Amino Acid Sequence","Click Chemistry","Ferric Compounds","Fluorescent Dyes","HEK293 Cells","Humans","Magnetite Nanoparticles","Microscopy, Confocal","Peptides","Polyethylene Glycols","Protein Binding","Receptors, Urokinase Plasminogen Activator"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7C2B4FDD4CC7D9C24956F9E6AF63AFD9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c3nr32922d","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Interdisciplinær Nanoscience Forskerskole"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, BRIC, BRIC Research Groups, Ploug Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"hansenlinepau","last":"Hansen","locid":"729ea402-8050-4923-a2a1-2bfeb5a6fd63","name":"Hansen, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben Kjær","key":"larsenesbenkjærunmackpau","last":"Unmack Larsen","locid":"82092ac6-5b78-4893-82dd-bb85986e3deb","name":"Larsen, Esben Kjær Unmack","name_org":"Unmack Larsen, Esben Kjær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik Holm","key":"nielsenerikhpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5af3517b-283c-4bf7-a032-7425c90913ee","name":"Nielsen, Erik H","name_org":"Nielsen, Erik Holm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik Holm","key":"nielsenerikholmpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8ea621ef-6fd6-46b9-a77c-32962ac0fc6f","name":"Nielsen, Erik Holm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"iversenfrankpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"f0babff1-2ee6-4435-8f25-4cd3589b8129","name":"Iversen, Frank","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Frank Horsbøl","key":"iversenfrankhorsbølpau","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Frank Horsbøl","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhuo","key":"liuzhuopau","last":"Liu","locid":"15bcdf20-3c44-4b3b-82e8-53859ec74a0c","name":"Liu, Zhuo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"thomsenkarenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"f4c356b3-e82b-4991-b7de-55ad6ffd6738","name":"Thomsen, Karen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Karen Sand","key":"thomsenkarensandpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Karen Sand","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"pedersenmichaelpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"871199c4-33bb-4fac-95ef-9a2266f30695","name":"Pedersen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-1146-0382","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Troels","key":"skrydstruptroelspau","last":"Skrydstrup","locid":"67f8ccf9-98a3-4760-a864-1d012fffc489","name":"Skrydstrup, Troels","orcid":"0000-0001-8090-5050","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Christian","key":"nielsennielschristianpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"32a7422d-cc2f-4301-87c9-951639ed3662","name":"Nielsen, Niels Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-2978-4366","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels Chr","key":"nielsennielschrpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7864241c-2257-4391-baee-6efc4b783bde","name":"Nielsen, Niels Chr","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Michael","key":"plougmichaelpau","last":"Ploug","locid":"01123eb9-85b9-4fc2-bed4-1fe702dba814","name":"Ploug, Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-2215-4265","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"kjemsjørgenpau","last":"Kjems","locid":"f5915d75-aca3-437a-9a9d-f4fdfef7accd","name":"Kjems, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-9317","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23835641"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c3nr32922d","issn":["20403364","20403372"],"issn_org":["20403364"],"journal":"Nanoscale","pages":"8192-8201","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Nanoscale","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84881501276"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7804499a-617a-4f89-adf7-ac9de52b0060","ku-a69f9800-9ee9-4877-a4ca-244665f6ee24"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Targeting of peptide conjugated magnetic nanoparticles to urokinase plasminogen activator receptor (uPAR) expressing cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.91-021431","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES:The Rome III criteria for irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) are recommended by guidelines to help identify the syndrome. The majority of IBS patients are managed in primary care, where a pragmatic approach to diagnosis is usually adopted, using clinical judgment and knowledge about the patient. Many general practitioners (GPs) have no or limited knowledge of the diagnostic criteria, few use them, and many consider IBS a diagnosis of exclusion. The aim of this study is to explore the sensitivity of the Rome III criteria in relation to a GP-based clinical diagnosis of IBS, to identify differences between Rome III-positive and -negative patients, and to describe the agreement between the various symptom-based criteria.METHODS:Patients aged 18-50 years, presenting in primary care with gastrointestinal complaints and identified as IBS patients by their GP, were referred for enrollment. The Manning and Rome I-III criteria were evaluated through interviews and patients completed the questionnaires The Gastrointestinal Symptom Rating Scale (GSRS)/The Gastrointestinal Symptom Rating Scale modified for use in patients with IBS (GSRS-IBS), Short Form 36, Irritable Bowel Syndrome Quality of Life measurement, Work Productivity and Activity Impairment questionnaire - irritable bowel version, and a questionnaire on use of health-care resources.RESULTS:A total of 604 patients were referred and 499 were included (mean age 32.8 (s.d. 9.5) years, 75% were female). The Rome III criteria were fulfilled by 376 patients (sensitivity 0.75, 95% CI 71-79%). Rome III-positive patients more frequently reported disturbed defecation, had a higher symptom burden, and lower disease-specific health-related quality of life compared with Rome III-negative patients. The various symptom-based criteria identified slightly different subpopulations with the highest agreement between the Rome II and III criteria.CONCLUSIONS:The Rome III criteria identified three in four patients labeled with IBS in primary care. The relevance of the Rome III for IBS in primary care is supported.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Engsbro, Anne Line","Begtrup, Luise Mølenberg","Kjeldsen, Jens","Larsen, Pia Veldt","Schaffalitzky de Muckadell, Ove B.","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","Bytzer, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-586067"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patients suspected of irritable bowel syndrome cross sectional study exploring the sensitivity of rome iii criteria in primary care","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ajg.2013.15","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-586067","identifier":[{"id":"84878942911","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23419383","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-2cec67e8-3989-4459-bc23-48da0b46fc1a"],"keyword":["Colon irritabile"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F9D26B2DEC603620A8C1A0F28B642E30"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ajg.2013.15","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Line","key":"engsbropau","last":"Engsbro","name":"Engsbro, Anne Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luise Mølenberg","key":"begtruppau","last":"Begtrup","locid":"373d454c-b304-4570-820f-15b1692dd74b","name":"Begtrup, Luise Mølenberg","orcid":"0000-0003-2006-8558","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"4893b496-ebc1-4498-92aa-836500b4cb45","name":"Kjeldsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-8148-6572","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia Veldt","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d6c16700-b7c7-4172-a8df-3e726624dc36","name":"Larsen, Pia Veldt","orcid":"0000-0002-8730-3703","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ove Schaffalitzky","key":"demuckadellpau","last":"de Muckadell","locid":"3bc4ff3b-1f9d-4045-85de-b1d6d16f57f3","name":"Schaffalitzky de Muckadell, Ove B.","name_org":"de Muckadell, Ove Schaffalitzky","orcid":"0000-0003-1969-2329","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"bytzerpau","last":"Bytzer","name":"Bytzer, Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23419383"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ajg.2013.15","issn":["00029270","15720241"],"issn_org":["00029270"],"issue":"6","journal":"The American Journal of Gastroenterology","pages":"972-980","publisher":"Wolters Kluwer Health","status":"p","title":"The American Journal of Gastroenterology","volume":"108"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84878942911"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2cec67e8-3989-4459-bc23-48da0b46fc1a"],"src"