{"abstract":"Objectives To assess the detection rate of triploidy at first-trimester screening for trisomy 21 and evaluate outcome in triploid pregnancies. Methods From 2008 to 2011, 198 427 women with singleton pregnancies underwent first-trimester screening between 11 + 2 and 14 + 0 weeks' gestation. Screening parameters included nuchal translucency, maternal serum free β-human chorionic gonadotropin (β-hCG) and pregnancy-associated plasma protein-A (PAPP-A). In all triploid fetuses, these parameters were re-evaluated. Karyotypes were established by invasive testing (chorionic villus sampling or amniocentesis) or postabortem and obtained from the Danish Cytogenetic Central Register and the Danish Fetal Medicine Database. Results A total of 30 triploid fetuses underwent first-trimester screening. Twenty-five were diagnosed as a result of abnormal first-trimester scan findings, a detection rate of 83.3%. Twenty-three fetuses were identified due to a high risk for trisomy 13, 18 or 21 and two fetuses due to structural abnormalities. The incidence of triploidy at first-trimester screening was 1:6614. A smaller crown-rump length than that estimated by date of last menstrual period was found in 95% of the fetuses with data available for evaluation. Eight fetuses had a larger biparietal diameter than expected for gestational age. Fetuses with a 69,XXX karyotype had significantly lower multiples of the median values for β-hCG and PAPP-A than did 69,XXY fetuses (P = 0.045 and P = 0.02 forβ-hCG and PAPP-A, respectively). No infants with triploidy were born in the study period. Among the triploid gestations detected on first-trimester screening, 20 (80.0%) women chose termination of pregnancy, four (16.0%) had spontaneous miscarriage and one (4.0%) was stillborn. Conclusion First-trimester screening for trisomy 21 also provides a high detection rate for triploidy.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Engelbrechtsen, Line","Brøndum-Nielsen, Karen","Ekelund, Charlotte Kvist","Tabor, Ann","Skibsted, Lillian","Farlie, Richard","Hoseth, Eva","Larsen, Torben","Petersen, Olav Bjørn","Stornes, Inger","Vejerslev, Lars O.","Zingenberg, Helle"],"cuid":["S03-087.50-025622"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["Danish Fetal Medicine Study Group","the Danish Fetal Medicine Study Group"],"keyword":["Abnormalities","Adult","Crown Rump Length","Denmark","Down Syndrome diagnosis","Female","Fetal Diseases diagnosis","First trimester screening","Gestational Age","Humans","Karyotyping","Nuchal Translucency Measurement","Outcome","Parental origin","Pregnancy","Pregnancy Associated Plasma Protein A analysis","Pregnancy Outcome","Pregnancy Trimester First","Triploidy","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"detection of triploidy at 000000000011 000000000014 weeks of gestation a cohort study of 000000000198 000000000000 pregnant women","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/uog.12460","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-087.50-025622","identifier":[{"id":"23494847","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84886949371","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b19c7e28-827b-4912-aea2-c084bfc144f8","ku-50dd4953-19bd-4169-a020-6e179bd586ff","sdu-df00febd-10cc-45d9-8512-a1b4b82293c9"],"keyword":["Adult","Chorionic Gonadotropin, beta Subunit, Human/blood","Crown-Rump Length","Denmark","Down Syndrome/diagnosis","Female","Fetal Diseases/diagnosis","Gestational Age","Humans","Karyotyping","Nuchal Translucency Measurement","Pregnancy","Pregnancy Outcome","Pregnancy Trimester, First","Pregnancy-Associated Plasma Protein-A/analysis","Young Adult","abnormalities","first-trimester screening","outcome","parental origin","triploidy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-155E092897F90D84418A735328D0A551"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/uog.12460","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Medical Genetics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Gynaecology and Obstetrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"aff