{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Line","Vinther-Larsen, Mathilde","Meilstrup, Charlotte","Holstein, Bjørn Evald","Koushede, Vibeke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-586733"],"event":{"end":"2013-09-26","place":"London, gb","start":"2013-09-24","title":"The 8th World Congress on Promoting Mental Health","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"positive mental health among adolescents are there socioeconomic differences","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-586733","ids":["sdu-2f48c29f-4254-46a4-8f6b-f2c16d17f37e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-052BD89DF61390E4B36D01BFAA9F255E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Children health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"70e5e888-ca96-4dae-b64a-36817ddc113b","name":"Nielsen, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4127-4361","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathilde","key":"vintherlarsenpau","last":"Vinther-Larsen","locid":"2ed449a2-142b-47de-9899-efa1dccbd166","name":"Vinther-Larsen, Mathilde","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"meilstruppau","last":"Meilstrup","locid":"71e55e89-4123-4012-b917-9ba55f543556","name":"Meilstrup, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-5705-1288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjørn Evald","key":"holsteinpau","last":"Holstein","locid":"303aa8e2-44ee-4317-ab4a-8f64355f7bf5","name":"Holstein, Bjørn Evald","orcid":"0000-0002-4348-280X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vibeke","key":"koushedepau","last":"Koushede","locid":"67798c78-14a3-4025-83ec-311b56fc0d15","name":"Koushede, Vibeke","orcid":"0000-0002-7302-1334","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2f48c29f-4254-46a4-8f6b-f2c16d17f37e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Positive Mental Health among adolescents : are there socioeconomic differences?","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-586733","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND & AIMS: Guidelines recommend a positive strategy based on symptom criteria to diagnose patients with irritable bowel syndrome (IBS). We conducted a randomized noninferiority trial to determine whether a positive diagnostic strategy is noninferior to a strategy of exclusion, with regard to patients' health-related quality of life (HRQOL). METHODS: We studied 302 patients (18-50 years old) from primary care who were suspected of having IBS and referred by general practitioners. Patients who fulfilled the Rome III criteria for IBS with no alarm signals were randomly assigned to groups assessed by a strategy of exclusion (analyses of blood, stool samples for intestinal parasites, and sigmoidoscopies with biopsies) or a positive strategy (analyses of blood cell count and C-reactive protein). Patients were followed for 1 year. The primary end point was difference in change of HRQOL from baseline to 1 year between groups (on the basis of the Short Form 36 health survey, physical component summary, and noninferiority margin of 3 points). Secondary outcomes were change in gastrointestinal symptoms, satisfaction with management, and use of resources. Findings of diagnostic misclassification were registered. RESULTS: A positive strategy was noninferior to a strategy of exclusion (difference, 0.64; 95% confidence interval, -2.74 to 1.45). The positive diagnostic strategy had lower direct costs. Each approach had similar effects on symptoms, satisfaction, and subsequent use of health resources. No cases of inflammatory bowel disease, colorectal cancer, or celiac disease were found. CONCLUSIONS: In diagnosing IBS in primary care, use of a positive diagnostic strategy is noninferior to using a strategy of exclusion with regard to the patients' HRQOL. Our findings support the current guideline recommendations. ClinicalTrials.gov, Number NCT00659763 and NCT01153295.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Begtrup, Luise Mølenberg","Engsbro, Anne Line","Kjeldsen, Jens","Larsen, Pia Veldt","Schaffalitzky de Muckadell, Ove B.","Bytzer, Peter","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-606704"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Clinical Laboratory Techniques methods","Female","Humans","Irritable Bowel Syndrome diagnosis","Male","Middle Aged","Primary Health Care methods","Quality of Life psychology","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a positive diagnostic strategy is noninferior to a strategy of exclusion for patients with irritable bowel syndrome","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cgh.2012.12.038","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-606704","identifier":[{"id":"84880579974","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23357491","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-750dbfbf-b6ca-41b0-9c5d-9092f3522b50"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Clinical Laboratory Techniques/methods","Clinical Medicine/methods","Female","Humans","Irritable Bowel Syndrome/diagnosis","Male","Middle Aged","Primary Health Care/methods","Quality of Life/psychology","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-67D027800903A1CE2CEEA6A606CDEFB5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cgh.2012.12.038","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luise M","key":"begtruppau","last":"Begtrup","locid":"373d454c-b304-4570-820f-15b1692dd74b","name":"Begtrup, Luise Mølenberg","name_org":"Begtrup, Luise M","orcid":"0000-0003-2006-8558","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Line","key":"engsbropau","last":"Engsbro","name":"Engsbro, Anne Line","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"4893b496-ebc1-4498-92aa-836500b4cb45","name":"Kjeldsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-8148-6572","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia V","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d6c16700-b7c7-4172-a8df-3e726624dc36","name":"Larsen, Pia Veldt","name_org":"Larsen, Pia V","orcid":"0000-0002-8730-3703","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ove","key":"schaffalitzkydemuckadellpau","last":"Schaffalitzky de Muckadell","locid":"3bc4ff3b-1f9d-4045-85de-b1d6d16f57f3","name":"Schaffalitzky de Muckadell, Ove B.","name_org":"Schaffalitzky de Muckadell, Ove","orcid":"0000-0003-1969-2329","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"bytzerpau","last":"Bytzer","name":"Bytzer, Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte E","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","name_org":"Jarbøl, Dorte E","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23357491"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cgh.2012.12.038","issn":["15423565","15427714"],"issn_org":["15423565"],"issue":"8","journal":"Clinical Gastroenterology and Hepatology","pages":"956-962","publisher":"WB  Saunders","publisher_org":"W.B. Saunders","status":"p","title":"Clinical Gastroenterology and Hepatology","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880579974"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-750dbfbf-b6ca-41b0-9c5d-9092f3522b50"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A Positive Diagnostic Strategy Is Noninferior to a Strategy of Exclusion for Patients With Irritable Bowel Syndrome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-606704","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The chapter describes the programme Paamiut Asasara. The programme mobilised the local community from locally defined values and promoted shared community resilience as well as individual and family resilience.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Berliner, Peter","Larsen, Line Natascha","de Casas Soberón, Elena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228193"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Community","Community mobilisation","Motherhood","Resilience","Social resilience"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"case study promoting community resilience with local values greenland s paamiut asasara","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4614-0586-3","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-228193","identifier":[{"id":"85028513988","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ad67beba-e285-471b-a255-2570ca57b4df"],"keyword":["Community","Community mobilisation","Motherhood","Pamiut Asasara","Resilience","Social resilience"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-3A47BB2E6A6F4151B06749B1374DB20A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4614-0586-3","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Department of Education - Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"berlinerpau","last":"Berliner","locid":"e2ead9b5-e0a9-432d-b296-3d877e8183bf","name":"Berliner, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Natascha","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Line Natascha","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"decasassoberónpau","last":"de Casas Soberón","name":"de Casas Soberón, Elena","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-1-4614-0586-3","edition":"1.","eisbn":["9781461405863"],"isbn":["9781461405856"],"pages":"387-399","place":"New York","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"a handbook of theory and practice","title":"The social ecology of resilience"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84893392416"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ad67beba-e285-471b-a255-2570ca57b4df"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Case study: Promoting community resilience with local values – Greenland's Paamiut Asasara.","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-228193","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Aim: The aim of this study was to determine whether a natriuretic peptide infusion during reperfusion can reduce cardiomyocyte ischemia–reperfusion damage. Materials and methods: The effect of B-type natriuretic peptide (BNP) activity was assessed in vitro and in vivo: the cellular effect was determined by assessment of intracellular caspase activity and troponin T release from cultured HL-1 cells subjected to short-term hypoxia–reperfusion. Cardiac effects were further examined in pigs (n=25) that had been subjected to 1 h of regional cardiac ischemia, followed by 3 h of reperfusion. Results: HL-1 cardiomyocytes responded to exogenous BNP with increased cGMP activity (∼3-fold, P=0.0037) and hypoxia–reperfusion with increased vascular endothelial growth factor and BNPmRNA contents (2.3- and 2.5-fold, respectively, P<0.0001) and caspase activity (2.9-fold, P=0.03), but without a decrease in apoptotic changes in the BNP-stimulated cells. Pigs tolerated the BNP and CD-NP (a CNP analogue) infusion well, with a decrease in systemic blood pressure (∼15 mmHg) and increased diuresis compared with the controls. Left ventricular pressure decreased in the pigs that received BNP infusion compared with controls (P=0.02). A similar trend was observed in the pigs that received CD-NP infusion, although this was not significant (P=0.3). BNP and CD-NP infusion in pigs reduced total cardiac troponin T release by 46 and 40%, respectively (P=0.0015 and 0.0019), and were associated with improved RNA integrity in the ischemic left ventricular region (P<0.05). Conclusion: We report that natriuretic peptide infusion in vivo reduces cardiomyocyte injury in acute ischemia–reperfusion, possibly through indirect mechanisms (e.g. increased diuresis and vasodilation). The results suggest a role for natriuretic peptide therapy in human cardiac ischemia.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kousholt, Birgitte Saima","Larsen, Jens Rolighed","Bisgaard, Line Stattau","Burnett Jr., John C.","Hasenkam, J. Michael","Gøtze, Jens Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-269231"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"natriuretic peptide infusion reduces myocardial injury during acute ischemia reperfusion","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/XCE.0b013e328356c67b","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-269231","ids":["au-f554a90f-450e-4241-b0fe-5affefebe5a0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-578813F0FA40A21DCB859ECF0971098A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/XCE.0b013e328356c67b","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Cardiothoracic and Vascular Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"mayo clinic rochester mn","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte S.","key":"kousholtpau","last":"Kousholt","locid":"b48ea490-8f1c-4a6a-a621-95ea949b1c3c","name":"Kousholt, Birgitte Saima","name_org":"Kousholt, Birgitte S.","orcid":"0000-0001-8286-3624","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","correspondin