{"abstract":"We present two cases of rickettsial infections in travellers caused by Rickettsia typhi and R. africae respectively. The two cases illustrate the widely varying symptomatology and aetiology. Incidence and treatment of the disease are discussed. The diagnosis is complex, and we believe that rickettsiosis is an underestimated cause of fever in returned travellers from the tropics. In the past two years only 26 cases have been diagnosed in Denmark. Whenever rickettsiosis is clinically suspected, empiric treatment with doxycycline should be initiated.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kibsgaard, Line","Lindberg, Jens","Villumsen, John Steen","Larsen, Carsten Schade"],"cuid":["S02-087.59-028131"],"event":{"end":"2010-05-29","place":"Hamburg, de","start":"2010-05-26","title":"3rd Northern European Conference on Travel Medicine (NECTM)","year":"2010"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animals","Anti Bacterial Agents","Bites and Stings","C Reactive Protein","Doxycycline","Fever","Humans","Infection","Male","Middle Aged","Philippines","Platelet Count","Rickettsia Infections","South Africa","Tick borne diseases","Ticks","Travel"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rickettsiose er en overset årsag til feber hos den hjemvendte rejsende","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/79480318/Ricketsiose_er_en_overset_rsag_til_feber_hos_hjemvendte_rejsende.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-087.59-028131","identifier":[{"id":"84864582005","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22668648","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d570f4f4-0567-4a43-89d6-6ae9b035dbf1","au-eb3b2924-6a0