{"abstract":"Specification theories as a tool in the development process of component-based software systems have recently attracted a considerable attention. Current specification theories are however qualitative in nature and hence fragile and unsuited for modern software systems. We propose the first specification theory which allows to capture quantitative aspects during the refinement and implementation process.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bauer, Sebastian S.","Fahrenberg, Uli","Juhl, Line","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Legay, Alex","Thrane, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-116452"],"event":{"end":"2011-08-26","place":"Warsaw, pl","start":"2011-08-22","title":"36th International Conference on Mathematical Foundations of Computer Science","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Irisa/INRIA Rennes","Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantitative refinement for weighted modal transition systems","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-22993-0_9","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-116452","identifier":[{"id":"80052136418","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e467d028-d91e-4b46-a10b-a531273482e2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B8975D446D052FBFC765FEB9FAA7E52A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-22993-0_9","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilians universität münchen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"n