{"abstract":"The aim of this study was to assess the association between lifelong cumulative glycaemia estimated by lens fluorometry and the presence of retinopathy in individuals with type 2 diabetes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Munch, Inger Christine","Larsen, Michael","Borch-Johnsen, Knut","Glümer, C","Lund-Andersen, Henrik","Kessel, Line"],"cuid":["S02-098.65-040464"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Diabetic retinopathy","Female","Fluorometry","Humans","Lens Crystalline","Logistic Models","Male","Middle Aged"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cumulative glycaemia as measured by lens fluorometry association with retinopathy in type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-010-2023-2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.65-040464","identifier":[{"id":"79953825268","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21190013","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-16da6f60-1c4e-4c8e-a1a3-756c0a0ac52d","sdu-bc35aaa4-161c-4c7a-8a88-55a6e2e570ff"],"keyword":["Adult","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2","Diabetic Retinopathy","Female","Fluorometry","Humans","Lens, Crystalline","Logistic Models","Male","Middle Aged"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A7EFDDF76E14B180312141BA78B8E24B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-010-2023-2","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, DaCHE - Danish Centre for Health Economics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Quality in the Healthcare Services"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Neurology, Psychiatry and Sensory Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"I C","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","locid":"a1af1ee5-c4b4-44d8-a7af-b7c1ce0882ac","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","name_org":"Munch, I C","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","name_org":"Larsen, M","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Knut","key":"borchjohnsenpau","last":"Borch-Johnsen","locid":"4f64cee7-e50a-4f8c-8d5b-7dc951e4914a","name":"Borch-Johnsen, Knut","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"C","key":"glümerpau","last":"Glümer","name":"Glümer, C","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"H","key":"lundandersenpau","last":"Lund-Andersen","locid":"5277856f-b771-4658-bb2f-b292ec78ee6f","name":"Lund-Andersen, Henrik","name_org":"Lund-Andersen, H","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"L","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","name_org":"Kessel, L","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21190013"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00125-010-2023-2","issn":["0012186X","14320428"],"issn_org":["0012186X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Diabetologia","pages":"757-761","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"p","title":"Diabetologia","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953825268"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-16da6f60-1c4e-4c8e-a1a3-756c0a0ac52d","sdu-bc35aaa4-161c-4c7a-8a88-55a6e2e570ff"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cumulative glycaemia as measured by lens fluorometry: association with retinopathy in type 2 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.65-040464","year":"2011","yearsub":2012}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Understanding of the biochemical reactions taking place during ripening of salted herring is still rather limited. Therefore, salted herrings were traditionally produced and the impact of the brine composition was evaluated in relation to the development of the characteristic texture of salted herrings. The aim of this study was to measure the texture changes during ripening using two differentmethods and to correlate the texture changeswith brine composition andwith biochemical modifications at themolecular level. RESULTS: During ripening (up to 151 days), hardness was higher in salted herrings compared to raw herrings, irrespective of the brine composition. However, the increase in hardness of herring prepared with extra brine occurred later. After prolonged storage (371 days), hardness was found for both batches to decrease to the level of raw herring. The increase in hardness during the ripening period could be explained by free-radical-induced cross-linking of myosin and the formation of aggregates. In addition, degradation of these aggregates correlated with the decrease in hardness observed at 371 days. CONCLUSIONS: Texture changes during ripening of salted herrings can be explained by oxidative reactions inducing myosin cross-linking followed by subsequent degradation of thesemyosin aggregates. The brine composition might play a role in the development of herring texture but this need to be investigated in more details. c 2010 Society of Chemical Industry","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christensen, Mette","Andersen, Eva","Christensen, Line","Andersen, Mogens L.","Baron, Caroline P."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-036880"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Division of Seafood Research"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"textural and biochemical changes during ripening of old fashioned salted herrings","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jsfa.4190","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-036880","identifier":[{"id":"78650208538","type":"scopus"},{"id":"20981729","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-bd2dc85c-c2b8-425c-95b7-d74d8f3b713f","ku-e1d35aca-4da6-40a4-b4b8-31d52ab6d1d8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-66410532A54E1BB1AF097A3B18F57DE4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jsfa.4190","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Food Science, Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Division of Seafood Research"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mette","key":"christensenmettepau","last":"Christensen","locid":"47671170-00da-4dce-91dd-bc09c06624e3","name":"Christensen, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"andersenevapau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Eva","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"christensenlinebachpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"857e6ade-425f-451b-9c22-6005b8215f25","name":"Christensen, Line Bach","name_org":"Christensen, Line","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mogens Larsen","key":"andersenmogenslarsenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"cb1b131f-69dc-46eb-bb7a-5d0161d84ab5","name":"Andersen, Mogens Larsen","orcid":"0000-0003-4694-486X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline P.","key":"baroncarolineppau","last":"Baron","locid":"cfa47c1e-f671-4f49-ae43-6a54c660078a","name":"Baron, Caroline P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Caroline","key":"baroncarolinepau","last":"Baron","name":"Baron, Caroline","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["20981729"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/jsfa.4190","issn":["00225142","04493257"],"issn_org":["00225142"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of the Science of Food and Agriculture","pages":"330-336","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of the Science of Food and Agriculture","volume":"91"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78650208538"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bd2dc85c-c2b8-425c-95b7-d74d8f3b713f","ku-e1d35aca-4da6-40a4-b4b8-31d52ab6d1d8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Textural and biochemical changes during ripening of old-fashioned salted herrings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-036880","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Progesterone treatment reduces the risk of preterm delivery in high-risk singleton pregnancies. Our aim was to evaluate the preventive effect of vaginal progesterone in high-risk twins. METHODS: This was a subanalysis of a Danish-Austrian, double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized trial (PREDICT study), in which women with twin pregnancies were randomized to daily treatment with progesterone or placebo pessaries from 20-24 weeks until 34 weeks' gestation. This subpopulation consisted of high-risk pregnancies, defined by the finding of cervical length ≤ 10th centile at 20-24 weeks' gestation or history of either spontaneous delivery before 34 weeks or miscarriage after 12 weeks. Primary outcome was delivery before 34 weeks. Secondary outcomes were complications for infants including long-term follow-up by Ages and Stages Questionnaire (ASQ) at 6 and 18 months of age. RESULTS: In 72 (10.6%) of the 677 women participating in the PREDICT study, the pregnancy was considered to be high-risk, including 47 with cervical length ≤ 10th centile, 28 with a history of preterm delivery or late miscarriage and three fulfilling both criteria. Baseline characteristics for progesterone and placebo groups were similar. Mean gestational age at delivery did not differ significantly between the two groups either in patients with a short cervix (34.3 ± 4.1 vs. 34.5 ± 3.0 weeks, P = 0.87) or in those with a history of preterm delivery or late miscarriage (34.6 ± 4.2 vs. 35.2 ± 2.7 weeks, P = 0.62). Similarly, there were no significant differences between the treatment groups in maternal or neonatal complications and mean ASQ score at 6 and 18 months of age. CONCLUSION: In high-risk twin pregnancies, progesterone treatment does not significantly improve outcome.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Klein, K","Rode, Line","Nicolaides, K H","Krampl-Bettelheim, E","Tabor, Ann","Larsen, Helle","Uldbjerg, Niels","Vogel, Ida"],"cuid":["S04-086.79-015504"],"filters":{"ad